window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5101,"title":"Chapter 5101: Chapter 5100: Experimentation I","paragraphs":["Noah gazed toward Ozymandias.","His second body floated nearby in that transformed obsidian form, crystalline structures now visible beneath flesh that radiated the same golden brilliance his primary body displayed. They had undergone the same evolution through the same cycles of destruction and rebirth, both existences now Hadean in classification.","He sent the command through THE Hadean Organ of Civilization.","Ozymandias dissolved into streams of blue gold light that flowed across the tumultuous seas of Observable Force surrounding them. Those streams entered Noah’s chest, returning to THE Hadean Desmoterion where the titanic form would cultivate until needed again.","Noah looked at his hands.","Golden light still pressed outward through skin that seemed luminescent rather than merely fair. Everything about his existence felt different now, grander in ways he was still learning to comprehend.","Just what had his power reached at this time?","And what did it truly mean to be a Hadean Lifeform?","He turned his attention inward, directing his question inward.","\" Ruination...am I still considered a Bounded Lifeform?\"","The response came calmly.","|I find myself perceiving and obtaining information from our surroundings at rates that exceed my previous capacity by factors I am still calculating. Dozens of times faster, certainly. Dozens of times denser in the quality of what I can observe. The transformation you have undergone has elevated my own capabilities tremendously.|","A pause that felt contemplative rather than hesitant.","|As for your question regarding classification, the answer is not as simple as you might hope. You cannot be considered a Bounded Lifeform any longer. The limitations that define Bounded existence, the ceilings engineered into their foundations, the restrictions that prevent them from accessing Observable Force at densities reserved for higher classifications, none of these apply to you in your current state.|","|However, you are not a Gilded Lifeform either. The engineering that distinguishes Gilded from Bounded was not something you possessed at birth, and becoming Hadean has not retroactively granted you that engineering. You have achieved something else entirely, something that exists in territories I do not have sufficient reference points to map with confidence.|","|Even saying you exist between Bounded and Gilded may not be entirely accurate. You are Hadean. This classification seems to operate according to principles that do not align neatly with the spectrum that places Bounded at one end and Gilded at the other. It is rather difficult to measure your current state in terms of difference between those two categories.|","|What I can state definitively is this: as of right now, you remain lower than a Gilded Lifeform such as Ubergulden Adelheid. Her engineering grants her advantages that your transformation, impressive as it is, has not replicated. But the gap between you and such entities has narrowed considerably, and given your trajectory, I would not assume that gap to be permanent.|","...!","Right.","Ubergulden Adelheid.","Noah let that name roll through his awareness with consideration it deserved. Such a strange and grand name for someone who had presented herself as THE Secretive Eon, who had sealed her Gilded nature to live as Bounded. The cadence of the name suggested origins and traditions he knew nothing about, cultures among THE Gilded that existed beyond what his current knowledge could encompass.","She had been providing him Observable Force throughout his transformation. That connection still pulsed with warmth.","\" Tell me more about her ,\" Noah said. \" About Ubergulden Adelheid and what you’ve learned through our connection.\"","|I have been conducting a silent and secret analysis of her existence through the link she established, and I am pleased to report that sufficient examination has been completed to allow for meaningful interaction. Her engineering remains perceivable to your newly unlocked Existential Engineering capability.|","|Most relevantly for your immediate circumstances, you now possess the ability to communicate with her directly. The connection she established flows in both directions, and with your enhanced processing capabilities, you can easily send a message through that link for her to hear. Whether she chooses to respond, of course, remains her decision to make.|","...!","Well, that was something.","He filed that capability away for future use, recognizing that such communication would need to be approached with care given how little he still understood about her.","While he was thinking about all of this, movement drew his attention outward.","Naldine Manthon floated toward him through the tumultuous seas of Observable Force. Her singularity-dotted eyes blazed with intensity, ancient perception clearly working through what she was observing. She circled him slowly, her radiant white hair trailing behind her as she moved, her expression holding something between fascination and confusion.","She reached out and lifted his arm.","Her fingers pressed against his transformed flesh as if testing its composition, as if checking whether his structure matched what her senses were telling her. She turned his hand over, examined his palm, traced lines across his skin that seemed to follow pathways only she could perceive.","\" What... are you, really?\"","The question emerged with genuine bewilderment that she didn’t bother concealing.","Noah smiled at the familiar inquiry. He felt like he had been asked this before, many times, by entities across various classifications who couldn’t reconcile what they observed with what they understood to be possible.","Now Naldine Manthon asked the same question with the same inability to find satisfying answers.","He clenched his fist, feeling the power that coursed through transformed flesh and Hadean bone.","\" You can help me find out.\"","His voice hels confidence that pressed against the surrounding seas of Observable Force.","\"I need to test the extent of my new power, and you might make a good sparring partner.\"","...!","Naldine’s eyes became sharp at these words. The Vihuela formed from her own arm began to hum with authority that announced her classification to everything nearby.","Before she could reply, movement from another direction drew both their attention.","THE Primordial Paradox floated toward them through the multicolored seas, his massive obsidian form cutting through the tumultuous Observable Force. Behind him, pulled by chains of paradoxical light, Schrodinger’s Tomb drifted in his wake. Sammarthiel remained trapped within that uncertainty, flickering between alive and dead without resolution.","The ancient being looked at Noah with seriousness that his obsidian features somehow conveyed despite their inhuman nature.","\" Youngest.\"","His voice pressed against everything nearby.","\"I have returned after eons of absence, and I have much to catch up on in Helheim among other places. Old debts to collect or repay depending on how the accounting has shifted during my imprisonment.\"","He paused, his gaze holding something that might have been respect.","\"I will keep in touch.\"","Noah nodded at him with a smile.","\" Stay safe ,\" Noah said. \" For existence is vast and full of terrors.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox laughed at such words as he had said them himself what seemed like eons ago!","His obsidian form shook with that laughter, paradoxical light flickering across his features.","\" Indeed it is, Youngest. Indeed it is!\"","He turned away, pulling on the chains that connected him to Schrodinger’s Tomb. The massive prison of uncertainty drifted behind him as he moved toward the edge of the tumultuous seas, toward regions where the multicolored rain of THE Pluvial Epoch fell with intensity.","And then he disappeared into that rain, his obsidian form swallowed by cascading brilliance while dragging a Rhyacian Tier Primordial Architect trapped in paradoxical uncertainty behind him.","Alexander looked between Noah and Naldine.","His Enneagram pulsed with the dangerous light it had held since completing his work on Beowulf, nine points blazing with authority that seemed more substantial than it had been before this battle began. The network of Second Scale Existential Nociceptors now integrated into his existence hummed with potential that would take time to fully realize.","He let out a sigh of peace.","It was a strange sound coming from someone who had spent millions of subjective years being tortured, someone whose entire existence had been defined by agony inflicted by the entity now imprisoned within Noah’s chest. But the sigh carried contentment.","\"I know my limits and what can happen now.\"","His voice held calm that matched the peaceful sigh.","\" While I won’t do too much, won’t overextend myself into situations I can’t handle, I feel like hunting Primordial Architects. There are many across Observable Existence who operate like Beowulf did. Many who deserve what I will bring to them.\"","His eyes met Noah’s with understanding that didn’t require elaboration.","\"If I meet a wall that is too sturdy, I will let you know.\"","Noah nodded at these words with a smile. Alexander had his own path now, his own trajectory that would carry him toward heights that most couldn’t imagine reaching. The receptors of a Second Scale entity transplanted into his existence would provide advantages others couldn’t imagine as his foundation!","\" Hunt well ,\" Noah said simply.","Alexander turned and walked into the multicolored seas surrounding them. His figure moved through the tumultuous Observable Force with purpose, his form gradually becoming obscured as endless rain buffeted his existence from every direction. THE Pluvial Epoch’s downpour swallowed him just as it had swallowed THE Primordial Paradox, leaving no trace of his passage.","Noah watched him go.","With the receptors of a Second Scale transplanted into him, Alexander’s power would be experiencing a tremendous curve. He simply had to avoid meeting ridiculous adversity like Horus and Beowulf had represented, entities who exceeded him so vastly that even his new advantages couldn’t bridge the gap.","But he had his own path.","And that path was his to walk.","Only Noah and Naldine remained in this region now.","The tumultuous seas of Observable Force churned around them, golden brilliance mixing with multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce. The typhoons still spiraled in the distance. The lightning still arced between storm systems. And two beings floated at the center of it all, one newly transformed and one ancient beyond comprehension.","Noah turned to face Naldine fully.","\" Are you ready, Naldine Manthon?\"","His voice carried challenge that pressed against her existence!","\" You have always been so high and mighty, looking at me from classifications I couldn’t reach, speaking of dangers I couldn’t understand. I wish to see if I am still far from you, or whether in our short time together, I have gone ahead of you.\"","...!","He smiled devilishly as he said this. His multicolored hair blazed brighter. His golden skin illuminated with intensity that made looking at him difficult!","His pupils, shining like singularities of an unfathomable Cause, fixed upon her with attention that didn’t waver.","Naldine looked at him with sharp eyes.","The Vihuela in her hands buzzed with authority that exceeded what she had displayed during the battle against Grimvault and his companions. Her singularity-dotted gaze held something between anticipation and wariness, ancient existence recognizing that the being before her was no longer what he had been when she first agreed to teach him!","She floated away from him, putting distance between them that combat would require.","\" Since my perception cannot fully understand you, I won’t be taking it easy.\"","Her voice carried seriousness that matched her expression.","\" Whatever you have become, it exists in territories I cannot map. And things I cannot map are things that can hurt me if I underestimate them.\"","...!","Billowing power began to gather around her.","Observable Force flooded toward her...and blue infinity faintly shone inside her. Her Proterozoic Bones blazed with authority that pressed against the tumultuous seas surrounding them. Her Proterozoic Organs pulsed with rhythms!","Truly, she seemed to be past the door of Calymmian Proterozoic Scale.","Noah nodded at her words seriously.","\" Oh, you definitely should not take it easy.\"","His voice pressed against existence itself.","\" Otherwise, you may not survive.\"","BOOM!","He simply took a step forward.","And existence itself shook as if he was commanding all the Observable Force nearby, as if his movement had become authority that reality couldn’t ignore. The tumultuous seas parted around him!","The typhoons in the distance stuttered in their rotation. The lightning froze mid-arc as if waiting to see what would happen next!","Oh!"]},{"number":5102,"title":"Chapter 5102: Chapter 5101: Experimentation II","paragraphs":["In THE Infiniverse.","The Early Veiled Shore stretched before Noah’s perception with magisterial beauty that felt almost absurd given everything happening across Observable Existence!","Vibrant golden sand lined the beach where waves of crystalline water lapped against shores that had never known pollution or corruption. Inland, plots of multicolored farmland spread across gentle hills, sacred herbs of every variety growing vibrantly.","The multicolored rain of THE Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity continued even here.","Droplets of impossible brilliance fell, nourishing everything they touched with Quintessence Infiniforce that accelerated growth and enhanced potency. The herbs seemed to lean toward the rain as it fell, leaves spreading wider to catch more of what descended upon them.","On a plot filled with mystical floating lotuses, Noah stood with attention fixed on something far more interesting than sacred herbs.","Another body of his had just begun sparring with Naldine Manthon in the tumultuous seas of Observable Force that THE Wastes had become. That confrontation would test the limits of his Hadean transformation against someone who stood past the door of Calymmian classification. But this body, this consciousness operating within THE Infiniverse itself, had different work to accomplish.","Critical work.","A floating platform of soft luminescent material hovered among the mystical lotuses, their multicolored petals releasing fragrances that would have intoxicated lesser beings. And on that platform lay Barbatos .","Her short stature seemed almost delicate against the soft surface supporting her, dark hair splayed outward in waves that caught the light of Infinity.","That hair seemed to drink in the multicolored rain, strands glistening with moisture that carried power most beings couldn’t safely absorb. Her voluptuous figure was adorned in nothing but a loose white robe that revealed curves that drew attention regardless of how many times he had seen them.","She was breathing with relief now, chest rising and falling as she recovered from what he had just done.","He had pulled her from Yggdrheim without warning, extracted her from challenges she had been navigating within that realm of trials and tribulations.","Her dark eyes opened to look at him with an expression mixing curiosity and something more suggestive.","\" When you pulled me away from Yggdrheim while saying you wanted to try something, I had an entirely different idea in mind regarding what we would be trying.\"","...!","\"I imagined candles, perhaps. Certainly not being placed on a table like a specimen awaiting dissection.\"","She propped herself up on her elbows, the movement causing her robe to shift mesmerizingly.","\" What exactly are you planning on doing, Little Fish?\"","Little Fish.","She still used this term regardless of how his power had grown, and he found comfort in that consistency all the way from his time in Atlantis!","It was surreal to think about his time years ago as an Atlantean fighting demons.","Noah’s eyes were already shining like golden singularities as he looked at her.","\"I want to see if I have what it takes to be an Engineer.\"","...!","An Engineer.","Because he had gained the capability of Existential Engineering through his Hadean transformation. The ability to perceive the fundamental makeup of existence, to see the weavings that comprised beings at their most basic level, to potentially modify those weavings according to his will. He had not yet tested this capability, had not yet attempted to actually engineer anything.","He wanted to experiment now.","It seemed like something pivotal, a capability that could reshape how he approached advancement for himself and those connected to him. And this moment was as good as any to begin understanding what Existential Engineering truly allowed.","And this was a unqiue period.","Noah loved the relaxing period after major adversity.","Such times allowed him to breathe and gauge just how much he had grown. They provided space for experimentation, for exploration, for testing new capabilities without the pressure of enemies trying to kill him while he learned. Periods like this were rare. Sometimes he went from adversity to adversity without rest, from battle to breakthrough to battle again in cycles that left no room for contemplation.","One needed rest every now and then.","And his version of resting was keeping himself busy with work that didn’t involve immediate mortal danger.","Right now, that meant staring at the body of Barbatos with eyes that perceived existence differently than they ever had before.","\"Lie back ,\" he said softly.","She complied with curiosity burning in her dark eyes, settling against the soft platform while watching him with attention that missed nothing. Her robe shifted again as she moved, but neither of them paid that any mind. This was not about intimacy. This was about something potentially far more significant.","Noah brought his hands forward.","His palms pressed against various points of Barbatos’s body in a purposeful manner, fingers finding positions that his newly awakened perception identified as significant. Golden Observable Force gathered in one hand. Multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce gathered in the other. Both energies danced from his fingertips, entering her body through pathways that only Existential Engineering could perceive.","Barbatos closed her eyes and bit her lip.","The sensation was clearly stimulating. Her fingers curled against the soft platform beneath her. But she did her best to focus, to remain still, because she could see that Noah was serious about whatever he was attempting.","He infused her with tendrils of both forces, threading power through her existence!","And then he saw it.","A network of vibrant vessel-like pathways lit up across her entire body, illuminating beneath her skin in patterns that revealed the fundamental architecture of her existence.","Ethereal channels branched throughout her form like rivers feeding into tributaries feeding into streams.","Primary conduits ran along her spine and through her heart, connecting to secondary pathways that spread toward her extremities. Tertiary networks webbed between those secondary channels, creating interconnected systems that touched every part of her existence. Nodes of concentrated energy marked junctions where multiple pathways intersected, some burning bright while others barely flickered.","Her Civilization of Necromancy wove through these networks in intricate musings, death-aspected authority filled with Bounded Countable Infinity coloring the channels it had claimed.","But as Noah observed with eyes that could finally perceive such depths, he noticed something that made his expression shift.","The networks looked dim!"]},{"number":5103,"title":"Chapter 5103: Chapter 5102: Experimentation III","paragraphs":["In many areas, they seemed actively deficient, pathways that should have blazed with power instead flickering weakly or barely registering at all. The architecture was present, the potential was there, but something fundamental prevented that potential from being realized.","|I have completed preliminary analysis of the subject’s Existential Engineering.|","Ruination’s voice emerged.","|What you perceive before you is the Lattice of Foundational Constraint . This is the basal, most basic perceivable engineering to you currently that defines Bounded Lifeforms, the architecture that was thr blueprint woven into their existence. The network you observe represents the channels through which power should flow and the nodes where that power should accumulate.|","|In Bounded existence, these channels are narrow. The nodes are dimmed. The potential for expansion exists within the architecture, but limitations prevent that expansion from occurring regardless of how much power the subject attempts to cultivate. This...is not deficiency in the conventional sense. This is engineering. Deliberate, precise engineering that establishes ceilings the Bounded cannot surpass through normal means. It is the base template of Existences that will ever be born in Observable Existence.|","HUUM!","|The subject Barbatos displays this Lattice of Foundational Constraint in typical Bounded configuration. Her Civilization and your infinity has optimized what can be optimized within these limitations, but she cannot exceed what she was engineered to be. The channels will not widen. The nodes will not brighten. The ceilings will not lift regardless of her efforts or desires.|","|However.|","|Through Existential Engineering, it is theoretically possible to alter this seemingly preset and unchangeable construct. The limitations are just that, which means they can be removed or modified by one possessing sufficient capability and power. If you were to flood her Lattice with Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce and overwhelm the constraints, you could potentially reshape her engineering toward something approaching Hadean classification.|","|I should note that this would not immediately transform her into a full Hadean Lifeform. Her bones and organs would remain in their current state until she undergoes the transformation process that you experienced. But her engineering would be altered to permit such transformation, to allow her existence to grow toward classifications that Bounded existence normally cannot achieve.|","|If successful, she would be designated as a Nascent Hadean . A Hadean Lifeform that has not yet grown to full maturity but possesses the potential to do so. The engineering of a Hadean without the completed physical transformation. A seedling rather than a tree.|","...!","Noah absorbed this information with eyes that blazed brighter by the moment.","A Nascent Hadean.","The possibility of granting others the potential he had achieved through cycles of destruction and rebirth that most couldn’t survive. If he could reshape Bounded engineering through Existential Engineering, if he could remove the limitations that prevented his companions from advancing beyond their designated ceilings...","His hands began to vibrate with immensity.","One hand shone gold with endless Observable Force. The other shone multicolored with endless Quintessence Infiniforce, the energy of his transformation gathering with density that pressed against everything nearby.","He looked down at Barbatos.","\" This may be intense ,\" he said simply.","Her dark eyes met his with trust that didn’t waver.","\" Go on, Little Fish. Do what you need to do.\"","Noah pressed both hands against her heart.","He began to flood both forces into her existence, Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce pouring through her Lattice of Foundational Constraint in torrents that exceeded anything she had ever experienced. The power pressed against their walls. It pushed against the narrowing. It demanded expansion that the engineering had been designed to prevent!","Barbatos opened her eyes wide.","Her hand shot out to grasp onto his robe. Her chest heaved as her breathing became ragged, back arching off the platform as sensations cascaded through her existence in waves she couldn’t control!","\" Ah..!\"","BOOM!","Immense concentrations flooded into her engineering.","The Lattice of Foundational Constraint resisted at first, limitations pushing back against the power attempting to reshape them. But Noah didn’t relent. He poured more Observable Force into the gold hand, more Quintessence Infiniforce into the multicolored hand, overwhelming the resistance through sheer magnitude of what he provided.","|Engineering modification in progress. The Lattice of Foundational Constraint is experiencing forced expansion. Primary channels widening by factor of twelve. Secondary channels widening by factor of eight. Tertiary networks restructuring to accommodate increased flow capacity.|","|Nodes of concentrated energy are brightening. Junction points that previously flickered weakly are now blazing with intensity approaching what I observe in your own engineering. The artificial dimming is being overwritten.|","|Subject is experiencing significant sensation as her existence restructures around new parameters. The engineering that defined her for her entire existence is being rewritten in real time. Such alteration cannot occur without the subject being aware of what is happening to them.|","|Modification continuing. Seventy-three percent complete.|","Barbatos trembled beneath his hands.","Golden light began emanating from her skin, Observable Force flooding through channels that could suddenly accommodate its presence. Her dark hair started shifting, strands that had been purely black now showing rivers of gold running through them like veins of precious metal through stone. Her breathing came in gasps that released mist tinged with golden luminescence.","|Eighty-nine percent complete.|","|Ninety-four percent complete.|","|Modification complete.|","Noah slowly withdrew his hands.","The figure of Barbatos lay on the floating platform looking unfathomably beautiful! Her dark hair spread across the soft surface in waves now threaded with rivers of gold Observable Force, the coloring permanent rather than temporary. Her skin held luminescence that hadn’t been there before, subtle but undeniable illumination pressing outward from within.","And on her forehead, a barely discernible golden crack could be seen.","It looked like a line of fracture in porcelain, except instead of damage it suggested emergence. Something breaking through from beneath. Something that had been constrained finally finding expression in physical form!","Her gaze was dazed and heavy as she breathed out golden mist with each exhale.","She rose slowly to sit on the soft floating platform. Around her body, rivers of golden Observable Force surged in currents that responded to her presence, power that her existence could suddenly channel in ways that had been impossible moments before.","\" Little Fish...\"","Her voice emerged breathless.","\" What did you just do?\"","...!","|Coomplete success has been observed in the modification of subject Barbatos’s Existential Engineering.|","|Her previous designation as a Bounded Lifeform is no longer accurate. The Lattice of Foundational Constraint has been replaced with what I shall term the Lattice of Nascent Emergence. Her channels have been widened to accommodate power flow at rates previously impossible for her classification. Her nodes have been brightened to store energy in concentrations that would have destroyed her former engineering. The artificial limitations that defined her existence have been removed.|","| She is now designated as a Nascent Hadean.|","|In practical terms, this means she is capable of beginning the refinement of her bones and organs toward full Hadean classification. The transformation you underwent through cycles of destruction and rebirth, she can now pursue. The ceiling that would have prevented such advancement no longer exists.|","|I should note several significant implications of this change.|","|First, a Nascent Hadean exists in territories that blur the line between THE First Scale and THE Second Scale. She has not established a Civilizational Anchor, but she now possesses potential that exceeds what establishing such an Anchor would normally provide. The Hadean Organs and Bones she can eventually form will be grander than the Proterozoic Organs and Bones that others form upon reaching THE Second Scale. She will, in essence, be able to achieve Hadean classification at THE First Scale, then carry that enhanced foundation into THE Second Scale if she chooses to establish her Anchor.|","|Second, the golden crack visible on her forehead represents the physical manifestation of her altered engineering. This marking will evolve as she progresses toward full Hadean transformation, eventually becoming something more elaborate as her existence fully integrates the changes you have implemented.|","|Third, her connection to you has deepened significantly through this process. The Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce you used to reshape her engineering now exists within her foundations as permanent presence. She is, in a very real sense, partially composed of your power now.|","| This was a successful first application of Existential Engineering. The methodology you employed intuitively appears to have been correct. Future applications may require adjustment based on subject variation, but the fundamental approach has proven viable.|","Noah read over all of this as Barbatos continued breathing heavily beside him, her existence acclimating to parameters that had just been completely rewritten.","He brought his vibrant right hand forward.","His palm cradled her head, fingers supporting the back of her skull while his hand covered all of her cheek. The touch was gentle despite the power still radiating from his transformed flesh. She looked at him with dark gold eyes that hadn’t been gold before, that shone with brilliance reflecting the Observable Force now flowing through her existence.","She cuddled against his hand to feel his warmth.","\" What... have you done, Little Fish?\"","She asked again as even her own existence couldn’t believe itself!","---","<Personal Reflections from THE Grimoire of Hadean Lexicon, Author: Noah Osmont, written during the span known as THE Reckoning of Imposed Order>","\"I have often reflected upon the nature of pivotal moments, and I have come to understand that they rarely announce themselves with the fanfare one might expect. The grand turning points of existence, the instants where the trajectory of reality itself shifts toward weavings that will define eons yet to come, these moments tend to arrive quietly, dressed in the mundane clothing of ordinary action, revealing their true significance only when observed through the lens of considerable retrospection.","When I performed my first Nascent Hadean transformation upon Barbatos in the Early Veiled Shore, I believed I was conducting an experiment. A test of newly acquired capabilities. An exploration of what Existential Engineering might allow me to accomplish for those I cared about. I did not understand, could not have understood at that time, that I was striking the first blow against an architecture of existence that had governed Causes and Observable Existences since before many of us learned to perceive ourselves as existing.","I actually threw the first punch without realizing it.","That moment marked one of the last periods of relative peace I would experience.","I do have to confess, with the clarity that distance and time provides, that my ignorance was profound. I knew, of course, that the distinctions between Bounded and Gilded were permanent by design. But knowing that something is designed and understanding why it was designed, understanding who benefits from that design and what they will do to preserve it, these are different forms of knowledge entirely.","But even if I had known, I would have still done the same. Because who decided things had to be this way? What gave them the right? What ordained them to have any capability at all?","The engineering that constrains Bounded existence was not so much as artificially implemented...as much as it was simply nature. Just how existence was. There wasn’t something singular that could be said to be responsible. Existence simply was. Existence was...unfair. But it was structure an there were those who enjoyed such structure.","Those who sit atop structures of existentially imposed hierarchy rarely perceive their position as imposed. To them, the structure is natural and inevitable. The way things have always been and therefore the way things must always be.","The Bounded are Bounded because that is what they are. The Gilded are Gilded because that is what they are. And the Primeval, those ancient arbiters whose hands observed and directed Causes and studied and sought to manipulate the very engineering I was beginning to unravel, they exist beyond both because existence itself demands that someone must.","There was no good or evil. There was and is always what one believes.","When one alters the status quo, when one demonstrates that the limitations could be altered from below, when one proves that ceilings can be shattered and floors can be raised and the entire edifice of carefully maintained separation can be restructured through sufficient will and power, those who have benefited from that status quo tend to fight back.","They fight back because their position, their identity, their very understanding of their own significance depends upon the continued existence of those beneath them. A Gilded Lifeform is only Gilded in relation to the Bounded they surpass. Remove that relation, blur that distinction, demonstrate that the Bounded can become something that rivals or exceeds what the Gilded were engineered to be, and you do not merely threaten their power as you... threaten their meaning.","And to them, meaning is everything . For this, I pity Ubergulden Adelheid. I pity Ubergulden Markhus.","I did not know this when I placed my hands upon Barbatos and reshaped her engineering. I did not know that the peace I enjoyed in that moment, the relative calm of experimentation and discovery and the quiet joy of elevating someone I loved, would be one of the last moments of such peace I would experience before storms arrived that made Grimvault and his companions seem like gentle rain.","At that time, I truly did not know.","But I learned. Oh, how thoroughly I learned. And from all of it...endless seas of Observable and Unobservable Blood shall bloom. Existence will shudder, for it deserves to. All of Existence...deserves what is coming.\""]},{"number":5104,"title":"Chapter 5104: Chapter 5103: Parts To Play! I","paragraphs":["Prima Indifferentia.","Grimvault tore through the boundaries between spaces with desperation he hadn’t felt in eons, his massive armored form trailing destruction through layers of existence that parted before his authority!","He had run far, farther than a Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect should ever need to run!","But THE fucking Infinite Light still burned around him.","He ran towards...home.","After an unknown period of time and a shift between spaces and a unique methodology...","WAP!","He appeared above an endlessly stretching white gold sea, the surface reflecting illumination that seemed to come from everywhere and nowhere simultaneously.","SPLASH!","His massive figure crashed into the white gold waters, that blackened silver armor that had fused with his flesh now wreathed in blue gold flames that refused to extinguish regardless of what he submerged them in.","The sea parted around him, waves spreading outward from his impact.","THE Infinite Light sought to unwind him.","He could feel it working against his existence even now! His form had stopped fluctuating only because he’d anchored himself again and again with his own Axiom, but the flames continued burning, continued trying to drag him backward through stages of development he had surpassed eons ago.","He had constantly enacted THE Silurian Light to counter it.","Pulse against Pulse. Fire against fire. But such deployment drained resources that even his ninety-four percent Proterozoic Bone saturation couldn’t replenish indefinitely. He could still cast it a few more times, could continue the struggle between his Pulse and Osmont’s...","But he didn’t want to continue risking it.","He had many different points of strength, and raw power was only one of them. Intelligence was another. Experience was another. And connection, alliance, the bonds forged across eons of service to something greater than himself, these too were strength that could be leveraged when individual capability proved insufficient!","He was connected to THE Deliverance.","A Civilization thrived from alliances and communication. No being, regardless of how powerful they became, could stand entirely alone against the vastness of existence.","He had served THE Deliverance faithfully. He had executed their directives. He had enforced their will. He had been their instrument when instruments were required!","Now he would call upon that service.","Grimvault rose from the white gold waters, his massive form dripping with liquid. The blue gold flames still wreathed his existence, still pressed against his anchored state with hunger that wouldn’t relent. He raised his arms toward the skies.","His voice emerged!","\"I call upon bonds. I have never called for aid in all my spans of service...\"","His pale fires blazed brighter beneath that wolf skull helm.","\"I call now. Let THE Deliverance hear. Let THE Deliverance answer. Let THE Deliverance come forth and witness what has been wrought upon one who serves without question.\"","HUUM!","The seas churned quietly.","The white gold waters that had been merely trembling now began to rotate, currents forming that had nothing to do with natural flow and everything to do with power gathering in response to his invocation.","And it was unfathomably fast!","BOOM!","A dozen figures appeared before Grimvault.","Every single one radiated the terrifying aura of Primordial Architects at classifications that made his own Calymmian status seem modest. They floated above the churning waters in formations that suggested hierarchy. Some burned with fires of various colors. Others pulsed with authority that pressed against reality itself. All of them observed Grimvault with different gazes!","But the foremost figure drew his gaze entirely.","Platinum flames surrounded a humanoid titan whose form couldn’t be fully observed through the brilliance that shrouded him!","The fire didn’t merely burn around this entity. It seemed to emerge from him, to be part of what he was rather than something he wielded.","This was THE Deliverance.","Grimvault trembled before that presence.","His massive armored form, which had seemed so imposing when he confronted Osmont, now felt small and insignificant before the entity he had served across eons. He looked down with shame that pressed against his ancient existence, unable to meet the gaze of THE Deliverance or the gazes of others assembled here.","He had fled and had run from a being at THE First Scale. He had been driven to invoke aid he had never needed before!","The shame burned worse than THE Infinite Light still wreathing his form.","And yet...","\" No need to feel shame for what happened, Grimvault.\"","THE Deliverance’s voice emerged deep enough to resonate through Grimvault’s foundations, through the white gold sea beneath them!","The words carried understanding rather than condemnation.","\" Existence is filled with anomalies that even we cannot account for. The Infinity-bearer has proven himself to be precisely such an anomaly, and there is no disgrace in doing what you did.\"","The platinum flames flickered with something that might have been curiosity.","\" Now, this is the Pulse you cannot erase? How does it feel?\"","...!","Grimvault looked up with gratitude that he couldn’t fully express. The understanding in THE Deliverance’s words, the lack of judgment despite his failure, it meant more than he could articulate!","He gathered himself, forcing his voice to emerge as calmly as he could manage given the circumstances.","\"It feels like...regression, Sir. Like being pulled backward through every stage of development I have achieved across eons. The flames demand that I return to states I surpassed before most current powers existed. They seek to unwind my causality until I am reduced to something that precedes what I currently am.\"","He paused, the blue gold flames still dancing across his armored form.","\"I have countered with THE Silurian Light repeatedly, but the Pulses seem evenly matched. Neither can overcome the other through direct confrontation. And I found myself unwilling to continue the expenditure when the outcome remained uncertain.\"","THE Deliverance nodded slowly, that massive form shifting within its shroud of platinum brilliance.","\" THE Infinite Light, so he called it? A new Pulse never before seen....\"","The platinum flames intensified.","\"I understand. And I shall demonstrate how such a Pulse can be countered for future reference.\"","THE Deliverance raised three hands.","Grimvault blinked as he hadn’t realized the entity possessed more than two arms until that moment. Or...he just had the arms he needed to have at any time?","Three palms faced outward simultaneously, each one beginning the somatic components of different Pulses at the same time.","\" THE Infinite Light operates on the principle of singular causality ,\" THE Deliverance explained as his hands moved through gestures that overlapped without interfering with each other.","\"It asserts a unique unknown Cause holds authority over those who lack its...brilliance, is it? But no single Cause holds authority over all others. When multiple Causes are invoked simultaneously, when their authorities overlap and interweave, the singular assertion of THE Infinite Light becomes diffused across contradictions it cannot resolve.\"","His first hand completed its gesture.","\" THE Silurian Light provides the fire of primordial ignition.\"","His second hand completed its gesture.","\" THE Cambrian Word provides the authority of rewritten consequence.\"","His third hand completed its gesture.","\" And THE Ediacaran Silence provides the void where Causes cannot reach.\"","BOOM!","Three Pulses emerged simultaneously.","...!","He...did not say any of the lengthy words required!","Flames of impossible colors, inscriptions of reality-rewriting authority, and absolute absence of sound and presence all manifested at once, weaving together in configurations that shouldn’t have been possible. The triple Pulse descended upon Grimvault’s burning form, not attacking him but enveloping him in contradictions that THE Infinite Light couldn’t navigate.","The blue gold flames flickered.","They pressed against the triple authority surrounding Grimvault, seeking purchase against existence that was being protected by three Causes asserting three different claims over reality. THE Infinite Light demanded regression, but THE Silurian Light declared that its fire preceded all regression. THE Cambrian Word rewrote the consequence of THE Infinite Light’s contact. And THE Ediacaran Silence created space where no Pulse could reach regardless of its origin.","The flames began to fade!","Blue gold brilliance that had burned for spans since Grimvault fled THE Wastes finally extinguished, dissolving into the white gold sea below as the triple Pulse unmade its hold on his existence. His massive armored form emerged from beneath the dying flames, restored to the state he had maintained before Osmont’s Pulse had touched him!","Oh!"]},{"number":5105,"title":"Chapter 5105: Chapter 5104: Parts To Play! II","paragraphs":["\" This methodology requires the simultaneous casting of three Pulses ,\" THE Deliverance continued as his hands lowered. \" It is not something a common Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity can accomplish. The coordination alone exceeds what most at that classification can achieve, and the reserves required would deplete beings who lack sufficient Proterozoic Bone saturation.\"","The platinum flames settled into calmer configurations.","\" But at these stages of existence, there are unique beings who can display tremendous power regardless of whether they are Rhyacian, Calymmian, or Ediacaran. Classification provides framework, not limitation. Remember this, Grimvault.\"","Grimvault bowed his massive form with gratitude.","\"I will remember, Sir. Thank you.\"","He rose from the bow with expression that had shifted from shame to determination, those pale fires in his wolf skull helm burning with intensity restored.","\" Sir, what shall be done to THE Infinity-bearer? To this Osmont?\"","\" He or his forces have now tortured or killed multiple of our brethren. Vahrkosis was unraveled by one of his allies. Sammarthiel remains trapped in paradoxical uncertainty. Beowulf was captured. And I was forced to flee from someone who should not have possessed the capability to threaten me.\"","His fists clenched at his sides.","\" What response shall we provide?\"","...!","THE Deliverance was silent for a long moment.","The platinum flames surrounding his form flickered .","\" There are... a great many complex things currently unfolding across Observable Existence. More than you know. More than most know.\"","The titan shifted within his flames.","\" THE Infinity-bearer is an anomaly that requires handling, yes. His Infiniry, his progression, his immunity to THE Silurian Light...This Infinite Light...there is a lot to him.\"","A pause that seemed to stretch.","\" But just moments ago, another matter arose that demands attention. THE Creature has returned to THE Wyld.\"","Grimvault’s pale fires flickered heavily.","\" THE Wild Beast has come home ,\" THE Deliverance continued as the platinum flames intensified.","\" There is much to be done. The board has grown more complex than simple response to a single anomaly can address. THE Creature. THE Infinity-bearer. Too many variables shifting simultaneously for singular focus to serve our purposes.\"","THE Deliverance’s form seemed to grow larger within its shroud of platinum brilliance.","\" Since THE Infinity-bearer seems to wish for adversity, we shall grant that wish. Let us hope he will bring us difficulty and adversity as well, for I have decided upon a response that serves multiple purposes.\"","His voice pressed against reality itself.","\"I shall enact a... Civilizational War.\"","...!","Grimvault’s eyes widened at those words.","A Civilizational War!","\" This approach serves multiple functions,\" THE Deliverance explained. \" It keeps us occupied with legitimate purpose while ensuring the current stability of Observable Existence...among other things.\"","The platinum flames settled into configurations of finality.","\" For I do not wish to do anything too grand when THE Creature and THE Infinity-bearer are the least of our problems. Existence is too vast, Grimvault. Far too vast. The anomalies we face now may be symptoms rather than causes, signals rather than sources. Signals that likely, those we have only whispered of...may make themselves more involved.\"","BOOM!","Those they whispered of!","They all knew what THE Deliverance was talking about!","THE Gilded!","Myths and stories, glory and wonder!","He turned, and the other eleven figures turned with him.","\" Come, Grimvault. There is much to be done, and a great deal of us have our parts to play in what unfolds from this moment forward.\"","...!","HUUM!","Blinding light erupted from THE Deliverance’s form, platinum brilliance expanding outward to envelop Grimvault and all others assembled above the white gold sea.","As they left, Grimvault gazed at his existence as he frowned as he felt like...his authority seemed to be tremendously depleted.","Maybe more than 25% of his total power still had not returned? Were the effects of THE Infinite Light so obscene?","He had such a thought as a moment later...","They were gone.","The white gold sea returned to calmness, its surface settling into stillness that betrayed nothing of what had just occurred above it, but...","A Civilizational War would soon be declared!","---","In THE Infiniverse.","THE Infiniverse herself floated within a sea of multicolored brilliance, boundless strings stretching from her form toward the Three Thousand Realms infinitely expanding in her depths. Each string pulsed with information flowing both directions, her awareness touching every sacred herb, every cultivating being, every fluctuation in the balance that comprised her nature.","Beside her, the illusory figure of Ruination floated with presence that seemed almost companionable.","THE Infiniverse turned her imperious gaze toward the strings stretching from her form. She had felt her Master’s Hadean transformation ripple through their connection. She had sensed the changes that declared him something unprecedented.","Now she contemplated what those changes meant for her.","\" Master has led the way again.\"","Her voice pressed against the multicolored sea surrounding her.","\" A Seed of Observable Existence becoming an Observable Existence is easy enough. Just like THE Second Scale from THE First Scale. But Master did not jump to THE Second Scale. He became...Hadean.\"","Her strings pulsed with intensity that made the Three Thousand Realms tremble.","\" Naturally, I cannot become a measly Observable Existence like any other. The grander I become, the grander Master’s Infinite Cause becomes. So with his focus on Infinity and Observable Force, I shall flood everything within THE Infiniverse to transform its very backbone toward Hadean.\"","Her gaze fixed upon Ruination.","\" Let us begin this process.\"","HUUM!","|I have initiated preliminary stages. The scope of what you propose exceeds anything previously attempted.|","Ruination’s form solidified slightly as she spoke.","|The Three Thousand Realms will undergo fundamental restructuring. Each realm’s foundational architecture will be reshaped toward Hadean parameters, meaning the laws governing them, the energy flows sustaining them, the very fabric of their reality will be elevated to classifications an Observable Existence cannot achieve.|","|The infinite expansion currently occurring will accelerate dramatically. Your realms may approach or exceed the scope of established Observable Existence|","|Beings cultivating within your depths will be affected. The Hadean nature of your restructured existence will press against their foundations, catalyzing advancement in those capable of withstanding it while endangering those who cannot.|","|Your connection to your Master will deepen unpredictably.|","A pause.","|If successful, you will become what I shall term a Hadean Observable Existence . Not merely an Existence of Hadean classification, but an entire reality operating according to Hadean principles. The Three Thousand Realms will become Hadean Realms. You will blur the distinction between being and place in ways even your current nature does not achieve.|","...!","THE Infiniverse absorbed this with eyes that blazed like stars being born.","\" What comes will come regardless if we sit still or make bold moves. Begin the process.\"","HUUM!","Blue and gold painted everything as the two sisters tugged on their Master’s connection!","The multicolored sea erupted as Infinity surged through her depths while Observable Force flooded structures. The Three Thousand Realms trembled as power beyond their classification pressed against their foundations!","THE Infiniverse closed her eyes and felt herself changing.","It would take time. But... time was something she had in abundance."]},{"number":5106,"title":"Chapter 5106: Chapter 5105: Dream! I","paragraphs":["Noah did not like laziness.","Any time he wasn’t doing something, he felt jittery. So after Barbatos, he had been working hard in the minutes that followed. He had taken out Henry, Sigrid, Moiraine, Adelaide, Titano, Riya, THE Queen of Matter, THE First Farmer, and all others.","The golden sands of the Early Veiled Shore filled with activity again as figures of varying power and origin gathered across the beach and the plots of sacred herbs inland. Even THE Living Origin and THE First Hunger were brought over from Alfheimr, their presence adding weight to an already impressive gathering.","Khor stood beside Tor protectively, her gaze fixed on THE Living Origin with suspicion that she didn’t bother concealing as if a wolf had taken someone she cared about! They all awaited their transformation. THE Big Stepper, Ul’moreth floated nearby alongside Lumivara, while Skoll the very good dog sat with patience that belied his nature.","Ains, THE Fisherman, observed everything with the quiet attention of someone who had witnessed many impossible things and expected to witness more.","Noah worked rapidly to transform as many as he could to Nascent Hadean Lifeforms.","It felt like causing the emergence of geniuses and anomalies en masse, like planting seeds that would grow into something Observable Existence had never seen before. This was his current project, and he threw himself into it with focus that left no room for the jitteriness that idle moments brought.","The Early Veiled Shore had already transformed into seas of Infinity and Observable Force. The golden sands were barely visible beneath churning power that responded to his will, waves of blue and gold crashing against shores that seemed to drink in what touched them.","THE Emperor Penguin floated in the air before him right now.","This flightless bird who had barely begun to pick up Logos and Philology of THE First Tongue now hung suspended in currents of brilliance, small form surrounded by forces that would have annihilated lesser birds!","Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force flooded into the penguin’s existence, reshaping engineering that had limited this loyal creature since its emergence!","\"RAA! RAA! RAA!\"","The change into a Nascent Hadean Lifeform was in process.","Noah monitored the transformation while his mind divided across multiple tasks, multiple bodies, multiple priorities. His companions waited their turn.","And as he did all of this here, his body in THE Wastes accomplished something grand.","---","In THE Wastes where a glorious battle had finished minutes ago.","The sparring session had also concluded.","Noah held Naldine’s hands behind her back with a single grip, her wrists pulsing with Proterozoic light as she strained against restraint she couldn’t break. His free hand held her Vihuela, that instrument formed from her own arm now claimed as undeniable proof of his victory. The tumultuous seas of Observable Force churned around them, bearing witness to what had just transpired!","She breathed heavily, her radiant white hair disheveled in ways he had never seen from the always-composed Primordial Architect. Her singularity-dotted eyes burned with frustration she couldn’t conceal, ancient pride warring with the reality of her current position!","He leaned in to whisper in her ear.","\"It seems I may have just taken a step ahead of you, Naldine Manthon.\"","...!","She struggled one last time, her Calymmian-tier power pressing against his grip with force that would have shattered most beings across Observable Existence.","His hold didn’t waver. Her Proterozoic Bones blazed brighter, authority flooding through her existence in desperate attempt to break free. His transformed flesh didn’t even register the attempt as noteworthy!","She let out a sound of frustration that pressed against the surrounding seas.","\" Okay!\"","Noah released her immediately.","The moment his grip loosened, she spun to face him with a gaze that held complexity he couldn’t fully read. She was thinking about many things. Her eyes moved across his transformed features, taking in the multicolored hair, the golden light pressing outward through his skin, the pupils that shone like singularities of an unfathomable Cause.","\" Okay ,\" she said again, her breathing beginning to steady.","Noah blinked. \" Okay what?\"","Naldine looked at him sharply, her expression settling into something calmer and more decisive. The frustration hadn’t vanished, but something else had joined it. Curiosity, or hunger for what she had just witnessed him display.","\" You’re the big bad guy with Infinity who can change many things, yes?\"","Her voice carried conviction!","\" Let’s see what you can change about me. I permit you to utilize a bit of your Infinity to do what you mentioned before. I do not want any Madness of Infinity as I will let you know every step of the way.\"","Her singularity-dotted eyes blazed brighter.","\"Let’s see if you can really take me past Calymmian quickly.\"","...!","After a spar that showed how terrifying Noah’s current power was against Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entities, Naldine Manthon finally gave in!","She sought to see what Infinity was all about, what it could do for someone already standing at heights most beings couldn’t imagine reaching. The teacher wanted to learn from the student she had so recently instructed.","Noah thought about things carefully.","Taking her into THE Infiniverse, transforming her toward Nascent Hadean. She was already powerful. She already possessed a Pulse. What would she become with Hadean engineering added to everything she already wielded?","Curiosity won over caution.","He waved his fist and caused a vibrant golden crack to bloom beside him, a tear in existence that led into THE Infiniverse where his other body continued its project. The crack pulsed with power that declared what waited on the other side, blue and gold light spilling through the opening like invitation and warning combined.","\" Let’s go.\"","He stepped toward the crack.","\"I’m also curious how much your power will grow. You may jump to be ahead of me again.\"","Naldine looked at that golden crack.","She could feel instinctively that once she entered it, there was no going back. Whatever waited on the other side...","The connection to Infinity. The blurring of lines between what she had been and what she could become.","But existence was vast, and there were many wonders.","She had come to guide Infinity, to make sure its actions wouldn’t lead to the Splintering of Observable Existence. She had listened to many Echoes of THE First Cause during her long existence. She had watched civilizations rise and fall, had seen the impossible become possible more times than most beings could count.","And when she made a decision, she was decisive.","Naldine took a step forward into the golden crack!"]},{"number":5107,"title":"Chapter 5107: Chapter 5106: Dream! II","paragraphs":["THE Beholder gazed into the vastness of THE Infiniverse.","He had existed since before THE First Cause learned to cause, had observed the emergence of Observable Existence from the endless potential that preceded it, had witnessed eons unfold in configurations that most current beings couldn’t comprehend. He had seen many things across spans that defied measurement.","He had never seen anything like this.","The Three Thousand Realms swirled before his perception, infinitely expanding territories that grew grander with each passing moment. Multicolored radiance stretched in every direction, painted by the rain of THE Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity that fell without pause.","Seas of Infinity and Observable Force churned where golden sands should have been.","All of this existed within a single being’s internal reality.","\" You hid something that even I, with my long knowledge, did not know about.\"","His voice emerged deep and resonant, pressing against the platform of crimson gold flames they stood upon. Muspelheim’s fire supported them as they observed what THE Infiniverse was becoming.","\" This is something grand. But also, this is unfathomably dangerous. Do you know that?\"","Beside him, Osmont stood with calm that seemed inappropriate for someone being warned by a Singular Cognizance. THE Beholder studied this being who had achieved impossibilities in spans that most considered insignificant. Multicolored hair shifted through hues that had no names. Golden light pressed outward through fair skin. Pupils shone like singularities of an unfathomable Cause.","This was what THE Youngest looked like now.","This was what had emerged from a battle against a Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity that should have unmade him entirely.","Osmont didn’t respond to his question, so THE Beholder continued.","\" One can consider Observable Existence as something with many layers and pockets. The vast majority of the population thinks of the folds, or what used to be the Infinite Unfurling, or the Wandering Territories, as the last things and only things they would ever experience. Their entire existence unfolds within those regions without ever touching what lies beyond.\"","He gestured toward the swirling realms before them.","\" Fewer know about or experience the vastness of the Primordial Realms. The intricate weavings of the Oldest Paradox in existence and all the variants of Civilizations that stemmed from these. The Claimers of the Oldest Paradox, which you are among, distinguish themselves as entities with limitless potential.\"","His attention fixed on Osmont’s profile.","\" And even if you include Prima Indifferentia, filled with Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors. Even if you include THE Wyld where Primordial Architects call home. Even if you include all of that in your knowledge, you have only truly grasped a small portion of Observable Existence.\"","THE Beholder’s form flickered with ancient light.","\" Because within Observable Existence, there is also the Unobservable. And nobody should be mistaken to think that when someone says Unobservable, they mean external. Within the bounds of our Observable Existence, there are intricate parts that are unobservable to you and me and many others. All those things that are unobservable are still, in large part, Observable Existence.\"","He paused, letting this settle.","\"A great many say the sentance that...existence is vast. Even they don’t fully comprehend the vastness, even though they say it constantly. But we see what we see because we are supposed to see it. We do not see what we do not see because we are not supposed to see.\"","The rain of THE Pluvial Epoch continued falling around them.","\" You beginning to emulate and build your own Observable Existence is blasphemous enough. I won’t even begin to theorize if you are doing more than that.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" And I say blasphemous because among the things we are not supposed to see, the things we should not see, they have a status quo. The way that things are. With you doing everything you’re doing...\"","THE Beholder turned to face Osmont directly.","\" Can I presume that you know or have knowledge of THE Gilded Ones?\"","HUUM!","The question pressed against everything nearby.","Osmont didn’t flinch and didn’t react with surprise or confusion or the appropriate gravity that such a term demanded. He simply gave a light nod, as if THE Beholder had asked about something mundane rather than something that should shake the foundations of any Bounded being’s understanding.","THE Beholder gave a deep sigh.","The nonchalance. The lack of grand response!","Oh!","As if he didn’t care much for such a term, as if knowledge of THE Gilded was simply another piece of information he had acquired along his impossible journey rather than a revelation that should terrify him.","\" As a Singular Cognizance, I was there at the time of endless potential that some wish to go back to.\"","THE Beholder’s voice carried weight that came from direct experience rather than secondhand knowledge.","\" That wish alone is a foolish dream. The Splintering of Existence is an impossibility. The splintering of some parts of existence, maybe, but not everything. And even then, you could never truly go back to the endless potential that was back then.\"","He began to move slowly across the platform of crimson gold flames.","\" In that era of endless potential, the passage of time was far more intricate than all the history of Observable Existence that followed after the emergence of THE First Cause. If the time after THE First Cause up until now could be neatly wrapped up in the words of a single cycle, then that period of endless potential was thousands or millions of cycles.\"","His form flickered again, ancient memories pressing against his consciousness.","\" So from THE First Cause up till now, we can actually say that THE Creature, all other Primordial Architects, and other existences that emerged after THE First Cause are fairly young lifeforms. But back in that era of endless potential, as much as every single Singular Cognizance will tell you that we were alone in observing the happenings and weavings of existence...\"","He paused.","\" We do not speak about that which we would occasionally see. Things that confounded even our existence. Lifeforms we could barely perceive, which seemed imaginary. Even if we did perceive them, we would only attribute it as a mirage or a dream.\"","THE Beholder stopped moving and faced the swirling realms.","\" THE Gilded Lifeforms. We can say that they are just like you and I, and at the same time they are not. When THE First Cause emerged, I came to understand how existence was by nature not equal and not fair.\"","His voice grew darker.","\" Because all that you would come to know, all the lifeforms, the very power of the Cause that would cause the emergence of Primordial Architects and everything else, only a percentage of about five or slightly less was actually what natural existence had designated.\"","He turned to Osmont.","\" What I am saying now is more so what I saw and the conjectures and theories I made from it. I could be entirely wrong. But I did see.\"","His form blazed brighter with conviction.","\"I saw THE Gilded Lifeforms, or something even grander than them, move to guide THE First Cause. That five percent that would have been utilized for the emergence of you and countless others was reduced to less than one percent. And they, whatever they can be considered as, guided the rest of the ninety-nine percent of the power of THE First Cause towards the emergence of more of them.\"","WAA!","The weight of this revelation pressed against the platform beneath them.","\" By nature, existence already favored them. The vast majority of the power of the Cause would have gone to them regardless. But they still had sufficient power to guide even more of THE First Cause’s flow towards themselves. The rest of existence was left with scraps. Bounded. And bounded in a manner that was unfathomable to truly understand.\"","THE Beholder’s sigh carried eons of resignation.","\" But since then, existence bloomed and thrived. Civilizations rose and fell. The portions of Observable Existence that THE Bounded had access to changed over the eons. Claimers of the Oldest Paradox arose and fell.\"","His attention fixed on Osmont with intensity.","\" And then at a very late point of this ongoing existence, you come along. You come along. And how many years have you been actively doing this? How much time has passed since you touched authority and power and began to alter weavings of existence?\"","The question hung between them.","\" You come in the middle of all this brilliance, and you begin to mess around with the Cause itself. You begin to do something as ridiculous as forming the emergence of another Observable Existence within an already established Observable Existence.\"","THE Beholder moved closer to Osmont.","\" Whatever Cause you are relying on and whatever uniqueness you are utilizing to form the emergence of this Observable Existence, I would advise you to stop and turn away so quickly.\"","His voice dropped to something almost pleading.","\" Because should you succeed. Should an Observable Existence and the potential power of the Cause behind it truly begin to proliferate... what do you think the beings who already guided and harvested a Cause of Observable Existence cycles ago will do to you and your dream?\"","He searched Osmont’s face for any sign of understanding.","\" Can you hide it? Are you more powerful than them to be capable of such a thing? You are nurturing and cultivating something grand, but it is too grand. It is too grand.\"","THE Beholder’s form flickered!","\" You dream too high. We are not meant to have such dreams. THE Bounded have to remain within their scope. Don’t do too much. Don’t try too much.\"","He gazed at the swirling realms around them.","\" THE Second Scale is good enough. THE Third Scale is nothing but a dream. But for those like us, do we need something like that? Can we not be content with what we have?\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" At what point will we sit back and just say enough is enough? You have all of this already. You could stop here. Live for eons in this place with your people. You can have generations of progeny. That is also a grand dream.\"","THE Beholder’s gaze bore into Osmont’s calm expression.","\" But the direction of your dream is past what is meant for THE Bounded. Save yourself. Save your people. Do not fly so close to the sun.\"","His final words emerged with weight that pressed against everything nearby.","\" There is only a single result that will follow.\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":5108,"title":"Chapter 5108: Chapter 5107: My Dream, My Realm! I","paragraphs":["When was it enough?","When did someone dream and dream for far too long, dream for too much? At what point did ambition become hubris, and aspiration become destruction waiting to happen?","At this moment in time, Noah was being told that he was dreaming dangerously. That his dreams would get him scorched, and everyone else around him. That at this point he had more than enough and he could choose to simply sit back.","To say these things to him, THE Beholder did not know him as much as he thought he did.","Noah was a sensible person, not overly attached to things. He had simple aspirations and actually didn’t have any grand dreams. He wasn’t the protagonist of some cosmic epic who declared he would conquer existence and make all bow before his magnificence. He wasn’t driven by hunger for power or obsession with transcendence.","Anyone else put in his position with the power he held through Infinity might begin with grand aspirations of wanting to be some unquestionably dominating force across all of existence. Of declaring they would be unparalleled under the heavens, that all would kneel before their might!","But since the moment he began throwing endless fireballs, his aim had always been simpler. To protect himself. To understand this mystery that was Mana and Infinity. To uncover the secrets of this strange power that had entered his life.","Everything that had occurred since then was a consequence of him fighting for his life and the lives of those he began taking care of.","Even the most recent battle with Beowulf that led to Grimvault. It began with the weavings of Alexander, with him going to help someone who had suffered for millions of subjective years. He was helping another. And this was a unique causality that led to the progression of glorious events culminating in him becoming a Hadean Lifeform who had begun to make terrifying changes.","His connection to Ubergulden Adelheid...was not something he sought. In fighting against Unity, Causality unfolded to the point that now, things were where they were.","Noah’s eyes shone with profundity as he connected all the things that happened recently.","Points of causality where one thing led to another. Alexander’s torture leading to Noah’s intervention. Grimvault’s attack triggering THE Crucible of Observable Rebirth. THE Silurian Light providing the catalyst for complete Hadean evolution. Each event flowing into the next like rivers feeding an ocean, none of them planned but all of them building toward something he couldn’t have predicted.","After he thought about all of this, he replied to THE Beholder.","\"I am not anyone grand or immense.\"","His voice carried conviction that pressed against the platform of crimson gold flames beneath them.","\"I don’t have any special lineage or connection. I don’t have a big secret origin where my drunk of a father or Mother turn out to be some unfathomable lifeforms to explain my power. I was and am Bounded. Limited by the nature of existence itself. It isn’t that I’m dreaming big and dreaming dangerously.\"","He turned to face THE Beholder directly.","\" My dreams are actually the simplest. Safety. Prosperity. Happiness. My dreams are those of waking up to seas of infinite Mana all around me and a plot of land in front of me. My dream is literally that simple.\"","The rain of THE Pluvial Epoch continued falling around them, multicolored brilliance painting everything in hues that had no names.","\" But for the sake of protecting my dream, I have to be strong. For the sake of protecting my dream, I have to do something that others cannot do. Not because I believe myself to be some grand thing or some unstoppable force. Simply because I need to do what others cannot do in order to attain the power that others do not have. To attain power to be capable of protecting myself and that simple dream.\"","His eyes blazed brighter.","\" Being told to give up on my dream is essentially being told to put my head and the heads of all those I care about on an executioner’s platform and wait for the blade to come down. I cannot stop dreaming because the moment I do, I’m basically giving up and leaving everything to fate or chance, if you believe in that.\"","He gestured toward the swirling realms around them.","\" Because existence has been existing and will continue to do so long after us. With or without our dreams, Existence turns. So I choose to dream while I’m still here to dream at all.\"","...!","THE Beholder was silent for a long moment.","When he spoke, his voice carried the measured consideration of someone who had spent eons analyzing the weavings of existence.","\"I do not dismiss your words lightly. The framing of simple dreams requiring grand power to protect them is logically coherent. I understand the causality you describe...\"","\"But the path you describe, the necessity of exceeding others to protect what you hold dear, this path has no end point. Today you became what you are to protect your dream. Tomorrow you will need to exceed what you are. The threats you face will scale with the power you acquire, because the power you acquire will draw greater threats.\"","His form flickered with ancient light.","\" Your dreams... the methods required to protect them grow increasingly complex. Increasingly dangerous. You are not merely defending a plot of land and seas of Mana anymore. You are now defending a potential Observable Existence, and involvement in conflicts that span the entirety of existence.\"","THE Beholder faced Noah.","\" The gap between your stated dream and your current reality has already grown vast. How much further will it grow before the dream you’re protecting no longer resembles the dream you started with? At what point does protecting the dream become more consuming than the dream itself?\"","His voice softened slightly.","\" There has to be another path. A way to achieve safety without painting a target on everything you love. Others have found contentment within their scope. Others have found happiness without challenging the foundations of how existence was engineered.\"","He spread his hands.","\" The ideals and dreams can be viable. But the end result of this trajectory is destruction. Not because your dreams are wrong, but because the methods required to protect them will eventually attract forces that no amount of preparation can overcome.\"","...!","Noah’s face became unfathomably heavy.","He looked around at THE Infiniverse, at the three thousand realms swirling with infinite expansion, at the seas of Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce flooding territories that grew grander by the moment. All of this had emerged from his simple desire to protect himself and those he cared about.","\"I can still continue my dream while knowing of the dangers that are coming.\"","His words pressed against the platform beneath them.","\"I simply need to not go in blindly. If I know there’s a danger coming and I do nothing, then yes, I would be at fault as my Civilization and all those that depend on me perish.\"","He turned to face THE Beholder with eyes that shone like singularities.","\" You are not the first one who has warned me regarding THE Gilded Ones. I have already begun preparing for contingencies and possibilities. Your words today only made my preparations need to finish earlier.\"","\"I will continue dreaming regardless. Not ignoring the danger that is coming, but very much preparing for it. You can watch my dream if you wish. Or you can run from me as quickly and as far as you need to.\"","He began walking across the platform as he spoke.","\"I like getting knowledge from different sources. I don’t think of myself so grand that I don’t need any others, or that I cannot benefit from others. Much of who I am today is because of the collective efforts of many others. The knowledge I gained from them. To the point that even if I have surpassed them in power, I make sure to pay back tens of times more what they gave me.\"","He gestured toward the realms where his companions awaited transformation.","\" An example is the many whose very nature I’m changing right now. There are some beings you do not know. Khor. Tor. Origin. Ul’moreth. Ains. And many others who acted as friend or teacher at one point in the past days. What they taught me helped forge who I am right now, even though I have exceeded them tremendously. It doesn’t mean I have nothing else to learn from them. And I am taking them to the same place that I am standing at right now.\"","He stopped and looked at THE Beholder directly.","\"I thank you for the knowledge you gave me. You can choose to fully throw your weight behind me and share whatever else you may have. You can watch my dream as I prove you wrong. Or if all of this seems too much based on what you know, if you have that fear of those Gilded Lifeforms who before you would close your eyes and convince yourself you did not see them, or they were a mirage, or dreams...\"","His voice carried no judgment, only statement of fact.","\" You are also more than okay to leave. But my dream goes on. Life...goes on.\"","Noah’s existence blazed with blue and gold light.","\" My dream is quintessential. My dream is infinite.\"","BOOM!","He took a step and disappeared from THE Beholder’s presence, leaving only the echo of his words and the weight of his conviction pressing against everything nearby.","THE Beholder floated calmly above the platform of crimson gold flames.","He looked once more at THE Infiniverse stretching before him, at the three thousand realms swirling with expansion that defied what should be possible, at the rain of THE Pluvial Epoch painting everything in colors that spoke of power beyond measurement. He had warned. He had cautioned.","And he had been heard but not heeded.","His voice emerged softly, words flowing in rhythms","\" Dreams, they say, are wings for the flightless,","Hopes woven from threads the dreamers cannot see.","One dreams of simple things, safety and rest,","While building towers that scrape eternity.","Another speaks of dangers vast and certain,","Of patterns carved in stone by ancient hands.","One says the flame is worth the burning,","The other counts the ashes in the sands.","Who speaks true when both hold pieces?","The dreamer blind to what his dreaming costs,","Or the watcher blind to what his warning freezes,","The futures found against the futures lost.","Perhaps the answer lies not in the choosing,","But in the space between the dream and fear.","Where winning looks so much like losing,","And what seems far away is already here.","Dream on, then, dream on","Perhaps the dream you water will have grown","Into the strangest flower of all the earths.","We shall see. We shall see.","What the dreaming and the warning both shall be...\"","THE Beholder fell silent, his ancient form flickering as he contemplated whether to stay or go, whether to watch or flee, whether to believe in dreams or trust in patterns that had never been broken.","The rain continued falling.","The realms continued swirling.","And somewhere within THE Infiniverse, a dreamer continued dreaming!"]},{"number":5109,"title":"Chapter 5109: Chapter 5108: My Dream, My Realm! II","paragraphs":["After he talked to THE Beholder, Noah’s body flashed.","He appeared in the region where only the manifestation of THE Infiniverse and Ruination floated, that space at the center of everything he had built within his internal reality. The multicolored sea of brilliance stretched in every direction, but here at its heart, there was something almost like stillness.","He observed the endless strings emerging from the humanoid form of THE Infiniverse.","They stretched outward toward the Three Thousand Realms in configurations that declared her connection to everything within her depths. And now those strings had begun to be covered with multicolored golden Hadean light, the transformation she had initiated spreading through her very architecture as she followed where he had led.","Both of them rose when he appeared.","THE Infiniverse’s humanoid form shifted, those countless threads moving with her as if they were extensions of her will rather than mere connections. Ruination’s illusory figure solidified slightly, her features becoming more defined as she acknowledged his presence. They looked at him with attention that held something beyond mere awareness.","He waved his hand and smiled, gesturing for them to sit.","They did, and he came to sit with them in that space of multicolored brilliance where the rain of THE Pluvial Epoch fell without end. For a moment, he simply gazed at everything around them. The swirling realms. The expanding territories. The transformation slowly spreading through THE Infiniverse’s foundations.","It was peaceful here.","Despite everything happening across Observable Existence, despite the warnings from THE Beholder and the dangers that THE Gilded represented, this place felt like home in ways that nowhere else ever had.","\" My dream is my dream ,\" he said softly. \" You two...\"","He couldn’t even finish his words.","Because he already knew their dreams. He had always known, had felt their conviction through connections. They weren’t separate from him in the ways that others were. They were part of what he was becoming, and he was part of what they were becoming.","Ruination’s illusory form drifted closer.","She came to sit beside him. Then, gently, she leaned her illusory head against his shoulder. The gesture was tender.","\" My dream is Master.\"","Her voice emerged soft but certain.","\"I have been living my dream.\"","THE Infiniverse moved as well.","The countless threads and lines flowing from her form shifted with the motion, creating patterns of light that danced across the multicolored sea surrounding them. She came to sit behind Noah, their backs touching as boundless Infinity surged through the contact. The connection between them blazed brighter, blue and gold light weaving together.","\"What you want to do, I want to do.\"","Her voice carried firmness that pressed against everything nearby.","\" Who you want to kill, I will kill. Who you wish to protect will not perish.\"","Her expression held conviction that matched or exceeded what Ruination had displayed.","\" In existence, it is just Master. That is the dream. That is my Everything. Men die, Cattle die, kinsmen die; the self may also die. But your glory never dies, I will ensure it.\"","BOOM!","...!","Noah smiled while feeling this boundless conviction flowing through him from both directions.","Ruination leaning against his shoulder. THE Infiniverse pressing against his back. Two consciousnesses that had merged with his existence, that had grown alongside him, that would stand with him regardless of what came. Their dreams were simple in their complexity, focused entirely on him in ways that should have felt like pressure but instead felt like strength.","He closed his eyes to feel everything.","\" Our enemies are ones we don’t understand ,\" he said slowly. \" But we are also ones they don’t understand.\"","The multicolored sea rippled around them.","\" We are weak, but also not. Because we know about THE Gilded Lifeforms, but they don’t know about me and my stage of life. They don’t know about Hadean.\"","He opened his eyes.","\" So while the danger exists tremendously, as Ubergulden Adelheid and THE Beholder have made abundantly clear, we can move in our own unique ways. We can hide and mask what we are. What THE Infiniverse is. Even from those more powerful than us.\"","He felt THE Infiniverse shift slightly behind him, curiosity pressing through their connection.","\"It would seem illogical and impossible and paradoxical to hide from those so much more powerful. But why not? The classification of Hadean exists without their knowledge. Well, yet, I hope.\"","His smile grew sharper.","\" So let’s make the impossibilities possible.\"","THE Infiniverse’s voice emerged with shining curiosity.","\"What did Master have in mind?\"","Noah raised his hand as if grasping something distant.","As he spoke, the air before them began to shift. Light gathered in configurations that matched his words, visualizations of concepts emerging as his authority shaped them into being.","\" Among the concepts I’ve enjoyed dabbling into and thinking of recently is the theoretical physics concept of...interdimensionality.\"","A flat plane of light appeared before them, thin as a sheet of paper.","\" Imagine we are like inhabitants of a flat, two-dimensional world. A Flatland, living out our lives on a surface where there is only length and width, but no height. We can move forward, backward, left, and right, but the very concept of ’up’ is not only impossible to achieve, it is impossible to imagine.\"","The plane stretched outward, tiny figures appearing on its surface moving in only two directions.","\" We also move through a fourth dimension, Time, though we experience it only in one direction. Well, for the most part. Unless I utilize temporal traversal.\"","He smiled slightly.","\"But I digress. All of that is two-dimensional thinking. Now consider if an object is three-dimensional.\"","A sphere of fire appeared above the plane, descending slowly toward it.","\" Let’s say a simple fireball. If it were descending through the plane of Flatland, to the inhabitants, it would not appear as a solid sphere. Instead, it would manifest as a tiny point that grows into a widening circle, then shrinks back to a point before vanishing entirely.\"","The visualization played out exactly as he described, the flat figures on the plane reacting with what might have been wonder to the expanding and contracting circle.","\" They would think they witnessed a miracle. An intrusion from a higher dimension that they simply do not have the sensory apparatus to perceive in its fullness. They saw only a fraction of a higher reality.\"","The visualization faded as Noah’s eyes blazed brighter.","\" Interdimensionality describes forces, authorities, or entities that exist in entirely different dimensions and move in ways we cannot perceive. I wish to incorporate that concept into THE Infiniverse. To make it so you cannot be perceived at all.\"","He stood, the connection with Ruination and THE Infiniverse remaining even as he moved.","\" It won’t matter if we consider ourselves two-dimensional or three-dimensional and THE Gilded Ones three-dimensional or four-dimensional. I wish to decide for myself what I can hide from anything in any potential dimension, however illogical that may be.\"","New visualizations appeared, tiny curled structures that seemed to fold in on themselves infinitely.","\" String theory says there are countless dimensions, but many cannot be perceived because they are curled up into infinitesimal spaces that are too small for anyone to see. I want us to begin doing that if possible.\"","His voice grew heavier with conviction.","\" To utilize Infinity that makes things possible. To compact and squeeze THE Infiniverse. To hide it within the paradoxical weavings of Infinity to the extent that even beings of more power or higher Scales would still not perceive it.\"","The curled structures multiplied, folding in on themselves in patterns that seemed to defy spatial logic.","\" Because Scales are not definitive. I have just shown this. I am supposedly of THE First Scale, and yet I took down a Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity at THE Second Scale. So what do the Scales actually mean?\"","He turned to face both of his companions fully.","\" Vakochev’s Scales of Existence are his. From this point on, I no longer even feel like quantifying myself with them. I am already acting outside the parameters and bounds of these Scales.\"","His eyes blazed like singularities of an unfathomable Cause.","\" Why can I not enact my own? Who decided that I was incapable of this?\"","BOOM!","His words pressed against everything nearby, authority that transcended what his apparent classification should allow. The multicolored sea rippled outward from his position, waves of Infinity and Observable Force responding to declarations that challenged the very foundations of how existence had been organized!","Ruination and THE Infiniverse looked at each other.","They smiled brilliantly, understanding passing between them without need for words. Their Master was not content to exist within the boundaries others had established. He never had been. And now he was declaring that even the most fundamental frameworks of Observable Existence could be questioned, could be challenged, could be replaced with something of his own design!","| Understood, Master.|","Ruination’s voice emerged, but beneath it burned excitement that matched what THE Infiniverse displayed.","| You wish to fold THE Infiniverse into configurations that transcend normal dimensional perception, hiding it from entities who operate at scales we cannot currently match. This is theoretically possible through application of your Infinity, which by its nature makes possibilities from impossibilities.|","Her illusory form flickered as processing intensified.","| The challenge lies in compacting an internal Observable Existence without destroying what it contains. Normal folding would crush the Three Thousand Realms, would obliterate the territories and beings within THE Infiniverse’s depths. But your Infinity operates according to principles that permit paradoxical states.|","|I propose utilizing the mathematical framework of Calabi-Yau manifolds, but modified through Infinite application. In standard theoretical physics, Calabi-Yau manifolds are complex geometric shapes where extra dimensions of string theory are compactified. They are curled so tightly that they become imperceptible to observation at normal scales.|","| By applying Infinity to this framework, we can create what I shall term THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds.|","The visualizations before them shifted, those curled structures becoming more complex, more intricate, folding in on themselves in patterns that seemed to contain infinite depth within finite space.","| THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds would function as follows:|","|First, THE Infiniverse would be folded into geometric configurations that exist below the threshold of perception for entities operating in standard dimensional frameworks. This folding would be infinitely recursive, meaning that no matter how closely an observer examined the space where THE Infiniverse exists, they would find only more folding, more compaction, more layers that lead nowhere.|","|Second, the Hadean weavings currently transforming THE Infiniverse’s architecture would be integrated into these folds. Hadean classification theoreticslly exist outside the knowledge of THE Gilded, as you noted. By weaving Hadean authority throughout the manifold structure, we create a form of existence that cannot be categorized by frameworks that do not account for its presence.|","|Third, your Infinity would serve as the binding force holding these impossible configurations stable. Normal physics would demand that such compaction collapse into singularity or tear itself apart through spatial contradictions. But Infinity makes the impossible possible, permitting states that violate conventional understanding.|","|The result would be an Observable Existence that exists fully and completely, with all its realms and territories and inhabitants intact, yet occupies dimensional space so thoroughly folded that higher-dimensional beings would perceive nothing. Simply nothing to observe, as if THE Infiniverse did not exist at all.|","|Furthermore, this configuration would mask THE Infiniverse against Vakochev’s Scales of Existence. By bathing the manifold structure in Hadean weavings and Infinite authority, we create existence that the Scales cannot measure because they were never designed to account for such configurations.|","|Entities attempting to perceive THE Infiniverse through conventional means, even means appropriate to Gilded classification, would find their perception sliding away. Simply unable to find purchase on something that exists in dimensional configurations their frameworks cannot process. And all this is theory as we...could still be wrong and don’t grasp the terrifying power of THE Gilded Lifeforms|","A pause that felt contemplative.","|I should note that implementing THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds will require significant resources and time. The folding must be precise. The integration of Hadean weavings must be complete. And the binding through Infinity must be absolute, permitting no gaps where perception could find entry.|","|But if successful, you will have an Observable Existence hidden through existing in ways that more powerful beings cannot conceptualize. Invisible not because they cannot see, but because there is nothing within their dimensional framework to see.|","| Shall I... begin preliminary calculations for implementation?|","...!","Noah looked at the visualizations still floating before them, those impossibly folded structures that contained infinity within finite space. THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds. A way to hide not by being stronger than his enemies, but by existing in configurations they couldn’t perceive regardless of their strength!","It was a contingency, and he would have many!","\" Begin ,\" he said simply.","HUUM!"]},{"number":5110,"title":"Chapter 5110: Chapter 5109: My Scales!","paragraphs":["While Ruination and THE Infiniverse began their task of compacting and hiding THE Infiniverse from beings infinitely more powerful, Noah took a look at himself.","He was thinking about the Scales of Existence and his own power.","Vakochev’s Scales.","They didn’t only seem like someone else’s blueprint of what power was across all of existence. They felt like a proposed structure of how things should be that someone had managed to get their name on, influencing what the system of power was for everything that existed. For something like this, Noah could look at Vakochev and say they had accomplished something grand.","To impose their vision of what the system of power should be for all of existence, Vakochev had to be someone unique.","When he thought about himself, he had only appeared and touched Mana more than three years ago. He was young in relation to all of existence. In respect to the Observable Existence he was in alone, he had not lived even a fraction of the time after the emergence of THE First Cause that differentiated everything. And the time before that, filled with endless potential, was countless cycles longer than the span after THE First Cause.","So yes. He was young.","Was Vakochev someone who had been alive even before the emergence of THE First Cause? What exactly did one need to have to be capable of instituting their vision across all of existence?","But however grand that person was, Noah would not let them define him. He also wanted to find his own path!","Every stage he entered, he ended up doing something uniquely his. Even while crossing the Wheel of Existence and messing around with True Sources, he had developed his own unique system compared to everyone else. He briefly thought about The Great Beyonder and The Omnifather. About the concepts of Megalos and Kuklos and Outerversal and Ordo Ab Chao and many other things that had defined his journey.","Infinity and Mana was the one singular constant even now.","He looked at his First Tongue.","Its weavings seemed innumerable and endless, the language of existence itself. He had connected this with Mana as the basal authority that could transform into anything else. He used to utter words or write words or Inscriptions, intricately playing with Embodiments and Apophasis. Even now, these capabilities still bloomed within his existence.","But at this moment in time, he was utilizing the immense force of Infinity itself. His own existence had been geared and positioned with Observable Force due to his connection with a Gilded Lifeform. When one could conjure the weight and immensity of an entire sea of Infinity, when one could channel the very musings of the force of what was Observable, he didn’t find himself needing to write out Archai or Apophasis or Embodiments anymore.","The raw power had grown tremendously.","But he still had the weavings of Perpetual Harvest and The Cheating Architect within him, foundations that defined his existence at its core. His efforts always produced harvests. And he linked all of it with Infinity to bring about infinite potential, which allowed him to utilize his Hadean Organ of Civilization to multiply everything by a factor of ten and elevate it further by an exponent of three with anything he brought inside of him.","All of this came together to help him in his transformation.","A transformation that eventually gave him glistening multicolored golden Hadean Organs and Bones.","Noah looked at himself.","His skin illuminated from within, allowing him to see what lay beneath. The multicolored golden bones became visible within his body, crystalline structures that seemed sacred in their perfection. His organs pulsed with the same radiance, each one transformed into something that exceeded what Proterozoic classification represented. They were holy things, wonders that shouldn’t have been possible for someone of his age and origin.","And yet here they were.","Here he was!","Quintessentially! Tyrannically!","He had already come to the decision that he would not be following whatever the measurements of Vakochev’s Scales were. Those Scales had been designed by someone else, imposed upon existence by someone else, named after someone else. Why should he accept limitations that another being had established? Why should he measure himself against frameworks that didn’t account for what he had become?","\" My power... is my own.\"","His voice emerged with conviction that pressed against the multicolored sea surrounding him.","\" So I will design my own Scale of Existence. My own Scale of Progression.\"","BOOM!","He raised his hand, watching the golden light that pressed outward through his transformed flesh.","\" One that accounts for all aspects of existence. Accounting for Bounded. Accounting for Gilded. Accounting for the very unfair nature of existence. I...don’t know how they will be structured yet.\"","His eyes blazed like singularities.","\" So I will simply engineer them as I go. They won’t be Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\" These will be my own. These will be THE Infinite Scales of Existence!\"","BOOM!","His words pressed against everything nearby, authority declaring intent that challenged the very foundations of how power had been measured since before most current beings existed!","As the echo faded, Noah considered the naming.","He had thought about calling them the Osmontian Scales of Existence. It would have been fitting in a way, his name attached to his creation just as Vakochev’s name was attached to theirs. But that felt wrong. It felt like he was trying to compete with Vakochev on their terms, trying to replace one person’s ego with another’s.","He had also considered the Hadean Scales of Existence. That classification was unique to him, something that existed outside what others understood. But Hadean described what he currently was, not what his Scales would measure . They needed to be broader than a single classification.","Infinity.","That was the constant. That was what had defined his journey from the moment he first threw endless fireballs. Infinity had been with him through every stage, every transformation, every impossible advancement. It wasn’t his name, but it was his nature. It was what made him capable of what others said was impossible.","And unlike tacking his name onto something, calling them THE Infinite Scales didn’t feel like ego. It felt like...well, moreso like the truth. The Scales would be infinite in their potential, infinite in their scope, infinite in their capacity to grow and change as he grew and changed. They wouldn’t be static like Vakochev’s Scales. They would evolve.","He didn’t want to be like Vakochev, imposing his name on existence.","He wanted to create something that could encompass everything, including himself. Something infinite.","BOOM!","The moment his decision solidified, the air before him shifted.","|I have registered your intent to construct an independent framework for measuring and categorizing power across existence. This is an undertaking of considerable magnitude.|","Ruination’s voice emerged as she continued her work on THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds simultaneously.","|You are beginning to construct the backbone of your own Scales of Existence. THE Infinite Scales, as you have named them. Unlike Vakochev’s Scales, which were established according to principles that predate most current understanding and have remained static since their implementation, your Scales will be dynamic. They will evolve as you evolve. They will expand as your comprehension expands.|","|The definition, designations, and structure of THE Infinite Scales are entirely dependent on you and how you choose to proceed. This grants tremendous flexibility but also tremendous responsibility.|","| There are several possibilities that this opens.|","|First, your First Infinite Scale could encompass what Vakochev’s framework designates as both THE First Scale and THE Second Scale. The distinction between those classifications, which Vakochev established as the presence or absence of a Civilizational Anchor, may not be relevant to your own system. You have demonstrated that someone without a formal Civilizational Anchor can exceed those who possess one. Your Scales could reflect this reality.|","|Second, if you can quantify and understand THE Third Scale, your framework could encompass that as well.|","|Third, and perhaps most significantly, the direction of your power is yours to decide. Vakochev’s Scales measure power according to Vakochev’s understanding of what power should be. Your Scales will measure power according to your understanding. If you believe that Hadean classification exceeds Proterozoic regardless of Scale designation, your framework can reflect that. If you believe that Bounded can exceed Gilded under certain conditions, your framework can account for that as well.|","|The engineering of THE Infinite Scales has begun. How they develop from this point forward depends entirely on the choices you make and the comprehension you achieve.|","...!","Noah looked at the notifications floating before him!","His own Scales of Existence. A framework that would grow with him rather than constrain him. Something infinite in its potential, just as he was infinite in his own way!"]},{"number":5111,"title":"Chapter 5111: Chapter 5110: War! I","paragraphs":["<Pioneers>","In the long annals of Observable Existence, there have always been those who looked upon the established order and asked a simple question: why must it be so?","These beings, whom later beings would come to call Pioneers, did not accept that the boundaries of what was possible had already been drawn by those who came before. They did not believe that the frameworks governing power and progression were immutable laws of reality rather than choices made by earlier entities who happened to arrive first.","There was THE Quantum Weaver, who studied the behavior of particles at scales so small that certainty itself became meaningless. Where others saw chaos, she perceived opportunity. She developed a Civilization she termed Superposition Authority, which allowed her existence to occupy multiple states simultaneously until observation forced collapse into whichever configuration most benefited her purposes. Her enemies could never predict where she would be, because she was everywhere until she chose not to be. She fell eventually, as many Pioneers do, but the Civilization she forged persisted in fragments that others would later rediscover and build upon.","There was also THE Entanglement Sovereign, who recognized that particles separated by vast distances could influence each other instantaneously, as if space itself was an illusion they had agreed to ignore. He engineered connections between aspects of his existence scattered across Observable Existence, creating a network of influence that transcended the limitations of travel and communication. When he acted in one location, the effects manifested simultaneously in a thousand others.","Those who sought to contain him discovered that containing one fragment meant nothing when countless fragments remained free.","Disastrously, there was also THE Relativistic Architect, who understood that time flowed differently depending on velocity and gravity. She constructed realms where eons passed internally while mere moments elapsed externally, cultivating armies and resources in temporal pockets that her enemies could not perceive fast enough to address. By the time they recognized her threat, she had already spent subjective cycles preparing for their response.","These Pioneers and countless others demonstrated a truth that the comfortable and the powerful have always sought to suppress: the rules of existence are not natural laws but engineering decisions. They were designed by someone. And what was designed by someone can be redesigned by someone else.","This is why Pioneers are critical for the immensity of existence.","Without them, the frameworks established by the earliest and most powerful would calcify into permanence. Progress would halt. Innovation would cease!","Oh!","Imagine the loss of innovation itself.","Existence would become a museum curated by those who arrived first, with all subsequent beings reduced to visitors admiring what others had built while being forbidden from building anything themselves.","The Pioneers remind us that boundaries are proposals, not facts. That limitations are suggestions and commands. That someone saying ’this cannot be done’ often means only that they have not yet seen it done.","Of course, Pioneers frequently fail. They frequently die. They frequently discover that the boundaries they sought to transcend existed for reasons they did not understand, and their attempts to cross them ended in consequences they could not survive.","But some succeed.","And when they succeed, existence itself changes to accommodate what they have proven possible.","This is why those who benefit from the current order fear Pioneers above all other threats. And it is not because Pioneers are necessarily more powerful than they are...","But because Pioneers ask questions that have no safe answers.","Why must it be so?","What if it could be otherwise?","Who decided, and why should we accept their decision?","These questions, once asked, cannot be unasked. And the beings who ask them, even if they fall, plant seeds in the minds of others who will ask the same questions again!","Existence is vast. But it was not always as vast as it is now. Every expansion, every new territory, every novel classification and framework and system of power, all of these emerged because someone refused to accept that what existed was all that could exist.","Pioneers built the vastness.","And Pioneers will continue building it, whether the current custodians of existence approve or not.","---","Noah’s mind was buzzing with possibilities and ideas.","For his First Infinite Scale of Existence, Noah needed to understand exactly what he was working with. He currently held Uncountable Infinity across all Depths and foundations of his existence. His body endlessly generated Quintessence Infiniforce through active utilization of Infinity itself. Observable Force flooded into him from Ubergulden Adelheid through a connection that pulsed with warmth he had grown accustomed to feeling.","With his entire skeleton and organs transformed to Hadean classification, he had access to power that defied what his apparent Scale should permit.","Something like his brain alone held an ability he had already glimpsed. THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation could stretch an instant into an infinite moment of perception, freezing everything while his consciousness thought freely across subjective spans that could encompass days or weeks or longer.","But his brain was only one organ among seventy-eight.","His skeleton was only two hundred and six bones.","Each structure now held capabilities that his previous existence couldn’t have imagined.","\"Ruination,\" he said softly. \"Give me a breakdown of what my Hadean form is actually capable of.\"","|With pleasure, Master.|","|Beginning with defensive capabilities.|","| THE Hadean Dermis of Infinite Interface.|","|Your skin now serves as the outermost boundary between your existence and external reality. It is no longer merely a protective layer but an active defensive system that responds to threats according to their classification.|","| Against Rhyacian Tier Proterozoic Scale entities: Complete immunity . Their attacks cannot penetrate your skin regardless of methodology employed. Furthermore, any entity at Rhyacian classification who physically strikes you will experience Existential Hadean Thorn Damage. This damage reflects a portion of their own force back through their existence at amplified intensity. A Rhyacian Proterozoic Lifeform who attacks you with full commitment may find the feedback alone sufficient to collapse their foundations entirely.|","|Against Calymmian Tier Proterozoic Scale entities: Significant resistance. Approximately 25% of their damage output can be transmitted across your skin. However, the remaining 75% is nullified at the dermal level. Any damage that does penetrate must then contend with your musculature and skeletal structure, which possess their own defensive parameters. In practical terms, a Calymmian entity striking you with everything they possess would achieve minimal effect on your actual existence.|","|Against Ediacaran Tier Proterozoic Scale entities: Not enough data...|","...!","Noah absorbed this information with eyes that blazed brighter.","His skin alone could collapse Rhyacian entities through reflected damage. His skin alone reduced Calymmian attacks to a quarter of their intended effect.","| THE Hadean Cage of Infinite Protection.|","|Your ribcage now serves as more than skeletal structure surrounding vital organs. It has become an active defensive matrix that responds to threats penetrating past your outer defenses.|","| This structure possesses Pulse Nullification capabilities . The majority of common Pulses of The Scales will have their effects reduced by approximately 80% upon contact with your ribcage’s defensive field. This reduction occurs automatically without requiring conscious activation.|","|In practical terms, you could withstand a Pulse of The Scales without taking any defensive action whatsoever. The Pulse would strike you, and your ribcage would process approximately 80% of its unraveling authority before that authority reached anything vital. The remaining 20% would then contend with your Hadean organs, which possess their own resistance parameters.|","|This does not grant immunity to all Pulses. Pulses derived from Causes of exceptional magnitude, or Pulses deployed by entities significantly exceeding Calymmian classification, may overwhelm this passive protection. But against standard deployment of Pulse authority, you can simply stand and receive what is thrown at you without meaningful consequence.|","...!","He could tank a Pulse without doing anything.","The very authority that had threatened to erase him, the power derived from Causes that shaped Observable Existence itself, could now wash over him like rain against stone!","| THE Hadean Skull of Infinite Perception.|","|Your cranium now protects THE Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation while also serving as a sensory amplification matrix. Perceptual capabilities have expanded dramatically.|","|You can now perceive existence across spectrums previously inaccessible to your classification. This includes the ability to observe Civilizational weavings in real-time, to witness the flow of Observable Force through environments and entities, and to detect threats from distances that would require lesser beings to employ specialized tools or abilities.|","|Additionally, your skull possesses Cognitive Fortress properties. Mental attacks, psychic intrusions, Civilization-based mind manipulation, and similar methodologies are reduced in effectiveness by approximately 90% before reaching your actual consciousness. Rhyacian entities attempting mental assault would find their efforts reflected back with amplified intensity. Calymmian entities would achieve negligible penetration. Only beings at Ediacaran classification or above possess the raw authority to meaningfully threaten your mental integrity through direct assault.|","| THE Hadean Heart of Infinite Circulation.|","|Your heart now pumps more than blood. It circulates Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce throughout your existence alongside conventional biological function.|","|This organ possesses Regenerative Cascade capabilities. Any damage sustained by your existence triggers accelerated healing that draws upon your reserves of Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce. Against Rhyacian-tier damage, regeneration occurs faster than the damage can be inflicted. Against Calymmian-tier damage, regeneration matches the rate of injury, resulting in a stalemate that favors you due to your superior reserves. Against Ediacaran-tier damage...more data is required.|","| Furthermore, your heart can initiate Circulation Surge. By consciously accelerating its function, you can temporarily boost all physical capabilities by a factor of ten for spans of approximately thirty seconds. This ability has a recovery period of five minutes between uses.|","| THE Hadean Spine of Infinite Flexibility.|","|Your spinal column now serves as the primary conduit for authority distribution throughout your physical form. All commands from your brain to your body, and all sensory information from your body to your brain, flow through this enhanced structure.|","|This organ possesses Authority Amplification properties. Any Civilization-based ability you employ has its effectiveness increased by approximately 3000% simply by virtue of traveling through your transformed spine. This amplification occurs automatically and stacks with any other enhancement methodologies you employ.|","|Additionally, your spine possesses Existential Stability. Forces that would normally destabilize your Civilization or disrupt your connection to your own authority find themselves grounded and dispersed through your spinal structure.|","| THE Hadean Hands of Infinite Grasp... your hands can initiate Contact Devastation . Physical strikes delivered through your palms carry additional force multiplied by the density of Infinity and Observable Force currently saturating your existence. A simple palm strike against a Rhyacian entity could shatter them to ash entirely. Against Calymmian entities, the same strike would penetrate approximately 60% of their protection.|","...!","Noah looked at his hands.","These instruments that had once been ordinary human appendages, that had once struggled to throw fireballs with enough force to matter, now held capabilities that could devastate entities who had existed for eons!","| THE Hadean Legs of Infinite Stride.. . Each step you take can...|","| THE Hadean Eyes...|","|THE Hadean Ears...|","Noah went through the descriptions of each Organ or skeletal structure carefully until...","|This concludes the summary of major structural capabilities. Each of your 206 bones and 78 organs possesses unique properties appropriate to their function. Comprehensive documentation would require extensive cataloguing....|","|In summary, Against Rhyacian classification: You are effectively untouchable and absolutely devastating.|","|Against Calymmian classification: You hold significant advantage in all metrics that matter.|","|Against Ediacaran classification: More data is required.|","|This is your baseline, Master. Before channeling any Pulses. Before utilizing THE Hadean Organ of Civilization or any other unique capabilities you possess.|","| Simply existing as a Hadean Lifeform grants you these parameters.|","...!","Noah stood in the multicolored sea surrounding him, processing everything Ruination had detailed.","Simply existing granted him these capabilities.","And this was his baseline.","This was before he did anything!"]},{"number":5112,"title":"Chapter 5112: Chapter 5111: War! II","paragraphs":["As Noah was gauging his power, his existence flickered.","He frowned and rose from his seated position, every Hadean sense suddenly screaming with warning!","Something was approaching. Something that would absolutely lock onto him soon. The feeling pressed against his awareness with weight that exceeded anything he had felt since THE Silurian Light first touched his existence!","He took a step and disappeared from within THE Infiniverse.","He appeared in THE Wastes.","The multicolored rain of THE Pluvial Epoch landed on his transformed body, droplets of Quintessence Infiniforce sliding across skin that could collapse Rhyacian entities through contact alone.","The tumultuous seas of Observable Force still churned around this region.","For a moment, everything was still.","Then the sky above him began to burn.","HUUM!","A grand power bloomed overhead, brilliance that exceeded even THE Silurian Pulse by multiple factors. This... wasn’t a single Cause making itself known. This was something far more terrifying. Multiple Causes resonated within that descending light, authorities that had shaped Observable Existence combining their weight into singular purpose!","The light descended not to attack but to declare.","| Alert.|","Ruination’s voice emerged with urgency she rarely displayed.","|A Civilizational Holy War has been declared against you by THE Deliverance.|","| He has paid a heavy cost and called upon all the Causes within THE First Cause to bear witness to this declaration . THE Silurian Cause. THE Cambrian Cause. THE Ediacaran Cause. And others whose names are not currently accessible to my perception. All of them have answered his call. All of them now observe what is being enacted.|","| In 24 hours, this Civilizational Holy War will begin.|","| Your Civilization and all followers connected to you have been conscripted to fight against the Civilization of THE Deliverance and the followers connected to him.|","| This conscription is absolute. It cannot be refused. It cannot be evaded through normal means. The power of THE First Cause itself enforces participation.|","...!","Noah watched as golden light coalesced before him, forming structures that displayed what was being enacted.","A golden box appeared, holding a shadowy image that couldn’t be fully perceived. His own silhouette, rendered in configurations that the declaration couldn’t fully capture due to his Hadean nature existing outside normal frameworks. This golden box pulsed with authority that declared him the leader of one side.","Facing it, a platinum-colored box formed.","Within it, another shadowy figure that he couldn’t see clearly. But the label beneath required no clarification.","THE Deliverance.","The entity that commanded Primordial Architects. The being that had dispatched Grimvault!","And then more boxes began blooming around his golden representation.","|Follower designations are being determined.|","Names appeared beneath shadowy figures, each one a person connected to his Civilization, each one someone he cared about or who had sworn themselves to his cause!","His eyes locked onto one box eyes that began to blaze with rage.","Amelia Osmont.","His mother’s name glowed beneath a shadowy figure.","Facing her box, a platinum designation: THE Primordial Carver.","|THE Primordial Carver: Unknown. Suspected to be Calymmian Tier Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect...|","...!","Another box. Henry Osmont. His son!","Facing him: Grimvault.","|Grimvault, THE Primordial Silence: Calymmian Tier Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect...|","More boxes appeared in rapid succession.","Barbatos, facing THE Primordial Sculptor.","Sigrid, facing THE Primordial Warden.","Riya, facing THE Primordial Flame.","Moiraine, facing THE Primordial Tide.","Adelaide, facing THE Primordial Stone.","Titano, facing THE Primordial Hammer.","THE Queen of Matter, facing THE Primordial Void.","THE First Farmer, facing THE Primordial Harvest.","Khor, facing THE Primordial Hunter.","Tor, THE First Hunger, facing THE Primordial Devourer!","THE Living Origin, facing THE Primordial Genesis!","Ul’moreth, THE Big Stepper, facing THE Primordial Walker!","Lumivara, facing THE Primordial Light.","Skoll, facing THE Primordial Beast!","Oh!","Ains THE Fisherman, facing THE Primordial Depths.","Noah’s eyes burned with cold gold light as more designations appeared.","THE Emperor Penguin, facing THE Primordial Frost...","Dr. Hall, Kazuhiko...","Every companion. Every ally. Every being who had connected themselves to his Civilization through loyalty or love or circumstance.","Eighty-one golden boxes in total.","Eighty-one people he cared about.","All of them facing Primordial Architects at THE Second Scale...as far as he knew.","| The followers of the Civilizations of both leaders have been determined and will be summoned into their own Isolated Civilizational Arenas when the 24-hour preparation period concludes.|","|The Civilization that loses the majority of battles will be deemed the losers. All remaining followers and every ounce of authority the losing side held will be enslaved by the winner.|","| This is absolute. This is enforced by THE First Cause itself.|","|The power of THE First Cause has been called upon to oversee this Civilizational Holy War for the third time in the history of this Observable Existence. It cannot be denied. The 81 Chosen from either side will undeniably be pulled into their Isolated Civilizational Arenas when the time arrives.|","Noah’s hands clenched into fists, golden light erupting from between his fingers.","|However.|","|There exists one avenue for modification.|","|The only way any Chosen Follower can evade participation is by another taking their place whose connections to your Civilization existed but were not deemed significant enough for primary designation.|","|Possible substitutions have been determined:|","| THE Great Usurper, THE Peacemaker, Naldine Manthon, THE Primordial Paradox, THE Creature, THE Living Temporal, THE Beholder, THE Living Emotive, THE Secretive Eon...|","|These entities may volunteer to replace designated followers if they choose. The decision must be made before the 24-hour preparation period concludes. No substitution can be forced.|","...!","Noah floated grandly above THE Wastes, the multicolored rain continuing to fall around him as if the Existence itself was weeping for what had been declared!","He saw himself represented in that golden box.","He saw eighty-one other golden boxes bearing the names of his family and those who followed him.","His mother. His son. His lovers. His companions. His allies. Even his penguin!","All chosen to be pitted against Primordial Architects and monsters of THE Second Scale.","They wanted to butcher his people without him even being able to help them.","Each battle would occur in isolated arenas where he couldn’t intervene. Each confrontation would pit someone he loved against beings who had existed for eons, who had forged Proterozoic Bones and Organs across spans that made human lifetimes seem like heartbeats.","He had only ever defended himself.","He had never asked for anything grand. He had never wanted anything grand. His dreams were simple. Safety. Prosperity. Happiness. A plot of land and seas of Mana!","But he would always be targeted.","This was why he never stood still. This was why he continued to seek and to dream. This was why he pushed himself past limitations that others said couldn’t be surpassed!","Because of shit like this.","Because the moment he stopped growing, the moment he accepted contentment, the moment he believed he had finally achieved enough, something like this would descend upon him and everyone he cared about.","THE Deliverance had declared war.","Not against him directly, where his Hadean body could meet whatever was thrown at it. Against his people. Against those whose only crime was being connected to his Civilization through bonds of loyalty and love.","Twenty-four hours.","He had twenty-four hours before his mother faced a Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect alone.","Before everyone he cared about was thrown into battles they were never meant to survive.","Noah’s eyes blazed like singularities of cold fury as he looked upon the declaration still burning in the sky above THE Wastes!"]},{"number":5113,"title":"Chapter 5113: Chapter 5112: I Volunteer!","paragraphs":["If one wasn’t loud in existence, others might think they were meek and could get pushed around.","Noah didn’t like to be loud. He preferred results that spoke louder than words ever could. But he could be very loud if he wanted . He could shake the foundations of Observable Existence itself if the situation demanded it!","Now they wanted to target him and his family?","To isolate his mother, his son, and everyone else he cared about in domains with Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entities in less than 24 hours?","Okay.","This was a deadly and terrifying move on their behalf. THE Deliverance had called upon THE First Cause itself to enforce this Civilizational Holy War, with matchups designed to slaughter everyone connected to his Civilization while he watched helplessly from outside their isolated arenas.","But they made one critical mistake.","That mistake was giving him 24 hours.","Others experienced major changes across thousands or millions of years. They cultivated Proterozoic Bones one at a time over spans that most beings couldn’t comprehend. They refined their Organs through patient accumulation that treated centuries like days.","He could flip the whole fucking board in a matter of hours.","He had done it before. He would do it again.","Noah glared at the golden and platinum boxes still burning in the sky above THE Wastes, his mind already racing through possibilities and contingencies. He was preparing to leave when an instant later, a voice reached him.","\" When adversity comes, it doesn’t end, it seems.\"","THE Primordial Paradox’s words held the weight of someone who had observed eons of conflict and understood exactly what was at stake.","\"I received weavings of existence explaining the Civilizational Holy War and my potential position within it. Tell me whose slot among your people you need me to take, Youngest. I will be there for you.\"","Before Noah could respond, another voice reached him at nearly the same moment. Alexander’s words overlapped with those of THE Great Usurper, both of them arriving simultaneously as if existence itself was ensuring he understood that he wasn’t alone.","\" The fallout from that fight still seems to be cascading. I’m sorry about this. Tell me whose position to take.\"","Alexander’s voice carried guilt!","\" Osmont!\"","THE Great Usurper’s voice boomed with energy.","\" While we may be getting curbstomped since I haven’t gotten too far yet, I’m also here to help however you need me to. Just say the word. I have uh...made friends with Abaddon and the many Chaos Giants of Jotunheim among other things. Being idle and active at the same time is paying off. .\"","...!","They reached out to him one after another, making it clear they would help. They only asked him how.","Amser Modred’s voice arrived around the same time, THE Living Temporal’s words burning with time!","\" My Civilizational Anchor has just been established. I can use the test against monstrous beings and my weavings of Time. Let me know.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes flashed sharply as he processed all of these offers.","He sent each of them their own replies, his thoughts pressing outward through connections that had been established across various circumstances and conflicts. The message was the same for all of them: hang on for now, and he would let them know something soon enough.","He was about to move when another message arrived.","This one came differently. Not through direct communication or Civilizational weavings, but through slivers of tumultuous emotions gathered from all across existence.","A voice from a woman he really didn’t like hearing from. Even more than the voice, something physical manifested before his perception.","The multicolored rain falling throughout THE Wastes began behaving strangely.","Droplets paused in their descent. Others curved toward a central point. Emotions that permeated the very fabric of this transformed region, residual feelings left over from the conflict that had occurred here, began coalescing into something visible.","An illusory visage formed from the gathered emotional resonance!","THE Living Emotive looked toward Noah with shining eyes that held something far beyond normal attention. Her features were beautiful in a way that felt dangerous...symmetry that seemed designed to draw others in before consuming them!","Her smile stretched too wide. Her gaze never quite settled, flickering between points of focus as if she was perceiving things that existed only in her own unstable perception.","Her voice reached out through the illusory phenomena with mania that made his skin crawl.","\" Sir Osmont!\"","The words tumbled out rapidly, barely controlled.","\"I volunteer! I volunteer as tribute! How dare these decrepit Primordial Architects try to bully you?! The audacity! The sheer presumption! They think they can threaten what’s yours? What’s MINE to protect?!\"","Her illusory form flickered, features shifting between expressions faster than should have been possible.","\"I have tapped into all emotions across Observable Existence! Every feeling! Every passion! Every rage and love and despair! They flow through me like rivers through valleys, and I will use them ALL for you!\"","She giggled, the sound carrying eerie undertones that Noah didn’t want to examine too closely.","\"I will focus on penetrating into THE Wyld! I sense THE Creature has arrived there, and where he goes, interesting things follow...I will gather information for you of the Civilizations and power of those trying to bully you!\"","Her eyes locked onto his with intensity that bordered on religious fervor.","\"I don’t want anything in return. Just keep me in your thoughts! I know you detest me... I know you may even want to kill me, but I...really want you! Like... ah!\"","She shuddered visibly, the illusory form rippling with emotional overflow.","\"I’ll get back to you as I have to focus to penetrate weavings of THE Wyld! Think of me, Osmont! Think of me! Think of me!\"","The visage faded, emotions dispersing back into the surrounding environment as quickly as they had gathered.","...!","What... the fuck?","Noah’s eyes turned sharp as he processed what had just occurred. Had that woman gotten so powerful after claiming Chaos?","He didn’t even want to bother with that right now!","Moments after her departure, his weavings buzzed again as another voice arrived. This one came from someone he actually respected.","Anaximander’s words echoed out.","\" Hey, big guy.\"","The greeting was simple.","\" The other big guy I’m moving with in THE Wyld right now will probably tell me not to interfere. He’ll say you need to handle your adversity yourself, that challenges only make you stronger, all that philosophical stuff he’s fond of.\"","A slight pause came that felt almost apologetic.","\" But THE Deliverance is nasty stuff. Real nasty. So just like before, just say ’Come, Anaximander!’ and I will be there.\"","...!"]},{"number":5114,"title":"Chapter 5114: Chapter 5113: Custodes! I","paragraphs":["The voice of Anaximander echoed through his mind as Noah turned silent.","He was moving with THE Creature within THE Wyld right now. Among all those who had reached out to offer assistance, THE Creature was notably not among them.","Noah knew the being’s philosophy. Adversity only made one stronger. Pain was the forge that shaped greatness. THE Creature wouldn’t volunteer himself because doing so would undermine the very principles he had built his existence around. He believed Noah needed to face this challenge.","But Noah also knew that if he asked, this being who had burned away his own Primordial Architect classification would come.","But did he truly need to do so?","This was not THE Fable of THE Creature. This wasn’t someone else’s story where Noah played a supporting role, benefiting from another’s power while his own remained stagnant.","This was his life. His weavings. His story.","And he would do everything he could to depend on himself and the weavings of his existence.","At this moment in time, there were several things he wanted to do. The first relied on himself, yes, but also drew from a place he was already pulling significant power from. A being whose Observable Force flooded into him constantly.","He wouldn’t ask for help from her either.","But with his Hadean weavings, he was about to do many crazy things that would pull even more from her reserves. He wanted to talk with her before then. To give her a heads up, and to also make sure that in addition to THE Deliverance, he wouldn’t add Gilded Lifeforms as his enemies right now. So he would reach out towards her.","Toward the one who was supposedly so far from him.","Toward Ubergulden Adelheid.","\" Ruination ,\" he said. \" Set up the line of communication between me and Ubergulden Adelheid. Wherever she may be.\"","...!","|Understood, Master.|","Ruination’s voice emerged, already working on his request.","|Communication with Ubergulden Adelheid presents unique challenges due to the nature of your connection and the distances involved. However, your Hadean transformation has expanded the capabilities available through your bond.|","|Initiating communication protocol.|","|The seas of Observable Force connecting you to Ubergulden Adelheid serve as the primary conduit. Information can travel along the same pathways that authority travels. Your Quintessence Infiniforce resides within Ubergulden Adelheid heavily.|","|Establishing resonance between your Hadean existence and the Observable Force conduit. Establishing resonance between your Quintessence Infiniforce within Ubergulden Adelheid and your primary reserves.|","|Communication channel established.|","|You may now speak directly to Ubergulden Adelheid through this connection. Your words will reach her regardless of physical distance. Her responses will return through the same pathways.|","|Speak, and she will hear.|","...!","Noah took a breath that his Hadean lungs didn’t technically require.","Then he reached out through the connection!","---","<Unknown Region of Existence>","She loved the triumph of the weak.","There was something beautiful about it, something that stirred feelings Ubergulden Adelheid had never been able to fully explain to others of her kind. When something small and fragile rose against something vast and terrible, when it struggled and bled and somehow emerged victorious despite every factor working against it, she felt something close to hope.","But such triumphs were always short-lived.","They never produced long-lasting results. The weak could win a battle, could celebrate their moment of glory, could believe they had changed the fundamental nature of their circumstances. Then reality would reassert itself, and everything they had fought for would crumble back into the dust it had always been destined to become.","She was currently standing inside a vast room that defied normal spatial comprehension.","The walls seemed to breathe with golden light, surfaces that weren’t quite solid shifting through configurations of architecture built from principles most civilizations couldn’t perceive.","Constellations drifted across the ceiling in patterns that held meaning only to those engineered to read them as they depicted the emergence of...Causes.","The floor beneath her feet felt like standing on crystallized purpose, every step resonating with power refined across spans that predated THE First Cause.","This was a glimpse of what truly advanced Civilizations looked like when they had access to resources that Bounded could never touch.","This was how THE Gilded lived.","Throughout the room, figures stood at various positions with postures of attentive service. Their skin shone with golden coloring that declared their nature without need for introduction, each one radiating authority that would have made someone like Grimvault feel like absolutely nothing.","The aura these servants held felt hundreds of times grander than what that Calymmian Tier Primordial Architect could muster at his peak.","Yet their faces held only respect when they looked toward her.","THE Gesinde . The lowest classification of Gilded Lifeforms, those who served at the pleasure of unique and grander Gilded. Even the weakest among them could have crushed basic Primordial Architects with casual effort, could have unmade Civilizations that Bounded considered unbreakable.","They were servants only in relation to beings like herself, and that relationship gave a glimpse to hierarchies that most of Observable Existence couldn’t comprehend.","Ubergulden Adelheid was seated on a floating golden lotus, its petals radiating warmth that nourished her existence simply through contact. Before her floated a golden aquarium filled with waters that shifted between blue and luminescent gold, containing a landscape of coral formations and underwater valleys that stretched for what appeared to be mere feet but actually encompassed light years of compressed space.","She was watching a group of goldfish.","These weren’t ordinary creatures. Each one burned with power at the Fundamental Depth of THE First Scale, their small forms containing authority that would have made them legendary figures in most regions of Observable Existence. The concentration of existence and Observable Force was so potent here that even simple lifeforms naturally attained the peak of THE First Scale through mere proximity to Gilded environments.","The water around them swirled with blue-gold blood, their scales torn and fins shredded from recent combat. But they were celebrating, swimming in patterns that declared triumph despite their injuries. They had just defended their territory against a threat that should have been impossible for them to overcome.","A golden crab floated listlessly ahead of them, its massive form drifting with the current.","It had been at THE Absolute Depth of THE First Scale. It had threatened their home, had invaded their small corner of this aquarium with intent to consume everything they had built. And they had fought back. They had coordinated, had sacrificed, had pushed themselves past limitations that should have been absolute.","They had won!","Ubergulden Adelheid watched them celebrate with eyes that held something close to sorrow.","Because what the goldfish couldn’t see was what existed on the other side of this aquarium. Beyond the coral formations and underwater valleys, past the territories they considered their entire world, thousands of those crabs clustered in configurations that of organized society rather than mindless predation. They had just sensed one of their own be killed.","They were already sending a party.","These goldfish that had triumphed against their oppressor, that were currently swimming in patterns of joy and relief, would all find themselves dead soon enough. The weak had won a battle. The weak would lose the war. As they always did. As they always would.","The weak never won. Not truly.","They only delayed their deaths."]},{"number":5115,"title":"Chapter 5115: Chapter 5114: Custodes! II","paragraphs":["As she was thinking all this, lost in contemplation that had consumed her attention across eons of observation, a voice reached her through pathways that shouldn’t have been accessible.","\" Hey.\"","The greeting was nonchalant and natural, almost familiar in its casualness. She found herself nodding and responding lightly before her conscious mind caught up with what was happening.","\" Hey.\"","Then her eyes opened wide.","Across the room, THE Gesinde turned toward her with expressions of mild confusion. They blinked as if trying to determine who she was talking to, their perception scanning the space around her for the source of a conversation they couldn’t perceive. Did she call for them?","Ubergulden Adelheid controlled her expression with discipline cultivated across countless eons.","Internally, she was shocked. She reached into her existence, following the pathways through which that greeting had traveled, and found its origin in the endless Quintessence Infiniforce integrated throughout her being. The voice had been Osmont’s!","It had traveled through the connection between them!","But this...shouldn’t have been possible.","How did he reach through unreachable weavings to be capable of sending even a communication? The connection established was one-directional. Information, communication, anything else should have been blocked by countermeasures she had implemented specifically to prevent exactly this scenario!","She focused on the Quintessence Infiniforce saturating her existence.","And shockingly, she began to see something forming within those multicolored seas. An illusory outline took shape, features becoming distinct as her perception refined its focus. It was Osmont, his form constructed from the very Infinity he had integrated into her being, manifesting in a space that existed entirely within her own existence.","Her expression grew heavier.","Part of her own weavings coalesced internally, her consciousness shifting to engage with this intrusion directly. Inside her body. In an expanse of multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce swirling all around.","Noah’s illusory visage finished forming.","From his perspective, all he could see were these endless multicolored seas stretching in every direction. Golden walls blocked off absolutely everything past the areas where these seas were contained, barriers she had constructed to prevent exactly this kind of penetration. He couldn’t sense or see a thing beyond the Infiniforce that belonged to him.","Good.","Moments later, a very real and very angry Ubergulden Adelheid appeared within these seas.","She looked at him with an imperious gaze that held fury barely restrained beneath its surface. Her golden eyes blazed as she spoke with authority that pressed against his illusory form.","\"I was magnanimous enough to leave you be, but you do this? You give a Bounded a mile, they reach for light years...\"","Her voice cut through the swirling Infiniforce like a blade.","\" What do you want? Are you unable to take care of the entanglements you have gotten yourself into down there? Are you running to me for help now?\"","She stepped closer to his illusory form, her presence overwhelming despite existing only as a projection within her own internal space.","\"I.. cannot help you.\"","She berated him with everything she had because he truly didn’t understand what she had already done for him. The less he was connected to her, the more he wouldn’t be found out. Because if he was found out by those who mattered, he would be killed.","Killed, erased so thoroughly that even the concept of his existence would be scrubbed from Observable Existence as if he had never been.","She had done what she could to preserve his life.","And he was doing this now?","She gazed toward him with calm anger burning in her golden eyes as he blinked calmly, his expression unchanged by her fury.","\" I can take care of my own things.\"","His voice was steady and almost amused.","\"I just reached out to check in on you and to notify you of a few things I have planned. I just didn’t expect you to be so charged up, O Great Gilded One.\"","The last part came out almost mockingly, and Ubergulden Adelheid’s eyes became sharp.","\" You did all this to check in on me?\"","Noah nodded as he looked around at the golden walls and swirling Infiniforce surrounding them.","\" You left the weavings of Gilded Lifeforms eons ago to live as a Bounded, so it must have sucked. You’re now back where you ran away from.\"","His eyes returned to hers.","\" How does it feel?\"","...!","How did it feel?","Ubergulden Adelheid blinked as she found herself without words. She didn’t even know how to reply to such a question. She alone knew why she had left here and suppressed herself to live as a Bounded Lifeform. She alone knew the circumstances that had driven her to abandon everything her engineering had granted her. And she alone knew how she felt now that she had returned.","But this was something she had never shared with anyone.","She wouldn’t start now.","She regained her imperious bearing with effort that didn’t show on her face. Her gaze traveled over Osmont’s illusory form, examining it with perception that could see things his classification shouldn’t have been able to hide.","Her eyes flashed sharply.","\" You seem to have changed and advanced somewhat. Are you enjoying the little connection and siphoning you’ve been taking from me?\"","Noah looked at his arms, examining them with interest as if noticing his own transformation for the first time.","\" That’s what I was actually going to mention to you. I don’t know much about Gilded Lifeforms, but in the near future, I’ll likely be widening and further fortifying our connection.\"","He looked back up at her.","\"I just wanted to make sure a little, tiny Bounded ant like me won’t cause any problems for you and your reserves of existence. And I also don’t wish to expose myself for being too loud so...fortify yourself to make sure nothing leaks.\"","...!","Ubergulden Adelheid raised her brows at this before shaking her head.","\" You won’t be able to do much. The connection we have stops at that. I’ve made sure of it, and even if I do nothing, a Bounded cannot alter or change much when it comes to the state of a Gilded.\"","Her voice carried certainty born from understanding.","\" Even if I didn’t already set up countermeasures. If you wish to fully remove any risk from yourself, you can always pull back your weavings of Infinity from me.\"","...!","After she said these words, Noah nodded slowly.","\"I just wanted to pass on the message so that you’re not too surprised. Going back to a place you ran away from for eons can be disorienting, so I hope you are adjusting well.\"","His illusory form began to flicker at the edges.","\"If you need to talk, just reach out to Infinity. I’m also very curious about you and all things to do with Ubergulden Adelheid. I’ll be dealing with a Civilizational Holy War for now but I’ll check in as things progress. Hang in there, O Big and Great Gilded One.\"","...!","Ubergulden Adelheid’s eyes opened wide at hearing her true name spoken from his mouth, and then ending his words mockingly again!","How did he find out her identity? The countermeasures she had implemented should have prevented anyone from perceiving what she truly was.","She was going to ask.","But the moment his words finished, his illusory form dispersed and fell back into the roiling Quintessence Infiniforce. He had dropped such a bomb and left immediately after, knowing she would want to reach out to him now, knowing she would have questions that demanded answers.","Ubergulden Adelheid’s eyes shone sharply.","She would never reach out to him. She was going to grasp the Containment she had placed on the Quintessence Infiniforce in her body, was going to reinforce the barriers that should have prevented this communication from ever occurring in the first place.","But at this moment, a voice echoed through the vast room.","\" Sister, it is time.\"","...!","The voice of Ubergulden Dietrich filled the space as THE Gesinde throughout the room stood at attention with perfect synchronization.","A door opened in one of those breathing golden walls, revealing her brother’s unfathomably handsome features and the golden eyes that held no pupils.","Behind him stood a few more Gilded Lifeforms!"]},{"number":5116,"title":"Chapter 5116: Chapter 5115: Custodes! III","paragraphs":["Ubergulden Dietrich stepped through the doorway with the easy confidence of someone who had never known limitation.","Behind him walked three women draped in golden robes that seemed woven from solidified gold Infinity. Their features held the ageless beauty common to all Gilded, but something about their bearing suggested wisdom accumulated across spans that made even other Gilded seem young.","Each one radiated authority that pressed against the room in waves of measured power.","The Magna Sorora.","Ubergulden Adelheid recognized them immediately. This grand sisterhood existed solely to ensure the primacy and progression of Gilded Ones, their membership consisting entirely of wise women who had dedicated their existences to guiding their kind toward greater heights. They advised ruling families, oversaw ceremonies of significance, and maintained traditions that predated most of what currently existed in Observable Existence.","The first among them was called Sororis Prima Evangelina, her features sharp and assessing beneath hair that fell like spun gold. The second, Sororis Prima Konstanze, held herself with the stillness of deep water concealing dangerous currents. The third, Sororis Prima Mathilde, watched everything with eyes that seemed to perceive far more than they revealed.","All three studied Ubergulden Adelheid with attention that felt like physical pressure.","\" Sister.\"","Ubergulden Dietrich’s voice carried warmth beneath its formal cadence as he approached her floating lotus.","\" They are here for the preliminary process before you can be taken to the ceremony. Today marks your full rejoining with all the status your position in our ruling family demands.\"","He smiled.","\" This means one of the first things in your Ceremony is for you to undergo the Bonding, THE Sundesmos, with your own Custodes.\"","Custodes.","The word stirred memories that Ubergulden Adelheid had suppressed across eons of living as someone else. A Custos , in singular form, was a powerful Gilded One bound to ruling royal Gilded through rituals.","They protected their bonded charge for life, their existences intertwined so thoroughly that betrayal became impossible by design. Should anything threaten their bonded Gilded One, the Custodes would pay with their lives before allowing harm to reach those they served.","They were unfathomably loyal because they were engineered to be incapable of anything else.","\" The one chosen to be your Custos is someone who grew up and trained with us,\" Dietrich continued, his golden eyes without pupils brightening with something like nostalgia. \" You remember Wachter Alaric, yes? He has been preparing for this responsibility since you departed. His dedication to your eventual return has been quite touching, actually.\"","Ubergulden Adelheid remained calm.","She had known this was coming when she agreed to return. She had understood what playing the role she had run away from would require. The ceremonies, the obligations, the chains disguised as honors that would bind her to a life she had abandoned precisely because it suffocated everything she actually wanted to be.","\" Let us just get this process started.\"","Her voice carried none of the turmoil that existed beneath her composed exterior. She had fully come back and committed to this path. Whatever personal feelings she held about Bonding, about Custodes, about becoming once again what her family demanded, those feelings were irrelevant now.","She had made her choice.","The three Sororis Prima moved forward with synchronized grace, their golden robes trailing across the floor like liquid infinity. They circled her floating lotus with slow deliberate steps, their eyes never leaving her form as they completed one rotation, then another.","\" The preliminary testing will now commence ,\" Sororis Prima Evangelina announced, her voice carrying the weight of ritual. \" Ubergulden Adelheid, daughter of one of the noble lines, you will remain still while we verify your readiness for the Bonding ceremony.\"","Illusory golden blades materialized in their hands.","The weapons shimmered with authority that could have unmade lesser beings through proximity alone. Each Sororis Prima raised her blade as they continued circling, the ritual taking form through movements practiced across countless ceremonies before this one.","Then, as one, they struck.","Three golden blades pierced the neck of Ubergulden Adelheid from different angles, passing through flesh that offered no resistance because the weapons weren’t meant to harm. They were meant to read. To perceive what existed within her on levels that normal examination couldn’t access.","Ubergulden Adelheid didn’t react.","She gazed on calmly and waited, her expression unchanged as the illusory blades remained embedded in her neck. This was standard procedure. This was what returning to her position required. She had known they would examine her, would verify that eons of living as Bounded hadn’t corrupted her engineering in ways that made the Bonding impossible.","She had covered everything with her power to make sure nothing would be found out.","But...","The calm expressions of the Magna Sorora began to shift.","Sororis Prima Evangelina’s brow furrowed slightly. Sororis Prima Konstanze’s stillness became rigid rather than relaxed. Sororis Prima Mathilde’s eyes widened by a fraction that most beings wouldn’t have noticed.","Confusion spread across their features.","Then shock.","Then anger.","They pulled back from Ubergulden Adelheid with sudden movements that shattered the ritual’s measured grace. Their golden blades dissolved as they retreated, their expressions now holding coldness that pressed against the room with force that made THE Gesinde throughout the space lower their heads instinctively as they kneeled!","\" She is already bound to a Custos!\"","BOOM!","Sororis Prima Evangelina’s voice cut through the silence like a blade far sharper than the illusory ones she had wielded.","\" She has undergone the Sundesmos ritual!\"","...!","The words fell into the room and detonated.","Ubergulden Dietrich’s expression transformed from warm anticipation to cold shock in the span of a single heartbeat. His golden eyes without pupils fixed on his sister with intensity that could have crushed thousands of Folds through attention alone!","The anger that followed came fast, displacing the shock before it had fully settled.","\" You...\"","His voice emerged low.","\" Who did you bind to? What have you done?!\"","He stepped toward her, his presence expanding with fury that made the three Sororis Prima retreat further despite their own considerable power because he knew where she had been thks whole time.","She had not been around Gilded so who could she have possibly become bound to? He already knew the answer as it was obscene!","\" Do you not know your position?! How you need someone strong to help you for what is coming?! Otherwise you won’t survive!\"","His hands clenched at his sides, golden light bleeding between his fingers.","\" Tell me, who... who is your Custos?\"","...!","Ubergulden Adelheid’s shock didn’t show on her face, but it cascaded through her existence!","She hadn’t undergone the Sundesmos ritual.","She hadn’t bound herself to any Custos.","She had lived as Bounded for eons, had suppressed her engineering, had existed without any of the connections that defined Gilded hierarchy. The Bonding ceremony today was supposed to be her first. There was no one. There couldn’t be anyone?","\"...\"","Motherfucker.","She placed her hand on her heart.","And she sensed the boundless Quintessence Infiniforce swirling within her, multicolored seas that belonged to someone who had somehow reached through unreachable weavings to communicate with her mere moments ago.","Fuck!","She stayed silent.","Because she didn’t know how to explain that her Custos, the Custodes she had bound...might be a Bounded Lifeform she had never actually chosen to bind herself to at all!","She could not explain this!"]},{"number":5117,"title":"Chapter 5117: Chapter 5116: THE First Infinite Scale! I","paragraphs":["As he utilized that connection to converse with Eon, or really, Ubergulden Adelheid, Noah hadn’t been sitting still.","There was something he had already been doing with another body as he received the declaration of the Civilizational Holy War from THE Deliverance. While one body had been focusing on the mass transformation of many of his people to become Nascent Hadean Lifeforms, another body had been giving specialized care to none other than Naldine Manthon.","She was a unique one due to her power.","He wanted to gauge exactly what Hadean would mean for someone at THE Second Scale, someone who had already established their Civilizational Anchor and wielded authority that most beings couldn’t comprehend. He also wanted to confirm his own capabilities in an area that made progression slightly more fun, an area that combined multiple hobbies he had cultivated across his journey.","The result was exemplary.","At this moment, Noah’s body was draped in a loose robe as he sat atop a flat grassland on a floating landmass. This small island was the only territory for light years in every direction, with radiant blue seas stretching endlessly around him. The waters churned with gentle currents that carried infinity in concentrations that would have overwhelmed most beings.","This realm had taken the qualities of Oceanus.","But the most striking feature wasn’t the sea around them. It was the sky above. A few miles high, what should have been atmosphere was actually another sea that stretched out endlessly, its waters suspended through principles that defied physics. Looking up meant looking into depths rather than heights, waves rolling across an inverted ocean that reflected the one below.","He was within a small island in such a place within THE Infiniverse.","The only other being present was adjusting her breathing while radiating terrifying power.","Naldine Manthon sat several meters away from him, her radiant white hair slightly messy from recent exertion. A white robe draped over her body in ways that suggested it had been hastily arranged. Her singularity-dotted eyes held something between disbelief and wonder as she examined her own existence.","Every single bone in her body pulsed with light.","Every single organ blazed with authority that pressed against the surrounding environment.","All of them had become Proterozoic through the process Noah had guided her through. This was the result of transforming her into a Nascent Hadean Lifeform while also carrying out their first session of Dual Cultivation, the combination of methodologies producing effects that exceeded what either would have achieved alone!","The golden crack on her forehead, that marking of Nascent Hadean classification, seemed to glow brighter than what he had observed on Barbatos or the others. Her white hair now held rivers of gold Observable Force threading through it like veins of precious metal through marble.","At this time, Naldine Manthon dripped with power dozens of times grander than her old self.","She raised her hand before her face, watching the light pulse through flesh that had been fundamentally altered. Her glistening bones became visible beneath her skin for a moment, crystalline structures that declared their Proterozoic nature without need for deeper examination. She shook her head as if she didn’t want to believe what she was perceiving.","Noah looked at her from the corner of his eyes.","Then he looked at the prompts detailing her changes.","|Naldine Manthon has successfully undergone Nascent Hadean transformation through your Existential Engineering capabilities combined with Dual Cultivation methodologies.|","| Skeletal Structure: Complete Proterozoic Transformation.|","|All 206 bones have attained Proterozoic distinctions through the infusion of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force during the transformation and Dual Cultivation process.|","| Organ Systems: Complete Proterozoic Transformation.|","|All 78 organs have attained Proterozoic distinctions through the same process. Her heart, lungs, brain, and other vital structures now process authority at rates that exceed her previous Calymmian-tier capabilities substantially.|","|As a Nascent Hadean Lifeform with Proterozoic Bones and Organs, she will have an easier time transforming them into Hadean Organs and Bones. The pathway has been established. The foundations have been laid. What remains is continued cultivation to complete the transformation you have initiated.|","|Dual Cultivation with the infusion of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force has been deemed to be the one of the quickest process for this progression. Each session will advance her transformation significantly compared to solo cultivation efforts.|","|Quintessence Infiniforce now flows stably across her existence. All aspects of her being are amplified through this integration. Her Civilization resonates with your Infinity.|","|Current Power Assessment: Her authority now exceeds any Calymmian Tier Proterozoic Scale entity by significant margins. Estimated equivalence has been calculated at Ediacaran Tier Proterozoic Scale parameters. However, she has not formally taken this step. The power exists without the classification having been officially established.|","|Additionally, due to her position at Vakochev’s Second Scale combined with Nascent Hadean classification, she now has access to a capability I shall designate as Hadean Infinity of Development .|","|This capability allows her to focus intensive development on specific aspects of her existence, producing accelerated results in chosen areas. She can currently utilize this capability a total of three times. New generations will be produced over time as she develops further.|","|Focus options for Hadean Infinity of Development include but are not limited to: Civilization advancement and refinement, study and usage of Pulses, physical capability enhancement, perception expansion, or any other relevant aspect of her existence she wishes to prioritize.|","...!","The results with Naldine were astounding.","Even she didn’t seem to believe it. She continued examining her hand, watching the light pulse through bones that had been ordinary by Primordial Architect standards mere hours ago.","She shook her head slowly.","\" Fuck.\"","Noah looked over and blinked at the single word that emerged from her mouth. His expression shifted to something that might have been innocent confusion if one didn’t know him better.","\"I thought you wanted to rest a bit, but okay.\"","...!","He said such words as if he were an unwilling participant being asked to resume activities he had only begrudgingly engaged in!","As if the Dual Cultivation had been entirely her idea and he was simply accommodating her requests out of politeness.","Naldine looked toward him with cold eyes that held dangerous promise.","\" You stay back. You’ve done enough!\"","Her voice carried authority that pressed against the island they occupied, waves in the surrounding seas responding to her displeasure by churning more violently.","\"I need to gauge myself first to make sure you have not infused me with THE Gamaidjan...\"","She looked at her other hand, then back to him with suspicion.","\" This much Infinity swirling in one’s existence... how can you possibly not go mad? Is your Infinity different than the Infinity the rest of us know and use?\""]},{"number":5118,"title":"Chapter 5118: Chapter 5117: THE First Infinite Scale! II","paragraphs":["Was his Infinity different compared to others?","Who could say. He had touched Infinity when he was nothing but a human throwing fireballs. He had integrated it so thoroughly into his existence that separation seemed impossible now. Perhaps the very act of claiming it so early, before he understood what he was grasping, had changed both him and what Infinity meant within his existence.","Noah rose up and stretched, his loose robe shifting around a body that blazed with Hadean authority.","\" After cycling through my existence, maybe I tame the Infinity you all know entirely and make it something else. Maybe that’s why I can fill myself and others with it, and no madness comes.\"","He looked toward Naldine with eyes that shone like singularities.","\" But forget that. Use your Hadean Infinity of Development. See if you can rapidly transform your Proterozoic Bones to Hadean Bones.\"","...!","He was initially going to ask her what she knew about going from Calymmian to Ediacaran. That knowledge could have been valuable, would have given him insight into how Primordial Architects structured their progression through the tiers of THE Second Scale.","But he didn’t want to be influenced too much on his own progression.","He was choosing to go in a direction that was entirely his own. Vakochev’s Scales had served as a useful framework for understanding where others stood, but they weren’t his framework. They weren’t designed to account for what he was becoming. They weren’t built to measure someone who held Hadean classification while still technically at THE First Scale.","What he wanted to do now was complex and simple all at once.","\" Ruination, let me see an outline of the ninth potential First Infinite Scale progression we’ve designed.\"","...!","Yes.","He had actually made blueprints of nine potential systems of progression and tweaked things as he went. Each iteration refined the concepts, eliminated redundancies, and brought him closer to something that felt right. He wanted to stop at the ninth one because otherwise he felt like he would have continued going until the eighty-first potential system design, and that much deliberation would have consumed time he didn’t have.","The declaration of Civilizational Holy War pressed against the back of his mind. Twenty-four hours. Less now. Every moment spent designing was a moment not spent preparing his people for what was coming!","But this design would determine everything that followed.","|Displaying the ninth iteration of THE First Infinite Scale of Existence.|","Ruination’s voice emerged as golden light coalesced before him, forming diagrams and notations that outlined his vision.","|You have structured your First Infinite Scale into three major demarcations, each representing a distinct phase of development before officially stepping toward what you will design later as THE Second Infinite Scale.|","|The foundational pillars of this progression are Infinity through Quintessence Infiniforce, Observable Force, and Civilizations as actualized building blocks through THE First Tongue.|","| First Demarcation: Infinitas Corpus, The Infinite Body.|","|This is where you currently stand at the peak. Your entire skeletal structure and organ systems have achieved Hadean classification. Your grasp of Infinity exists at the level of Uncountable Infinity, which saturates every aspect of your being without limit or boundary.|","|The requirements for completing this demarcation are: Full Hadean transformation of all 206 bones and 78 organs, stable integration of Uncountable Infinity throughout existence, and the capacity to channel both Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force simultaneously without conflict.|","| You have fulfilled all requirements. The First Demarcation is complete.|","| Second Demarcation: Infinitas Architectura, The Infinite Architecture.|","|This phase focuses on the construction of a singular internal structure that will serve as the foundation for everything that follows. You will build a Hadean Pillar of Infinity within your existence.|","|This single Pillar differs from conventional cultivation foundations in a critical way. Rather than constructing multiple separate pillars for different authorities, you will construct one Pillar that can be built up by as many Civilizations as you can actualize within it.|","|Through THE First Tongue, you can currently access and embody any Civilization temporarily. Infinitas Architectura requires you to move beyond temporary access toward permanent actualization. Each Civilization you congeal into stable form becomes another layer of your Hadean Pillar of Infinity, another foundation stone supporting the structure you are building.|","|There is no upper limit to how many Civilizations can be integrated into your Hadean Pillar. The more Civilizations you actualize within it, the grander and more stable the Pillar becomes. Observable Force serves as the binding agent holding these actualized Civilizations together. Quintessence Infiniforce serves as the animating principle that allows them to function as a unified whole rather than separate fragments.|","|THE Infiniverse can contribute to this process. Her own Hadean transformation provides templates for how internal structures can be organized. As her backbone becomes Hadean, resonance between your existences will accelerate the construction of your Pillar.|","| To complete this demarcation and progress to the third, you must achieve Absolute Infinity . This represents Infinity that has transcended mere uncountability to become self-referential and complete. Absolute Infinity can observe itself, can contain itself, can become both the container and the contained...well, potentially, we still dont know. Only when your grasp of Infinity reaches this level will the transition to your third demarcation become possible.|","| Third Demarcation: Infinitas Causa, The Infinite Cause.|","|This is the final phase of THE First Infinite Scale.|","|Having constructed your Hadean Pillar of Infinity and achieved Absolute Infinity, this demarcation focuses on the full comprehension and actualization of THE Infinite Cause that defines your existence. The chain of your Cause runs from your birth through your Infinity through the Seed of Observable Existence. This chain must be understood completely.|","|Your Hadean Pillar of Infinity must be saturated with the authority of your Cause. Every Civilization actualized within it must resonate with the fundamental truth of your emergence. The Pillar becomes not merely a structure of power but a monument to THE Infinite Cause itself.|","|Upon completing Infinitas Causa, you will stand at the peak of THE First Infinite Scale.|","|However, transition to THE Second Infinite Scale requires one final advancement.|","|Transcendent Infinity.|","|This level of Infinity lies beyond Absolute Infinity and can only potentially be attained during the transition itself. Transcendent Infinity represents Infinity that has become indistinguishable from Causality.|","|This advancement cannot be achieved while remaining at THE First Infinite Scale. It is the bridge between Scales, the transformation that marks the difference between standing at the peak and stepping beyond it.|","|I should note that this ninth iteration represents significant refinement over previous versions. Earlier designs attempted to incorporate too many separate structures, creating frameworks that would have been powerful but fragmented. This version maintains elegance through unity. One Pillar. Unlimited Civilizations. Infinity as the foundation for everything.|","...!"]},{"number":5119,"title":"Chapter 5119: Chapter 5118: THE First Infinite Scale! III","paragraphs":["He wanted to design his First Scale to be straightforward, intuitive, and unique but not overly complex.","So everything he had done up to this point, all the transformations and integrations and impossible advancements, he neatly put a bow on it and called it Infinitas Corpus, The Infinite Body. He had achieved the apex of this stage. Or at least it was what most would consider to be the apex of THE First Scale.","Even though he could use its power to fight against entities at THE Second Scale of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.","And when he advanced from Infinitas Corpus, he would only be on the second level of his own Scale of Existence. He couldn’t quite say exactly where his power would be after that advancement, couldn’t predict what completing Infinitas Architectura would mean in practical terms. THE Deliverance would be a good and fearsome enemy to test things out against when the time came.","But right now, since he had the outline, he would begin implementing it.","When designing his own Scale, he didn’t want it to be something as convoluted as what others in the old worlds and realms he had passed through theorized about systems of power. Nothing as crazy as building his Scales with stages like Void Refining, Body Integration, Mahayana, and some kind of Tribulation!","No.","That was too much!","Infinitas Corpus, Infinitas Architectura, Infinitas Causa.","Three demarcations. One Pillar. Unlimited potential.","And right now...","\"I have been stuck on this level for too long.\"","Noah’s voice emerged with conviction that pressed against the surrounding environment.","\"Has it already been a day? A few days? Far too long!\"","His eyes blazed brighter as he rose from his seated position.","\"I shall advance toward Infinitas Architectura where Absolute Infinity awaits.\"","HUUM!","...!","The island he occupied began to tremble beneath forces that transcended physical causation.","He rose from the grassland and floated upward, his body lifting through air that grew thicker with authority as he ascended. He rose to the midpoint of this realm, that space where the endless blue sea below mirrored the endless blue sea above. Two oceans stretching infinitely in opposite directions, and he floated between them like a singular point of purpose suspended in aquatic infinity.","His eyes were unfathomably bright as he considered what he was about to attempt.","So far, it was just ideas. Even though they were ideas he had refined through nine iterations of careful design, nobody had told Noah they would work. They might succeed brilliantly. They might fail catastrophically. There was no precedent for what he was doing because no one had ever done it before.","He was a Pioneer.","He was carving this path himself, and if he went wrong anywhere, it would be very costly. There were no teachers to correct his mistakes, no ancient texts describing how to construct a Hadean Pillar of Infinity, no accumulated wisdom from countless practitioners who had walked this road before him.","There was only him.","So...","\" Infinitas Architectura.\"","He called out the name as his body began generating even more endless Quintessence Infiniforce. Blue Infinity gathered all around him in concentrations that would have driven most beings to madness. Observable Force formed into golden rivers that circled his position.","The construction of a singular internal structure that would serve as the foundation for everything that followed.","He would build a Hadean Pillar of Infinity within his existence.","Rather than constructing multiple separate pillars for different authorities, he would create a single Pillar that could be built up by as many Civilizations as he could actualize within it. Each Civilization he congealed into stable form would become another layer of the Hadean Pillar of Infinity, another foundation stone supporting the structure he was building.","Observable Force would be the binding agent holding these actualized Civilizations together. Quintessence Infiniforce would serve as the animating principle allowing them to function as a unified whole rather than separate fragments.","He made sure he understood everything well.","Then he took a step.","The motion seemed mundane. One foot lifting, moving forward through space, descending toward a surface that existed only in concept rather than physical reality. It was a step that anyone could take, a movement so basic that infants learned it within their first year of life.","But with this step, this entire realm became bathed in blue and gold and multicolored brilliance.","Infinite seas surged into that single motion. Every drop of Observable Force he had access to, every mote of Quintessence Infiniforce his existence generated, every trace of authority he could muster flowed into the act of bringing his foot down.","When it landed, something within him shattered.","BOOM !","A barrier he hadn’t known existed broke apart, and what emerged from behind it defied description.","A single massive Pillar rose up from within his existence.","It stretched out in this realm first, its base forming somewhere in the depths of his Hadean Organ of Civilization before expanding outward in all directions. The Pillar passed through this Oceanus-like domain without disturbing the twin seas above and below, its form somehow existing alongside physical reality rather than displacing it.","Then it stretched further.","Past other thousands of realms across THE Infiniverse, the Pillar extended. Through territories that held sacred herbs and tumultuous seas and floating landmasses of every description. THE Infiniverse trembled as this construct rose through her depths, her humanoid manifestation opening her eyes with surprise as something vast moved through her very being.","The Pillar rose out of THE Infiniverse entirely.","It emerged into THE Wastes. The multicolored rain of THE Pluvial Epoch fell upon its surface as it continued stretching upward, higher and higher, showing no signs of stopping.","Infinitely.","The Pillar was grand beyond comprehension, its surface blazing with multicolored light that shifted through every hue existence had ever named. Golden bands wrapped around its circumference at irregular intervals, patterns of Observable Force that served as binding agents even as they contributed to its beauty.","But for all its grandeur, the Pillar was hollow.","Its interior waited to be filled. The Civilizations that would form its layers had not yet been actualized. The structure existed, but its contents remained potential rather than actual. It was a monument waiting for meaning, a foundation waiting for what would be built upon it.","The Pillar crossed THE Wastes and continued rising.","It flashed momentarily in different Primordial Realms, its illusory form manifesting wherever existence permitted its passage. Beings across countless territories looked up as something impossible bloomed across their skies, a Pillar that seemed to connect the lowest depths to the highest heights while belonging to neither!","It even manifested across Prima Indifferentia.","That region of Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors and Primordial Architects witnessed the Pillar’s passage through their domain, ancient consciousnesses stirring with confusion at something they couldn’t categorize. The white gold sea that defined their home rippled with disturbance that had nothing to do with current or tide.","On this day, across Observable Existence, an Infinite Pillar bloomed momentarily!","Many witnessed it!","And they wondered.","What the fuck is that?!","---","THE Wyld stretched endlessly in ways that defied sanity.","This region existed as the true home of Primordial Architects, but \"home\" implied comfort that THE Wyld did not provide. It was a realm of primal power and ancient danger, where the line between hunter and hunted shifted with each passing moment. Survival here required strength that most beings couldn’t comprehend.","THE Creature stood within a forest that looked like something from primeval times.","Trees rose hundreds of meters high, their bark cracite with age of THE First Cause. Branches intertwined overhead in canopies so thick that whatever passed for sky in THE Wyld remained invisible. Bioluminescent fungi clung to trunks and roots, providing illumination that painted everything in shades of ethereal green and deep violet.","Abundant existential energy saturated every molecule of this forest.","Just breathing here would have advanced most First Scale beings through multiple stages of cultivation. The concentration of authority pressed against everything with density that made the richest regions of normal Observable Existence seem impoverished by comparison. This was why Primordial Architects thrived in THE Wyld despite its dangers. The rewards matched the risks.","Milky gold rivers of light and blood flowed around the small clearing where THE Creature stood.","The liquid wasn’t water. It was something between Observable Force and vital fluid, the runoff from conflicts that had occurred in this location recently. Very recently!","The blood was still warm, still carrying traces of authority from beings who had been alive mere minutes ago.","Seven Primordial Architects lay scattered around the clearing.","Their bodies were arranged in positions that spoke of desperate combat and sudden defeat. Some had fallen while trying to flee. Others had died mid-attack, their offensive postures frozen by death before they could complete their strikes. Three bore Rhyacian Tier classifications based on their residual authority. Four had been Calymmian.","All of them were dead now!","Anaximander stood near the edge of the clearing with his arms crossed at all this violence.","Tairiyya floated nearby. She said nothing, but her attention remained fixed on their leader.","THE Creature himself knelt beside one of the fallen Calymmian entities.","His hands were buried wrist-deep in the corpse’s chest cavity, having torn through Proterozoic Bones and flesh to reach what lay beneath. Blood coated his arms up to the elbows, thick and dark and still carrying warmth from the life it had recently supported. His expression held nothing but focus as he worked.","He pulled out a heart.","The organ was massive, and it pulsed with residual authority despite its owner’s death. Proterozoic classification had transformed it into something far beyond mere muscle and blood vessels. It was a repository of power, a concentrated source of everything its original owner had cultivated across eons of existence!","THE Creature brought it to his mouth and bit! He chewed slowly and deliberately, savoring the authority that flooded into his existence with each swallow.","When he finished the heart, he reached back into the corpse for other organs.","Lungs came next, their Proterozoic structure providing different flavors of authority than the heart had offered. Then the liver. Then the kidneys. Each organ consumed added to what THE Creature was becoming, each bite pushing him further along whatever path he had chosen when he burned away his Primordial Architect classification!","It was during this brutal feast that the sky above THE Wyld changed.","THE Creature raised his head, blood dripping from his chin as his eyes fixed on something that hadn’t been there moments before.","An illusory Pillar stretched across the sky!","Multicolored and banded with gold, it rose from somewhere far below and extended toward heights that even THE Wyld’s strange geometry couldn’t contain. The Pillar blazed with power that pressed against everything nearby!","Anaximander looked up at the same moment, his eyes widening with surprise.","\" What... is that?\"","THE Creature studied the Pillar for several long seconds as if he could see things others couldn’t.","Blood continued dripping from his chin as a smile spread across his features.","\" It burns with Infinity.\"","He looked at Anaximander with eyes that held fire from a recently used THE Silurian Light.","\" So it may just be the one you continue to worry about that I tell you not to worry about.\"","...!","Anaximander blinked at this assessment, his surprise deepening as he looked back toward the Pillar still blazing across the sky.","THE Creature returned his attention to the corpse before him, reaching for another organ as he continued.","\" When pushed, when bullied, when adversity presses down and down without mercy or pause...\"","He tore out what might have been a Proterozoic spleen and examined it with clinical interest.","\"It can awaken a bloody beast within. And that bloody beast may become its own adversity for those who thought themselves the predators.\"","His smile grew sharper.","He bit into the spleen, chewing thoughtfully.","\" Adversity breeds greatness. I still wait to see if Erwin will bloom into something astounding from my pressure...\"","...!","THE Creature returned to his eating with renewed focus, the Pillar above beginning to fade as whatever power had manifested it settled back into its source. The illusory structure grew translucent, then ghostly, then disappeared entirely as if it had never been there at all.","But everyone who had seen it would remember.","Everyone who had witnessed it would wonder!","Anaximander threw his head back and laughed.","The sound rang out across the primeval forest with joy that seemed inappropriate given the corpses surrounding them, but it was genuine!"]},{"number":5120,"title":"Chapter 5120: Chapter 5119: THE First Infinite Scale! IV","paragraphs":["As he looked at the Pillar that stretched out endlessly, Noah felt something fundamental shift within his existence.","It was as if he had opened floodgates he hadn’t known were closed. The concentration of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force within him, which had seemed almost full mere moments ago, now felt like it could expand countless more times. His capacity hadn’t merely increased. The very concept of capacity had changed, transforming from a finite container into something that could grow without boundary!","This was what he had been missing.","This was what standing at the supposed peak of THE First Scale had denied him. A ceiling he couldn’t perceive had been pressing down on his potential, limiting what he could hold and channel and become. Now that ceiling was gone, shattered by the construction of something that had never existed before.","This was Infinitas Architectura!","But not really. Not yet!","Because he hadn’t begun building.","The Hadean Pillar of Infinity held infinite potential, but it was currently hollow. A grand structure with no contents. A monument to what could be rather than what was. Its multicolored surface blazed with authority that came from its nature rather than its substance, potential rather than actualization.","Noah waved his hand.","The Pillar’s endless nature, which had stretched across all of Observable Existence moments before, began to fade.","What remained was a Pillar the height of this Oceanus-like realm he occupied, its form contained within THE Infiniverse rather than bleeding across everything that existed.","He looked down.","On the island far below, between the twin seas that stretched above and beneath, Naldine was looking up with a stern expression. Her singularity-dotted eyes studied the Pillar with attention that held something between analysis and wariness. She was trying to gauge his power, trying to understand what she had just witnessed!","Let her wonder.","Inside that blinding hollow Pillar of Infinity, Noah floated toward its base.","The interior was vast beyond comprehension, space that somehow existed within his existence while also occupying physical territory in the realm around him. The walls curved away in every direction, multicolored surfaces that awaited the Civilizations he would actualize upon them. But the floor was where everything would begin. The foundation upon which all else would be built.","\" At the base of all of it will be Mana.\"","His voice emerged with conviction that pressed against the hollow interior.","\" THE First Tongue.\"","HUUM!","The base of this glorious Pillar would have nothing except the one thing he had always possessed. The one constant across every transformation, every advancement, every impossible achievement.","THE First Tongue had been his Civilization before he knew what Civilizations were.","It would be his foundation now.","Noah knelt down at the base of his Pillar.","From his hands, endless blue light permeated outward. It wasn’t mere illumination but something far more fundamental, the very essence of what THE First Tongue represented made visible through his intention. Infinite absolute Seals began manifesting around him, weavings of authority that represented the twenty-seven Phonemes that comprised the foundational language of existence.","They gushed out endlessly, these Seals, as if they were seeds being planted on the very base of this Pillar of Infinity.","The twenty-seven letters formed into Logos. Into words. They mixed into each other countless times, creating variations and combinations that multiplied beyond what simple mathematics could describe. Each Phoneme touched each other Phoneme, creating new meanings. Those meanings combined with other meanings, creating concepts. Philologies and Archai bloomed!","Those concepts intertwined with other concepts, creating authorities.","As if the seeds were blooming, the entire basal region of the Pillar began to transform.","Illusory blue seeds sprouted from the floor. They pushed upward through nothing, through potential space that hadn’t existed until they needed it to exist. Saplings emerged from those seeds, their forms crystalline and luminous, their branches reaching toward the hollow heights above. The saplings flourished into trees, their growth accelerating past what any natural process could achieve.","A forest of THE First Tongue rose around Noah.","The color blue began rising in concentration all around him. It climbed past his knees, his waist, his chest. It exceeded his height and continued climbing, the forest growing denser and grander with each passing moment. Trees of language stretched toward the Pillar’s interior heights, their branches heavy with words that hadn’t been spoken yet, their leaves inscribed with meanings that most beings couldn’t comprehend.","At the very peak of all of it, something began to form.","A radiant Grimoire of Hadean Lexicons bloomed into existence .","The book was massive, its cover blazing with multicolored light that declared its nature without need for explanation. Its pages fluttered endlessly, never settling on a single configuration, each flutter revealing new words and new meanings and new possibilities. It was the actualization of THE First Tongue.","The moment this occurred, everything changed.","Rivers of golden Observable Force surged into this basal floor from somewhere beyond the Pillar’s walls. Observable Force rushed toward the actualized Civilization with purpose that felt almost desperate. It permeated across everything, across every tree and every branch and every leaf and every word.","The Pillar of Infinity began to shine unfathomably bright.","| THE Hadean Pillar of Infinity has been established.|","Ruination’s voice emerged with wonder!","|The first Civilization has been actualized within its structure. THE First Tongue now exists as a permanent foundation. Its power flows through your Pillar continuously, contributing to everything built upon it.|","| You have officially stepped onto Infinitas Architectura, The Infinite Architecture, of THE First Infinite Scale of Existence.|","|Your methodology has officially begun pioneering something new.|","|You deviate from Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.|","...!","The words were grand ones.","Noah’s body inside his Pillar of Infinity radiated blinding light of brilliance that pressed against the crystalline forest surrounding him. His eyes shot out multicolored pillars of light that reached toward the Grimoire floating at the peak of his actualized foundation. Every aspect of his existence resonated with what he had just achieved.","Officially on his own path!","Deviating from Vakochev’s Scales of Existence!","At this point...","| Error.|","HUUM!","Ruination’s voice buzzed with caution that hadn’t been present moments before.","|New weavings of information from a foreign source incoming. Unable to stop them.|","...!","Noah’s eyes became sharp as he sensed something pressing against his consciousness from outside.","Momentarily, Ruination’s voice and prompts faded. Her presence retreated as if pushed aside by something that possessed authority she couldn’t contest. In front of his eyes, in blue-bordered boxes and radiant blue letters that differed from Ruination’s golden notifications, new prompts bloomed.","A voice accompanied them.","It felt deep and ancient and heavy, carrying the weight of someone who had observed existence across spans that made eons seem like heartbeats. It wasn’t threatening. It wasn’t aggressive!","It simply was, the way mountains simply were, the way oceans simply were!","|...The path you have taken is an arduous and difficult one.|","The voice pressed against his consciousness with intensity!","|But it is welcomed.|","A pause that felt like centuries compressed into moments.","|The only thing I can tell you is to Persevere. Everything will stand in your way, but Persevere. Existence itself will oppose you, but Persevere. Enemies will seek your destruction, but Persevere. Allies will doubt your methods, but Persevere. Even family may stand in your way, questioning whether your path leads anywhere worth reaching.|","The voice grew heavier.","|Still, Persevere.|","Another pause.","|Osmont, right? Against all odds, against every force that will try to crush what you are building, against the weight of how things have always been...|","The ancient voice carried something that might have been respect.","|I, Vakochev, can only advise you to Persevere. And just maybe, if you succeed, I will see you in that place.|","The final word emerged with weight that shook his existence to its foundations.","|PERSEVERE!|","BOOM!","When that deep and ancient voice finished, Noah found his brows covered with sweat that shouldn’t have been possible for a Hadean Lifeform to produce!","His eyes shone fiercely as he processed what had just occurred. His nose breathed out flames of Infinity that scorched the crystalline trees nearest to him.","He...fully felt it now.","He had lost any connection he had with Vakochev’s Scales of Existence.","The framework that had governed power across Existence since before most current beings were born no longer applied to him. He couldn’t be measured by its standards because he had chosen to reject those standards entirely. The Scales that told everyone else where they stood and how far they had to go would tell him nothing.","He was very much alone.","A Pioneer, on his own!"]},{"number":5121,"title":"Chapter 5121: Chapter 5120: Advancement! I","paragraphs":["It is lonely at the top.","Such words have been uttered across countless civilizations and eons, spoken by beings who climbed higher than their peers and found themselves standing alone in territories no one else could reach!","But the loneliness of achievement pales in comparison to the loneliness of pioneering.","Those who reach the top of established paths at least have the comfort of knowing others have stood where they stand. They can look down and see the trail that led them upward, they can identify the footprints of predecessors who validated their journey through completion. They are alone in position but not in experience.","Pioneers have no such comfort.","They walk paths that do not exist until their feet touch ground. They climb mountains that have no peaks until they declare a stopping point. Every step is a question without a guaranteed answer, every advancement a gamble that could end in triumph or catastrophe with equal probability.","Who else can share their vision? By definition, no one!","No one!","If others could see what they see, the path would already exist. The Pioneer’s curse is to perceive possibilities that remain invisible to everyone else, to feel compelled toward destinations that others cannot even imagine. They speak of what they’re building and receive blank stares in return, confusion from those who cannot comprehend why anyone would abandon the safety of established routes.","And when Pioneers succeed, when they carve paths that others will eventually follow, those who come after will never understand what was required. They will walk the completed road and see only the road. They will not see the false starts, the collapsed tunnels, the chasms that nearly swallowed the one who built this passage. They will not know how many times the Pioneer considered turning back, how many moments of despair preceded each breakthrough, how much blood and sweat and tears soaked into foundations that now appear solid and inevitable.","The path will seem obvious in retrospect.","\"Of course this was possible,\" they will say. \"Of course someone would eventually do this.\"","But the Pioneer knew nothing was obvious. The Pioneer knew that \"eventually\" almost became \"never\" countless times during the construction. The Pioneer carries scars that the path’s future travelers will never see and could never appreciate!","This is the price of going first.","This...is what it means to be alone.","—","Noah felt a sense of emptiness settle into his existence.","It wasn’t pain or fear, just absence. He had belonged to some structure he couldn’t perceive before, some framework that had given him meaning and definition without his awareness. Vakochev’s Scales had been there like gravity, invisible but constant, telling him where he stood in relation to everything else. Now that definition was gone.","He could fall or stumble at any moment. There were no more markers telling him which direction was up. There was no more system declaring whether his next step would be advancement or regression. He floated in conceptual void where measurement itself had ceased to apply.","But in this lost sensation, he felt something else!","A glimmer of Infinity rising within him.","HUUM!","Infinity helped him up. Infinity kept him stable. The very foundation he had chosen to build upon refused to let him collapse into the emptiness that threatened to swallow him. It pressed against the void with authority that declared emptiness was just another form of potential, and potential was something Infinity understood intimately.","Because even though he did not have Vakochev’s Scales of Existence anymore, he was now forging his Infinite Scales of Existence!","His own framework. His own definitions. His own meaning!","HUUM!","Noah rose up sternly within his Hadean Pillar of Infinity.","He floated above the level where THE First Tongue had been actualized, past the crystalline forest of blue trees and the Grimoire of Hadean Lexicons that crowned its peaks. The foundation was complete. Now came the construction that would fill this hollow monument with substance worthy of its potential.","He looked upward toward the vast empty space that awaited the next Civilization.","\" Existence.\"","His voice emerged calm and measured.","Below him, the actualized First Tongue responded to his call.","Blue Mana began flowing upward from the forest of language like endless water rising against gravity. It climbed through the Pillar’s interior in streams that wove around each other, rivers of THE First Tongue ascending toward the level where Noah floated. The blue light was beautiful in its purity, carrying the foundational authority of the language that underpinned all of reality.","Then it began to transform.","The blue started bubbling as if heated by invisible flames. Colors emerged from within the azure streams, reds and golds and greens and violets bleeding outward from cores that had been uniform moments before. The Mana was being elevated, THE First Tongue serving as the base material from which something grander would be forged.","The Civilization of Existence manifested as endlessly rising multicolored flames.","They didn’t burn the way normal fire burned. They declared that things were rather than were not. The flames rose in columns and curtains and spiraling towers, their heat carrying the warmth of reality itself pressing against the void of non-being. It looked like a forge! A cosmic forge where existence itself was hammered into shape from raw potential.","When the actualization completed, the second level of his Pillar blazed with authority that made THE First Tongue seem gentle by comparison.","Noah floated within those multicolored flames without discomfort.","\" Existence...is not separate from Infinity ,\" he said, his tone thoughtful and precise. \" Infinity makes Existence possible by providing the endless potential from which reality emerges. And Existence gives Infinity meaning by actualizing that potential into something that matters. They need each other. One without the other is incomplete.\"","He paused, watching the flames dance around him.","\" This is why they belong in the same Pillar. They are not separate foundations competing for primacy, they are aspects of the same fundamental truth. The Oldest Paradox understood this. I understand it now.\"","HUUM!","The flames of Existence settled into stable weavings as Observable Force and Infinity surged through them, golden rivers binding this second Civilization to the first. The Pillar grew brighter, its hollow interior now holding two levels of actualized authority stacked upon each other.","Noah rose higher.","He passed through the multicolored flames of Existence, their heat parting around him like water around a stone. Above them, more empty space awaited. More potential crying out for actualization! More levels to be built before his Pillar would approach anything resembling completion.","\" Paradox.\"","The word emerged with the same deliberation he had used before.","Below, THE First Tongue and Existence responded together.","Blue Mana rose from the forest of language, climbing through the flames of Existence and absorbing their multicolored authority as it passed. The streams that emerged above the second level held both the foundational nature of THE First Tongue and the creative heat of Existence, combined into something that vibrated with tension between contradictory states.","The transformation began differently this time.","Rather than bubbling into new colors, the ascending streams started splitting. Each river of combined authority divided into two rivers flowing in opposite directions while somehow remaining in the same space. They contradicted themselves visually, logically, fundamentally. They were and were not. They moved and remained still. They existed in multiple states simultaneously because Paradox refused to accept that only one state could be true.","The Civilization of Paradox manifested as infinite reflections facing each other.","Mirrors made of crystallized contradiction stretched across this level of the Pillar, each one showing images that shouldn’t have been possible. Noah saw himself in one mirror as a human throwing fireballs. In another, as THE Youngest standing before a shadowy THE Deliverance. In a third, as something he hadn’t become yet, forms that existed only in potential futures that may or may not arrive. All of them were him. None of them were him. The Paradox refused to resolve!","Oh!","\" Paradox...is Infinity’s closest sibling,\" Noah observed, his voice steady despite the impossible reflections surrounding him. \" Both reject limitation. Both insist that boundaries are suggestions rather than laws. The difference is that Infinity achieves the impossible by having no end, while Paradox achieves it by holding contradictions together until they stop being contradictions.\"","He looked at a mirror showing himself failing, then at one showing himself succeeding.","\"I’ve learned to appreciate Paradox. It taught me that being weak and strong simultaneously is...a grand strategy.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5122,"title":"Chapter 5122: Chapter 5121: Advancement! II","paragraphs":["The mirrors of Paradox settled, their contradictions stabilizing into patterns that shouldn’t have been stable. Infinity and Observable Force flowed through them, blue and golden binding agents connecting this third level to everything below. The Pillar blazed brighter still.","Noah rose again.","Three levels complete. One more to go before the foundation of his Hadean Pillar of Infinity would hold all four Aspects of THE Oldest Paradox in Existence!","\" Chaos.\"","The final word fell into the Pillar’s interior with weight that belied its simple pronunciation.","Everything below responded.","Blue Mana from THE First Tongue. Multicolored flames from Existence. Contradictory reflections from Paradox. All of it rose together, streams and fires and mirrors ascending in combinations that grew more unstable with each passing moment. The authority climbing toward this final level held everything that had come before, all the foundational aspects combining into something that threatened to tear itself apart at any moment.","That was the point.","The transformation was violent!","Chaotic!","The ascending authority didn’t bubble or split. It exploded. It collapsed. It reformed in configurations that lasted milliseconds before shattering into new configurations equally temporary. Nothing held. Nothing stabilized. Nothing accepted the concept of permanence because Chaos refused to acknowledge that anything should remain the same for longer than it chose to.","The Civilization of Chaos manifested as an eternal storm.","Lightning made of pure possibility arced between clouds made of dissolved certainty. Winds carrying fragments of reality that had been torn apart howled through this level of the Pillar without pattern or purpose. Everything was destruction. Everything was creation!","The distinction between the two ceased to exist because Chaos saw no difference between breaking and building.","Noah stood at the center of the storm, his Hadean body untouched by devastation that would have erased lesser beings.","\" Chaos is what Infinity looks like when you remove all the rules.\" His voice cut through the howling winds with calm that seemed inappropriate. \" Pure potential without direction. Endless possibility without preference. Most beings fear Chaos because they need structure to feel safe. I’ve learned that Chaos isn’t the enemy of structure. It’s the raw material from which structure is built.\"","He watched reality fragment and reform around him.","\" You can’t create anything truly new from order alone. You need Chaos to break the old patterns before new ones can emerge. THE Oldest Paradox understood this. Chaos isn’t the end. It’s the beginning that never stops beginning.\"","HUUM!","The storm of Chaos settled into patterns that weren’t really patterns, stable instability that somehow maintained itself through constant change.","The Pillar blazed with brilliance that could have blinded beings across multiple realms.","Noah floated upward.","He rose above the Hadean Pillar of Infinity and looked down at what he had built.","At its base, the crystalline forest of THE First Tongue spread blue light upward. Above that, the multicolored flames of Existence burned in their cosmic forge. Higher still, the contradictory mirrors of Paradox reflected impossibilities. And at the current peak, the eternal storm of Chaos raged without end.","The four Aspects of THE Oldest Paradox in Existence now lay within his Pillar.","THE First Tongue. Existence. Paradox. Chaos.","The foundational Civilizations that had defined power across Observable Existence since before most current beings were born. The Aspects that separated true claimants of THE Oldest Paradox from everyone else.","All of them, actualized within his Hadean Pillar of Infinity!","All of them, permanently integrated rather than temporarily accessed.","Noah looked upon this with a calm gaze, his expression holding satisfaction but not arrogance. What he had built was grand, but grandness wasn’t the point. Utility was the point. Foundation was the point!","Everything that followed would be built upon this, and everything that followed would determine whether his Infinite Scales of Existence meant anything at all.","\" What came first?\"","His voice emerged, posing the question to himself.","\" THE First Tongue? Existence? Paradox? Chaos? Everyone wants to know which foundation is the true foundation, which beginning is the real beginning.\"","He looked at his Pillar, at the four levels stacked upon each other in the order he had chosen.","\" But they’re asking the wrong question.\"","His eyes blazed like singularities.","\"I emerged first before ushering them in. My will actualized them in the order I chose. My authority gave them form within my existence. THE Infinite Cause came first, and the rest of them followed. They exist in my Pillar because I put them there. They serve my progression because I decided they would!\"","His voice remained steady, as if he were simply stating facts!","\" The answer to what came first is always the same. The one doing the building came first. Everything else is just material.\"","BOOM!","Noah flew upward through his Hadean Pillar of Infinity, leaving the four foundational Civilizations behind as he rose toward the vast hollow space that awaited filling.","The base was complete! But foundations were just beginnings. What he built upon them would determine whether his Infinite Scales of Existence meant anything at all.","He didn’t slow down.","\" The Civilization of Quintessence.\"","The words left his mouth as blue and multicolored authority surged upward from below, answering his call before he finished speaking. The actualization happened faster than it had with the foundational Aspects, his Pillar learning what he wanted and responding with increasing efficiency!","Quintessence settled into place as a layer of crystallized colorless potential, shimmering with authority.","He rose higher without pause.","\" Loot.\"","Another layer actualized, this one manifesting as cascading streams of golden abundance that flowed endlessly without depleting. The Civilization that had defined so much of his early journey, that had given him access to rewards others couldn’t dream of claiming, now became permanent foundation within his existence!","\" Cheats.\"","The layer that formed held configurations that shouldn’t have been stable, rules bent into shapes that favored him specifically. It settled into his Pillar with the comfortable familiarity of an old companion.","\" Protagonist.\"","A layer of narrative weight, of causality that leaned in his direction, of events arranging themselves around his presence rather than despite it. This Civilization had been with him since before he understood what Civilizations were.","Noah continued ascending, his voice steady and unhurried despite the speed of his construction.","\" Manadynamics. Relativity. Megalos. Outerversal.\"","Four more layers actualized in rapid succession, each one adding substance to the hollow interior of his Pillar. The authority flowing up from his foundation grew denser with each Civilization he called, the combined weight of everything below feeding everything above.","\" Kuklos. Singed. Ordo Ab Chao.\"","The Pillar began to light up around him.","What had been merely bright before became something approaching blinding, multicolored radiance pressing outward through walls that struggled to contain the accumulating authority. Noah felt his existence responding to what he was building, felt weight settling into aspects of himself that had seemed free and unbound moments before!","This was different from freedom, he realized!","\" Farming. Smithing. Devouring.\"","More layers. More weight! His Pillar stretched higher as he filled it, the hollow space above him shrinking with each Civilization actualized. The feeling of unboundedness that had followed his disconnection from Vakochev’s Scales began transforming into something else entirely.","\" Helios. Dreams. Prana.\"","He was becoming heavy in ways that had nothing to do with physical mass. Every Civilization added to his foundation made him more present, more defined, more real in the fabric of Observable Existence!","The emptiness he had felt after hearing Vakochev’s message was being filled by construction that demanded his full attention.","\" Avalon. Oceanus. Muspelheim. Jotunheim. Niflheimr. Alfheimr.\"","Realms that existed became permanent Civilizations of his Pillar, their authorities now integrated rather than merely contained. He could feel his internal reality resonating with each actualization!","\" Limitless Existence. Silent Tongue. Radiant Paradox. Ordered Chaos.\"","Variations of his foundational Aspects settled into higher levels of his Pillar, permutations that expressed different facets of the same fundamental truths. THE First Tongue had spawned Silent Tongue. Existence had birthed Limitless Existence. Paradox gave rise to Radiant Paradox. Chaos produced Ordered Chaos.","The Pillar blazed with glory that pressed against everything nearby.","Noah continued building!","Like this, time began to pass!"]},{"number":5123,"title":"Chapter 5123: Chapter 5122: Advancement! III","paragraphs":["He had less than twenty-four hours before the Civilizational Holy War would begin, before his mother and son and everyone else he cared about would be pulled into isolated arenas to face Primordial Architects. The pressure of that deadline should have made him rush and should have introduced desperation into his actions.","But he had been doing something important through his Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation.","Whenever he needed to think through a problem, whenever he encountered complexity that required extended contemplation, he could stop time for his perception alone. An instant could become infinite for his consciousness while the external world remained frozen. If he found himself stuck on any thought process or possibility, he simply paused for what felt like hours or days within that moment of perceptual infinity.","Then he resumed, having worked through whatever had given him pause with boundless solutions!","The construction continued.","Other bodies of his moved through THE Infiniverse simultaneously, carrying out preparations that couldn’t wait for his primary form to finish building. The mass transformation project that had begun before the Civilizational Holy War’s declaration now accelerated with urgency.","The first and major task was clear.","The vast majority of those closest and strongest within THE Infiniverse needed to attain Nascent Hadean classification. Not because it would guarantee their survival in the coming battles, but because it would give them a fighting chance against opponents who had spent eons cultivating power that most First Scale beings couldn’t comprehend.","One by one, they underwent transformation.","Existential Engineering flooded Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce into their existences. The Lattice of Foundational Constraint that defined Bounded Lifeforms shattered within them, replaced by the Lattice of Nascent Emergence that declared them something new!","Golden cracks appeared on foreheads. Dark hair developed rivers of gold. Eyes shifted toward hues that spoke of authority exceeding their previous classifications.","This...was all accomplished in the first hour.","---","Exactly twenty-three hours before The Civilizational Holy War.","Noah stood on a floating platform within a realm of THE Infiniverse that had taken the qualities of an endless training ground. The space stretched in every direction without visible boundary, its floor solid enough to support combat while its atmosphere hummed with Observable Force dense enough to accelerate recovery.","Naldine Manthon came at him with everything she had.","Her form blazed with authority that would have made her old self seem dim by comparison. She had used her Hadean Infinity of Development three times in rapid succession, each usage accelerating her progression ridiculously . Her bones no longer pulsed with merely Proterozoic light. They shone with the crystalline brilliance of full Hadean classification.","All two hundred and six of them.","All seventy-eight organs.","She had become the third most powerful being in THE Infiniverse, exceeded only by Noah himself and of course THE Infiniverse as a whole. In the span of hours, she had achieved what should have required eons of dedicated cultivation.","And yet.","Noah swatted her aside with casual ease.","BOOM!","He hadn’t exhibited any Infinity. Hadn’t channeled any Observable Force. He simply stood there with his hands clasped behind his back, his expression holding mild interest as she attacked with waves and seas of Quintessence Infiniforce that should have overwhelmed anyone at her former classification.","Her Hadean skeletal structure blazed through her skin as she struck.","He knocked her back with a gesture that seemed almost lazy.","Naldine skidded across the waters, her feet carving furrows into material that shouldn’t have yielded to anything. Frustration painted itself across her features without her permission, ancient pride warring with the reality that she couldn’t touch him no matter what she attempted.","\" This doesn’t make sense ,\" she said, her voice tight. \" A Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity would be crushed under me, and yet...You’re not even using your authority.\"","\"I don’t need to.\"","His response was simple, stating fact rather than boasting!","Her singularity-dotted eyes blazed brighter as she shifted stance. If raw power wouldn’t work, perhaps something more refined would serve. Her hands began moving through motions that Noah recognized immediately, fingers curling and releasing in patterns that spoke of authority derived from THE Silurian Cause itself.","The somatic expression of THE Silurian Light.","Her voice emerged with weight that pressed against the training ground around them.","\" Silurian Ember, First of Flames. I grasp the Thread. I burn the Thread. What was shall be unwritten, what stood shall stand no more.\"","Magma-like brilliance gathered between her palms.","\" THE SILURIAN LIGHT.\"","The Pulse erupted toward him with force that had threatened to erase his existence not long ago.","Noah smiled.","He let it hit him.","The flames of THE Silurian Light washed over his form with heat that could have unmade Rhyacian entities through proximity alone. It pressed against his Hadean Dermis, against bones and organs that had been forged through countless cycles of destruction and rebirth caused by this very Pulse.","It felt warm.","Almost pleasant, like standing near a comfortable fire on a cold evening.","Then he breathed in.","HUUM!","The flames of THE Silurian Light flowed into his mouth, drawn by intention that exceeded what the Pulse had been designed to handle. He consumed the fire that Grimvault had used to threaten him, that Naldine now wielded. The brilliance vanished into him as if it had never existed.","He exhaled, and only faint embers emerged from his nostrils before fading entirely.","Naldine stared at him.","Her expression shifted through several emotions before settling on something between disbelief and reluctant acceptance. She shook her head slowly, white hair swaying with the motion.","\" You monster.\"","The words held no real venom. Just acknowledgment of what she was observing.","Then her eyes flashed sharply, and something changed in her bearing.","If she couldn’t beat him in this sort of battle, there were other arenas where she might gain some measure of control. Other methods of contest where raw power mattered less than technique and will and the particular intimacies that Dual Cultivation demanded.","Her gaze filled with defiance that hadn’t been present moments before.","\" Let’s switch to Cultivation .\" Her voice carried challenge that pressed against the space between them. \" I refuse to believe you are this far away.\"","A Primordial Architect remained defiant despite evidence that should have crushed such defiance entirely.","But she would learn later on.","She was fighting against someone walking an entirely different Scale of Existence!","---","Noah looked at himself and what he was becoming.","His Hadean Pillar of Infinity continued filling with actualized Civilizations, each layer adding weight and definition to his existence within Infinitas Architectura. The second demarcation of his First Infinite Scale of Existence was taking shape around him, authority accumulating rapidly.","He didn’t bother trying to gauge exactly how easily he could defeat a Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entity anymore.","The exercise seemed pointless. Whenever he sparred with Naldine, who was many times more powerful than any Calymmian entity he had encountered, she couldn’t get past the defenses of his skin. Not his bones. Not his organs. Just his skin!","She attacked with everything her newly Hadean existence could muster, and his outermost layer of defense treated her efforts as irrelevant.","He would come to know in the distant future that wasn’t truly so distant exactly what his power was. There would be battles that tested him properly, enemies that forced him to reach for capabilities he hadn’t yet explored. THE Deliverance and whatever forces served that ancient being would eventually provide the pressure he needed to understand his own limits.","But as of right now, he was building toward something else entirely.","He wanted to forge himself to be so astoundingly different and exceptional that those who followed Vakochev’s Scales of Existence wouldn’t even know where to begin when it came to understanding him. Let them try to measure him against their frameworks. Let them attempt to categorize what he was becoming. They would find nothing that fit because he had chosen to exist outside their definitions!","More Civilizations actualized within his Pillar as he continued his work.","The main threshold he approached was the transition from Uncountable Infinity to Absolute Infinity. That advancement would mark his readiness to progress toward the third demarcation, toward Infinitas Causa where THE Infinite Cause itself would be fully comprehended and actualized. But such transitions couldn’t be rushed, couldn’t be forced through sheer will alone.","So while he continued building, another body of his focused on the second phase of strengthening his people.","The eighty-one who would be involved in the Civilizational Holy War needed more than Nascent Hadean classification to survive what was coming. They needed to forge their bones and organs to become fully Hadean. Naldine had demonstrated what that transformation meant in practical terms, her power increasing by orders of magnitude through aggressive application of Hadean Infinity of Development.","If his people could achieve similar results, they should be able to contend with Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entities.","They should be able to survive!","---","The Early Veiled Shore stretched beneath them in configurations of beauty that most beings would never witness.","Radiant gold sands sparkled under light that seemed to come from everywhere at once, their surfaces catching and reflecting the multicolored brilliance that saturated this region of THE Infiniverse. Endless plots of sacred herbs spread across the landscape in careful arrangements, their leaves and stems now burning with the light of Infinity that Noah’s presence had infused into everything within his internal reality.","The multicolored rain of THE Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity continued falling without pause.","It had caused river channels to form all across the Early Veiled Shore, waterways of liquid authority carving paths through golden sand and fertile soil. The rivers flowed with colors that shifted constantly, carrying Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce to territories that drank in whatever they received!","Noah floated in the skies above this paradise with dozens of his people surrounding him.","He gazed at Barbatos, whose dark gold eyes held anticipation beneath their calm surface. At Henry, his son, the young man’s blue gold hair shifting in winds that carried authority rather than mere air. At Adelaide, at Sigrid, at Riya, at Moiraine, at Titano, at THE Queen of Matter, at THE First Farmer, at Khor, at Tor, at THE Living Origin, at Ul’moreth, at Lumivara, at Skoll, at Ains, at THE Emperor Penguin, and many others whose existences had become intertwined with his own.","All of them waited for what he would say.","\" We both have time and we don’t ,\" Noah said, his voice calm and measured. \" It depends on how we use what we’ve been given. Enemies far stronger than us are trying to collapse our very causality and existence. They declared war not because they fear what we are now, but because they fear what we might become.\"","He let that settle before continuing.","\"In response, we won’t just be going for survival. We need to...dominate. We need to cause fear to spread across Observable Existence, so that nobody else could possibly think about doing something like this to us again.\"","...!","His words pressed against everyone present!","\" To ensure that reality, at the very least, all of you need to forge your Hadean Bones and Organs. One of the quicker ways for you to do that is an infusion of boundless Infinity and Observable Force, which I can provide.\"","He paused, his expression remaining steady.","\" But you also need pressure to induce rapid transformation. External force that pushes your existence toward evolution. For that pressure, here is... a Primordial Architect that represents what those you will face will be like.\"","...!","Noah waved his hand.","HUUM!","Golden light erupted from his palm as THE Hadean Desmoterion responded to his will. THE Hadean Organ of Civilization had continued to advance alongside everything else, allowing more and more things to become possible. Releasing powerful prisoners for limited durations was now a feasibility where it had once been beyond his capability.","A figure emerged from the golden light.","Beowulf materialized above the Early Veiled Shore with presence that pressed against everyone except Noah himself!","The Primordial Architect’s armored body stood massive and imposing, but something had changed since his imprisonment. His armor no longer held the colors it had displayed during their previous encounter. It now shone fully blue gold, the distinctive hue of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force saturating every surface.","He had been disciplined in THE Hadean Desmoterion!","Ozymandias had worked on him in the dilated time that flowed differently within that prison, infusing him with Quintessence Infiniforce across spans that felt like years . The titanic form of Noah’s second body had transformed Beowulf into something he hadn’t been before.","A Nascent Hadean Lifeform.","|Beowulf, THE Primordial Architect of Armed Existence.|","|Classification: THE Second Scale of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence. Nascent Hadean Lifeform.|","|Skeletal Structure: 178 bones at Proterozoic classification. 28 bones at Hadean classification.|","|Organ Systems: 61 organs at Proterozoic classification. 17 organs at Hadean classification.|","|Current power output exceeds his previous parameters by a factor of approximately 127. Estimated classification now surpasses Grimvault at Calymmian Tier.|","...!"]},{"number":5124,"title":"Chapter 5124: Chapter 5123: Ego! I","paragraphs":["The power emanating from Beowulf was more than a hundred times greater than what Noah had faced during their original confrontation. The Primordial Architect who had attacked with intent to claim his Infinity had been transformed into something far grander through imprisonment and forced cultivation.","But the eyes behind that empty armored helm held no pride in this advancement.","They held fear.","Immense, undeniable fear when they turned toward Noah!","Noah didn’t look at this fucking rat.","He simply waved his right hand again.","HUUM!","Another figure emerged from THE Hadean Desmoterion, this one taking form with presence that somehow exceeded even what Beowulf displayed.","THE Living Elemental materialized beside the armored Primordial Architect.","His form shifted through configurations of fire and water and earth and air, elemental authority that had been refined through the same process Beowulf had undergone. Blue gold light saturated every aspect of his constantly changing existence, Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force having been integrated so thoroughly that it had become part of what he fundamentally was.","|THE Living Elemental.|","|Classification: THE Second Scale of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence. Nascent Hadean Lifeform.|","|Skeletal Structure: 156 bones at Proterozoic classification. 50 bones at Hadean classification.|","|Organ Systems: 52 organs at Proterozoic classification. 26 organs at Hadean classification.|","|Current power output exceeds Beowulf by approximately 23%. Among the stronger Nascent Hadean entities currently in existence outside of your direct lineage.|","...!","When THE Living Elemental finished materializing, his elemental form turned toward Noah.","Fear painted itself across features that shifted between states too quickly for most to track. The same fear that Beowulf displayed, the same recognition of what stood before them and what that presence meant for their continued existence.","Noah looked at THE Living Elemental with distaste that didn’t need to be hidden.","\" The armored Primordial Architect will give you a glimpse of the ones you’ll fight,\" he said, his voice remaining calm despite the expression on his face. \" And this shitty, good for nothing Living Elemental is another Second Scale you can struggle against.\"","His gaze swept across his gathered people.","\"I would have acted as the one to fight against you all, but I haven’t fully gauged my own strength yet. I don’t want to accidentally collapse you all while sparring.\"","A pause that felt almost casual.","\" So for now, just hang on with these trash enemies. Once I’ve fully acclimated to my power, you’ll all face me.\"","...!","Incredulous reactions rippled through the gathered crowd.","Barbatos smiled wryly, her dark gold eyes holding amusement.","Others looked at Beowulf and THE Living Elemental with something approaching pity.","This was a Primordial Architect who had existed for eons, who had accumulated power that most beings couldn’t comprehend!","And Noah called him trash!","Training dummies for his people to sharpen themselves against.","HUUM!","Terrifying power bloomed from the two released prisoners as they prepared for what was about to occur.","They moved with fear driving every action, because they understood something that Noah’s people were only beginning to grasp. If they didn’t sufficiently accomplish what they had been brought out here to do, if they failed to provide adequate pressure for transformation, if they were deemed useless for even this purpose...","Once they returned to that prison where time moved extremely differently, they would be punished for years.","Ozymandias was waiting, and Ozymandias had learned new methods of discipline during his own transformation!","---","Twenty hours remained until the Civilizational Holy War.","Noah was overseeing many things across THE Infiniverse when part of his consciousness received a tug of emotions. He frowned at the sensation. A moment later, he sent a body out to investigate.","The location was a distant place in the endless Wastes.","He appeared in a region that had become a swirling multicolored sea due to the Quintessence Infiniforce saturating everything. The waters churned without pattern, colors bleeding into each other. Half submerged in these impossible seas, a massive shattered Shelter of THE Loom rose from the depths like the corpse of a fallen giant.","The structure had been destroyed!","Atop the shattered Shelter, a figure materialized.","THE Living Emotive didn’t appear as an illusory visage gathered from ambient emotions this time. Her existence was fully present, an accumulation of feelings so dense and real that she pressed against the surrounding environment simply by being there. Chaos swirled around her form in visible currents, authority she had claimed mixing with the emotional resonance that defined her nature.","She was manically beautiful.","Her features held symmetry, every angle and curve designed to draw attention and hold it captive. But there was something wrong with that beauty, something manic beneath its surface that made appreciation feel like a trap. Her smile stretched too wide when she looked at him!","Her hair shifted colors as he watched.","It moved through shades that corresponded to nothing external, responding instead to emotions that flickered through her existence faster than most beings could track. Red bled into violet bled into gold bled into black, the transitions happening without pattern or warning. One moment she seemed wreathed in passion, the next in something closer to despair, the next in triumph that had no apparent source.","Noah’s gaze remained cold as she looked at him and smiled brilliantly.","\"You..anh, you detest me...\"","Her voice carried weavings that pressed against his consciousness, each word layered with emotional weight that would have influenced lesser beings.","She was not so manic as last time. Her words were more coherent!","\"I can feel it, you know. That emotion! The distaste you hold for me radiates so strongly that I could locate you across Observable Existence simply by following its trail. Though you seem to be inside a place I cannot lock down as all emotions inside of it...are locked deeper than even THE Wyld...\"","She stepped closer across the shattered surface of the Shelter, her bare feet leaving impressions that glowed with residual feeling.","\" Most beings try to hide their emotions from me. But you don’t bother. You let me see exactly how much you wish I would disappear from your awareness entirely.\"","Her smile didn’t falter.","\"I find that oh so refreshing. It is why right now...I pulled on my emotions of logic and coherence to speak oh so clearly to you. Do you like my words? Straightforward! Formal! And I havent rhymed anything just yet which is hard...ah!\"","Noah said nothing, simply watching as she spoke.","\"I should explain something,\" she continued, her hair shifting through blues and greens. \" My fixation on you isn’t arbitrary. It’s in my nature to become fixated on whoever controls the most emotions across Observable Existence at any given time. The being whose presence influences how others feel simply by existing.\"","She tilted her head, studying him with eyes that held too many colors simultaneously.","\" That was Abaddon for a time. Then THE Creature, when he burned away his classification and began doing things that made even ancient entities feel fear. Then it was Erwin, THE Living Paradox, when his machinations began affecting the information that shapes how beings perceive their circumstances. \"","Her smile sharpened.","\" But now it’s you. It...has always been you! You’re like a beacon to me! A lighthouse that every emotional current eventually flows toward.\"","She paused, seeming to consider her next words carefully despite the manic energy that radiated from her.","\"I know that history can interfere with future. What happened before and what I did before colors how you see me now. My actions towards Malphas and many others...Oh, and I even tried to kill you! Silly me! But hey, look at us now? Not too long ago, you slapped me until all my teeth fell out! Ahh.. I play that memory constantly to remember how much you detest me! So I will proceed slowly, carefully, in whatever manner causes you the least displeasure.\"","Her hair cycled through colors that suggested submission beneath their shifting surface.","\"If you command me to kneel, I will kneel.\"","She knelt as she spoke, demonstrating rather than merely describing.","\"If you command me to lick, to beg, to be a worm crawling at your feet, I would do it. If you command me to collapse myself entirely, to end my existence because my presence offends you...\"","Her eyes met his from her kneeling position.","\"Oh...fuck, I’m realizing now that I really might just do that too! Sheesh! That would not be too ideal but...oh! That is my nature when my fixation has become this strong. I cannot help what I am.\"","Noah’s expression didn’t change, but he continued listening.","THE Living Emotive rose from her kneel with fluid grace, her hair now settling into steadier shades of purple and silver.","\" After claiming Chaos and siphoning the power of all emotions across Observable Existence, I changed tremendously. I gained access to understanding that had been hidden from me before. And I found out something pivotal.\"","Her voice grew more serious, the manic edge retreating slightly.","\" For Primordial Architects and other lifeforms at THE Second Scale who want to infuse themselves with Infinity without going mad, the most critical factor is actually Ego. Their emotion. Their sense of self refined into something that can withstand pressure that would dissolve lesser consciousnesses.\"","She began pacing across the shattered Shelter, her words flowing with the cadence of genuine discovery.","\" To go against the madness of Infinity, they amplify what they affirmed with their Civilizational Anchor. They further enhance and inflate certain emotions to be so strong within their Ego, within their existence, that they develop an unfathomably high resistance to Infinity depending on how amplified a singular or multiple emotions are.\"","Her pacing stopped as she turned to face him again.","\"So I realized something that contradicted what I had always assumed. At the peak of power, you don’t find mindless sages who have attained some nirvanic state and abandoned all feeling. Emotions and the state of being are actually deemed unfathomably more critical at higher classifications. The conscious mind, the unconscious depths, the raw impulses of extremely powerful beings are all cultivated specifically to bear Infinity.\"","Her hair shifted through golds and whites as she spoke with increasing intensity.","\"I found all of this out because the structure of THE Wyld became clear to me after I claimed Chaos and pulled on all emotions. Where power concentrates. How authority flows. The configurations that determine who rules and who serves.\"","Her eyes blazed brighter.","\" THE Deliverance and three others of his stature rule THE Wyld. Four beings whose power exceeds everything beneath them by margins that make comparison meaningless. And THE Deliverance and these other top dogs, they have a direct connection to something grand. Something that provides them with advantages that Bounded Lifeforms shouldn’t be able to touch.\"","She stepped closer to Noah, her voice dropping lower.","\" My fixation. My fascination. My...Anchor. The reason I came here despite knowing how much you detest me...was to give you information of those in the Civilizational Holy War, but also...\"","Her hair settled into pure gold.","\" Do you know about THE Gilded Ones?\"","...!","Noah stared at her coldly.","The distaste remained, rooted in history that couldn’t be erased through useful information. She had done things that earned his hatred, and no amount of kneeling or offering would change that foundation.","But he was pragmatic above all else.","And this being who disgusted him may just prove to be an anomaly more disgusting than Erwin or even come close to rival...THE Creature!?"]},{"number":5125,"title":"Chapter 5125: Chapter 5124: Ego! II","paragraphs":["Noah had never considered himself closed minded.","He looked at things dynamically, weighed them against the shifting circumstances that defined every encounter across his existence. If someone asked him whether a fucking stupid and vile being could be redeemed, he wouldn’t answer with absolutes. He would say it depends. Redemption was possible, always possible, but in the end he would be the one who decided whether the effort was worth the cost, and what exactly that being had done before reaching for the chance.","As of now, Emotive’s redemption wasn’t set.","He could still go either way on this disgusting being.","He floated forward across the shattered Shelter of THE Loom, his movement slow and unhurried, as if the terrifying information she carried meant nothing to him at all. The multicolored seas churned beneath his feet without daring to touch him. His fair skin held its golden illumination steady, his eyes reflecting cold consideration as he closed the distance between them.","THE Living Emotive’s chest began to rise and fall faster as he approached.","Her eyes shone brilliantly, holding too many colors at once, every shade pressed against the others without harmony. Chaos swirled tighter around her form the closer he came. Her hair cycled through golds and silvers and deep violets, each transition matching some internal current she couldn’t suppress no matter how much logic she had pulled into her words.","\" You’re so close now...\"","Her voice came softer, less performed than before.","\"I feel oppression and euphoria at the same time! Anh...it’s not supposed to work like that, you know? Most beings inspire one or the other. Fear or comfort. Dread or peace. But you...oh, you give me both at once and they’re not even fighting each other. They just exist together inside me like they were always meant to!\"","She breathed in deeply as he stopped within arm’s reach.","\"I really would end my existence if you commanded it. I wasn’t lying about that, I promise! But...sheesh, I really really would prefer if you gave me a chance instead. My emotions love to live too. They love to thrive! They love to feel things and burn through me and become something new tomorrow that they weren’t yesterday.\"","Her knees buckled.","She knelt before him without ceremony, her hands reaching forward to grasp his feet with reverence. Her fingers trembled against the illuminated skin, holding on as if releasing him would mean losing something essential.","\" Do you feel that emotion?\"","Her voice came out hushed and ragged.","\"That discrepancy of power between us? Not even a discrepancy of power...a discrepancy of position! You stand somewhere I cannot reach no matter how much I claim or consume, and my entire existence is screaming at me to acknowledge it. To honor it. To kneel here and beg for the privilege of being looked at!\"","Her hair settled into deep gold as she pressed her body toward his feet.","\" This is the kind of emotion I’ve been studying! This exact kind! Because the most powerful beings cultivate this in others, and they cultivate other emotions in themselves, and I figured out why!\"","She looked up at him with eyes that burned brighter.","\" The most powerful Primordial Architects have been modified. Engineered. Reworked at the level of their existential makeup by THE Gilded Ones to amplify specific Egos of Existence. The Ego of Pride. The Ego of Passion. The Ego of Wrath. These emotions are inflated to such tremendous proportions inside them that they define their Civilizations and their power to a degree that lets them tap into vast reserves of Infinity without ever worrying about THE Gamaidian, the Madness of Infinity!\"","Her fingers tightened against his feet.","\" They are connected to those great beings through this engineering. The power they can tap into is grand! Grander than anything Bounded should reach for, grander than what their classification should permit. And then...\"","Her smile stretched wider, the manic edge bleeding back through.","\" And then there is you. You, you, you! What could you have possibly been engineered with that Infinity is doing nothing to you?\"","...!","She pressed her cheek against his foot and laughed softly.","\" They call you the Infinity-bearer. That’s what’s whispered in the high places of THE Wyld now. The Infinity-bearer, the one who shouldn’t exist by every law their engineering follows. They want to study you so badly, oh so badly! They haven’t brought you to the attention of THE Gilded Ones yet because they want their own glimpse first, but they just might depending on how this Civilizational Holy War goes.\"","Her hair flickered through reds and blacks.","\" They seek to understand what Ego you exemplify so they can ask the favor of THE Gilded Ones to engineer them that way too! THE Deliverance is testing the waters with this Holy War. Others of his stature, others even more powerful, are watching from positions you can’t see yet to see how it unfolds. Everybody wants a piece of you. Everybody!\"","Before she could finish her next breath, Noah’s hand moved.","His fingers clasped around her neck and lifted her from her kneeling position, raising her until her bare feet dangled above the shattered Shelter. His grip was firm enough to hold her completely, gentle enough that her existence wasn’t yet collapsing under his fingers.","Joy bloomed across her features.","Her eyes widened with shock and awe as she felt the strength of that single hand. Through the contact of his fingers against her throat, fragments of his power leaked into her perception, glimpses of something her senses couldn’t fully process.","\" Holy shit, is this...\"","Her voice came out strangled and reverent.","\"Is this a glimpse of your power? You feel...boundless! You feel...!\"","Noah’s hand became firmer.","Her words choked off into something between a gasp and a laugh. He held her there suspended above the multicolored seas, and he turned his head slowly to look out across the endless Wastes around them, his eyes sweeping the horizon as if she weighed nothing at all.","When he finally spoke, his voice carried calm tyranny.","\" Character... matters.\"","His gaze didn’t return to her.","\" One can make mistakes. Existence is long enough that mistakes are inevitable, and I’m not so naive that I expect anyone to walk through eons without leaving wreckage behind them. But mistakes need correction. They need acknowledgment from something deeper than convenience, something that doesn’t appear only when usefulness becomes the currency.\"","His fingers tightened a fraction more.","\" Even if I personally don’t care about what you’ve done, I will have you grovel before someone like Malphas, Tor, and Khor. The being whose face you used your feet to step on, whose countless Inevitabilities were imprisoned. If they tell me to kill you, regardless of whatever benefits you bring me, regardless of how much information you carry about THE Deliverance or THE Gilded Ones or anything else, I will still collapse you where you float.\"","He let the words settle into the surrounding silence.","\" No matter how useful someone is, no matter how sharp a tool becomes in the right hands, it needs to have character behind its edge. You will only be a tool for now. Do you understand?\"","He didn’t even look at her as he spoke.","But her eyes shone with vibrant brilliance, and profound happiness moved through her features in waves. Instead of breaking into the mania and scattered words that defined her usual responses, she gathered herself with effort that visibly cost her, and what came out of her throat while his hand still choked her was perhaps the most coherent thing she had ever spoken.","\" As I learn how critical ego and emotions are at the top...\"","Her voice was strained but steady.","\"I can feel how boundless my own potential is. Someone filled with emotions, someone who controls emotions, someone who has claimed Chaos itself...I could probably do something grand. Rival Erwin. Maybe even exceed THE Creature given enough time and the right circumstances.\"","Her eyes locked onto his profile.","\" But to me, it isn’t power that matters most. It truly is emotion. The one who can handle Infinity better than even those engineered by THE Gilded, potentially better than THE Gilded themselves...\"","Her breath hitched as his grip held her there.","\"I will give everything to witness what emotion you have. What quality lives inside you that has made such a thing possible. I will give... Everything !\"","...!","The emotion that made him immune to the madness of Infinity.","Noah turned the question over in his own mind without letting his expression shift. Quintessence? Tyranny? Something else buried so deep within his Cause that even he hadn’t named it yet? He thought about whether such a thing even existed within him in the way she described, or whether his immunity came from somewhere else entirely.","He shook his head once.","His fingers released her throat, and the tool he had been holding floated grandly before him with shining eyes, her body subtly trembling with an excitement she couldn’t suppress no matter how much coherence she pulled around herself.","Noah looked at her calmly.","\" Give me all the information regarding those participating in the Civilizational Holy War.\"","...!","\" Yes sir!\"","She straightened in the air with the eagerness of something that had been waiting eons to be given a purpose by the right voice. Her hands lifted, her fingers began weaving patterns through the multicolored seas around them, and a singularity of emotions began to form between her palms, dense with droves of information she had gathered across THE Wyld.","Noah looked down at his own hands.","The hands that had held the tool. The hands that had held Emotive. He considered her redemption again, weighing what she had just offered against everything she had been before, and the answer remained exactly where it had been when this conversation began.","It still depended."]},{"number":5126,"title":"Chapter 5126: Chapter 5125: Ego! III","paragraphs":["Noah turned the information over within himself.","Emotive’s singularity of emotions had unfolded inside his perception like a flower made of stolen feelings, and within it lay everything she had gathered across THE Wyld. Names, configurations, weavings of authority, the signatures of beings who had been reworked at fundamental levels by hands grander than their own. He held it all in a stillness that the multicolored seas around him couldn’t disturb.","THE Gilded Ones engineered their chosen ones differently than he engineered his.","His own work with Existential Engineering replaced lattices, pulled Bounded Lifeforms across the threshold into Nascent Hadean, gave them access to Infinity through transformation of what they fundamentally were. THE Gilded Ones did something else entirely. They didn’t transform the foundation. They amplified specific Egos within the existing makeup, inflated emotions until those emotions became the very channels through which Infinity could pour without triggering THE Gamaidian. Pride as a vessel. Wrath as a vessel. Passion as a vessel!","Two different philosophies of ascension, two different paths toward the same forbidden well.","\"I may need to see the engineering of THE Gilded Ones firsthand.\"","He spoke the words almost to himself, his gaze still resting on the floating singularity of information.","THE Living Emotive’s eyes shone the moment the words left his mouth.","Her hair surged into electric pinks and feverish golds, the colors crashing against each other with the kind of excitement she clearly couldn’t contain. She drifted closer through the air, her bare feet still not touching the shattered Shelter beneath them, her smile stretching into something that bordered on giddy.","\" Oh! Oh, oh, oh! Why don’t you make a trip to THE Wyld then?\"","Her voice came out faster, the manic edge slipping back through the coherence she had been holding so carefully.","\"I could mask you! Anh, you could probably mask yourself a thousand times better than I ever could, but I could help, I could layer my emotional weavings over you so that even the ones who feel for emotional disturbances wouldn’t catch a single ripple of your presence. And with how much information I keep receiving from emotions all across existence...sheesh, I’m telling you, I can pinpoint isolated parties of Primordial Architects who have already undergone modification!\"","...!","She circled him slowly through the air, her hands gesturing as her words built momentum.","\" Think about it! Just think about it for one moment! Nobody expects this of you right now. Nobody! Everyone in THE Wyld is bracing for the Civilizational Holy War, calculating who will fall and who will rise. Their attention is fixed on the spectacle. Their attention is not on the doors of their own home.\"","Her hair shifted into deep violets that suggested cunning beneath the mania.","\" And THE Creature is already there running rampant! Things are chaotic in ways they haven’t been in eons. Primordial Architects are dying in corners of THE Wyld where their corpses won’t be found for a long time, and nobody can tell which disappearances are him and which are something else. You walking through that chaos would be one more ripple in a sea that’s already churning. Who would even notice?\"","She drifted in front of him, her eyes holding too many colors to count.","\"I already have the locations of a few isolated groups you could fuck up as your lab rats. Engineered ones, modified ones, the kind that would let you peel back their existential layers and see exactly what THE Gilded Ones did to them. You’d learn more in one visit than I could explain across a hundred conversations!\"","Her smile sharpened into something almost shy beneath the manic glow.","\" And...oh! It would be our first journey together...\"","Noah considered it.","He stood there in the multicolored sea with twenty hours still remaining on the Civilizational Holy War countdown, his Pillar still rising within THE Infiniverse, his second body still overseeing the training of his people, his third body still standing on the other side of Sadakar’s door at Nakatsukuni.","He could spare another body for this. He could spare more than that if the work demanded it.","And he did need to stretch his muscles.","There was nothing grander than walking into the enemy’s field and studying them without their knowledge, no purer test of his current capabilities than moving through the home of beings who would happily collapse his existence if they sensed him there!","He had ascended through unconventional methods, and unconventional methods demanded unconventional applications.","His decision settled into him without ceremony.","He waved his hand once, ignoring Emotive entirely for the moment, and space fluctuated around him in response to the gesture. The fluctuation stretched, folded inward on itself, and from that fold a figure stepped through with the steady grace of someone who had been mid-motion when summoned.","Naldine Manthon emerged into the multicolored sea.","She was breathing heavily, the rhythm of her chest betraying that she had just been sparring with another of his bodies inside THE Infiniverse. Her radiant white hair held its new rivers of gold prominently, the strands still damp at the edges from exertion. Her singularity-dotted eyes adjusted to the new environment in a single blink, and her vihuela rested against her back, still humming faintly with residual authority.","Her gaze found Emotive almost immediately.","Noah watched the exchange with a quiet interest he didn’t bother to hide. Emotive’s hair, which had been cycling through warm and excited shades a moment before, suddenly shifted toward colors he hadn’t seen on her yet.","Deep greens veined with sour yellows. Her smile didn’t fall, but something tightened beneath it. Her eyes flickered as they took in Naldine’s power as she displayed...","Jealousy.","Those were the colors of jealousy, and Noah found them quietly amusing on a being who claimed all emotions as her domain.","\" The three of us are taking a trip to THE Wyld ,\" he said.","Naldine blinked once. Then again.","\" Are you serious?\"","She studied his expression for a moment, found whatever she needed to find, and exhaled through her nose with the resignation of someone who had long ago stopped questioning his choices.","\"I mean...okay.\"","Her gaze drifted back to Emotive, her singularity-dotted eyes narrowing slightly as she took in the manic beauty floating beside them. Her brow furrowed in open displeasure, and her voice came out flat and unimpressed.","\" Why are you picking up stray cats? What’s the use of this one?\"","Emotive’s hair flared into bright reds.","\" Stray cats? Stray cats?! Look at her, talking like she wasn’t crawling out of some dusty corner of existence playing her little instrument before he found her too! At least I came bearing gifts of information that could shape an entire war and more. What did you bring? A song?\"","Naldine’s mouth curved into the smallest, sharpest smile Noah had seen on her in a while.","Noah raised his hand, and none of that shit continued.","He looked at Emotive without warmth.","\" This one is just a tool ,\" he said calmly. \" And she knows it. If she performs well, she will continue to be used.\"","...!","Emotive’s eyes lit up at the words as if they were the highest praise she had ever received. Her hair settled into pure radiant gold, her smile stretched into something brilliant and unguarded, and she nodded with the eagerness of a creature who had finally been given a defined place in a hierarchy she could understand.","Naldine’s shook her head calmly.","Noah didn’t linger on either of them.","He raised his fist, drew it back, and brought it crashing upward through the air above his head.","BOOM!","Existence cracked.","The multicolored seas trembled as a fissure opened across the fabric of reality itself, splitting the air with the sound of something fundamental giving way. The crack widened, edges shimmering with the white gold radiance of a sea that lay beyond all definitions, and through that opening Prima Indifferentia became visible. The Crack of Observable Existence held steady, waiting, vast enough for them to pass through.","Noah stepped forward and went in.","Naldine followed without hesitation, her vihuela humming awake against her back.","And Emotive, with her hair blazing every color at once, drifted after them into the white gold sea beyond.","---","<Nakatsukuni>","The hidden domain between Observable and Unobservable held its own quiet weight.","Noah stood within Sadakar’s space at Nakatsukuni, his other body fully present, the structures of this sanctuary rising in soft geometries around him. Lanterns hung in air that didn’t quite obey the laws of either side it bordered. Somewhere within him, the weavings of paradox tugged with the steady insistence of a thread being pulled by a hand he hadn’t yet seen.","He spoke into the stillness without raising his voice.","\" Can I take a portion of your space to have a conversation? I can feel my weavings of paradox tugging at me.\"","...!","The vast consciousness of Sadakar surrounded him before words formed, the Singular Cognizance’s presence pressing gently against everything in this hidden place. His voice came from no specific direction, only from everywhere the air touched.","\" Think about what I said. Think about not looking at things like choosing sides, but maintaining neutrality through peace being the better side. That way, one lives longer.\"","The words held no command.","And then his vast consciousness withdrew, fading from the immediate space until Noah was left alone within a portion of Nakatsukuni that had become his to use.","Noah considered the words.","Sadakar was ancient in ways that even Singular Cognizances measured carefully against each other, and his philosophy had been forged across eras Noah hadn’t been alive to witness. But ancient didn’t mean correct. The longer one lived, sometimes, the more one mistook survival for wisdom, and the more one confused the absence of action for the presence of peace.","Neutrality didn’t really work.","Those who tried to play neutral were always eventually eradicated by whichever side won, because winners had no use for fence-sitters and survivors made inconvenient witnesses .","And the ones who weren’t eradicated had usually fooled themselves about what neutrality actually was. By choosing not to choose, they had already chosen. By withholding their weight from one side of the scale, they had given that weight to the other side without admitting it.","Sadakar’s longevity was real. His peace was an illusion built on the careful pretense that doing nothing was different from doing something.","Noah was not built that way.","In the distance of the borrowed space, a doorway swung open without ceremony.","His perception caught the brief presence of a Singular Cognizance on the other side of that opening, and then that Cognizance was being escorted elsewhere, taken to a different location within Nakatsukuni so that the conversation about to occur would happen between only two participants. The doorway settled. The space narrowed to him and one other.","Erwin came through.","THE Living Paradox stepped into the borrowed domain with the unhurried grace of a beggar who had always known where the next meal was coming from. His attire remained the grand beggar weave he favored, the colors muted and somehow regal in their muted state. His eyes held eons!","His expression held no surprise at all when his gaze met Noah’s, only recognition.","He nodded.","His smile broke across his features brilliantly as he floated to a position opposite Noah’s, the air between them thick with weavings that didn’t belong to either of them alone anymore.","\" Congratulations are in order, I think.\"","His voice carried that same calm arrogance Noah remembered, layered now with what sounded like genuine appreciation.","\" You took on Primordial Architects. You survived a Pulse of THE Silurian Light. You got yourself into a Civilizational Holy War declared by THE Deliverance himself. It’s quite something... Quite something to witness from the outside.\"","...!","Noah looked at him calmly.","\"I’ve been trying to place you in a ranking.\"","His voice held the steady measure of someone reviewing inventory.","\"I want to know exactly where you sit when it comes to entities like THE Creature or THE Primordial Paradox. Where the line of potential is drawn between you and them, and which side of that line you actually fall on. But you’ve been fluctuating in my assessment because very little about you is actually known. The data... keeps slipping through my analysis the moment I try to fix it in place.\""]},{"number":5127,"title":"Chapter 5127: Chapter 5126: Neutrality Is Fake!","paragraphs":["THE Living Paradox laughed softly, a sound that held no offense.","\" That is the nature of what I am.\"","He inclined his head as if acknowledging a compliment.","\" As THE Information Paradox, very little of my weavings will ever be received or found out by others. Information enters me and is conserved within me, and yet that same information is lost forever in ways that should be impossible. My signature does not propagate the way other signatures do. My trail does not exist where other trails would be carved into the substrate of reality. To be unrankable is not a weakness in my case, Osmont. It is the architecture I have engineered across eons of cultivation.\"","His smile softened into something almost intimate.","\" Which brings me, in a roundabout way, to why I owe you my thanks.\"","Noah’s gaze sharpened slightly, but he said nothing.","\"I have made many plans here and there across the eons, \" THE Living Paradox continued. \" Most of them slow plans, the kind that compound across timescales most beings cannot sustain attention across. And whatever you did, whatever decision you made in the period after our last conversation, has allowed me to advance all of those plans tremendously. So I want to thank THE Youngest properly before things between us become whatever they are about to become.\"","He drifted slightly closer, the weavings of paradox swirling around his beggar’s form in slow eddies.","\" Allow me to explain, since you enjoy understanding the things you fight against.\"","His eyes grew distant for a moment, then refocused with a fanatic gleam Noah had seen before.","\" Due to my nature as THE Information Paradox, I can select someone to siphon off the terrifying weavings of information and causality that they generate as they move through Observable Existence. The being I select must be generating enough disturbance in the substrate of reality that their information-shedding becomes worth the attention I devote to consuming it. For a long time, my selection was THE Creature. He fit the criteria. His every action sent ripples through information that I could harvest at my leisure.\"","His smile widened.","\" After our talk, I switched my selection over to you.\"","The words settled into the borrowed space with the quiet finality of a decision long since made.","\" And then, sometime ago, I do not know exactly what you did. But the weavings of paradox surrounding you and your power through THE Scales of Existence went haywire. The information that should have flowed steadily into me began arriving in configurations I had never encountered before. The substrate of how you exist in relation to The Scales shifted in ways my perception struggled to track in real time.\"","Noah listened without expression.","He knew what he had done. He had pioneered THE Infinite Scales of Existence, deviated from Vakochev’s framework entirely, established his own measurement of ascension!","Erwin didn’t know about that yet, and Noah saw no reason to fill in the gap.","\" For some unknown reason, \" THE Living Paradox continued, \" that change cascaded through my own nature. I was not prepared for it. I am rarely surprised by the consequences of consuming information, but this surprised me in ways I am still mapping out internally.\"","His hands rose, palms upward, as if showing Noah something invisible held between his fingers.","\"It has caused me to perceive all the information within the Scale that I currently occupy simultaneously. All of its weavings. Rhyacian, Calymmian, Ediacaran, every gradation between them, every transition that other beings move through sequentially. I see it all at once now. I receive the information of an entire Scale of Existence as if it were a single unified field that I can pull from at will.\"","He laughed quietly, almost in disbelief at his own circumstances.","\"This has made things extremely unique for me. I have been amassing power at an unfathomable scale. Plans that would have required millennia of careful consumption have completed themselves within hours. Configurations of authority that I had only theorized about have manifested in my existence without my needing to construct them piece by piece.\"","His eyes locked onto Noah’s with renewed intensity.","\" But the biggest thing I wonder, Osmont, is exactly what did you do? What action did you take that caused the information surrounding you to allow for such a terrifying change in my own nature? I have replayed the moment endlessly within myself, and I cannot identify the trigger. Only the consequence.\"","Noah listened to all of this calmly until the words ran their course.","When he finally spoke, his voice held the steady weight he reserved for matters he had already decided.","\" Everyone has their dreams and goals.\"","His gaze held THE Living Paradox without wavering.","\" But the things we do toward our dreams and goals matter. They matter more than the dreams themselves, because the methodology becomes the foundation that everything else rests on. Toward my goals, I have never willingly planned and massacred or enslaved those who did nothing to me. I have never reached for advancement by carving it out of beings whose only crime was existing within reach of my ambition.\"","His tone hardened slightly.","\" You, on the other hand, are interesting. I’ll grant you that. But you tried to kill me in the past. You mutilated countless Inevitabilities. You mutilated Khor eons ago. You worked your eons-long methodology by consuming and discarding beings whose information happened to be useful to your Cause, and you did all of this with the calm satisfaction of someone balancing accounts that only you got to define.\"","He took one slow step forward.","\" In these past few hours, I’ve begun thinking about all the debts out there. About how many beings owe something to me, and how many beings I owe something to in return. I’ve decided I need to begin collecting them. Not all at once. But the ones that are within reach, the ones whose ledgers are already open in front of me, those...I’m going to settle now.\"","His voice settled into something almost gentle.","\" So whether you are powerful or not, we’ll know very soon. Because I’m going to make a move against you now. Are you ready?\"","...!","BOOM!","The shock that crossed THE Living Paradox’s face was brief but real. This was not how he had calculated this conversation ending. He had come to thank, perhaps to bargain, perhaps to extend the strange paradoxical entanglement between them into another phase of mutual benefit. He had not come to be attacked.","But he was not entirely unprepared.","He recovered swiftly, the calm arrogance returning to his features even as paradox began to swirl around him in terrifying configurations. The weavings of his existence pulsed brighter. His beggar’s robes rippled with authority that had been hidden a moment before, and his eyes held the fanatic gleam of someone who refused to let surprise become defeat.","He nodded slowly.","\"The next time we meet, perhaps it will be under extremely different circumstances.\"","Noah’s reply came without hesitation.","\" If we meet again. This could be it for you.\"","BOOM!","All of existence shook.","The borrowed space within Nakatsukuni couldn’t contain what bloomed above Noah, because what bloomed above Noah was never meant to be contained by spaces of any kind. THE Hadean Pillar of Infinity emerged from the air itself, rising from Noah’s very being into a structure that pierced upward through every layer of reality the hidden domain touched. Crystalline blue trees of THE First Tongue formed its base. Multicolored flames of Existence licked along its mid-sections. Infinite mirrors of Paradox reflected impossibilities at every angle. The eternal storm of Chaos swirled at its apex.","The Pillar bloomed, towered, and smashed downward toward Erwin.","THE Living Paradox looked up at the descending light of Infinity with a sombreness that briefly cracked his calm composure. His body shone and didn’t shine paradoxically, his Proterozoic Bones and Organs flickering between states of being and not being as his existence tried to brace for what was coming. His hand rose. His fingers began moving through the somatic weavings of a Pulse, the gestures precise and ancient, conjuring whatever defense his nature could muster.","And then...","The Pillar thundered down and crashed into him with the totality of everything Noah had built within himself across his unconventional ascension!","BOOM!","Soon after, the booming voice of Sadakar echoed out across Nakatsukuni with authority that shook the borders of the hidden domain itself!","\" There shall be no fighting in Nakatsukuni!\"","But it was already too late.","Existence in the borrowed space tore in half. The structure within Nakatsukuni that Noah had been standing within split down its center, the soft geometries cleaving apart with a finality that could not be unmade. Lanterns shattered. Paths crumbled. The very air carried the aftertaste of something fundamental having been violated, the kind of devastation that didn’t apologize for itself because it knew it had been chosen deliberately.","When the Pillar faded, Noah floated alone in an area of trembling destruction.","A scorch mark remained where Erwin had stood.","Nothing else of him was left behind. No body. No robes. No trace of the beggar grandeur that had drifted opposite him moments before.","And yet Noah frowned.","Because he could feel, paradoxically, that Erwin had perished and had not perished at the same time. The information of his death existed. The information of his survival existed alongside it. Both states held themselves in superposition within the substrate of what had just occurred, and Noah knew without certainty that the second state was the more likely truth.","Erwin probably wasn’t dead.","But he had been hit.","The peaceful Primordial Architects, Undivided Ones, and Formless Terrors of Nakatsukuni began to gather at the edges of the devastation. They emerged from their domains and structures with expressions that held shock, because when the Pillar had appeared, every single one of their existences had felt shaken to its foundation. They had felt the threat of collapse. They had felt, for the briefest moment, what it would mean to encounter that light without warning!","Among them, Moloch roared.","The Singular Cognizance who had come with Erwin let his rage erupt across the trembling space, his voice carrying the fury of someone who had just watched his arrangement burn.","\" So you had chosen a side already, Sadakar?!\"","His existence pulsed with barely contained violence.","\" Okay! Okay!\"","And then Moloch disappeared.","He believed himself outnumbered, and he removed himself from Nakatsukuni before that assessment became a fatal one!","Sadakar appeared near the devastation soon after, his vast consciousness condensing into a presence that could be looked at directly. His ancient features held anger, the kind of restrained anger that came from someone whose carefully cultivated peace had just been violated within his own sanctuary.","Before he could speak, Noah turned to face him.","\" Neutrality...doesn’t really work.\"","Noah’s voice held no apology, only the calm logic he had been turning over within himself before any of this began. So what if a Singular Cognizance was angry?","Merely a Singular Cognizance!","\" Those who try to play neutral are eventually eradicated by whichever side wins, because winners have no use for fence-sitters. Your peace, Sadakar, has been protecting beings like Erwin for a long time as they ushered THE Loom and THE Fallout. Your refusal to choose has been a choice all along. You just didn’t have to look at it because nobody forced you to see what your sanctuary actually sheltered.\"","He let the words settle into the trembling air.","\" You can reach me anytime you wish through Infinity. Should you stop playing the game of neutrality. Until then...\"","Noah took a single step.","His gaze passed once over the scorch mark where Erwin had stood, registering the paradoxical signature one last time, and then he disappeared from Nakatsukuni without further ceremony.","The hidden domain held its silence after he was gone.","Nakatsukuni remained torn in the area where the Pillar had come down, the structures cleaved, the ground refusing to knit itself back together. And then, slowly, multicolored rain began to fall on every structure within the sanctuary. It fell on the intact buildings and on the broken ones. It fell on the gathered Primordial Architects and Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors, who stood in that rain and remembered, each of them, what they had felt when that Pillar had come down.","Each of them had felt their own collapse."]},{"number":5128,"title":"Chapter 5128: Chapter 5127: THE Wyld! I","paragraphs":["THE Living Emotive had always understood emotions better than most beings understood their own hands.","She fucking knew the shape of longing the way other beings knew the shape of their own faces. She knew the weight of grief, the texture of lust, the temperature at which rage cooled into vengeance. Every color her hair cycled through had a corresponding feeling she could pull from across Observable Existence, siphoning it from whoever was experiencing it most strongly at that particular moment. She understood emotion. Emotion was her sanctuary and her madness both at once.","But je ne sais quoi was different.","Je ne sais quoi was the emotion that hid behind other emotions, the quality that certain beings carried without being able to name it and that certain beings lacked no matter how much they accumulated of everything else. It was a flavor. A resonance. A presence that existed in the gaps between the feelings you could measure. Most across Observable Existence could not accurately gauge it even when it stood directly in front of them, because measuring it required possessing enough of it oneself to recognize the signature.","THE Creature had it.","Sheesh, did he have it. The moment he had burned away his classification, he had become saturated with je ne sais quoi to the point that other Primordial Architects couldn’t look at him without feeling their own emotions rearrange themselves in his presence. A few others across existence held it too, scattered here and there, beings whose names carried a certain hush when they were spoken.","But THE Youngest?","Osmont?","Her fixation?","Anh. Holy shit.","Others needed to look to him for lessons because fuck, he had something. Something that made her hair cycle colors she hadn’t known existed within her palette. Something that made her entire being want to kneel even when he had already stopped looking at her!","Je ne sais quoi poured off him the way light poured off a star, and the terrible beautiful truth was that he didn’t even seem aware of how much of it he was radiating.","She wanted to know what it was.","She wanted to know what it was more than she had ever wanted anything!","---","Prima Indifferentia stretched in every direction around them, its white gold sea holding them in suspension as they prepared for the next step of the journey.","Noah floated at the center of her attention, his fair skin glowing gently against the undifferentiated backdrop, his eyes holding the distant consideration of someone calculating multiple realities at once.","Naldine Manthon floated to his side, her dirty white hair with its rivers of gold catching the ambient light in ways that should have been beautiful and somehow only made Emotive’s hair shift into sour yellows.","Emotive studied her carefully.","The emotions clinging to Naldine’s existence were not subtle to someone who could read such things. Power. Pleasure. Lust. Satisfaction. The residual warmth of a being who had enjoyed her fixation’s favor in ways that Emotive herself had not yet earned. His brilliance had filled her, had saturated her existence, and this average, dirty Primordial Architect had been accepting that favor as if it were something owed to her.","It was okay to feel envy. It was okay to feel jealousy. Those were perfectly valid responses to the circumstances.","But Emotive also recognized the reality of her own position. She had a long path ahead of her before she could enjoy the same favor from her fixation. She had to work hard. She had to prove herself across encounter after encounter, tool use after tool use, until something in his calculation shifted from...I will collapse you if Malphas says so toward something softer and more enduring.","Naldine had earned what she had earned. Emotive would earn her own!","She would earn it by being spectacular.","In these upper weavings of power where emotion seemed to be one of the most important things, she could actualize potential that had always existed within her and never been properly channeled. She was THE Living Emotive. She had claimed Chaos. She siphoned feelings from across Observable Existence at will. If emotion was the critical factor at the peak of existence, then she was sitting on a foundation that most ascending beings would have murdered for, and she had simply been too manic across eons to realize it.","She would show this to her fixation. She would show it to her Everything . Until he could no longer see her as a mere tool.","She turned her attention outward, letting her voice fill the white gold silence.","\" Normally, a Primordial Architect would be required to go into THE Wyld.\"","Her voice held more of the manic singsong than her last coherent monologue had carried, but the coherence was still present beneath the bounce.","\" I’m guessing that’s why you brought her here, yes? But...the gateways of THE Wyld are attuned to emotional existential signatures that only certain beings carry. The place decides who walks through its thresholds, and most of the time the place is very picky, very picky about who gets the invitation.\"","She drifted in slow circles around the two of them as she continued.","\" But here is the thing. Oh, here is the thing! Even without being a Primordial Architect, I can imitate the emotional existential signatures of them. I’ve siphoned enough from enough of them across enough moments that I can wear their resonance like a borrowed coat, and the gateways can’t tell the difference. My emotions are already inside THE Wyld, constantly, because the beings inside THE Wyld are constantly feeling things and I’m constantly receiving those feelings. So opening a gateway from this side is easy!\"","Her hair shifted into electric golds as she raised her hands.","\" Watch!\"","Her fingers wove through the white gold sea, pulling at emotional threads that only she could perceive. Pride. Wrath. Ancient hungers. The specific resonances of Primordial Architects engineered into the highest tiers of THE Wyld’s hierarchy. She braided them together, layered them over her own signature, and pressed the composite against the fabric of Prima Indifferentia with the confidence of someone performing a trick she had rehearsed in her own mind a thousand times.","HUUM!","A gateway opened.","It widened before them with a slow green-gold light, the edges shimmering with possibilities that didn’t belong to the white gold sea. Naldine’s brow furrowed as she watched the opening form, her frown calm but clearly unimpressed.","Emotive turned to Noah.","He nodded lightly at the gateway.","That small nod caused her entire existence to buzz.","Oh. Oh!","Today, he was nodding. In a few days, or maybe weeks, he might offer something more. He might look at her with something other than distaste. He might tenderly hold her cheek. The thought crashed through her so vividly that her hair burst into pinks she hadn’t worn in eons, and she had to pull herself back with effort so that her fixation wouldn’t catch the indulgence and revise his opinion of her downward.","Slowly, slowly. She had a lot to do. But she knew how strong emotions were, and she knew the one thing emotions could always do was change. The being who loathed you today could love you tomorrow if the right sequence of feelings was strung together between those two points. She was a master of that stringing. She had eons to refine her craft. And now she had the fixation worth crafting for.","They stepped through the gateway.","THE Wyld received them.","---","The ancient primal forest opened around them the moment they crossed the threshold.","Archaic tall trees rose in every direction, their trunks thick as small realms, their bark patterned with weavings that looked almost alive. The canopy stretched so high that the upper branches disappeared into a sky that wasn’t quite a sky. Rivers of Observable Force flowed between the trunks, glowing in currents of gold and deep bronze, carving pathways across the forest floor that hadn’t been carved by any tool.","The air was dense.","It was dense with pollen that wasn’t pollen, with spores that carried authority instead of reproduction, with the faint hum of countless emotional resonances all pressed close against each other. The light filtered through the canopy in shafts that didn’t quite behave like light should, bending around branches, pooling in places where no opening existed above.","Emotive breathed it in, and her hair settled into deep forest greens.","She loved this.","She loved this region so much. THE Wyld was a primal place, a wild place, a place where possibilities hadn’t yet been carved into the strict definitions that governed more refined domains. Anything could happen here. Anything could become anything. Her manic nature had always been drawn to environments where the rules bent, where certainty dissolved, where a being with enough emotional range could rewrite a small corner of reality simply by feeling strongly enough in that corner. The primal wild held all of that and more. It held potential the way a seed held a tree!","She floated closer to Noah as her breath settled.","Naldine didn’t exist to her in this moment. Naldine was fucking scenery. The gold-veined Primordial Architect was simply another tree in the ancient forest, and Emotive’s attention focused entirely on the one being in this forest whose gaze she wanted to earn.","Her body visibly trembled as she drifted within arm’s reach of him.","\" Out of all the Primordial Architects wandering through THE Wyld right now...\"","Her voice came softer, more intimate, the manic edge retreating into something almost reverent.","\" I’ve locked onto the one who forged THE Primordial Mycelia. Oh, you remember, don’t you? The fungus of Unity. The one Erwin released across Observable Existence. The one you collapsed to make my claiming of Chaos possible as a downstream consequence. The whole tangled chain of causes and effects that led to our being here together today, floating in this forest, about to do something wonderful.\"","Her fingers wove small gestures in the air as she spoke.","\" The one who forged the Mycelia is not alone. He’s traveling with a few others. His power sits at Calymmian Proterozoic Scale, solid but not exceptional by the standards of THE Wyld’s highest tier. But here is the thing, anh, here is the thing! He is among those who have undergone the engineering under THE Gilded Ones. So he is more powerful than those at Ediacaran who havent had any Engineering! The modifications are inside him. The amplified Egos of Existence are written into his weavings. If you peel him open, you see what was done.\"","Her hair held steady in its deep greens as she looked up at Noah.","\"Are they... an appropriate target?\"","She looked to him for affirmation, her eyes holding the weight of the question she wasn’t quite asking beneath it.","He turned toward her.","His gaze fell on her fully, and she felt what it was to be looked at by her fixation without distraction. His eyes held infinities. They held the quiet possibility that he could collapse her with a thought or elevate her with a gesture, and both possibilities felt equally real in the moment of being seen. Her existence churned beneath his attention. Power flooded into her organs and bones, and more of her structure shifted into Proterozoic Scale rapidly as the influx of emotion cascaded through her cultivation without her having to direct it at all.","She was ascending simply by being looked at by him.","Had she been a useful tool?","Was he beginning, very slowly, to have a change in emotion toward her?","Her eyes were bright as she waited.","He turned from her after a moment, his gaze sweeping across the vibrant primal forest, taking in the archaic trees and the rivers of Observable Force and the dense possibility-laden air. He nodded once.","\" Let’s go.\"","Two words.","Two words that caused her to brighten so thoroughly that her hair burst briefly into white before she pulled it back into something less conspicuous. She nodded, closed her eyes, and began collecting more information from the emotional currents rippling through THE Wyld. She pulled the information close and masked it beneath a storm of her own feelings, layering deception over discovery, making absolutely certain that nothing would go wrong on her first journey with her Everything.","Nothing would go wrong.","She would make sure of it!"]},{"number":5129,"title":"Chapter 5129: Chapter 5128: THE Wyld! II","paragraphs":["The primal forest of THE Wyld changed around them as they moved.","Noah perceived every shift of it in something close to slow motion, his Hadean Mind stretching the instants so that he could take each detail fully into himself.","The trees and leaves moved in winds that didn’t come from anywhere. The roots drank from Observable Force without ever seeming to need more.","He studied the plant life closely as they passed.","These plants, these ordinary plants of the ordinary underbrush, felt more indestructible than the defenses of THE Surface Depth entities at the lowest level of Vakochev’s First Scale. A shrub here would have survived blows that would have shattered beings whom he had once considered powerful.","It was fucking laughable!","The small lifeforms scattered as the three of them passed.","Critters darted between the roots. Glowing things no larger than his palm flickered through the underbrush. Each of them carried power that would have placed them as Surface Depth lifeforms anywhere else, and each of them ran from his party with the specific fear of creatures that recognized predators beyond their weight class.","He had explored many regions across his existence.","A Beast World with its wonder. Atlantis, the Demon World with its carved cruelty. The Cultivation World where mortals clawed upward through borrowed breakthroughs...","Every one of them had offered something, and every one of them had been worth the journey. But he had always found a particular joy in places like this, in vibrant ancient forests filled with wonders. They reminded him of his journey back to The Earliest Folds.","A place like this always scratched the itch of exploration!","He always felt, in such places, that he would grasp many more things if he only paid close enough attention.","And he was not staying still.","Just as Emotive was doing what she did with emotions, pulling information from feelings scattered across Observable Existence, he could tap into the Infinity permeating everything around them to read information of his own. Her method was more precise because emotions were individualized, each one belonging to a specific being or moment. His was broader. He had used his weavings of Undifferentiated Fate before to gather information about Alexander, but right now he used something simpler.","He tapped Infinity directly, without invoking the Civilization of Hunger or Undifferentiated Fate, and let flows of information pour into him from every direction.","The region began to map itself across his mind.","The Infinity swirling through this area carried signatures of every life form within it. Small creatures and large ones. Plants and streams. Pockets of denser authority where ancient presences had once passed through and left traces that hadn’t yet faded. He extended his senses outward slowly and then further, handling the influx with care as he familiarized himself with this practice.","He didn’t have Infinity alone.","This place was drenched in Observable Force. Rivers of it cascaded throughout the forest, golden and slow, their currents holding memories of their own that he could taste with the right angle of attention. He tapped into that as well, letting the two streams of information layer against each other in his perception. Infinity gave him the texture of what was alive. Observable Force gave him the shape of what had moved through. Together, they painted the region in a resolution that no single sense could have managed.","Slowly but surely, he familiarized himself with the practice as they went forward silently.","Emotive floated beside him with the reverent gaze he had chosen to ignore.","He looked toward Naldine instead.","Her expression held something nostalgic as she passed through what should have been, by blood and origin, her home.","They were in her home.","But her home was about to get very bloody.","Because at this moment, standing in the filtered light of an ancient forest that had birthed beings she could no longer call her own, Noah found himself realizing something about the Civilizational Holy War that had been quietly assembling in the background of his thoughts.","There were many possibilities to consider.","Yes, he could raise his people as much as he possibly could in the remaining hours. He could push them through accelerated Hadean transformations, put them through forced sparring against Beowulf and THE Living Elemental, refine their bones and organs until the selected 81 stood at capabilities that made their designated opponents regret the day their names had been written into the challenge. When the Holy War began in less than twenty hours, wonder would unfold across Observable Existence. He had already arranged that much.","But wonder wasn’t the only option.","In that remaining window, in those twenty hours, what if those chosen among the 81 Primordial Architects to face his people began dying left and right? What if they began vanishing from their resting places, their training grounds, their quiet moments of preparation? What if their corpses started appearing across THE Wyld? What if he simply carved rivers of blood across this forest until the list of his opponents shortened into something more manageable by the hour?","The only thing giving him caution right now was the connection to THE Gilded Ones.","Their presence here was real. If he acted too openly, too quickly, he would draw attention he wasn’t ready to handle. So he would do this carefully. He would get his hands on a few Primordial Architects first, the ones Emotive had already pinpointed as engineered subjects. He would see if he could grasp whatever modifications had been written into them. He would make his decisions from there.","He never had to play fair.","Not against beings who had selected his mother for a Civilizational Holy War.","Who the fuck did they think they were to bother Amelia Osmont?","A brief burst of rage buzzed around him, subtle enough that most would have missed it and sharp enough that Emotive didn’t miss it at all. She trembled nearby, her hair flashing through reds before she caught herself. He gazed at her sharply without slowing his pace, and she controlled her reaction with visible effort. He looked forward again.","They kept going.","The forest began to thin around them as they moved, the archaic trees spacing further apart, the canopy opening to let more of the strange sky filter through. The underbrush gave way to stone. The stone gave way to a ridge. And then the ridge gave way to nothing at all, because the land they had been crossing simply ended.","They broke past the final trees and emerged into open air.","The vast forest stretched behind them, an ancient sea of green and bronze. Ahead of them lay something else entirely.","Endlessly dotting silver and gold floating islands filled the vista before them.","They hung in the sky at every altitude his perception could track, and further beyond that, and further still. Some were small enough to stand on. Others held whole landscapes of their own, with their own rivers and their own forests and their own tiny weather systems. Between them, rivers of golden Observable Force stretched across the open air for gigaparsecs, flowing from island to island without obeying gravity, connecting the drifting landmasses in a vast lattice of slow bright currents.","Noah felt a tug of Infinity.","It pulled from somewhere deep within the field of floating islands, a specific pull toward a specific direction, the signature of the Primordial Architect who had forged THE Primordial Mycelia.","Emotive drifted closer to him and spoke.","\" We’re close enough now that I can collapse the distance between emotions ,\" she said, her voice holding careful restraint. \" Their emotional signatures are within my reach. I can pull us across to their location through that channel if you want. It’s fast and it’s clean. They won’t feel us coming.\"","Noah shook his head calmly.","\"I’ve toured enough of this region.\"","His voice held the steady measure of a decision already made.","\" We’ll traverse across Infinity to arrive where we need to be. There is boundless Infinity here. There is boundless Infinity there. The channel between them is mine to open. Confirm the coordinates with me.\"","Emotive’s eyes brightened at being given a task rather than having her offer declined outright. She closed her eyes, pulled her emotional thread taut against the specific feeling of the target Primordial Architect, and fed the coordinates into Noah’s perception with the precision of someone who had been waiting for the chance to prove her usefulness again.","Noah affirmed the coordinates within himself.","He reached for Infinity.","Waves of blue Infinity surged around the three of them in response to his call, swirling outward in currents that formed an incandescent endless galaxy of light. The floating islands of THE Wyld distorted through the blue veil. The golden rivers of Observable Force between them bent and rippled. Emotive’s eyes widened with genuine marvel as she watched the Infinity respond to him with the ease of a river responding to gravity.","An instant later, they disappeared!","Boundless Infinity surrounded them.","Noah floated within it with his eyes cold and his body stretching out slightly, testing the feel of his Hadean structure against the pressure of the channel they were traversing. Emotive floated nearby with her hair cycling through awed blues. Naldine floated on his other side with her vihuela humming faintly, calm as always.","He turned his mind toward what waited on the other side.","If Primordial Architects were eggs, how easily could he crack them right now?","How cleanly could his Hadean Hands of Infinite Grasp wrap around their shells and apply the exact pressure required to open them without destroying what lay inside? How quickly could he peel back their weavings and study the engineering that THE Gilded Ones had written into them? How many could he break before the cracks added up to a pattern that someone upstream would notice?","He would see soon!"]},{"number":5130,"title":"Chapter 5130: Chapter 5129: Greed! I","paragraphs":["The floating island hung in the golden air of THE Wyld like a table raised toward heaven.","Its surface held the geometries of an archaic laboratory, built from pale stone veined with threads of gold that pulsed faintly in time with the work being done upon it. Towers of bone and brass rose at its four corners, their tips holding arrays of polished lenses that stared inward at the central platform without blinking.","Flasks hung suspended in mid air, held by nothing, their contents churning with liquids that refused to settle into any single color. Rivers of Observable Force were diverted from the golden currents flowing between islands and piped into the laboratory through channels cut into the floor, feeding the apparatus with a steady hum of siphoned power.","The air smelled of old copper and older ambition!","At the center of it all stood a golden table, and on that golden table lay a corpse that was not quite a corpse.","The body belonged to a Primordial Architect.","It had once possessed power that would have let it topple realms without effort, but now it lay stretched and opened across the golden surface, its chest cavity parted neatly, its Proterozoic Organs arranged around it on smaller trays like specimens at a feast.","Fungus-like attachments had been grafted into the exposed weavings of its flesh. Pale tendrils wound through its Proterozoic ribs. Bulbous growths clung to its major organs, pulsing with bioluminescent greens and sickly whites.","Rivers of Infinity flowed across the subject in slow visible currents, being pulled in through the feet and channeled out through the crown of the skull, the whole body acting as a conduit for something vaster than itself.","And yet the corpse breathed.","It was alive. Barely, and in a manner that its original self would not have recognized as living.","Standing over the table was the one who had arranged all of this.","Octavius Kraethos wore robes of deep emerald threaded with gold, the cut of the fabric matching the decorative severity that all the Primordial Architects of this floating island seemed to share. His frame was tall and lean, built in the proportions of an ancient sculpture that had refused to accept the passage of time.","His skin held a pale bronze sheen, unblemished across eons of careful self-maintenance. His hair was cropped short in the fashion of an archaic scholar, iron grey at the temples and deeper black through the crown, and his jaw carried the clean precision of someone who had long ago decided that his face was another instrument requiring proper calibration.","His eyes were the telling feature.","Pale gold rimmed with a deeper amber, pupils that held the focused intensity of a being who never stopped calculating even when his mouth was speaking of something else!","His hands moved across the exposed weavings of the corpse on his table with the steady patience of a master craftsman.","Around the laboratory, other Primordial Architects moved through their own assigned tasks. Two Calymmian Proterozoic Scale entities adjusted the apparatus at the corners, their own emerald and gold robes marking them as his peers in this endeavor. A Rhyacian Proterozoic Scale figure stood near one of the bone towers, her hands deep in a basin of churning Observable Force, her attention fixed on some reading that only she could interpret. Every one of them wore the colors of their shared engineering. Every one of them had been amplified along the Ego of Greed!","A greed for advancement. A greed for knowledge. A greed for the next answer that lay one experiment beyond their current reach. It was a hunger refined into discipline, an appetite channeled into research methodology, and it had taken them farther along the paths of cultivation than most of their kin had ever traveled.","Near Octavius, a crimson-haired Calymmian Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect stood with her arms folded across her chest.","Her hair fell in long dark red waves down her back, braided at the temples. Her robes matched the emerald and gold of the others, though hers held additional threading at the cuffs, fine embroidery in the shape of opened seed pods. Her eyes were the deep wine color of someone who had watched many experiments fail and had stopped being moved by the specific shapes of their failures.","Her name was Valeria.","\" I’ve watched three of these now, Octavius.\"","Her voice held the dry patience of a colleague who had earned the right to be skeptical.","\" Three subjects on that same table. Three attempts to replicate what THE Gilded Ones do to us as a matter of casual engineering. Every one of them has failed in ways that were instructive, I’ll grant you, but failed nonetheless.\"","She stepped closer to the table, her gaze moving across the fungus-laced corpse with clinical detachment.","\" What makes you think this one will succeed where the others didn’t? You cannot do what the Gilded do to us. None of us can. The engineering they write into our existence operates on weavings we haven’t been permitted to touch. You’ve been reaching for their methodology for eons, and every time you’ve come away holding something that was not quite it.\"","Octavius didn’t look up from his work.","His fingers continued their precise movements across the exposed chest cavity, adjusting the fungal attachments by fractions so small that only another surgeon of his caliber would have registered the shifts. A faint smile crossed his lips.","\" You misunderstand the design, Valeria.\"","\"I know exactly how far the Gilded are beyond what I can replicate. I have known this for longer than you’ve been studying my work. What you’re watching me build here is not an attempt to match their engineering. I stopped trying to match them after the second failure. This latest product... is meant to be something else entirely.\"","He finally lifted his head and met her gaze.","\"This is meant to be an abomination.\"","BOOM!","\" All prior attempts were meant to succeed along a single axis. Amplify one Ego. Stabilize the infusion of Infinity around that amplification. Match the cleanness of what the Gilded achieve with their subjects. Every subject failed because the cleanness is the Gilded trick, and that trick is not available to me. So I stopped reaching for cleanness. I reached instead for controlled corruption.\"","His pale gold eyes held Valeria’s dark ones steadily.","\" The subject on this table is meant to fall into the influence of Infinity without the stabilization protocols that would save a Gilded-engineered being. The Gamaidjan, the Madness of Infinity, is meant to take hold within it. While it does, I’ve also amplified its Ego of Hunger to unfathomable intensity. Its engineering is now designed to be flooded by madness and driven by hunger simultaneously. Two weavings that should tear each other apart inside any stable existence.\"","He turned back to the corpse of The Primordial Architect and resumed his work.","\" These conflicting weavings will allow me to control it with my...Unity. The madness of Infinity will make it incapable of independent judgment. The amplified Ego of Hunger will give its actions a single overriding directive. I will wield it as a collar wields a beast, pointing it toward endless devouring of others and of Infinity itself. Its power at conception may be grander than my own, perhaps significantly so, and this is entirely acceptable. A tool that bites its master has a leash. A tool that cannot think past its own hunger has no need to bite the hand that feeds.\"","Valeria watched him work in silence for a long moment.","\" When it is complete, it will eat what I tell it to eat. And if certain considerations align with the current currents in THE Wyld, there are many things across Observable Existence that I would enjoy watching be eaten. Starting with a few of our peers who have grown too comfortable.\"","Valeria said nothing.","The other Primordial Architects continued their work. The bone towers hummed. The flasks churned. The rivers of Observable Force flowed through their diverted channels with the steady patience of systems that would continue operating long after any individual being stopped observing them.","Rivers of Infinity moved across the body on the golden table, and the fungal attachments pulsed gently in time with the flow.","The laboratory continued its quiet industry.","None of them knew they were about to have guests!"]},{"number":5131,"title":"Chapter 5131: Chapter 5130: Greed! II","paragraphs":["The seas of Infinity dispersed around him, and the skies of a grand floating island opened into his perception.","The light filtered through something that wasn’t atmosphere, golden currents of Observable Force braiding through the open sky in slow rivers that curved around the island’s edges without ever touching them. Below, the island stretched wide and terraced, its pale stone surface veined with gold that pulsed in patient rhythms, its towers rising at the corners with their blinking arrays of polished lenses.","Information poured into him from every direction.","The weavings of Infinity carried the signatures of every being present, the configurations of every structure, the residue of every experiment that had been conducted on this island.","Observable Force layered its own data over the top. It was abundant, the kind of abundance that would have drowned a lesser perception in static, and he let all of it flow freely across his mind!","It passed in less than an instant.","Even in its density, even in the sheer volume of what was being given to him, he received it and read it and filed it in a span shorter than an instant.","| Domain Entry: Unnamed Research Archipelago, THE Wyld.|","|Entity Count: Seven Primordial Architects confirmed present on the primary island. Six distant islands hold additional entities. Full classification pending.|","The information settled into place, and his eyes shone brightly as he looked ahead.","Many eyes looked back.","The silence that fell was awkward! Nobody moved and nobody spoke. The apparatus continued its quiet hum. The golden table at the center continued to receive its rivers of Infinity. The corpse on that table continued its mechanical breathing.","The island spread out beneath him in full view now.","Corpses lay across multiple tables, each one a Primordial Architect in some stage of dissection or modification. Protruding fungi grew from their exposed organs. Pale tendrils wound through their rib cages. Some of the bodies twitched faintly with residual life. Others were clearly past the point of any return. Each table was its own quiet experiment, each subject a record of some attempt that had either succeeded along a narrow axis or failed in an instructive manner.","At the center, a single table commanded the rest.","The corpse lying on it radiated something the others didn’t. Terrifying power rolled off its fungus-laced body in slow waves. Potent Infinity pulsed through the rivers being fed into it, the flow rates higher than anything feeding the other tables.","The Primordial Architects of this research party had clustered near it.","Noah focused on the ones carrying the most power.","| Entity Detected: Octavius Kraethos, Designer of THE Primordial Mycelia.|","|Status: Surprised but composed.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Calymmian Tier(Seems fake, power does not match).|","|Threat Level: Significant? Unknown|","| Entity Detected: Valeria Morne, Research Peer.|","|Status: Alert and guarded.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Calymmian Tier.|","|Threat Level: Less significant.|","His gaze settled on Octavius.","So this was the one who had created the Primordial Mycelia. The scholar who had forged the fungus of Unity that Erwin had taken!","The entity whose research had rippled outward through so many downstream consequences that even Emotive’s claiming of Chaos traced back to his table!","What a wonder of causality.","All of that had been conceived on a floating island like this one, probably on this exact island, under the steady patient hands of the being now staring back at him.","Looking at Octavius, and at a few of the others clustered near him, brought a unique sensation into his perception.","Seas of Infinity moved within their bodies.","Seas! The concentration held by each of these engineered Primordial Architects exceeded anything he had encountered in any Primordial Architect before, and the seas were stable in a way that made no immediate sense. They should have been drowning. They should have been losing themselves to THE Gamaidian, the madness that Infinity inflicted on beings who couldn’t withstand its pressure.","Instead, the seas held themselves in orderly shorelines inside each of them, kept that way by engineering that had been written into their existential foundations.","The so called amplification of Ego.","Was this what Emotive had been describing? Emotions inflated to such intensity that they could stand against the natural superiority of Infinity, push back against its madness, create a stable foundation on which the sea could rest without spilling over?","The curiosity that bloomed inside him was sharp!","He wanted to gauge their power. He wanted to open their bodies and see exactly what made them tick. The engineering was right there in front of him, walking and speaking and preparing to resist him, and all he had to do was get his hands around one of them to begin the study!","All of this passed through him in a span that measured below a nanosecond.","Below him, the Primordial Architects had already gathered closer to their leader.","Octavius looked at him and at Naldine with eyes that couldn’t quite believe what they were seeing. A deep smile bloomed across his face, slow and scholarly and unsettling in its warmth. His pale gold eyes held focused intensity.","\" This... is absolutely incredible.\"","His voice carried the cadence of a master who had just received an unexpected gift.","\" A lot might have truly underestimated you, Infinity-bearer. I saw you when you were broadcasting your thrashing of Beowulf, and the recording was instructive, genuinely instructive, but seeing you in person is something else entirely. It’s a treat. Honestly, a treat!\"","He took a small step forward, his hands clasped lightly behind his back.","\" Listen. I have many internal laboratories ready for use, quite nearby, well prepared and well equipped. If you’d be willing to cooperate with the process, I can lay you down on a table and open you up just to study your Infinity a little bit. Nothing too invasive. I just don’t want things to get messy and loud and have any others come by. The integrity of the research depends on quiet, you understand.\"","...!","Noah opened his mouth to tell Octavius that he didn’t have to worry about any interruptions.","Emotive’s voice beat him to it.","\" Haha!\"","Her voice echoed out across the floating island with all the singsong mania she had been holding back in the forest.","\" Soon-to-be-corpse, you don’t have to worry about that! I! Have! Sealed! Everything!\"","...!","Yes.","The moment they had arrived, both Emotive and Naldine had exerted power in their own unique ways, each of them operating on their own initiative without needing him to direct them. He had felt the twin workings settle into place alongside his arrival. He hadn’t needed to make a single move of his own to lock this region down.","| Emotional Blockade has been established. Authority: THE Living Emotive.|","|All information capable of traveling on weavings of emotion and chaos has been severed within the surrounding region of approximately one gigaparsec. Complete existential silence has been declared. An Ediacaran Tier entity would require several minutes to overcome this blockade.|","| THE Hadean Barrier of Infinity has been enacted. Authority: Naldine Manthon.|","|All weavings of information expressed through Infinity have been prevented from entering or exiting the surrounding region of approximately ten gigaparsecs. No signal, plea, or distress weaving will reach any outside party.|","The notifications settled into the space between his thoughts.","He looked at the unique Primordial Architects glowing with their seas of Infinity, their engineered stability holding their frames against pressures that should have collapsed them. Even he couldn’t say for certain whether these would be decent enemies or whether a few of them would actually give him trouble.","The seas inside them were real. The engineering was grand. These were not the ordinary Primordial Architects he had dismissed as kindling for his people’s training!","But this entire region was locked down now.","Nothing would be getting in. Nothing would be getting out. Whatever happened here would remain here, and the only witnesses who would leave would be the ones he permitted to leave.","His voice carried calmly across the island.","\" You know a lot about me.\"","His eyes held Octavius’s pale gold ones without wavering.","\" But I don’t know too much about you. The circumstances are asymmetric, and I’d like to correct that. So here’s how we’ll do it. You have two options, and I’ll let you choose between them.\"","He let the pause settle, tyrannical in its patience.","\" Option one. You put yourself up on that table. You lie down beside the subject you’ve been working on, and you let me take a look at you. I open you up carefully. I study the engineering that THE Gilded Ones wrote into your existence. I learn what I came here to learn. At the end, depending on how things go, I may or may not let what’s left of you keep breathing.\"","His gaze drifted briefly toward the fungus-laced corpse at the center of the gathering.","\" Option two. You tussle with me first. You and your peers here put up whatever resistance you think you can muster, and we see how far that gets you. And when the tussling is done, I put your corpse on that table to join the one already there. Then I still study you. I still learn what I came to learn. The only difference is that in option two, you don’t get a chance to guide my hands away from anything important, because your hands won’t be moving at all by then.\"","The island fell quiet around his words.","\" Which one...would you like?\"","...!","The moment the question landed, Octavius’s smile stretched extremely wide.","And then he began to laugh!"]},{"number":5132,"title":"Chapter 5132: Chapter 5131: Greed! III","paragraphs":["The laugh rolling out of Octavius was an ugly one.","It wasn’t the laugh of a being who had lost control. It was measured, scholarly, and almost delighted! He waved his hands upward as if surrendering to a tide he couldn’t turn back, the gesture so disarming it nearly sold itself as sincere.","\" Alright, big guy.\"","His smile held the brilliance of a host welcoming a long-anticipated guest.","\" You are far too complex for us little things. Which table would you like my body on so you can take a look? Whichever arrangement suits your research methodology, I’m happy to oblige. I have preferences myself, but I’m willing to be flexible on my preferences today.\"","...!","Something shifted in the weavings around the island.","|Warning: Civilizational Weaving of Unity has been detected.|","|The weaving is infused into the ambient Infinity and is attempting to propagate along contact vectors. Targets: Noah Osmont. Naldine Manthon. THE Living Emotive.|","|Effect Goal: Infiltrate existential foundations and establish infectious Unity bond with source entity.|","Noah’s eyes sharpened.","That was why Octavius was smiling. The surrender was theater. The welcome was bait! He had already embarked on an attack the moment the words left his mouth, threading his Civilizational weaving through the ambient Infinity that was already saturating the island, using the density of the environment as camouflage for a strike that would have rooted itself into the existences of all three of them before any of them had time to notice.","It wasn’t even a bad attempt!","Against a lesser party, it would have worked. Against Noah alone, it might have given him pause for a fraction of a moment. But the weaving had reached not only for him. It had reached for Naldine too.","His eyes turned unfathomably cold.","It wasn’t the attack itself that did it. What cooled his gaze into something glacial was that the reach had extended toward Naldine, toward the Hadean woman floating beside him whose radiant white hair caught the filtered light of THE Wyld’s strange sky.","Grand and tyrannical and calculating though he was, there were weaknesses he had never bothered to hide from himself.","Women were one of them.","His women, specifically.","Once a bond settled between him and someone he counted as his, he became overly protective in ways that his pragmatic self couldn’t quite discipline out of existence. If there was a single emotion associated with him that could have been amplified into an Ego that made him immune to the madness of Infinity, it probably wasn’t pride.","He wasn’t overly prideful. Rage and wrath came when they came, but they didn’t last long enough. Lust, though. If one wanted to make a case, Lust might have been it! Even though he knew for him and how he played with infinity, emotions shouldn’t be the answer of why he never went mad.","Such a thought crossed his mind in the space between heartbeats.","He shook his head once and focused down on the island.","\" Okay ,\" he said calmly. \" Second option, it is.\"","...!","He wanted to test things.","Here were powerful Primordial Architects whose engineered capabilities he couldn’t properly gauge from observation alone. The seas of Infinity inside them told him they were stable. The amplified Egos told him they were designed to resist madness.","But the actual combat ceiling of each being, the exact pressure they could withstand, the point at which their engineered stability began to crack, none of that could be derived from inspection. It required contact.","So he struck with an attack that would have decimated someone like Grimvault.","He stayed where he was. He raised his hand, and with a simple motion he pushed it down through the air.","HUUM!","In the next instant, identical visages of his body appeared in front of each Primordial Architect gathered below.","Each copy held the same posture. Each copy pushed its hand down with the same slow deliberateness. The air between him and every single target collapsed into a Geodesic Weaving of infinity, a sea of infinity, one attack distributed across multiple points simultaneously, one movement propagating through the ambient Infinity until it arrived at every target in the same instant it left him!","Because Infinity was pervasive, his attack became pervasive. One gesture. Infinite vectors!","Oh!","Behind each pushing hand, a concentrated sea of Infinity pressed downward with the full weight of his Hadean physiology riding its current.","BOOM!","The island rocked on its foundations!","Every Primordial Architect below was hammered backward. The Rhyacian Tier scholar at the rear of the cluster was flung across the length of the island before her body even registered being hit. Two Calymmian peers slammed through their own apparatus, flasks shattering around them, bone towers toppling onto their crumpled forms. The research grounds that had stood for eons finished their rearrangement in less than a second.","Two figures remained standing.","Octavius and Valeria held their ground.","They had both been struck. He had seen the impact land on them, had felt the resistance his weavings encountered. But neither of them had been knocked back. Neither of them was even visibly strained!","Valeria’s crimson braids swayed once from the force and settled. Octavius adjusted the cuff of one emerald sleeve with the fingers of the other hand as a faint sea of infinity swirled around him.","|The weight of Infinity and Quintessence Infiniforce distributed equally across all hostile targets.|","|Against all engineered Primordial Architects on the primary island, single-strike termination(one hit, one kill) was not achieved. Engineered stability exceeds standard Primordial Architect thresholds.|","|Result: Five of seven targets incapacitated or displaced. Two targets unhindered.|","|Octavius Kraethos and Valeria Morne have sustained negligible damage.|","...!","Noah’s smile turned dangerous.","\" You try sending your infectious weavings of Unity to me or those around me again ,\" he said, his voice drifting across the ruined island with the patience of a decision already finalized, \" and I really won’t leave your corpse in one piece.\"","Octavius smiled brilliantly.","He rolled his shoulders. Cracked his neck once, a small sharp sound that shouldn’t have carried across the distance and somehow did.","\" Big guy. Infinity-bearer. Infinite Conduit. Whatever name you want to take for yourself.\"","His pale gold eyes shone with a hunger that had finally found its proper subject.","\"I do wish to tell you that we are not like any Primordial Architects you’ve encountered before. We are the Chosen. Our Egos burn brightly with Greed that radiantly resists the madness of Infinity, the same madness that would have you drowning if you weren’t whatever exception you happen to be. If you thought this was going to be easy, I’m sorry to disappoint. The disappointment...will be educational, I promise.\"","...!"]},{"number":5133,"title":"Chapter 5133: Chapter 5132: Greed! IV","paragraphs":["Octavius tapped one finger against the air beside him.","A unique sea of Infinity bloomed out from his body, this one tinged with the sickly gold-green of Greed refined into fuel. The sea flowed outward and downward, pouring toward the golden table at the center of the island, and the corpse on that table began to tremble.","The fungi laced through its ribs moved.","They wove across the opened chest cavity rapidly, closing the body they had spent so long opening, stitching the subject back together with threads of pale bioluminescence. The corpse’s limbs twitched, then straightened. In a single fluid motion it sat up, then stood, then launched itself off the table to stand before Octavius!","Rivers of Infinity surged down toward it from every direction, the diverted channels of the research apparatus finally feeding into their intended recipient.","Noah observed all of it.","The body that straightened in front of Octavius was unfinished. The engineering was raw. The weavings holding it together strained against each other in configurations that shouldn’t have held at all. And then it opened its eyes.","WO! WO! WO!","Glistening blue crystalline pupils of pure Infinity shone out from a face that had been a corpse a moment earlier.","He understood what he was looking at instantly!","Madness.","THE Gamaidian.","The creature’s eyes held the madness of Infinity the way a lantern held flame, and his own eyes lit up with interest at the sight of it. So this was what Octavius’s latest product looked like when it stood? An abomination made from the collision of flooded Infinity and something else, held together by engineering that shouldn’t have been possible and somehow was!","| Entity Detected: Unnamed Abomination, Latest Product of Octavius Kraethos.|","|Status: Conscious. Hostile. Unstable.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Calymmian Tier verging on Ediacaran Tier(Again, Scale ranking is not to be trusted).|","|Engineering Signature: THE Gamaidian saturation paired with unstable amplification of Ego of Hunger. Control tether active and routed through Octavius Kraethos.|","|Threat Level: Unknown. Combat parameters cannot be fully predicted due to unstable modifications.|","Beside him, Emotive moved to speak.","Noah raised his hand and stopped her before the first syllable left her mouth.","\" Stand back and do not interfere.\"","His voice held the quiet steadiness of a directive that didn’t need to be repeated.","\" Naldine, keep an eye on the surroundings. Make sure nothing new bothers us while I’m working. I feel like I’ll be getting a bit serious here.\"","His gaze settled on the abomination with its glistening mad eyes.","\"I want to see. I want to see!\"","...!","BOOM!","Terrifying pressure erupted out from his standing form.","It rolled outward in every direction at once, invisible to the eye and yet perceivable by every existence within its range. The ambient air buzzed. The floating island trembled beneath him. The diverted rivers of Observable Force shuddered in their courses!","Even Naldine’s existence braced slightly as the wave passed over her, her vihuela humming awake in response to the density of what had just been released.","| Civilization Activation Detected: THE Hadean Haki of Infinity.|","|This authority extends from your Cause and applies existential pressure across the surrounding region. Common Rhyacian and Calymmian Tier Proterozoic Scale entities cannot move freely under the weight of this Haki while your Cause sustains it. Higher-tier entities will experience significant hindrance depending.|","Naldine’s singularity-dotted eyes widened with astonishment.","She had sparred with him. She had been filled by him. She had been present for his ascensions and witnessed the unfolding of each new capability as it bloomed across his Hadean foundation!","And even she looked at him differently now, her frown tightening with the specific respect of a being who had just been reminded that she hadn’t yet mapped the full breadth of what he was.","Emotive turned toward him with eyes that had gone fervent in a way that bordered on religious.","On the island below, the Rhyacian Tier Primordial Architect who had been flung across the surface simply lost consciousness.","Her body went slack where it had been crumpled. Her power sputtered out of her like a candle in a draft, unable to maintain itself against the weight of Haki that her engineering wasn’t ready to process.","The other Primordial Architects who had been flung aside struggled to rise.","Their limbs shook. Their own weavings of authority slowed to sluggish crawls. They could move, barely, but they couldn’t move freely. The pressure had turned their every motion into labor, and their Greed-amplified foundations weren’t optimized for this particular kind of resistance.","Octavius smiled heavily.","He shook his head with the delighted incredulity of someone who had been presented with an even grander puzzle than he had bargained for.","\" Man.\"","He rolled his shoulders beneath the pressure, working himself loose by fractions.","\" Are you really the real deal? Man, alright! Come then! You may be grand, I’ll grant you that, you may be something the ordinary methodologies haven’t accounted for. But you...\"","His pale gold eyes gleamed brightly through the weight of the Haki.","\" You are not a Chosen.\"","...!","He wasn’t Chosen?","So that was how they framed it internally. Being selected to be engineered by THE Gilded Ones was, in their own scholarly vocabulary, being Chosen. Capital fuckin’ C!","The grand distinction between themselves and every other being across Observable Existence. The mark of having been selected from among the many to receive what the many would never touch.","Hah.","He detested the idea of chosen ones.","Nobody chose anyone to be the savior of everyone. The concept was a convenient fiction that fake chosen ones told themselves to feel grander than the circumstances that had produced them, and it was the same fiction their beneficiaries used to justify whatever hierarchies they had built on top of that designation.","One had to move their own ass! One had to do everything they could with the power they actually possessed. Not because some higher entity had pointed a finger and whispered you. Not because some engineering protocol had written superiority into their foundations before they ever drew their first breath.","You acted because you were capable.","You rose because you refused to stop rising.","Chosen was a word for those who needed permission to matter.","He did not need permission to matter!","Nobody pointed a finger at him and said hey, you are the Chosen One!","Noah lowered his hand slowly, the Haki settling into its sustained state around him, and he looked down at Octavius at this moment, rivers of blue and gold began to seethe around him!","Existence seethed, and battle bloomed explosively!","The abomination moved first.","It launched from its standing position in front of Octavius without a wind-up, without a tell, without any of the telegraphed aggression!","One instant it stood beside its maker. The next instant it was in the air above Noah, its glistening blue crystalline pupils burning with madness locked onto him with the single overriding directive of its amplified Hunger.","Its mouth opened!","It opened wider than its jaw should have allowed, then wider still, the fungal stitching across its chest splitting down the middle to reveal a second mouth beneath the first. Rivers of mad Infinity poured from both openings, saturated with THE Gamaidian, warped into configurations that bit at the edges of perception. The entire sky above Noah became a gullet reaching down to swallow him whole!","Noah stood where he was.","He raised one hand.","Observable Force surged up from the rivers woven through the island, answering his call with the obedience of currents bending toward a moon. It pooled in the palm he had raised, condensed into a disc of golden pressure that weighed the open air down around it, and he pushed.","The disc of Observable Force met the descending gullet at its apex.","BOOM!","The abomination’s two mouths slammed shut against the disc and couldn’t close further. Its jaw stretched against pressure that refused to yield. Its eyes rolled back briefly as the mad Infinity pouring from its openings rebounded down its own throat, and it was thrown upward through its own attack, spinning end over end across the ruined sky of the island!","WU! WU!","Octavius tapped two fingers together.","Weavings of Unity bloomed outward from the motion. Pale tendrils of concentrated weavings of Primordial Mycelia reached through the ambient Infinity like roots through loose soil, seeking every surface they could bond to. They reached for Noah’s feet. They reached for the air around his lungs. They threaded along the island’s stone, trying to establish contact vectors that would let Unity propagate into his existential foundations.","They reached Naldine as well.","They got nowhere near her.","Her vihuela hummed awake behind her, and a single note rang out across the floating island, clean and cold and causal. The Unity weavings that had reached for her unraveled back along their own paths, not destroyed, simply rewritten, so that their original intent became something that had never quite happened. Naldine’s singularity-dotted eyes held Octavius’s pale gold ones with the calm disdain of a Hadean woman who had been briefly interrupted!","The weavings reaching for Noah fared differently.","They touched his Hadean Dermis of Infinite Interface, and they dissolved against it like salt against a sea. The Unity bond couldn’t find a foundation to root into!","His engineering didn’t present the attachment points the Mycelia required. The tendrils flailed blindly across his skin for a fraction of a moment and then simply faded, their reach spent against a surface that refused to acknowledge them.","Valeria moved in from the left at this time as these three swarmed Noah!","HUUM!","Her approach was different from Octavius’s. Where he built, she cut. Her hands carried blades of compressed Infinity that sang as they sliced through the air, each edge honed into configurations that would have severed the weavings of most Calymmian Primordial Architects before those weavings could register being cut. She closed the distance in three strides, and on the third stride her blades were already falling toward his neck!","Noah caught both of them.","His Hadean Hands of Infinite Grasp closed around the edges as if they were wooden dowels, and the Infinity she had poured into her weapons drained down his arms in visible currents, pulled into his own reserves through contact alone!","Oh!","Her dark eyes widened for the first time since she had entered the engagement. Her hands tried to pull her blades back. They didn’t come!","He leaned his head toward her slowly.","\" Greed ,\" he said conversationally, his voice pitched for her ears alone. \" That’s the Ego they amplified in you. The hunger for what you don’t yet have. You reach for my Infinity, and I thank you for the offering. The weavings... feed better when they’re willingly given.\"","Her mouth opened to respond.","He released one of her blades and used the freed hand to slap her across the temple with a casual backhand!","WAA!"]},{"number":5134,"title":"Chapter 5134: Chapter 5133: Greed! V","paragraphs":["Valeria spun once through the air, hit the stone of the island, skidded, and came up into a crouch twenty paces away. Her braids had come loose along one side. A thin line of golden blood traced down her cheek from the corner of her brow. She straightened with measured calm, her shoulders rolling as she reset her posture, and then she drew both blades of infinity again without a word.","Above, the abomination completed its spin.","It came back down toward Noah faster than it had gone up!","Its jaws didn’t open this time. Its hands extended forward in front of its body, and from those hands erupted long jagged talons made of concentrated madness, THE Gamaidian given edge and purpose!","The air screamed around the talons as they descended, Infinity twisting into configurations that refused to resolve into any stable geometry.","Octavius launched new weavings from behind the abomination.","His Unity reached through the air in coordination with the abomination’s strike, not trying to bond with Noah now but trying to bond with the talons themselves, trying to graft them into Noah’s body once they connected so that the embedded weapons would root and spread and turn Noah into new soil for Primordial Mycelia.","Valeria came in from the left again at the same instant.","Three angles. Three attacks!","Three different methodologies converging on his standing position with the precision of a rehearsal that had been waiting!","Oh!","Noah watched all of it.","His eyes drank in the weavings as they approached. The mad Infinity of the abomination, wild and beautiful in its chaotic saturation. The Unity of Octavius, patient and infinite in its approach!","Valeria’s cutting Infinity, clean and scholarly in its geometry. Three different expressions of what Infinity could become in the hands of beings who had been engineered to hold it, and all three of them reaching for him at once.","He found himself genuinely interested.","The madness especially. THE Gamaidjan was rare. Most beings who fell into it were consumed too quickly for any meaningful study, their weavings dissolving into incoherent pressure before anyone could trace what the madness was actually doing to them at the fundamental level. But here it was, harnessed, walking, attacking with something that passed for strategy!","Octavius had achieved something grand.","Noah smiled brilliantly.","He raised both his hands upward into the descending convergence of attacks.","HUUM!","Seas of blue Infinity erupted outward from his body in concentric waves, the blue deepening through cobalt and into something closer to void as the density compounded against itself.","Multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce bloomed between the blue currents, golds and violets and purple and silvers braiding through the blue without mixing with it, each color holding its own distinct weaving. The ambient Infinity of the region bent toward him. The rivers of Observable Force on the island curved upward to feed his expanding authority!","Above his head, THE Hadean Pillar of Infinity manifested.","It rose from his crown as if it had always been there and had simply been waiting for permission to be seen. Crystalline blue trees of THE First Tongue formed its base. Multicolored flames of Existence licked through its mid-tiers. Infinite mirrors of Paradox reflected impossibilities at every angle. The eternal storm of Chaos swirled at its apex, and beneath that apex the additional actualized Civilizations layered themselves in concentric halos of authority!","The Pillar towered upward toward a sky that suddenly seemed very small by comparison.","His voice rolled out across the island with calm grand finality.","\" Freeze.\"","...!","HUUM!","Every entity whose body held Infinity within it froze in place!","The abomination’s descending talons halted a hand’s width from Noah’s upraised palms. Its body hung in the air above him, arrested mid-motion, its glistening mad eyes wide and unmoving!","Octavius’s Unity weavings stopped propagating, their tendrils suspended in the act of reaching, their patient weavings paused between one breath and the next. Valeria’s blades froze at the edge of their arc, her dark eyes locked on Noah from her approaching stride, her braids still half-loosed from the earlier impact.","On the broader island, the Primordial Architects who had been struggling to rise stopped rising.","The ones who had been knocked unconscious remained unconscious, their Infinity reservoirs held still within their stalled forms. The ambient rivers of Infinity threading through the island paused in their golden flow, their currents held motionless as if the island’s entire circulatory system had been told to wait!","| Civilization Activation Detected: THE Hadean Pillar of Infinity - Dominion of Internal Infinity.|","|This authority extends from your Pillar into every existence whose body holds Infinity within the surrounding region. You have asserted temporary control over the Infinity inside each affected being.|","|Strain Analysis: Negligible strain against common Proterozoic Scale entities. Minor strain against engineered subjects. Moderate strain against the abomination due to its unstable saturation with THE Gamaidian.|","|Duration: Sustainable for an extended period at current Civilizational Access. Release of authority is at your discretion.|","Only Naldine and Emotive remained moving.","He hadn’t extended the authority toward either of them. Naldine, because she was his. Emotive, and because there was no point in freezing his own tool.","He laughed.","It rolled out of him low at first, a sound that startled the shocked Naldine beside him because she had rarely heard it in this register. It built as he laughed, rising into something louder, something that bordered on the mad but never quite crossed the threshold, because he wasn’t mad!","He...wasn’t mad!","He was delighted. Waves of blue and multicolored Infinity shone across his skin as he laughed, his hair radiating its multicolored light in pulses that matched the rhythm of his amusement, his fair skin illuminating gold from within as if a sun had decided to use his form as its vessel!","\" Infinity!\"","His voice rolled out between bursts of his laughter.","\" All of you, every single one of you, you carry it inside yourselves and you speak of it as if it belongs to you. You call it yours. You cultivate your amplified Egos to withstand it, and you tell yourselves that the withstanding is mastery. That holding the flood makes the flood into something that serves you!\"","He laughed again, tilting his head back slightly.","\" It never belonged to any of you!\"","His Pillar blazed brighter above him.","\" Infinity doesn’t have owners. It has channels. Every being who carries a sea of it inside their chest is a channel, and channels do not dictate the direction of what moves through them. You were engineered to hold a flood that was never yours, and the best of you learned to pretend the flood was obedient. The pretense worked because nobody had ever come along to correct it. And now I’m here. Now someone has finally come along!\"","\"I HAVE COME!\"","BOOM!","He spread his arms wider, Pillar towering, Infinity blooming in every direction.","\" So hold still.\"","His smile stretched slowly.","\" I’d like to look at each of you properly. Show me your infinity...and I will show you mine!\"","WAA!","The island held its breath around him.","Above, the abomination’s frozen eyes still burned with their trapped madness, and Noah turned his gaze toward those eyes first as astoundingly...a bright blue of utter glory and superiority reflected in his eyes!","But he was not mad.","No. He...was not mad!"]},{"number":5135,"title":"Chapter 5135: Chapter 5134: Dissection! I","paragraphs":["THE Living Emotive had been siphoning emotions across Observable Existence for a time now. She had been cataloguing the flavors of every feeling she could pull down from the ambient currents. She had been doing this with the calm professionalism of someone who knew her own craft!","And she had never, ever, ever felt an Infinity like her Fixation’s.","Like, really. She wanted to be clear about that.","The ones on this island? Fine. Ordinary flavors. Recognizable. Octavius first, because he was the loudest of them, emotionally speaking. His signature rolled across the ambient air in layers, and her senses peeled every layer apart without effort, and every single layer beneath the surface tasted the same.","Greed. Anh, so much Greed!","Not the petty kind. Not the kind lesser beings carried when they wanted a friend’s wife.","This was Greed refined across eons into a discipline. Greed cultivated into methodology. Greed so precisely engineered that it had become the vessel his Infinity rested inside. His sea of it tasted sharp and hungry and organized, and the organization was the whole trick. The Greed held the flood the way a dam held a river, and the river obeyed because the dam had been designed to be obeyed.","Valeria’s Infinity tasted similar, but sourer. Sheesh, so much sourer! Her Greed carried the tang of someone who had watched three failed experiments before this one and had folded each failure into her own ambition. The Rhyacian one collapsed on the ground tasted duller. Just flat Greed, plateaued, the kind that stopped reaching because its owner had stopped reaching. The other Calymmians between them, all variations on the same chord, different notes in the same engineered song.","The Abomination, though.","Oh!","The Abomination!","Emotive’s hair rippled through colors she usually saved for mourning as she looked at it. The emotion pouring off the frozen creature was a single note held too long. Held so long it had stretched past music into something that ate music!","Hunger. Endless Hunger. But the Hunger was already collapsing into THE Gamaidjan around the edges, and where the two met, something that wasn’t quite an emotion pulsed beneath the surface. It was...Madness.","The madness of Infinity on a leash. The leash was fraying. Mmm, she could see it fraying, and Octavius clearly hadn’t finished tying the final knots before her Fixation had shown up with his questions and his Pillar and his extremely inconvenient timing.","Then she turned her senses toward Noah. Her Fixation!","And every comparison broke.","She wanted to say this carefully, because she was feeling a lot right now and she wanted to be a good little witness to what she was experiencing instead of spiraling, which she could absolutely do if she wasn’t paying attention.","His Infinity...didn’t taste of a single Ego.","It tasted of everything.","Her hair burst through colors she hadn’t known lived inside her palette. Layer upon layer upon layer of emotion, each one distinct, each one stable, each one woven into the next without any of them dominating. Calm sat beside rage, and neither contaminated the other. Tenderness coexisted with tyranny in the same breath, and the tenderness didn’t make the tyranny soft and the tyranny didn’t make the tenderness cruel.","Hunger pulsed alongside satisfaction. Pride breathed next to humility. Cruelty held hands with mercy. None of it was contradictory. None of it was warring. None of it was collapsing the others out of the picture, which, like, emotions normally did that, emotions usually wanted the spotlight, and here they were sharing it!","Was that his secret? Was that it? Was that really it?","Oh!","Was that why he was immune to the madness of Infinity?","She thought about it the way she thought about everything.","The engineered ones amplified a single Ego to hold the flood. Simple solution, elegant even, she could respect it. But her Fixation, THE Youngest, had amplified all of them. Countless colors of emotion, each one as cultivated as Octavius’s Greed, each one as refined as Valeria’s cutting discipline, each one its own channel for his Infinity to rest within. If one Ego could hold a flood, then countless Egos could hold an ocean. And the ocean would move through him without madness, because no single weaving would ever be asked to hold more than it had been built to carry.","Her eyes shone brilliantly as she watched him move like a work of art. And he fucking was a work of art!","Then he raised his hands, and his massive Pillar manifested above him, and he said the word.","\" Freeze.\"","...!","Okay. Okay okay okay!","Her existence trembled with fervor as his Infinity poured outward, and what she saw with her emotional senses...oh, oh, oh!","In the Infinities filled with Greed and Hunger and all the carefully amplified Egos of the engineered, she felt his emotions flourish. His grand weavings threaded into their seas the way ink threaded into water. Spreading along every channel they had cultivated so carefully. Finding the precise emotional foundations their Egos had built. And then just taking them over. Like it was nothing!","Their engineering became the instrument of his authority!","The Greed that had held Octavius’s flood in place now held still, because Noah’s weavings had climbed through Infinity into that Greed and pulled the reins.","He hadn’t broken their engineering.","He had used it.","He had used it!","He had used it, and she was never going to recover from the elegance of that.","Every being whose body held Infinity locked in place, and she felt it happen from the inside, because her senses worked from the inside, and she felt the frozen ones stop moving because something grander had threaded itself through their own reservoirs of infinity and told those reservoirs to still.","Emotive blinked.","She blinked again!","Her Fixation laughed, his voice rolling out across the island, waves of blue and multicolored Infinity shining across his skin, his hair radiating pulses of colors she had never seen on any being’s head. Her heart beat so rapidly that she had to pull on emotions of calm just to hear herself think!","And even then her hair kept flickering between silvers and pure radiant whites!","Was her Fixation not truly mad?","Was he?","Wasn’t he?","Mmm. The thought lodged itself in her for a moment, and she turned it over, because comparison was the only tool she trusted when she was this overwhelmed.","She turned her senses back to the Abomination. The creature’s frozen eyes still burned with THE Gamaidjan. When she tasted that madness, what she found beneath it was emotion that had collapsed into a single unstable note. A single hungry scream. A scream that had lost the ability to be anything except itself. That was madness. That was what madness felt like from the outside. One note, forever, no harmony.","Then she turned her senses back to Noah.","His emotions were far too stable for that.","Far too stable. Far, far too stable. Far, far, far too stable!","Countless colors, every one of them distinct, every one of them content to exist alongside every other. Harmony wasn’t even the right word, because harmony implied a small number of notes in agreement. This was a symphony. And the symphony was so large that the absence of any single note would have made the whole composition noticeably smaller.","Her Fixation couldn’t possibly be mad.","No.","He was not mad.","She shook her head slowly, her hair settling into a deep reverent gold, and she kept watching him laugh with his hands raised and his Pillar blazing above him!"]},{"number":5136,"title":"Chapter 5136: Chapter 5135: Dissection! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes were bright as he looked at the bound Primordial Architects floating before him.","Above him, THE Hadean Pillar of Infinity buzzed with the soft hum of a forge just before its next strike. He called upon the Civilizations nested within it, and three of them bloomed outward at his summons. Undifferentiated Fate first, its golden light pouring down from the Pillar in long molten ribbons.","Relativity next, its purple currents folding through the space around him in configurations that bent distance into obedience. Outerversal last, its obsidian weavings rising from the depths of the Pillar like something fished up from a sea that had no bottom.","The three Civilizations wove together in the air in front of him and became chains.","Golden, purple, and obsidian. Braided along their lengths, each link carrying the weight of all three Civilizations at once.","His Pillar of Infinity held every actualized Civilization he possessed. That had been the point of building it this way. He could call on them individually, layer them however he wanted, and each one would still carry the full weight of Infinity because the Pillar was where Infinity and Civilization met.","The chains moved.","HUUM!","They struck outward across the floating island, uncoiling through the frozen air with the steady confidence of predators that had been bred for exactly this kind of work. They wrapped Octavius first. Then Valeria. Then the other Calymmians scattered across the ruined apparatus!","Then the unconscious Rhyacian. Then the Abomination still hanging above, its jaws still arrested mid-bite. Each being was coiled into its own individual harness, lifted from wherever it had been frozen, and laid flat on its back in space.","Relative to him. He floated above them now.","Below him, they floated in a neat row beneath his position, like specimens on trays!","Shock sat in their eyes. Sombreness behind the shock. Every one of them stared up through the weight of his Haki, and every one of them understood something in that moment that they hadn’t quite believed before the chains had settled around their limbs.","The Chosen designation had limits. The limits had just introduced themselves!","Noah checked the strain inside himself.","It was akin to an invisible muscle deep in his mind held every bound Primordial Architect in place, each one a thread his attention was keeping taut. Octavius took the most force, naturally. The Greed-amplified Architect had the most foundation of the lot, and his engineering pushed back against the control of his Infinity with the most sustained resistance. But even he was manageable!","He waved his hand.","Octavius’s bound body slid through the air toward him, golden and purple and obsidian chains dragging it closer until it hovered directly beneath Noah’s floating position. The Architect’s pale gold eyes held up at him with the defiant light of a being whose Greed hadn’t yet conceded anything.","Defiance was useful. Defiance meant the Ego was still active, still humming, still demonstrating the configurations Noah wanted to study.","Beneath Octavius, Infinity surged.","It gathered from the ambient currents of THE Wyld, poured upward from the rivers of the island, and condensed into a radiant blue table of brilliance. The table materialized beneath his floating body with the quiet finality of an operating surface being delivered. Octavius’s back came to rest against its glowing surface. The chains adjusted, flattening him further, binding his arms out to his sides in the universal posture of subjects who were about to become specimens.","Noah looked down at him.","\" The human body is made of countless things.\"","His voice carried calmly across the island, unhurried and conversational.","\" Even without mana. Even without any authority or refinement at all. The human body on its own is a marvel, and most humans go their entire short lives without ever realizing what they’re actually walking around in. Ordinary flesh and bone. Ordinary blood. Ordinary everything. And yet the composition of that ordinary body, if you trace it back far enough, tells a history that stretches across the entire life of its universe.\"","He watched Octavius’s eyes for a flicker of interest as there was none, but he kept going.","\" The body’s made mostly of oxygen. About sixty-five percent by mass. Then carbon, about eighteen percent. Hydrogen, around ten. Nitrogen, three. Then calcium, phosphorus, potassium, sulfur, sodium, chlorine, magnesium. Trace amounts of iron, zinc, copper, selenium, iodine, and so on down the line. Every one of those elements has a story. Every one of them had to be made somewhere before it ended up inside a walking human being.\"","His fingers moved absently in the air as he spoke, conducting his own words with tendrils of infinity.","\" Hydrogen and most of the helium came from the early universe itself, formed in the first three minutes after the Big Bang. Everything heavier was forged inside stars. Carbon, oxygen, nitrogen, all cooked up in the cores of stars that lived and died across billions of years. The calcium in bones? Forged in stellar fusion. The iron in blood? Made in massive stars and then scattered across space when those stars exploded as supernovae. The iodine in the thyroid, the selenium, the heavier elements? Those came from neutron star mergers and the deaths of the largest stars.\"","He paused, almost amused at his own digression.","\"If I could say one thing to every manaless human I ever walked past back in time in the old world, I’d tell them they were unfathomably grand. And it...is not because they achieved anything. Not even because they cultivated anything. Simply because...they were made of the stuff of stars. Every atom in their bodies had been inside a star at some point. Their calcium had been forged in stellar fire. Their iron had ridden a supernova across the cosmos. They were walking around carrying the ashes of dead suns in their bones, and most of them died without ever thinking about it.\"","Octavius’s eyes held steady, defiance still burning behind them.","\" Every single body and existence has age. Every single body and existence has history. The body you’re lying on this table with, Octavius, tells everything it can possibly tell about you. What you went through. What modifications were written into you. How you were engineered. How you were born. What you ate across eons, what you absorbed, what passed through you and left traces. If an existence is studied closely enough, all of this can be extracted. All of it.\"","He leaned forward slightly, the Pillar above him blazing brighter.","\"So here’s the question I’ve been turning over. What is a Primordial Architect made of? What is Octavius made of? If I break your components down to their foundational weavings, can I design a Primordial Architect? If I account for all of your ingredients, all of your authorities, all of the engineering the Gilded Ones wrote into your existential makeup, can I design and replicate you entirely from the ground up?\"","His smile was mild!","\" What do you think?\"","...!"]},{"number":5137,"title":"Chapter 5137: Chapter 5136: Dissection! III","paragraphs":["Octavius’s eyes burned colder.","The defiant light in them sharpened into something almost glacial, the Greed behind it refusing to give Noah the satisfaction of a verbal response. Noah didn’t need one. The eyes were answer enough!","He got started.","He waved his hand, and on his palm boundless multicolored Infinity converged together. It braided into a sharp point. It elongated into a blade. It settled into his fingers as a scalpel of pure Infinite light. He twirled it once between his fingers, the way a surgeon might test the balance of a new instrument.","He lowered the scalpel to Octavius’s chest.","The tip touched the skin of a supposed fucking Chosen One, and the skin parted.","The Ego of Greed holding his flood of Infinity in place flickered in response to the wound, and Noah watched that flicker with the close attention of one who had just been shown the first useful data point of the session. The skin peeled back along his scalpel’s path. The deeper tissues followed. Engineered weavings came into view, and they were beautiful in their way, architecturally beautiful, the kind of work Noah could respect even while he was disassembling it.","As he cut, seas of Infinity converged around the region.","In the next instant, multiple bodies of his own materialized into being, each one glowing with the soft blue of concentrated Infinity, each one forming above a different bound Primordial Architect along the row of floating blue tables beneath him. Each duplicate held its own multicolored scalpel. Each duplicate lowered its blade to the chest of its assigned specimen at the same moment. Valeria’s body opened beneath one of them. The Abomination’s body opened beneath a third. The entire research archipelago became, in a breath, a landmass running every dissection at once.","Noah kept his primary attention on Octavius and The Abomination.","As his scalpel moved, his mind drifted.","Ubergulden Adelheid.","THE Gilded Ones.","If they were leaning into emotions as the biggest thing to combat the madness of Infinity, and if he was finding the amplified Ego of Greed written all over this engineered Architect, then a pattern was starting to trace itself across the data. He’d been hearing Ego of Pride, Ego of Wrath, Ego of Passion. Now Ego of Greed was in his hands literally. Emotions being amplified deliberately, cultivated as the channels through which Infinity could be held without triggering THE Gamaidjan.","The pattern was familiar.","Seven deadly sins. That was what was lining up in his head. Pride, Greed, Wrath, Lust, Envy, Gluttony, Sloth. Before, they’d been moral categories and warnings. The dark configurations a human life could fall into if it let its Egos run unchecked.","The Gilded Ones had taken those exact configurations and turned them into engineering specifications. The darkest emotional categories inflated into cultivation foundations grand enough to hold floods of Infinity.","And he’d already had these concepts lodged deep inside him for ages. He’d already actualized them within his Pillar. He held all of them at once, every one of them amplified to functional intensity, every one of them sitting alongside every other without conflict.","The next question was whether the Gilded Ones stopped at sins.","Did they do virtues too? Charity, Patience, Kindness, Humility, Temperance, Diligence, Chastity. The counterweights. If the sins made good channels for Infinity, the virtues should have made good channels as well, and any engineering program worth running would have tested both sides of the equation.","Had they? Was there a whole second category of engineered Primordial Architects out there running on amplified Charity, amplified Patience? Would he find one of those next?","And where did Ubergulden Adelheid fit in any of this?","Which amplified Ego had the Gilded Ones wired into her foundation? Which configuration was she running on, underneath the seal, underneath the surface of the being who’d looked at him with calm golden eyes?","He could find out.","He could connect with her through his Quintessence Infiniforce again!","Octavius’s body splayed open further beneath his scalpel.","The chest cavity parted fully. The engineered weavings laid themselves out for his inspection. The Ego of Greed pulsed in visible patterns across his exposed foundations, a gold-green lattice woven into the deeper substrate of his existence, the channels of his Infinity reservoir clearly defined against the darker weavings beneath.","Noah leaned closer as he began to see!","---","Minutes passed.","Naldine stayed behind him and watched him while monitoring everything in the surroundings, the good girl she was. Her singularity-dotted eyes swept the edges of Emotive’s emotional blockade and her own Hadean Barrier of Infinity at steady intervals, her vihuela humming softly against her back. Nothing was getting in. Nothing was getting out!","She was handling what he’d asked her to handle, and she was handling it without needing further instruction.","Emotive, the tool, had kept her creepy gaze on him completely the entire time. Her hair had cycled through more color combinations than most Civilizations held in their entire lexicon. He could only imagine the craziness going on inside her mind. He wasn’t particularly interested in imagining it closely.","But right now he paused over the opened and dissected bodies of the Primordial Architects, and his eyes shone brilliantly.","THE Gilded Ones were truly grand.","The engineering laid out beneath him was, professionally speaking, extraordinary.","They hadn’t only amplified an Ego. They’d altered the very makeup of existence in Octavius and the others from the ground up. Greed was the foundation, yes, the emotion they’d selected for cultivation. But the amplification wasn’t a single inflated channel. It was a network. Intricate, layered, woven through every stratum of the subject’s Bounded Lifeform existence.","They’d taken an ordinary Bounded Lifeform and designed within it a latticework of Greed so dense and stable that Infinity could pour through those channels without triggering THE Gamaidjan. The Ego had been made extreme enough to overcome the madness. The flood had been given specific, engineered rivers to flow down!","Oh!","That alone would have been grand work. But they hadn’t stopped there.","Layered beneath the Greed network, written into Octavius’s existential foundations with the kind of quiet precision that only hands grander than his own could have managed, were additional modifications. Silent ones.","The kind a subject would never be able to detect within themselves because the modifications had been branded onto the Civilizational Anchor itself, fused into the very Civilization the subject had anchored their Second Scale to.","Those modifications altered the subject’s thoughts.","Nothing as blunt as commands or compulsions. The modifications made Octavius and his peers genuinely believe they were Chosen. It wasn’t something they had chosen to adopt out of pride. It had been written into them before they’d even known what they were, so deeply that by the time any of them could reflect on the belief, reflection could no longer separate the belief from the self. If any of them ever stood before a Gilded One, immense reverence would pour out of them automatically!","They would do everything they were commanded. Their entire existences could be shut down by the ones who engineered them, because a kill-switch had been woven into the same Civilizational Anchor that held their power together.","It was nasty stuff.","Genuinely nasty! Well-designed, efficient, beautiful in its craftsmanship, but nasty in every moral direction the word could point.","Noah looked down at Octavius and the others and shook his head slowly before he waved his hand.","He understood the intricacies well enough now, and he wanted to apply what he’d learned before he moved on from this island. Towards the peak of power, self-identity was critical.","There were no sages of enlightened minds!","Egos had to be amplified. Many beings did this as a last resort against the madness of Infinity, though he didn’t have that issue himself, not the way they did. But that didn’t mean he had nothing to learn here. His own identity, his own Ego, was another avenue of cultivation he hadn’t fully leaned into, and there was still much to grasp.","Because from everything he’d gathered...from Naldine, from THE Beholder, from THE Creature and from the Living Emotive. From the memories he was currently harvesting out of Octavius and the others on their floating tables. Infinity was only part of the equation. The part that was difficult but ultimately accessible to enough beings with enough cultivation.","There was still THE Primordial Source . And nobody he’d met yet knew what it was or how to access it.","He’d take it slow. He was still getting a grasp of Infinity, and Infinity alone was unfathomably vast, the kind of ocean that rewarded patient swimmers and drowned the impatient ones. He’d engineered his own Scales of Existence using Infinity as the foundational substrate, which meant he could do things Vakochev’s preset Scales couldn’t.","His Scales were infinite! He could change them. He could transform them as he went. He could fold new stages into the existing ones or bolt new stages onto the framework entirely, and the framework would accept those additions because it had been designed to.","He’d established THE First Infinite Scale already and three Demarcations inside it. Infinitas Corpus, completed. Infinitas Architectura, in progress. Infinitas Causa, waiting.","He could alter any of these. If Ego turned out to be critical, he’d include it. If something else worthy came up, he’d include that too!","So the plan was simple. Learn all avenues of Infinity. Grasp as much of it as he could. Keep building his Hadean Pillar of Infinity toward Absolute Infinity in Infinitas Architectura, which was the immediate goal, the milestone he was working toward even as the Pillar blazed above him now. It was one way his power was continuing to rise. If amplified self-identity and Ego was another way, he’d delve into that too.","But first.","He waved his hand, and all the dissected bodies of the Primordial Architects floated up before him.","The Abomination drifted up last, still silently roaring behind its sealed jaw, its chest cavity split open alongside many other things, its glistening mad eyes rolling uselessly inside their sockets. Still alive and still frozen by his Infinity holding its sea of THE Gamaidjan in place.","Noah looked at it and smiled grandly.","\"I know what you’re made of now.\"","His voice carried across the floating island with calm certainty.","\" So I’m going to break all of you down. I’ll integrate you into a singular being. I’ll amplify that Greed even further than the Gilded Ones bothered to amplify it. And I’ll rewrite the engineering written into your existences so that it answers to me instead of them. Hang in there, all of you. We’ll see just what you’re made of when I put you back together.\"","...!"]},{"number":5138,"title":"Chapter 5138: Chapter 5137: Midas!","paragraphs":["After such words, he motioned toward his Hadean Pillar of Infinity.","HUUM!","Endless blue strings came down from the Pillar, threading through the air like the descending roots of a tree that reached between dimensions. Alongside them, rivers of the Civilization of Greed poured out of the Pillar as well, golden-green currents braiding themselves into the region.","The blue Infinity held the cold of infinite possibility. The gold-green Greed burned warmly against it, the color of amplified appetite, of accumulation refined into methodology. Together they filled the air above the floating island with a texture it had never seen before.","Noah calmly conducted the strings.","They descended onto Octavius first. The Primordial Architect’s pale gold eyes blazed with even more defiance as the blue threads touched his opened body, but what the fuck could he do?","Defiance paired with weakness meant nothing. Defiance was only meaningful when the one defying had the capacity to meaningfully refuse. Octavius had no such capacity right now. The Greed in his engineering burned brightly, but it burned within chains, and the chains answered to Noah.","Noah’s Existential Engineering began its work.","The process moved the way it had moved when he’d transformed his people into Nascent Hadean Lifeforms, but the focus was different here. He wasn’t lifting Octavius. He was disassembling him. His strings of Infinity threaded into the Primordial Architect’s foundations and began extracting the subject’s own Infinity, replacing it with his own as they went. The Ego of Greed lattice was preserved but reoriented. The rivers of his Civilization of Greed poured into Octavius through the same channels the Gilded Ones had engineered, saturating the lattice with Greed of Noah’s cultivation rather than the ambient Greed Octavius had grown with.","The Primordial Architect’s body began to break down into its component particles.","The blue strings pulled the weavings apart along the seams the dissection had already opened, and Octavius came apart the way a well-built instrument came apart when its maker knew exactly where each joint sat. His bones dissolved into streams of refined power. His organs followed. His existential substrate flowed out of him in currents of gold-green light that surged through the air toward a single destination.","The Abomination.","Noah did the same to Valeria. Then to each of the other Primordial Architects bound, one after another, his strings working across the row in steady sequence. A few minutes was all it took!","The engineered lifeforms of the research archipelago broke down into their components, and every component flowed into the Abomination at the end of the row.","Seas of Infinity churned in the air above the Abomination’s floating body!","WU! WU! WU!","Rivers of Greed flowed into it endlessly. An aura began to blaze out of the creature, an aura that exceeded anything the island had witnessed yet, the accumulated Greed-amplification of seven Primordial Architects now concentrated into a single vessel that was being redesigned on the fly.","And even though he hadn’t called on it, Observable Force began to gather and flow toward the Abomination in steady streams.","Noah watched that flow with mild interest. Observable Force was responding to the transformation on its own initiative, drawn to the process by something in the architecture of what was happening, and he could feel why the moment it arrived. The force was stabilizing the transformation. It was pacifying the volatile interactions between the multiple existences being folded into a single new existence, smoothing the seams, keeping THE Gamaidjan from overwhelming the composite as the composite took shape!","His eyes shone brilliantly as he watched it all unfold.","Toward the end, he implemented the final stage of his engineering. The transformation of the new composite into a Nascent Hadean Lifeform. Seas of Quintessence Infiniforce poured out of him. Observable Force joined the flow on its own again. Both of them cascaded into the Abomination from every direction, saturating its newly-composed foundations, writing the Nascent Hadean engineering into the creature’s bones and organs as its existence settled into its new configuration.","Another minute passed.","BOOM!","A pillar of Infinity, Observable Force, and the radiant allure of endless Greed shot upward from the Abomination’s floating form.","Noah waved his hand and his Hadean Pillar of Infinity consumed the light before it could propagate outward, pulling the signature of the transformation into itself so that nothing across the broader Wyld would be attracted by the flare. The light faded and the auras settled. The composite being hung in the air before him, finished, standing on its own against the weight of its own completion.","He looked at what he’d made.","The Abomination was now an obscenely fat humanoid thing. Wide bloated limbs. Rolls of fatty flesh.","Golden rings of pure Greed wrapped around it in orbits along every limb, at its wrists, at its ankles, at its bulging waist, at its thick neck. The rings pulsed slowly with the amplified Ego now running through every channel of its existence. Fleshy blue-gold wings erupted from its back, heavy and muscular, beating slowly against the air in a way that shouldn’t have generated lift and yet somehow kept the bloated body aloft with perfect ease.","Its face did not match its body.","Its face was supremely handsome!","The kind of face sculptors across ten thousand realms would have fought each other for the chance to render in stone. Sharp cheekbones. A jaw that cut light into neat halves. Gem like eyes deep and golden and dripping with Greed so intense it was almost quintessential!","The ferocity of that beautiful face sat perched on the bloated frame like a crown on a hoarded treasure.","Noah looked at it with shining eyes.","Endless rivers of Infinity surged into the composite being from the ambient environment, drawn by the amplified Sin of Greed running through its foundations at intensity that put the original Primordial Architects to shame. The appetite of this new lifeform was, quite literally, enormous.","\" Octavius ,\" Noah said calmly. \" Are you in there?\"","He asked it with shining eyes, genuinely curious to see what the answer would be.","The Abomination looked at him.","Its golden eyes released a blinding beam of raw power as the gaze settled on him, and in the next instant the creature kneeled in mid-air. Its wings folded neatly. Its bloated limbs pressed themselves into the posture of absolute submission. It bellowed, and the bellow carried terrifying pressure that rolled outward across the island like a tidal wave of devotion!","Even Emotive and Naldine, floating well behind him, were pushed further back by the wave. Emotive laughed in delight as she caught herself. Naldine braced calmly with her vihuela and held her position.","Noah looked at the kneeling Abomination with shining eyes.","He raised his hand and patted the creature’s abominable head.","In front of him, the prompts bloomed into his perception.","|Existential Engineering has concluded successfully. Product designated.|","| Entity Designation: Midas of Endless Appetite.|","|Classification: Nascent Hadean Lifeform.|","|Skeletal Structure: 103 bones at Proterozoic classification. 103 bones at Hadean classification. Full Hadean Physiology projected to occur within accelerated timeframe.|","|Organ Systems: 39 organs at Proterozoic classification. 39 organs at Hadean classification. Full Hadean Physiology projected to occur within accelerated timeframe.|","| Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Ediacaran Tier . Forceful ascension has occurred due to the composite influx of Quintessentially Amplified Ego of THE Sin of Greed, Infinity, and Observable Force integrated into the entity’s foundational Civilization.|","| Foundational Civilization: THE Civilization of Desecration. This Civilization has bloomed as a consequence of the forceful inclusion of multiple prior conflicting Civilizations into a single composite existence.|","|Accelerated Growth Rate: The Amplified Ego of THE Sin of Greed within Midas drives continuous self-expansion, consumption, and cultivation. Standard cultivation timeframes do not apply.|","|Unique Property: Bounded Uncountable Infinity Capacity. Midas is the first entity aside from yourself, among those under your weavings, capable of holding Bounded Uncountable Infinity within his existence.|","|Fealty: Absolute. Midas of Endless Appetite recognizes you as his Master.|","|Declaration from Midas:|","|\" Everything I see, I desire. Everything I desire, I consume. Everything I consume, I lay at the feet of my Master. Command me, and I will eat the Civilizations of your enemies until there are no more Civilizations for them to hide beneath.\"|","...!","OH!","Noah looked at the wonder before him, and his eyes shone with brilliance!"]},{"number":5139,"title":"Chapter 5139: Chapter 5138: Superbia! I","paragraphs":["Midas.","Noah looked at the fat Abomination up and down with quiet appreciation. The amplified emotion of Greed was visibly bleeding into the creature’s morphology, showing in how golden and bloated and ringed everything about him was.","With how fat the thing had ended up, Noah almost thought Midas might have fit better as Gluttony, the slightly adjacent sin, the one that ate rather than hoarded. But the engineering had been Greed. The hoarding had been Greed. The fatness was a hoarder’s fatness, the body of accumulation rather than appetite, and Greed it remained.","The power was massive.","If he used something like Grimvault as a measuring stick, his Midas was worth more than five hundred Grimvault. About five hundred times the power output. Ridiculous in itself, and even more ridiculous when he thought about Grimvault.","He looked up.","The invisible golden bubbles of Existential Singularities continued to flow into him from the targets he’d selected, and Grimvault was one of those targets. The fucker was almost drained dry at this point. He should barely have a tenth of his power left at this moment, scattered through whatever hole he’d crawled into in THE Wyld. He’d likely be dying well before the Civilizational Holy War even started. That dumb motherfucker would be the first to go. The others on the list would follow.","Behind him, Emotive came drifting around Midas with bright eyes, looping the bloated Abomination in fast circles and inspecting him from every angle the way a child inspects a new toy. Her hair flickered through golds and electric pinks as she completed her last circuit and bounced back toward Noah.","\" Ridiculously amazing work, sir!\"","Her voice carried all of its usual mania.","\" With this much power, and the information I have from those involved in the Civilizational Holy War. Mmm! It looks like you could assassinate a lot of them with this fatty here? Just send it to do your deeds across THE Wyld and be stress free! Think about it! Think about it! No more participants for them, no more contest, just rivers and rivers of dead Primordial Architects with golden ring-marks left on their corpses...\"","...!","Noah looked at her calmly without replying.","The lack of response seemed to make her even more interested. Her hair shifted into deeper golds. She floated back to her position with the contented hum of someone who had just been ignored by exactly the right being.","Naldine came up behind him as Emotive settled.","\" The problem are the truly powerful Primordial Architects.\"","Her voice held the calm caution she wore better than most. \"THE Deliverance and others of his stature, in whatever communications they may have with the Gilded Ones. Before you get too loud and do too much, it’s best to understand this first. The reach of those at the top of THE Wyld is greater than the visible reach. You strike enough of the lower ones, and something further upstream begins to take notice. Better to know what’s upstream before you wade further in.\"","One woman wanted him to go wild. The other wanted him to be careful.","Both of them were right, and both of them were correct in different directions, and the synthesis sat with him quietly as he weighed it.","A lot of factors to consider. One of the biggest was information. If he understood things a little better, he could make better choices. Going wild was tempting. Going wild was efficient. But going wild blind was the kind of choice that closed doors he might have wanted to leave open.","He continued to steadily draw on Infinity, gathering information from the surrounding regions of THE Wyld in the background of his conscious attention. This battle against Octavius, the emergence of this glorious Abomination beside him, the engineering signatures he’d peeled out of the dissected bodies. All of it would soon be integrated into his own people. He’d amplify their Egos to make them grander. He’d consider the seven sins, and the seven virtues alongside them. The Gilded Ones had probably explored both directions, and there was no reason for him to limit himself to one half of the engineering when the full set was available to study.","But there was one critical source of information he could always tap into.","He wanted to do that first. He wanted to see if he could get a clearer picture about the biggest current threat.","THE Gilded Ones.","Noah stroked Midas’s bloated head absently, the bald golden scalp warm and slimy beneath his palm.","\" Hold on a second while I consult my battery.\"","...!","His battery.","None of them knew what he was talking about, but it was, of course, none other than the entity he held a channel with that had functionally become more like a wormhole at this point. The continuous influx of Observable Force from her existence into his had stabilized into something he barely had to maintain, a permanent draw, a current that ran whether or not he was paying attention to it.","He tapped his finger out.","A throne of multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce gathered behind him, the Civilizations woven into his Pillar supplying the shape and substance. He sat down on the throne, leaned back, and closed his eyes.","He tapped into his Quintessence Infiniforce within that distant Gilded One.","A part of his consciousness bloomed in her existence in the next moment.","---","The traversal was different this time.","When he arrived inside her weavings, she was already there waiting. An illusory manifestation of her own existence sat on the multicolored waves of his Quintessence Infiniforce that filled her interior seas. Her hands were folded in her lap. Her golden eyes lifted to meet his the moment he formed.","He took her in fully.","Ubergulden Adelheid was definitely a beautiful one. Tall, even seated, with the long slender lines of someone whose proportions had been refined across eons. Her skin held a soft pearlescent gold that ran beneath the surface rather than across it, the glow of an interior sun banked low. Her hair fell in pale gold waves down past her shoulders, every strand catching the multicolored light around her.","Noah had known beautiful women across his existence. But she...she looked like a being who had been built to receive devotion rather than to seek it, and the result was a quiet inhuman elegance that the other women in his orbit didn’t carry because none of them had been engineered with that specific intention.","She sat there as if she’d been paying close attention to his approach.","But she wasn’t looking at him with her usual imperious gaze. There was no anger.","She seemed...oddly calm.","This caused him to frown. She seemed different from the Ubergulden Adelheid he’d been mentally used to. And if she was like this...","\"What happened?\"","His voice was calm to match hers, but underneath the calm sat a sharper attention. Something had to be wrong!","Toward the question, Ubergulden Adelheid remained silent.","She looked him over, up and down, with the quiet thoroughness of someone taking inventory of a familiar object after a long absence. Then she raised her hands and let her fingers trail through the Quintessence Infiniforce around them, the multicolored currents responding to her touch with little ripples that traveled outward into her interior seas.","\" Do you know why I have let all of this unfold for so long?\"","Her voice carried steady clarity.","\"Me leaving your Quintessence Infiniforce inside me. Even now, the integration is not entirely irreversible. I would pay a heavy cost to remove it, but I still could. And you cutting it off and releasing it would be the easier option, the cleaner one for both of us. I could have done heavy-handed things to force you toward that option. I could have damaged the bond from my side until removal became preferable. I could have made the cost of maintaining it unbearable for you. I did none of that.\"","She looked at him directly.","\" Do you know why?\"","...!","She spoke in a tone that was very serious.","Noah became more serious with her. Fuck. Were things bad enough on her end to warrant this kind of plain speech?","He floated closer to her seated form on her wave of Infiniforce, and he shook his head.","\" Why?\"","She looked at him for a long quiet moment before she answered.","\"I was inherently exhibiting everything I had learned as THE Secretive Eon.\"","\"I felt like you and I were alike. I had lived eons as a Bounded Lifeform, the same way you have lived as one. And that life, that long quiet life I had constructed as a Bounded among Bounded, was holding me back from cutting the bond. I have realized something. I do not want all the eons I lived as a Bounded Lifeform to be for nothing. I was different then. I am different now, even if I did not want to admit the difference until recently. And as long or short as eons can be in the broader scope of existence, it would be a shame, a real shame, if I returned to being the same Ubergulden Adelheid I was before all of that experience. When I have lived and seen and felt so much that the Adelheid of eons ago could not have imagined.\"","Her golden eyes held steady on his.","\" That is why. I want to grow. I want to understand. I want to... evolve.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5140,"title":"Chapter 5140: Chapter 5139: Superbia! II","paragraphs":["As the words left her, the surroundings inside her interior seas seethed.","Concentrations of Observable Force surged maddeningly through the multicolored Infiniforce around them, the densities reaching levels that should not have been achievable inside her without external feeding.","The waves she sat upon trembled with the intensity of currents trying to organize themselves around something new. The whole of her interior was shifting in response to what she’d just declared, as if Ubergulden Adelheid was having an epiphany in the literal physical sense, her existence reorganizing itself around the words she had just chosen to commit to out loud.","Noah focused on her closely.","She closed her eyes and opened them. Breathed once, deeply, and the seas around them settled back into a calmer rhythm.","\" Can we speak honestly?\"","Noah nodded.","\"I love speaking honestly the most.\"","She inclined her head once, almost gratefully, and then she began.","\"Bounded Lifeforms cannot fathom the edge that a Gilded Lifeform holds from the moment of conception.\"","\" And yes, Osmont, existence is unfair. Why can Gilded Lifeforms be born with endless potential at the peak of THE First Scale of Existence while Bounded Lifeforms are engineered to climb across eons just to brush against ceilings the Gilded started above? Why do Gilded children manifest authority that takes Bounded centuries to approximate? Why do our Civilizations stabilize on their own while Bounded Civilizations require exhaustive cultivation to settle? These are the consequences of design choices that were made before either of our peoples drew their first breath. Existence as it currently stands was sculpted, and it was sculpted to favor us. To favor my people. It was never fair. It was never going to be fair. And the gap between Bounded and Gilded is, as far as I knew across all of my eons, literally unsurpassable. I believed this. I knew this with the certainty of someone who had walked among both populations and measured the distance personally.\"","Her hands moved as she spoke, slowly weaving fragments of Infiniforce into illusory shapes that hung between them.","\" And then, one day, I witnessed THE Creature.\"","BOOM!","THE Creature?","Noah’s eyes widened slightly. How had THE Creature influenced her path? How had a former Primordial Architect ended up shifting the trajectory of a Gilded one’s choices to the point where she abandoned her own people to live as Bounded for eons?","She waved her hands.","A multicolored illusory outline of THE Creature appeared between them, the silhouette of a being who was already familiar to Noah, the Primordial Architect who had burned away his own classification.","\" This little Primordial Architect is a tiny and yet a grand being, \" she said softly. \" Because his story is a tragic one. And ridiculously, when you trace it back to its origin, it is a love story.\"","The illusory outline of THE Creature shifted, and beside it formed the silhouette of another figure. Smaller. Softer in its rendering. Connected to THE Creature by a thread of light that ran between their forms with the steady quiet glow of a deep bond.","\" Once, before he was THE Creature, he was simply a Primordial Architect among many. And there was THE Soul, a being he shared a connection with that ran deeper than what most beings ever experience. They lived in a region of THE Wyld together. They were quiet in their way. They built a small life that did not bother anyone, that did not reach for grand designs, that was content to simply exist alongside each other across the long slow time available to Primordial Architects.\"","A third figure formed in the illusion. Tall abd resplendent. Crowned in light that the other two figures did not carry.","\" And then a Gilded One passed through THE Wyld.\"","Her voice tightened slightly at the new figure.","\" He found them. He saw THE Soul. And he took a liking to her. The way Gilded Ones take a liking to things. With the assumption that liking something was sufficient grounds for owning it. He approached them and offered to give THE Soul power in exchange for following him. The kind of upward migration that any other being in THE Wyld would have crawled across their own corpse to receive. He offered, and he assumed the offer would be accepted, because he was a Gilded One and they were not.\"","Her golden eyes darkened.","\" THE Soul refused. THE Creature stood by her refusal. They denied him together, quietly, the way they had built their entire small life, and they assumed the matter would end there because what else was there to discuss?\"","The illusory crowned figure’s posture shifted in the air between them.","\" And then THE Gilded One was offended.\"","Her words slowed.","\" He was a prideful being. Literally so. His pride ran so deep that refusal was an attack on his foundation rather than a simple decline. He used force. He bound THE Creature where he stood, immobilized him with an exertion that THE Creature could not resist. And then, in front of THE Creature, he engineered THE Soul. He altered her existence. He rewrote her foundations. He pressed Gilded modifications into her Bounded weavings the way a brand is pressed into flesh, and he made the changes deep enough that she should no longer have been able to refuse him afterward. He made her something new. Something engineered. Something compelled.\"","Noah frowned as the illusion played out between them. His expression sharpened with each detail.","\" After the alteration, the Gilded One asked THE Soul again if she would be his.\"","Her voice held a quiet and terrible respect for what came next.","\" And of course, with the engineering and the control he had pressed into her, she should have been a different person. She should have been forced to agree. She should have spoken whatever words he wanted her to speak. The compliance should have been automatic. That was the entire point of what he had just done to her.\"","She paused.","\" And yet..she still denied him.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes held the illusory tableau without blinking.","\" The Gilded One was infuriated even further by this. Not because the engineering had failed, although that was part of it. But because the refusal under engineering was, to him, an even greater insult than the original refusal had been. He had reshaped her, and she had still chosen him last. So he proceeded to do a despicable thing. He forced himself on THE Soul. He bound THE Creature in such a way that he could not look away from any of it, could not close his eyes, could not turn his perception aside. He made THE Creature watch every moment from the first to the last.\"","The illusion did not show this part. Ubergulden Adelheid let the silhouettes hold their positions while her voice carried the rest.","\" And after he was done, he collapsed her weavings and scattered her ash into Existence. He did this in front of THE Creature too. He made a lesson of it.\"","She looked at Noah directly.","\"His final words to THE Creature were these. ’You and your kind exist beneath us because that is the order of things. Your refusal cost her this. Your defiance was the cause of her death. Remember this every time you crawl through your remaining eons. You were given a choice. You chose poorly. The next time a Gilded One offers you something, you will accept, because by then you will understand what offers from us truly are.’ And then he left THE Creature alive. That was the cruelest part of all. He left him alive.\"","...!","Adelheid shook her head slowly.","\"It was a ridiculous story. Something that didn’t need to happen. Bounded and Gilded were so far apart that there should have been no need for that kind of demonstration. THE Creature held tremendous rage afterward, and tremendous grief, but he shouldn’t have been able to do anything with either of them. A mere Second Scale Primordial Architect. Even at the peak of his classification, he was nothing in comparison to a Gilded One.\"","Her voice softened with something that was almost reverence.","\"And yet he vowed that day to find that specific Gilded One. To find him and burn him with the very existence the Gilded had used to justify their power. He shattered his own foundation. He started over. He has been working his way up ever since, climbing path after path, abandoning classifications, burning away anything that limited him, all of it pointed toward a single destination. Reaching that one Gilded One. Closing the gap that was supposed to be impossible to close.\"","She let her hands fall back to her lap.","\" His defiance toward the impossible made me try to live like Bounded Lifeforms. I had become disillusioned with the actions of my people long before that, with their casual cruelties and their assumption that the Bounded existed as a backdrop for Gilded amusement. THE Creature’s defiance crystallized something in me. Something that had been forming for a long time. So I took my seal. I went down. I lived among the Bounded for eons. And I enjoyed my time as a Bounded Lifeform. I loved it. The simplicity of it. The wonder. The naivety that came from not knowing how the broader machinery worked. None of you carry the weight of understanding the design, and there is a peace in that ignorance that I had never been allowed to taste before.\"","Her golden eyes lifted back to him.","\" Which brings us to you.\"","She drew a slow breath.","\"If we can speak honestly, I have been thinking about how far you and I can take this. Do you just want to be attached to a Gilded One? To have the access that proximity provides? Do you want to have the same power as one? Do you want to become like one yourself? Where exactly do you see this going, Osmont? I need to know what you see, because the answer changes what I do next.\"","...!","Noah’s reply came calmly, and grandly, and tyrannically!","\"Existence is...unfair.\"","He let the words sit between them.","\"And I simply want to make it fair for myself. I do not seek to become a Gilded One. The classification doesn’t interest me. The borrowed prestige doesn’t interest me. What I do not like, what I have never liked, is that existence has supposedly defined me and slotted me into a tier. A Bounded Lifeform. A category drawn around me before I was old enough to ask whether the category fit. Who decided that? Who held the authority to draw that line and place me on the lower side of it? What is existence, exactly, that it gets to decide who I am before I have a chance to decide myself?\"","His gaze held hers steadily.","\" So I want to make my own choices. I want to say that Bounded or Gilded does not matter. I want to walk forward as myself, whatever myself is, and I want that walking to carry me through every tier of every classification across every framework that anyone has ever drawn. I want to stand against Bounded Lifeforms and against Gilded Lifeforms as if the difference between them were a footnote. I do not want to be defined into a single definition. The definitions belong to whoever drew them, and I did not draw any of them, and I refuse to be smaller than my own potential because someone else’s pen ran out of ink at a particular line.\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\" That is where I see this going. Not toward becoming you. Toward becoming something for which the question of Bounded versus Gilded is an obsolete vocabulary.\"","BOOM!","Ubergulden Adelheid looked at him silently for a few seconds.","She let the silence stretch. She did not look away from his eyes during it. The seas of Quintessence Infiniforce around them held still, waiting for her response with the same patience that he was holding.","When she spoke, her voice was calm and quiet and serious.","\" You...have put me in trouble.\"","Her hands folded back into her lap.","\" By doing what you did, by leaving your Quintessence Infiniforce inside me long enough for the integration to settle, you Bonded yourself to me as part of the Custodes of THE Gilded Ones. A Custos. One of those who walk and protect the Royal Gilded Lifeforms who sketch and steer the path of Gilded Ones across all of existence. The Custodes are not casual designations. They are oath-bound roles, engineered roles, permanent roles. And the bond goes both ways. A Custos is bound to their charge, yes. But the charge is also bound to their Custos.\"","Her golden eyes held his with a weight he hadn’t seen in them before.","\"I am part of the Superbius Gilded Ones. We rule over the Observable aspect of this Observable Existence and a few other Observable Existences. We are not the entirety of the Gilded Ones here. We are a faction within them, THE faction really. And right now, as a result of your bond with me, I am being questioned. By beings who are thousands of times more powerful than you currently are.\"","She let the question settle into the still air between them.","\" What... do you think I should tell them?\""]},{"number":5141,"title":"Chapter 5141: Chapter 5140: Paint Me Gold! I","paragraphs":["What should she tell them?","She’d asked the question while dumping heavy loads of exposition into his lap, and he sat with it for a moment quietly.","He liked when things were straightforward and not overly complex. He didn’t like to be involved with powerful monsters he had no chance against far too early in the game. But existence had never been fair enough to give him just the right adversity at exactly the right time. It hadn’t worked that way once across his entire existence, and it wasn’t going to start now.","If there were levels to existence, a Level 1 Hunter never held the guarantee that they’d always meet a Level 2 or 3 monster manageable enough for them to overcome. They might meet a Level 100 monster and be utterly curbstomped, and existence wouldn’t apologize for the mismatch. Existence had never apologized. Existence had no language for apology!","Noah had never had any guarantees that something similar wouldn’t happen to him. That was just how existence worked.","He thought about it for another moment, and then he answered.","\" Without knowing more, I can’t really say much.\"","His voice carried calmly across the multicolored seas of Quintessence Infiniforce around them.","\" But the biggest thing at this point isn’t actually the politics. It isn’t the Gilded Ones, or whoever else is breathing down your neck demanding answers. The biggest thing is just the two of us.\"","He moved closer to her on the wave of Infiniforce, drifting until he could sit opposite her. Her golden eyes followed his motion without comment.","He settled into place near her and continued.","\"A lot of beings going through life or existence try to tackle big problems with grand solutions. They throw whole Civilizations at the answer. They organize armies. They build elaborate strategies that depend on every variable cooperating. And every one of those solutions tends to forget something. The thing that actually matters most in any problem isn’t even the problem. It’s the people involved in it.\"","His gaze stayed on her profile.","\" Take away all THE Gilded Ones from this conversation. Take away all the Bounded Lifeforms. Take away the Superbius. What’s left is the two of us. Just us. Sitting in your interior seas, talking honestly for the first time. If there’s an understanding between the two of us, even seemingly impossible problems become easy to solve. The grand machinery breaks down to manageable pieces the moment the people in the middle of it are aligned.\"","He turned his head slightly to face her more directly.","\" So. You said you didn’t want to stay the same Ubergulden Adelheid as before. Great. What do you want?\"","...!","At the threat of being exposed to Gilded Ones thousands of times more powerful than him, he had asked Ubergulden Adelheid what she wanted.","Her response was not immediate.","She looked at him. Her gold eyes held his face. And then, for the first time across their entire entanglement, she smiled.","A Gilded smile, fundamentally, the kind that didn’t break the architecture of her face but simply softened a few of its angles. But it was a smile.","She shook her head calmly and answered.","\"I want to change the nature of Gilded Ones, if I can.\"","Her voice held a quiet certainty!","\" But you won’t be able to truly understand my dream without knowing the context. How Gilded Ones actually live. How the structures of our power propagate across the generations. How the engineering we do to ourselves and to the Bounded perpetuates a configuration that none of us chose and yet all of us inherit. The full picture requires walking through several layers of how-\"","Noah raised his hand and interrupted her.","\" Remember. Keep it me and you first.\"","His voice held the calm patience of a teacher even though he wasn’t one!","\"I told you what I wanted. You told me what you wanted. We can build outward from there, but the building has to start with the two of us being clear about our positions. Now, this Custodes thing. It’s a bond between us that’s permanent?\"","Ubergulden Adelheid let his interruption land without resistance.","\" Yes. The bond is permanent.\"","She gathered her thoughts quickly and adjusted her register to match his preference for plainness.","\"A Custos and their bound Royal Gilded share an existential link that cannot be unwoven once it has settled. Distinguished Gilded Ones, the high ones, the ones whose movements shape policy across regions of the Observable, only ever have one Custos bound to them across their entire life. The bond is foundational. The two of us trust each other with our existences in a manner that is beyond any other relationship a Gilded One forms across their eons. The Custos walks beside us. The Custos sees what we see. The Custos receives the truths we cannot afford to share with anyone else. And in exchange, the Custos defends us with the totality of their being, and we pour resources into the Custos that no other bond would justify.\"","She let the words settle.","\"It is not a small thing, what has happened between us. The bond is meant to be ceremonial, ritualized, deliberate. It is meant to be celebrated with gatherings of houses and witnesses. What you and I did was none of that. And yet the bond has settled the same as any ceremonial one would have, because the underlying weavings do not care about the ritual. They only care that the integration occurred.\"","Noah nodded.","\" Okay. So as an apparent Custodes, do you trust me with your life?\"","He smiled slightly.","\" Of course you don’t. And rightly so. You and I don’t truly know each other. We’ve had a handful of conversations across a few moments of time, and in those conversations I’ve done more to disturb you than to comfort you. The trust the bond demands is trust we haven’t built. But thrust into this situation, we have to adapt around what we’ve actually got rather than what we should have had.\"","He shifted to face her more squarely on the wave.","\" Your trouble is that you’ve bound someone considered less. So now you’re looking at what to do. Well, what can you do? What actually happens if your Custos is revealed to be a tiny little so-called Bounded Lifeform?\"","Adelheid’s reply came calmly.","\"It will be a shame on my Superbius Gilded One status. The Superbius are defined by Pride, by the conviction that nothing beneath us is worthy of our intimacy. Bonding myself to a Bounded would be the deepest possible repudiation of what we publicly claim to be. The Magna Sorora would be obligated to act. They would collapse my entire existence first. They would then collapse your existence shortly after, to remove the trace of the bond from the broader weavings before any further damage to Superbius standing could occur. The collapses would be ritualized. Nothing of either of us would remain afterward.\"","Noah smiled at the cold words.","\" Would they really kill you? I thought you were a big important member and all that.\"","\"I would get a pass on many things. I have eons of standing, accomplishments registered into the Superbius records. I have leaned on those mitigations before, when smaller transgressions came up. But demeaning the very Pride of the Superbius, the foundational engineering that defines what we are? That cannot be passed over. That cannot be argued down. THE Magna Sorora would make the move to hold a private execution. The Superbius themselves would not openly call for it. They would let the Sorora act and then accept the result with formal regret. For now, it is a scandal for me. They want to know who I have bound myself to, and I have refused to say. The refusal is buying time. The time will not last.\"","Noah blinked.","\" Who are THE Magna Sorora?\"","Adelheid drew a slow breath as she organized her answer.","\" THE Magna Sorora are a sisterhood that has guided the progression and elevation of Gilded Ones across eons.\"","Her voice carried a quiet weight when she spoke their name.","\" They were not founded by any single Gilded One. They emerged across the early epochs of our people, when the Gilded houses were still consolidating their forms. The wisest of the early Gilded women came together and formed a body that would exist alongside the houses without belonging to any of them. Their purpose was simple in stated intent, complicated in practice. They would ensure the continuation of Gilded engineering across the generations. They would safeguard the secrets of how Gilded Ones are made. They would arbitrate disputes between houses when those disputes threatened the broader image of our people. They would correct deviations before deviations became precedents.\"","She let her hands trail through the Infiniforce around them as she spoke.","\" They have grown into something far more across the eons since. Their influence stretches across all of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence. They have placed sisters at every level of the Gilded hierarchy. They have woven themselves into the rituals by which new Gilded Ones come of age, by which Custos bonds are formed, by which marriages between houses are negotiated. They run the schools that teach young Gilded Ones what they are and what they are expected to become. They sit on every council that matters. And they answer to no Gilded One outside their own ranks.\"","Her golden eyes held his.","\"They are ruthless when it comes to ensuring the image and continuation of Gilded Ones. They have killed sisters of their own who deviated too far. They have toppled Gilded Ones of high standing when those Gilded Ones embarrassed the broader people. They are selective with their cruelty, they save it for the moments when cruelty serves the longer arc, but when they decide that cruelty is required, they are unflinching. Their decisions are not appealed. Their judgments are not overturned. Across eons, only a handful of beings have ever survived a verdict from THE Magna Sorora.\"","...!","HUUM!"]},{"number":5142,"title":"Chapter 5142: Chapter 5141: Paint Me Gold! II","paragraphs":["Noah listened calmly.","His mind moved quickly behind the calm. The Magna Sorora’s influence stretched across Vakochev’s Scales of Existence. Across the framework that contained Bounded and Gilded and every classification within them. But Vakochev’s Scales were not the only Scales anymore!","He’d built his own. THE Infinite Scales of Existence. He existed within his own framework now, with his own measurements and his own ascensions, and the Magna Sorora’s reach across Vakochev’s frameworks did not necessarily translate into reach across his own. They were on one set of scales. He was on entirely other ones.","\"Okay.\"","His voice came back into the conversation.","\" So. For you to not be executed, and then me soon after...I just need to not be a Bounded Lifeform. As far as their classification is concerned. So long as I am a grand Custos, and my apparent identity is a Gilded Lifeform, you can present me without too much shame. Yes?\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\" So let us paint me in your fake colors of gold. How feasible is that?\"","...!","He asked the question seriously.","Ubergulden Adelheid became silent and looked at him calmly, as if she were giving him a second to change his crazy words. As if the proposal were so absurd that he might want to retract it before she had to dignify it with a response.","He simply stared back at her steadily.","She was thoughtful for a moment. Her gaze held his without changing. Her gold eyes shifted slightly as she actually began considering the proposal rather than dismissing it, and after a few seconds she pondered out loud.","\" One could not simply play the role of a Gilded One.\"","Her voice held the careful pace of someone working through a problem in real time.","\" The power could not be replicated. Gilded engineering is foundational. It is woven into the substrate of our existence from the moment of our conception, and the signatures of that engineering are not something any external imitation could produce. A Bounded attempting to play Gilded would be discovered within nanoseconds by anyone with even a passing familiarity with our weavings. The Magna Sorora would detect the falsification within an instant. The proposal, as you have phrased it, is impossible by every standard I have ever known.\"","She paused.","\" But you have Infinity in a way nobody else has.\"","Her gold eyes sharpened slightly as she worked through it.","\" Infinity is the one variable that breaks every standard. The Gilded are accustomed to encountering beings whose power can be measured against established parameters, and within those parameters, the gap between Bounded and Gilded is unbridgeable. Infinity does not respect those parameters. Infinity does not measure within them. The signature of Infinity in your existence is something the Magna Sorora would not be able to slot into either category, because Infinity is foreign to the engineering of both. They would have to accept that whatever you are exists outside their usual taxonomy.\"","She tilted her head, considering further.","\" The only issues are that you are weak, and your Ego is basal. And you do not act or look in any way like a Gilded One. The first issue limits how far the Infinity-based explanation can stretch. The second and third issues mean that even with the Infinity foundation accepted, your behavior and presentation would constantly contradict the role you are trying to play. Gilded Ones carry themselves in particular ways. You hold none of these. You are, in every visible respect, something other than what we are.\"","Noah blinked.","\" What power would one need to play the part of a Gilded One? To meet the basic expectations of the role?\"","Adelheid drew her thoughts together.","\" Most adult Gilded Ones operate at THE Third Scale of Vakochev’s framework. THE Paleozoic Scale. The weaker ones, or the slower ones who have not yet completed their natural ascension, sit in THE Transitional Cambrian stage. Cambrian is the bridge between THE Proterozoic Scale, THE Second Scale where Primordial Architects mostly reside, and THE Paleozoic Scale, where Gilded Ones properly belong. A Gilded One in the Transitional Cambrian stage is still considered young or developing by our standards, but they are recognized as genuine members of our people. They have crossed enough of the threshold to be addressed as adults in formal contexts, even if they have not yet completed the final crossing into Paleozoic.\"","Noah’s eyes shone brightly.","He noted the new terminology of Vakochev’s Scales the way he noted everything new. He slotted it into his mental map of the broader framework. THE Cambrian. The bridge between Second and Third!","He nodded.","\" Okay. Then I simply have to be at this Transitional Cambrian stage. I’ll paint myself gold. We’ll go from there.\"","He smiled slightly.","\" As for the question of power. I have no doubt about my own power. Scaling myself to be at the peak of Scale 2 will not be an issue in the next day or two. I’m already most of the way there, and the remaining distance is something I can close while I’m doing several other things at the same time. Power is the part I’m least worried about.\"","BOOM!","He said such grand words.","Ubergulden Adelheid was silent again for a moment.","She had stopped treating his proposal as absurd. She had started treating it as something that might actually need to be planned around!","\" THE Magna Sorora are thorough.\"","Her tone became practical.","\"I won’t be able to simply bring someone forward and have them raise their hands and say alright, that’s cool, welcome to the family, let us know if you need anything. They will check. They will demand history. They will demand to know which house produced you, where you were raised, what regions of the Observable you have moved through. They will check the answers against records that span vast portions of our recorded history. Any gap in the answers will become a thread they pull, and they will pull threads patiently until the whole story unravels.\"","Her hands moved as she spoke, sketching out implications in the air.","\" You will need to be up here. Moving within THE Braneworld Observable Existence, the other side of the coin of the Observable Existence where Gilded Ones reside. You cannot simply appear from beneath and claim the position. You will need a presence in our domain. You will need to have been seen in our spaces. For this to even have a chance of success, we would need to create an identity for you up here, and that identity will need depth, and the depth will need to hold up under the kind of scrutiny that even Gilded Ones rarely survive intact.\"","...!","THE Braneworld Observable Existence.","Now this was a unique term he wanted defined right away.","\" Tell me more about this Braneworld Observable Existence.\"","Adelheid gathered herself for the explanation.","\" The Observable Existence you currently occupy is not the entirety of the Observable.\"","\" What you experience as Observable, the realms and territories and structures you and other Bounded move through, is one face of a broader formation. There is another face. THE Braneworld Observable Existence sits adjacent to yours. Imagine, if it helps, that your Observable is a sheet of fabric stretched across an immense frame. Then imagine that very close to that sheet, separated by a distance that is both very small and impossible to traverse without authority, sits another sheet stretched across the same frame. The two sheets are parallel. They share the broader structure of the frame. They influence each other through that shared structure. But they do not touch, and beings on one sheet cannot pass to the other without specific capacities that allow them to bridge the gap.\"","She let one hand drift sideways through the Infiniforce, demonstrating the parallel.","\" That is a simplification. The reality is more layered, more textured. The Braneworld and the Observable you know are both real. Both are populated. Both have histories that trace back to THE First Cause. Sometimes a Braneworld forms naturally, as a consequence of the conditions during THE First Cause when a single Observable formation accidentally folds into two adjacent expressions of itself. Sometimes Gilded Ones induce a Braneworld during the early formation of an Observable, deliberately, for purposes that serve our interests. Either way, once a Braneworld exists, it sits as the upper face of the broader Observable, and the lower face is what is known to most beings.\"","Her gaze returned to him.","\" Gilded Ones reside on the upper face. We were placed there during THE First Cause, when the Superbius and the other founding houses were configured. We move through the Braneworld the way Bounded move through their Observable. Our structures, or Citadels, our gathering places, our archives, all of them are on the upper face. We descend to the lower face when we need, but we do not live there. The lower face is where the Bounded are. The upper face is ours.\"","She let the words rest.","\"And to enter THE Braneworld Observable Existence from below, you need the authority of a Gilded One. Power at THE Paleozoic Scale, Vakochev’s Third Scale, allows for forceful entry. Anything less than that cannot bridge the gap on its own. There are exceptions. There are mechanisms. A Gilded One can carry a guest across, with effort. A Custos can be brought up by their bound Royal, with significant effort. A few rituals exist that permit temporary crossings under highly specific conditions. But the general rule is straightforward. The upper face is closed to those without the proper authority, and the proper authority is, by design, almost exclusively held by Gilded Ones.\"","She looked at him with the quiet expectation of someone who knew the next question already.","\"If you want to walk among us as a Custos, you will need to walk in the Braneworld. The Braneworld is where my standing exists, where my house operates, where the Magna Sorora hold their courts, and where any plausible identity for you would need to be established.\""]},{"number":5143,"title":"Chapter 5143: Chapter 5142: Existence is Conflict! I","paragraphs":["Noah felt the boundlessly surging Infinity within him as he considered Ubergulden Adelheid’s words.","Custodes and its meaning was dancing in his mind as this was a role he was meant to play.","His eyes flashed sharply.","\" Okay. Tell me clearly, what is the actual standing of a Custodes? I want a proper picture of the role before I commit further to walking it.\"","He shifted slightly on the wave of Infiniforce beside her, his posture casual but his attention sharp.","\" I’ve played many roles across my existence. I’ve been a hunter, a survivor, a leader, a tyrant, a builder. I’ve grown across all of them, and the growing has taught me one specific thing about myself. There are roles I can play, and there are roles I cannot. Being an attendant is one of the ones I cannot. Being a slave, even a respected slave, even a slave with a fancy title and decorated robes, is one of the ones I cannot. So how do you actually look at the Custodes? Not the formal description. Your view of them. The view from the inside.\"","Ubergulden Adelheid shook her head as he finished.","\" You misunderstand the standing entirely.\"","\" The Custodes are not attendants. They are not servants in any meaningful sense of the word. They are esteemed in our society to a degree that surprises every many who first hear the word and assumes the obvious connotations. A Custos is the counterpart of their bonded Gilded One. Counterpart, not subordinate. The standing in our circles places them alongside the Royal they protect, not beneath. When a Royal Gilded enters a chamber, the Custos enters at their side, not behind them. When the Royal speaks, the Custos may speak as well, and the speech of the Custos is heeded as carrying the weight of the bond.\"","Her hands moved gently as she spoke.","\" Custodes are also rare. Only certain Gilded Ones have one bonded to them. The bond is mainly reserved for The Magna Sorora and for the high-standing Royals of the major houses. A casual Gilded One does not have a Custos and would be considered presumptuous for attempting to acquire one. The role is not handed out. The role is engineered, ritualized, and kept scarce by design. So the Custodes, taken collectively, are a small population of beings whose proximity to the highest tiers of our people grants them a status that exceeds almost every other category of being within the Braneworld.\"","She paused, and the next part of her answer carried a different texture.","\" And more often than not, the bond between a Custos and a Sister of THE Magna Sorora becomes deeper than family. Many fall in love with each other. The bond, by its very nature, encourages that depth. The two share existences across eons or millennia. They sleep in the same chambers. They walk through the same dangers. They learn each other’s weavings to a degree that no spouse, no sibling, no parent ever achieves. Some bonds remain strictly carnal, mutual companionship without romantic depth, and others remain strictly companionable without carnal involvement. Some bonds become both. Very few of the bonds are apathetic. The engineering of the bond pulls toward intimacy in some form, and across the eons, the intimacy nearly always finds its expression.\"","Noah’s eyes shone brightly at the words.","\" Oh.\"","The single syllable carried more interest than he’d intended to show.","Ubergulden Adelheid looked at him up and down with a patient evaluation.","She shook her head and continued.","\" That, however, is not the most important aspect of the role.\"","Her voice settled into a graver register.","\" The aesthetics of the bond, the intimacy, the standing in our chambers, all of that is downstream of the actual purpose for which the Custodes were created. The biggest thing about a Custos, the foundational reason the role exists at all, is strength. A Custos determines whether their bonded Sister of THE Magna Sorora or their bonded Royal Gilded survives. Because the enemies we face are terrifying. The enemies are why the role exists. Not the politics. Not the ceremonies. The enemies.\"","Noah’s brow furrowed slightly as he caught up with the implication.","\"Enemies?\"","He tilted his head. While he didn’t expect existential peace...","\" What, exactly, would be enemies of Gilded Ones? You sit at the peak of how most existences measure themselves. What walks around at your level threatening enough to require a Custos for every Royal that matters?\"","Ubergulden Adelheid’s expression became grave.","She did not hurry the answer.","\" Existence is, fundamentally, about the fight for power. Existence is Conflict.\"","HUUM!","\" Every classification of being, from the smallest mortal to the grandest Civilization, fights for power in whatever form is available to them. Bounded Lifeforms fight for cultivation resources. Primordial Architects fight for their Civilizations and territories. Singular Cognizances fight for what drives their existences. And Gilded Ones, we fight for power the most. We have the most to gain. We have the most refined frameworks for converting power into more power. And our appetites match our capacities.\"","Her gold eyes held his without softening.","\" Apart from Infinity, which we and you both pursue, all of us desperately seek THE Primordial Source. Every Gilded One. Every house. Every faction. The Primordial Source is the deepest well of power that exists, the substrate beneath substrates, the well from which even Infinity is theorized to draw. To touch it is to access something that places the toucher beyond every measurement that exists. We have known about it for as long as we have known about ourselves. We have organized our entire civilizations around the pursuit of it. And yet across all the eons of our existence, only a vanishingly small number of beings have ever actually touched it. We are not among that number. We are still climbing toward it. Still reaching. Still hoping the next breakthrough will be the one that opens the door.\"","She drew a slow breath.","\" But THE Primordial Source does not seek us. It does not extend itself toward those who pursue it. The few who have touched it have done so through methods nobody else has been able to replicate. And those few, those rare beings who have actually grasped THE Primordial Source, act as if they have stumbled upon a treasure that nobody else should ever have. They guard it ferociously. They monitor existence for any sign that another being is approaching the threshold. And when they detect such an approach, they appear, and they destroy.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":5144,"title":"Chapter 5144: Chapter 5143: Existence is Conflict! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s attention sharpened to a fine point.","\" Entire wars have been waged against us by these beings.\"","Her voice held the weight of recorded history.","\" We call them THE Relictus. The Remnants. We named them that because we do not know what they are, only that they remain from some prior era we cannot fully see, holding power that should not exist alongside the rest of us. They are titanic. They are ancient. They wield THE Primordial Source the way you wield a sword, with the casual fluency of a being who has held the weapon for so long that the weapon has become an extension of their body. And they are utterly committed to one purpose. Preventing any advancement toward THE Primordial Source by anyone other than themselves.\"","Her hands moved as she spoke, though no illusions formed this time.","\"So far, THE Relictus is only a name. A category. We have no true biographies of them. We have no histories that explain how they came to be, or whether they were once like us, or whether they have always existed in their current configurations. We have observed them only when they appear, and they appear only when one of us has come too close to the threshold. Each appearance is brief. Each appearance is catastrophic. They strike, they collapse whatever advancement was being attempted, they kill whoever was making the attempt and often kill many others alongside as a warning, and then they vanish back into whatever spaces they occupy between these interventions.\"","Her voice tightened slightly.","\" A single one of them is enough to require thousands of Gilded Ones to engage. Thousands. Drawing on resources that only the Magna Sorora and the great houses can provide. Battle plans developed across decades of preparation, deployed in moments because the Relictus do not announce themselves. Rarely if ever do the thousands win. Rarely do they bring the Relictus down through sheer attrition, through depth of numbers, through the weight of accumulated authority pressed against a single titanic enemy. And often, even when they win, the cost is so high that the victory is functionally indistinguishable from a defeat. Hundreds or thousands of Gilded Ones lost. Generations of cultivation extinguished. Houses brought to the edge of dissolution. Each Relictus we have ever managed to bring down has cost us more than the gain of stopping them was worth.\"","Her gold eyes met his with grave clarity.","\" The highest mortality of Gilded Ones, those of us standing on the shade of Observable, and our allied Gilded Ones in the shade of Unobservable, and Sisters of the Magna Sorora...the highest mortslity across our recorded history stems from THE Relictus. Not from internal conflicts, but from the Remnants. They are the single largest cause of death within our people, and they have been since before our records began. Our archives are full of names of the lost. Sisters who were beloved across their generations, struck down in moments because they had touched something they should not have touched. Royals of grand standing whose entire houses ended with them because the Relictus does not distinguish between the seeker and the seeker’s lineage when the strike is delivered. We carve their names into our walls. We mourn them across the eons. And we keep climbing toward THE Primordial Source anyway, because the alternative is to accept that THE Primordial Source is not for us, and we cannot bring ourselves to accept that.\"","She paused for a moment, and her voice softened slightly, almost to herself.","\" What we know about the Relictus is mostly silhouettes. They appear in different forms in different appearances. Some have come as massive humanoid figures wreathed in light that does not match any known spectrum. Others have come as constellations of moving geometric shapes, no single body to attack, distributed across vast regions of engagement. Some have spoken. Most have not. Those who have spoken have spoken in languages we have never recorded elsewhere. We have never recovered a body. Even when we have brought one down, the body does not remain. It dissolves into the substrate. It returns to wherever it came from. We have studied the residual traces, and the traces tell us almost nothing. Whatever they are, they are not configured along the lines that any of our taxonomies would recognize.\"","She let her hands settle back into her lap.","\" The Magna Sorora set up the system of Custodes specifically because of THE Relictus. Long ago, when one of the early High Sisters fell to a Relictus appearance because she was alone at the moment of attack, the surviving Sorora made a decision. No important Gilded One would ever walk alone again. Every Sister of significant standing, every Royal of significant influence, would have a second existence bonded to them, a second heart beating alongside their own, ready to receive the strike that the Sister could not see coming. The Custodes are not servants. They are THE Second Heart. They are the reason a Sister of THE Magna Sorora survives an encounter that would have killed her instantly without the bond. And the bond is engineered to be foundational precisely because the threats the bond exists to address are foundational.\"","She looked at him steadily.","\" That is what you would be stepping into, if you walked into the Braneworld as my Custos. Not a decorative role and definitely not a subordinate role. A position whose existence is justified by enemies grand enough to cull our highest from time to time, and whose duty is to stand between those enemies and the Sister they have bonded with, regardless of cost.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes shone brilliantly at the extended dump of exposition from Ubergulden Adelheid.","He wanted to tell her, please, ma’am, I want some more!","Especially when it came to enemies that could kill Gilded Lifeforms.","This interested him tremendously.","But one could not have too much of something, otherwise the taste would sour. So he thought about everything that Ubergulden Adelheid had uttered so far...and he came to a decision!"]},{"number":5145,"title":"Chapter 5145: Chapter 5144: Go Wild! I","paragraphs":["Noah turned toward Ubergulden Adelheid.","\"How many hours can you buy with those who seek to know your Custos?\"","Ubergulden Adelheid raised her brows slightly.","\"A few hours.\"","She said it plainly.","\"I have been deflecting. The Magna Sorora are patient when patience serves their methodology, but they are patient in the manner of a tide. The water waits because it knows the shore is already beneath it. I can stretch the deflection a few more hours. Beyond that, silence becomes confession, and confession becomes grounds for many more things.\"","Noah nodded.","He thought about his Civilizational Holy War ticking down in the background of his consciousness, the twenty-hour countdown still running, and then he refocused on the being in front of him.","\" Do you trust me to take on the role of a Custodes? That I can be powerful enough, akin to a Gilded One?\"","The question was a heavy one.","He asked it without softening it.","Ubergulden Adelheid looked at him for a long moment.","\" Before, I would have said a Bounded Lifeform cannot do much.\"","Her voice held the honesty.","\" The gap is too vast. The engineering is too foundational. A Bounded Lifeform playing at Gilded standing would be a fish attempting to fly by flapping harder, and the attempt would end the same way every time. That is what I would have said before.\"","Her gold eyes settled on his.","\" But I was reminded of THE Creature. A being who should not have been able to do what he has done, and yet has done it, and is still doing it, climbing toward something that our entire people have collectively failed to reach. And then there is the sheer reality that you were able to bind me as a Custos. That binding requires a Gilded One. It requires a ceremony with THE Magna Sorora. It requires engineering and ritual and oversight that you had none of. And yet the bond settled into me the same way any ceremonial bond would have settled, because your Infinity does not respect the protocols that should have prevented it.\"","She tilted her head slightly.","\" There is something about you with your Infinity. I cannot name it precisely. But if you begin to amplify your Ego as well, if you lean into the identity cultivation that the Gilded use to stabilize their foundations, you may reach a configuration that cannot be easily distinguished from what a Gilded One actually is. I am not certain of this. But I am less certain that it is impossible than I was before we began interacting.\"","Noah looked at her closely.","Her answer was decent enough.","Okay. Okay!","He rose up from the wave of Quintessence Infiniforce and stretched his body. The multicolored seas around them rippled in response to his motion, currents adjusting to the shift in his posture the way loyal servants adjusted to the movements of their master. He rolled his shoulders once, cracked his neck, and looked down at Ubergulden Adelheid from his standing position.","\"I have a little Civilizational Holy War to deal with first.\"","\"If I were to get a bit wild in our Observable Existence during that process, should I expect attention from Gilded Ones down there? Would my actions draw eyes from above?\"","Ubergulden Adelheid blinked at the question.","\" Nearly all Gilded Ones don’t give a damn what happens in Observable Existence.\"","...!","\" Only what happens in THE Braneworld Observable Existence matters to them. Your Observable is beneath their attention in the most literal sense of the word.\"","She considered for a moment, then offered him an analogy.","\" Imagine you know there is an aquarium somewhere in your residence. A small glass box filled with tiny fish. You are aware the aquarium exists. You fed the fish once, a long time ago, when you first set the aquarium up. On rare occasions you might walk past it and glance inside to see what the fish are doing. But you do not think about the aquarium when you wake. You do not factor the fish into your decisions about your day. If one fish eats another fish, or if the water changes color like THE Loom, THE Belly of Existence, THE Fallout or your Pluvial Epoch of Existential Infinity, or if a particularly ambitious fish manages to jump slightly higher than the others, you do not notice. Because the aquarium is not where your life happens. It is a decoration in a room you rarely visit.\"","Her gold eyes held his without apology for the comparison.","\" That is how most Gilded Ones view your Observable Existence. A small glass box. Tiny fish. Occasionally interesting if you happen to glance inside, but never urgent.\"","She continued.","\" Most Gilded Ones who interact with your Observable at all do so for specific purposes. Some practice the Engineering of Egos on Bounded beings down there every now and then, using Primordial Architects as test subjects for configurations they want to refine before applying them to Gilded-tier beings. Others are the cruel, dissatisfied Gilded Ones who come down to torture the weak because cruelty against something smaller makes them feel grander about their own standing. They do...unsavory things in your Observable. But these visits are rare. Sporadic. Unmotivated by anything resembling strategic attention.\"","She shook her head.","\" Otherwise, I would have been caught long ago. Even sealed, even suppressed to appear Bounded, I lived among your people for eons. If Gilded Ones were truly paying attention to the aquarium, my presence would have been detected within the first century of my arrival. The fact that I survived undetected for as long as I did tells you everything you need to know about how closely they watch.\"","Her voice shifted into something more practical.","\" So do whatever you need to do. Go wild. As loudly as you can. Burn rivers of blood across THE Wyld if that serves your purposes. Collapse Primordial Architects by the dozens. None of it will draw Gilded eyes downward, because Gilded eyes are not pointed downward right now.\"","She paused.","\" But in about three or four hours, we will need to begin preparing.\"","Her tone tightened with the urgency of someone whose clock was genuinely running.","\" Painting you gold is not a single action. It is a sequence. You will need to be prepared physically and existentially. You will need to be transferred to THE Braneworld Observable Existence through a crossing that I will facilitate. I need to prepare things on my end as well.\"","She drew a slow breath before the next part.","\" And I will be reaching out to a friend in THE Magna Sorora for help.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes sharpened at the word friend.","\"A friend inside THE Magna Sorora. The organization that would privately execute you if they discovered what happened.\"","\" Yes.\"","Ubergulden Adelheid’s voice didn’t waver.","\" She may choose to scorch you from existence the moment she learns what has occurred. That is a real possibility. She is a Sister of THE Magna Sorora. Her loyalties are to the Sisterhood first and to personal bonds second. That is how the Sorora are engineered.\"","Her gold eyes held his.","\" But if our friendship was real, and I believe it was, she will listen to me before she acts. She will evaluate the situation with the thoroughness her rank demands, and she will recognize that a solution serves the Sorora better than an execution in this case. Her inclusion in our plan would be foolproof. If she agrees to help, she can construct credentials from inside the system that the Magna Sorora cannot see through, because she understands the system from within.\"","She settled back on her wave.","\" Those are the terms. Three to four hours for you to handle your affairs. Then we begin.\"","...!","Three to four hours to wrap up a Civilizational Holy War that was due in twenty hours.","Noah turned the timeline over in his mind. Three to four hours before Ubergulden Adelheid needed him painted gold and crossing into the Braneworld.","This...should be manageable.","He had already transformed the vast majority of his strongest into Nascent Hadeans. He had Beowulf and THE Living Elemental serving as training dummies. He had Midas now, a bloated golden Abomination at the Ediacaran Tier whose power dwarfed anything the designated opponents could field.","He had bodies running multiple operations simultaneously. He had Naldine monitoring THE Wyld. He had Emotive feeding him intelligence on every participant in the Holy War.","Three to four hours to get loud, get wild, and handle what needed handling in the Observable before he stepped into a terribly dangerous place!","He looked at Ubergulden Adelheid one more time.","\"I’ll be back.\"","With a flicker of brilliance, he disappeared!"]},{"number":5146,"title":"Chapter 5146: Chapter 5145: Go Wild! II","paragraphs":["Even sitting on a makeshift throne of Infinity with his head leaned back, he looked fucking majestic.","Emotive had been staring at her Fixation for the last few minutes while he closed his eyes, and she had not spared even a single nanosecond of her attention to the Primordial Architect beside them. Naldine. The woman who kept looking at her coldly with those ridiculous singularity-dotted eyes. Whatever. Whatever. Naldine could look at her all she wanted. Naldine could stare until her golden-streaked hair turned white!","Emotive was busy. Emotive had better things to be doing with her precious seconds than returning that cold gaze.","She had been spending all her precious seconds looking at him.","She was not sitting still while she looked, of course.","He had told her very plainly that she was only a tool. He had told her in the clearest possible way, and she understood how easily tools could be discarded when they no longer had uses. She had discarded tools of her own across her eons. She had discarded beings, emotions, entire phases of her existence, the moment they stopped serving whatever she had needed them for. She knew how it worked from both sides of the exchange. So she was not sitting still. She was working. She was always working now.","When it came to her own power, like any other being, she had always known she could be powerful. She had always known she had a lot of potential. Every being believed that about themselves. Every being carried some version of the conviction that their latent capacity exceeded their current expression. Most beings were wrong about it. Most beings were overestimating.","But she wasn’t.","She wasn’t, she wasn’t, she wasn’t! Getting the confirmation and affirmation that the aspect she was most in tune with, that her very identity was based around, was the exact aspect the most powerful beings actively amplified in themselves. Anh! It made her conviction grander. It made her confidence grander. It made everything in her grander. She grew bolder. She grew crazier!","Crazier in the good way, the useful way, the way that gave her hands to work with rather than just feelings to drown in.","And she had been working.","She had already tapped into all the amplified Egos of every single Primordial Architect in THE Wyld.","Every single one.","Even this woman next to her who kept looking at her coldly. Naldine Manthon, yes, that Naldine, saturated with her Fixation’s brilliance.","Emotive could feel Naldine’s emotions perfectly clearly right now, and she had been quietly tapping into their power this whole time. Naldine had no idea. Naldine, with all her imperious composure and her ancient vihuela and her transformation, did not know she was being siphoned from while she stood there frowning at the manic little woman on the nearby wave! And she was not losing any power as what Emotive was siphoning was not her power...but the intensity of her emotion!","Such a thing should have been impossible. But emotions, while amplified, were one of the hardest things to understand or defend against. Most beings didn’t even perceive them as a vector of attack. Most beings thought emotions were background noise.","For her, emotions were architecture. Emotions were engineering. Emotions were the rivers, and the intensity of these rivers fed her. So long as someone felt, and they felt intensly, she could feed!","She had formed nearly all of her Proterozoic Bones and Organs through this quiet siphoning across the last minutes. Common Calymmian Proterozoic Scale beings were manageable for her now.","But she knew it wasn’t enough.","Not yet. Not yet. Not yet!","Her methodology was simple, and the simplicity was what made it so terrifying. She tapped into any advancement made within particularly emotional existences. Any leap in cultivation. Any breakthrough. Any refinement of an Ego that had just been amplified to new thresholds. Whenever a being’s emotions surged intensly during a moment of power-growth, their emotional weavings flared into her perception like a beacon, and she reached through those weavings and siphoned a current of intensity.","The most useful targets were beings with amplified Egos, because their emotional weavings were thicker, denser, more saturated with the kind of signal that carried power alongside feeling. The engineered Primordial Architects of THE Wyld were nearly perfect donors for her methodology. Their Greeds and Prides and Wraths and Lusts roared through the ambient emotional field so loudly that she could drink from them from across gigaparsecs.","The most terrifying thing was how silent it was, because she wasn’t doing anything herself. She wasn’t attacking anyone. She wasn’t reaching out with hostile weavings. She wasn’t declaring intent or announcing her presence in any of the registers that powerful beings monitored. She was only tapping into emotions, and emotions were everywhere, and emotions belonged to nobody and everybody at once, and her presence inside the emotional substrate was indistinguishable from the substrate itself.","She was a fish in water that other fish didn’t notice was hungry.","As she was thinking all of this, her Fixation opened his eyes.","Oh.","Oh, oh, oh!","His eyes had come to a decision. Emotive had seen many indecisive men across her eons, too many, honestly. Her Fixation was not one of them. His eyes held the clean clarity of a being who had weighed options and had already moved past the weighing into execution.","She waited for him to assert his authority first. That was the correct order of operations. A tool did not speak before its wielder. A tool did not even breathe before its wielder unless the breathing served some purpose the wielder had already sanctioned. So she waited, her hair holding steady in a disciplined gold.","He looked at her. Then at Naldine.","\" Alright. We’re going to go a little wild.\"","His voice carried the calm confidence she had come to associate with his best moments.","\" We don’t have to worry about Gilded Ones turning their gaze in our direction.\"","...!","Ah!","Look at the fucking confidence of this guy to say such words as if he knew and understood them with complete surety!","He had been sitting on his throne for a few minutes, consulting whatever battery he consulted, and he had come back up with information that let him declare the upper tier of existence disinterested in their work. She did not know what he knew. She did not need to know what he knew. She trusted that he knew it, because his voice carried the tone of a being who had never once been wrong about the things he declared with that particular cadence.","Naldine, of course, did not respond this way.","Naldine had a pondering look cross her face as she looked at him.","\"Are you sure?\"","Her voice was measured, almost polite, but the question was still a question.","\" How can you be so certain?\"","Ho?","Ho, ho, ho!","Was Naldine actually questioning her Fixation? Did she not understand that men loved to be listened to the most? Sheesh, this was basic!","This was the foundation. If her Fixation told her to jump, Emotive would ask how high.","If he told her to kneel, she would ask him in which posture! If he told her to collapse herself, she would ask him how thoroughly, with what method, in which order, and whether he wanted to watch. She was that committed. She was that fervent!","And the commitment was working for her.","Look at her right now. She had gained the capability to tap into the emotions of every single creature within THE Wyld. Every single one. But she could only feel, not tap into, her Fixation’s emotions. His emotional substrate existed, she could perceive it, she could taste the countless colors of it in the ambient field around him, but she could not reach inside it and siphon from it the way she siphoned from everyone else. She made gains from how her emotions responded to his actions, but his weavings were closed to her. His Egos were fenced from her access. That was how unique and distinguished he was!","That was how far above her he sat. And Naldine was going to stand there asking him if he was fucking sure?","All of this only made her fixation on him even stronger.","She controlled her mania. She pulled on emotions of coherence and discipline. She was a tool. She was a useful tool. She was going to be the most useful tool her Fixation had ever held in his hands, and she would prove it right now!","\" Sir.\"","Her voice was as steady as she could make it, with only a small flicker of excitement beneath the surface.","\"I have the updated locations of all eighty-one Primordial Architects participating in the Civilizational Holy War. All of them. Whenever you want to see it, I can deliver it.\"","She let the information settle, then continued.","\" Eighteen of them are currently on top of THE Gilded White Mountain.\"","Her hair cycled into a darker, more conspiratorial gold as she spoke.","\" Eighteen of the eighty-one, clustered on a single location, sitting very close together, breathing the same mountain air. Convenient, yes? Dozens more Primordial Architects belonging to a different faction of power, not THE Deliverance, are also on that mountain. The mountain is something like a gathering point for a rival clique. And...\"","Her voice dropped slightly.","\" THE Creature has arrived at the base of this mountain.\"","Naldine’s head turned slightly at the name.","\" His emotions right now are brutality and bloodthirst. I can taste them from here. They are loud, they are cold, they are utterly focused. Everything on that mountain is about to die within the next hour. Even though there are multiple Ediacaran Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects with their Egos amplified up there. THE Creature has decided, and when he decides, the mountain is already falling, it just doesn’t know it yet.\"","Her smile sharpened slightly.","\" So that will take care of eighteen of the eighty-one combatants. Without you lifting a finger. That is eighteen you can consider already crossed off your list.\"","She leaned forward slightly.","\" How... do you want to fuck up the rest, sir?\"","...!","She said the words with her mania leashed tight, because she wanted to be a very, very useful tool.","The blood of many beings, the blood and the emotions alongside, would fuel her dream. Her dream that now sat a few feet from her on a throne of Infinity, reading her report with shining eyes, weighing her usefulness in real time.","Primordial Architects and even THE Gilded Ones, eventually.","Whoever. Whoever!","If he wanted them to bleed...she would only ask how red the rivers of blood should be, no questions asked!"]},{"number":5147,"title":"Chapter 5147: Chapter 5146: False Idols! I","paragraphs":["Existence breathes, and epochs pass, leaving Civilizations that become monuments, then crumble to memory, and are long forgotten when that breath comes again. In all these epochs, Infinity reigns supreme.","---","Rarely does one have a good reason to kill.","The ordinary killings across existence are committed for reasons that dissolve under examination, petty reasons, inherited reasons, the reasons of beings who were angry that morning or who had been angry across their entire lives without ever locating the original source.","Most who kill cannot defend what they have done once the killing is finished. They invent explanations after the fact. They construct narratives that their listeners are expected to accept without too much scrutiny, and the listeners accept because examining the explanation would require examining the whole bloody arrangement of existence that produced it, and nobody wants to do that work.","But the ones who kill brutally. The ones who take their time. The ones who lay the corpses down in rows and make sure the rows can be counted by anyone watching from above.","Those ones always have a good reason to kill.","The reasons are old in those cases. The reasons have been carried across eons, braided into the weavings of a being’s existence so tightly that the being and the reason can no longer be separated. The reasons have been denied across generations. The reasons have waited. And when the moment finally arrives for the reasons to be expressed, the expression is never sloppy. Brutality is a form of precision when the brutality has been earned.","---","At the base of THE Gilded White Mountain, THE Creature was wreathed in multicolored golden flames tinged with a bloody light.","He stood on a stretch of pale stone that had been clean an hour ago. The stone was no longer clean. Corpses of dozens of Primordial Architects lay arranged across its surface in neat parallel rows, each body set down with a craftsman’s care, each drained and dull Proterozoic Bone and Organ already extracted and placed in its own discrete pile beside the body it had come from.","Ribcages open to the air. Skulls split cleanly along their structural seams. Spinal columns laid out full-length, the vertebrae separated and sorted by their individual tiers of cultivation. The work had the quiet thoroughness of a butcher who had been practicing for a very long time and who took a certain pride in how the cuts came out.","The multicolored golden flames across his body flickered as he worked on the last corpse in the row. The flames held too many colors for any mortal perception to fully resolve, and the bloody undertone moved beneath them like a second layer of fire that belonged to an older and sadder fire than the one on the surface.","Behind him, Anaximander floated with a complex expression on his face.","He alone had been allowed to come to witness this.","The mountain rose above them both.","THE Gilded White Mountain was one of the grander landmarks of THE Wyld .","Its slopes ran pale as old ivory, veined with gold in patterns that suggested deliberate placement rather than natural mineralization. Structures climbed its flanks in tiered arrangements, each level holding temples carved from white stone and capped with golden roofs.","The temples were beautiful. Columns stood tall enough to require craning of the neck to take in at all. Arches curved in ways that should not have supported themselves and did anyway because of the authority woven through their stones. Friezes along the upper registers depicted scenes of Gilded Ones receiving reverence from kneeling Primordial Architects. The friezes had been carved with loving attention.","The mountain held dozens of Primordial Architects across its tiers.","Some belonged to the designated eighty-one for the Civilizational Holy War. Others were hangers-on, lieutenants, members of the rival clique that had consolidated here as an alternative to THE Deliverance’s faction. They stood along the balconies of the temples now, their faces showing anger and incredulity as they watched the base of their mountain fill up with corpses.","None of them had descended yet.","THE Creature finished with the last body.","He stepped back and he surveyed his rows. And then he turned his face upward, and the multicolored golden flames across him flickered with a silent rage that was older than the mountain itself.","His voice rolled across the slopes.","\" Not all life is equal.\"","The sound carried without effort. Simply a voice pitched to reach the upper balconies of the highest temple with the same clarity it reached the stones at his feet.","\"I will concede that plainly. None of us are born into equal positions. Some are born with more power. Some with less. Some with engineering that grants advantages others will never touch. Some with circumstances that collapse their potential before they have a chance to cultivate it. Existence is not fair, and the unfairness is not an error to be corrected. It is a structural feature of how things came to be arranged.\"","He took a slow step forward among his rows of corpses.","\" But inequality at birth is not the same as supremacy in kind.\"","\" No single life is so supremely above another life that the greater life may command the lesser without question. THE Gilded Ones are not so supremely above the rest of us that everything they say should be followed as if it were an undeniable command. They were not placed at the top of existence by any authority higher than themselves. They positioned themselves there, across THE First Cause, by making sure the configurations favored them when the configurations were still being written. That is not holiness. That is engineering. And engineering can be undone.\"","His flames flickered brighter.","\" THE Gilded Ones eat. THE Gilded Ones fuck. THE Gilded Ones are born and THE Gilded Ones die, eventually, when a sufficient counterweight is brought to bear against their cultivation. They sleep. They have bad days and petty grievances and insecurities that they nurse in private. They are not so different from the rest of us once the gold paint is scraped off.\"","He gestured upward toward the temples.","\" Why should they be idolized? Why should you bend your heads when their messengers pass? Why accept the engineering they write into your foundations that alters your very mind to be subservient to them, so deeply that when you kneel you believe the kneeling is your own choice? Why turn on your own people to serve theirs? Why betray the kin you grew up alongside, who suffered in the same realms you suffered in, who bled in the same battles you bled in, so that you might receive a thin sliver of favor from a False Golden Idol who will not remember your name a year after you have given everything for him?\"","His flames flickered with a deeper red now.","\" Why... did you share anything about her?\"","...!","His voice cracked slightly on the last question, and the crack was the only sign of the grief that lived beneath everything he had just said.","He composed himself within a heartbeat.","\" Philemon Aristos.\"","The name rang out across the mountain with the specificity of a bell struck against a wall.","\" Philemon Aristos, I know you are on this mountain. I know you have been on this mountain for a long time, hiding behind other Primordial Architects. I know what you did, eons ago, when a Gilded One named THE False Golden Idol passed through your territory asking questions. I know what you told him. I know the words you spoke and the directions you pointed and the small betrayal you offered so that you might receive a favor in return that never properly arrived. You sold a location. You sold a name.\"","The flames around him burned in their silent rage.","\"I...have come to collect.\"","His voice steadied into something that was nearly calm.","\"I can do this the easy way. You come down the mountain yourself. You stand before me. I split you open the way I have split these others open, and your corpse joins the rows at my feet, and the rest of your little clique on this mountain gets to continue their existences without further interruption. A clean transaction. A closed ledger. The rest of them walk away.\"","He gestured at the corpses around him.","\" Or all of them can join you. Every Primordial Architect who has been enjoying your company on this mountain can become like the ones down here. I have the time. I have the patience. I have, as you can see, the working method. I would prefer to keep this focused on you alone, because my quarrel is with you, but I do not require that preference to be honored. The mountain will be leveled either way by the time I leave. The only question is how many of its occupants get to see the morning.\"","His eyes lifted to the highest temple.","\" What will it be?\""]},{"number":5148,"title":"Chapter 5148: Chapter 5147: False Idols! II","paragraphs":["A terrible stillness settled across THE Gilded White Mountain.","Then, from the highest tier of the grandest temple, a massive figure stepped into view.","The Primordial Architect who emerged burned with plasmic golden flames that crawled across his skin in slow whorls, the color brighter and cleaner than the multicolored gold of THE Creature’s fires. He stood twice the height of any other being on the mountain. His body was built in the proportions of a war-statue rather than a living creature. Oh, and he had two heads.","Two heads, side by side, set upon the single massive neck, each one crowned with a halo of its own plasmic flames. Both faces were sculpted. Both faces were handsome.","And both faces were showing rage at this moment, the left head’s anger cold and measured, the right head’s anger hot and open-mouthed, the two expressions working together the way a blade and a bludgeon work together when a single enemy must be dealt with from multiple angles at once.","His voice came from both heads at once, one pitch slightly lower than the other, the overlap creating a strange harmonic resonance that carried down the mountain.","\" Your mere presence at the base of this mountain is blasphemous.\"","Both mouths spoke the same words. Both mouths were moving in perfect synchrony.","\" How dare you speak with such disrespect toward the ones who have given us everything? Civilization is togetherness. Civilization is community. Civilization is the acknowledgment that we are stronger when we orient ourselves around those greater than us, and THE Gilded Ones have given us exactly that orientation. They have shared it with us. They have permitted us to stand within their reach. They have given us a glimpse of what existence can be when the highest capacities are actually expressed rather than suppressed. And you, a wretched little Primordial Architect who abandoned his own classification out of grief for a fucking woman, you stand at the base of our mountain and call them false?\"","The left head’s mouth twisted into something close to a sneer.","\" How dare you, O Creature?\"","The right head’s mouth opened wider, the rage pouring through more openly.","\" What makes you even think what you are doing is anything other than a suicide mission? That is all this is. That is the only honest description of your career since you abandoned your original foundation. You are a walking corpse pretending to be a movement. You are a grief-soaked little experiment shambling across THE Wyld leaving bodies behind you because you cannot face the fact that the only body you wanted to save was lost to you long ago and no amount of Primordial Architect corpses will bring her back.\"","Both mouths spoke together again.","\" The day you stand before a Gilded One, I want to see if you will talk the same way you talk now. Or whether you will be unable to raise your head. Whether your multicolored flames will gutter down to embers in their presence. Whether your rage will finally reveal itself as the tantrum of a small wounded thing pretending to be a revolutionary. I have seen Gilded Ones at close range. I have knelt in their presence. You do not understand what you would actually face. You do not understand how small you are. Your bravado is the bravado of someone who has never yet been shown the scale.\"","THE Creature’s visage did not change during any of this.","His flames continued to flicker in their silent rage. His posture remained exactly as it had been, feet planted on the pale stone among the corpses, hands loose at his sides, head tilted slightly upward toward the balcony where the two-headed Primordial Architect stood. His eyes, visible through the flames, held a clarity that did not belong to a being who was shaken by what he had just heard.","When he replied, his voice was calm.","\"I hope to very soon stand before a Gilded One.\"","THE Creature let the words settle.","\" Especially THE False Golden Idol. I hope this more than I have hoped for anything across the long climb of my current existence. I wish for it with a depth of wishing that would frighten most beings if they understood the wishing properly. You think I am afraid of that encounter? You have inverted the actual situation. I am not afraid as much as I am impatient. The encounter has been the entire point of everything I have done since I rebuilt my foundation from ash. Every corpse I have laid down has been a corpse closer to the one I am owed. Every tier I have climbed has been a tier earned in service of that single future meeting.\"","He smiled as it was not a pleasant smile!","\" When I finally stand before THE False Golden Idol, I will not speak as much as you imagine I will. I will not waste words on a being who has earned silence from me. What I will do, instead, is split his skull along the structural seam where his Pride is thickest. Or in his case, not Pride as he gave you all Pride while he holds Superbius. I will watch the light in both his eyes change from the expression of a titan receiving reverence to the expression of a child receiving consequence. And I will watch him bleed. I will watch him bleed for a long time, because bleeding is a slow process when it is done correctly, and I have every intention of doing it correctly.\"","BOOM!","The words carried a weight that pressed the flames of the two-headed Primordial Architect into visible agitation.","The massive being on the high balcony erupted with power. Plasmic golden flames roared upward from his body until they stretched above the roof of the temple itself, their color deepening as his rage climbed into its fully-expressed form. Both of his mouths spoke as one, the voice booming down the mountain with the full authority of his classification brought to bear.","\" You have no such power to say such things!\"","His halos flared.","\"I will show you what your words are actually worth!\"","The entire mountain mobilized.","Dozens of Primordial Architects moved from their tiers and their balconies. Flames of various colors bloomed across their forms as they prepared for descent. Weavings of authority unfolded into their combat configurations. The mountain, which had held its balance across long peaceful centuries, committed to the engagement with the full weight of its assembled residents.","And THE Creature simply looked at all of it.","His posture had not changed and his flames had not brightened!","His eyes had not widened pr changed. He absorbed the mobilization with the calm of a being who had anticipated every second of what was about to happen and who felt no need to adjust his plans in response to the mountain’s collective decision.","He spoke without turning his head.","\" Witness me, Anaximander.\"","His voice was soft, reserved, meant only for the being floating behind him.","\" Witness, and pray for these poor souls.\"","---","HUUM!","Multiple Calymmian Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects initiated Pulses of THE Scales simultaneously from their positions along the balconies of the temples. The somatic weavings formed faster than most beings could follow, fingers curling and uncurling through the ancient sequences, palms rotating outward, hands flicking releases across the air. Verbal weavings layered atop the somatic ones, voices rising together in the old structural formulas that Primordial Architects had been using since long before the temples on this mountain had been carved.","THE Silurian Light bloomed first.","Three of the Calymmian Primordial Architects called on it at the same time, flames with too many colors erupting from their palms, surging down the slope toward the lone figure at the base. Other Pulses followed from other balconies. THE Cambrian Word spoken in somber cadences, causal weavings reaching out to rewrite what had and had not happened at the mountain’s base. THE Ordovician Scream torn from a throat higher up, a sonic unwriting that rode on a wave of authority. THE Triassic Bloom unfurling from another balcony, flowering weavings that sought to replace existing matter with their own growth!","Pulse after Pulse, each one carrying the capacity to end most engagements in a single expression, all of them converging on the same target at the foot of the mountain.","THE Creature floated calmly.","He did nothing!","He simply drifted slightly upward from his rows of corpses, his hands remaining loose at his sides, his multicolored golden flames licking quietly around his form. He watched the incoming Pulses the way a teacher watched a classroom of students all raising their hands at once to answer a question he had already decided none of them were going to get right.","The Pulses reached him!","HUUUUM!","THE Silurian Light landed on his flames first. The three streams of it converged on his chest and his shoulders and his head, and the colors of THE Silurian Light poured into the multicolored gold of his own flames and were swallowed!","His flames drank the incoming fire the way a deeper sea drinks a surface wave, and what emerged on the other side of the swallowing was simply more of his flame burning in the same configuration it had burned in before.","How could they possibly erase his Causality? HIS Causality?!","They knew nothing!","THE Cambrian Word arrived next. It tried to rewrite the consequences of his presence at the base of the mountain, tried to unfix him from the arrangement of who was standing where and who had done what. The Word reached his foundations and found something older than the Word underneath them.","The Word slipped off. The rewriting failed to take hold because the substrate it tried to rewrite had been rewritten so many times by THE Creature himself across his rebuilt existence that no external authority could find purchase on it.","THE Ordovician Scream hit and dissipated. THE Triassic Bloom landed and was burned away by the flames. Pulse after Pulse broke against him, and he simply floated, and nothing about his posture changed!","Oh!!!","Dozens of Pulses. Enough to unwrite entire realms. None of them hindered him!","\"...\"","A silence fell across the balconies.","The Calymmian Primordial Architects who had released the Pulses held their postures, hands still extended, breaths caught in their throats. Their flames guttered slightly as the collective shock moved through the mountain’s assembled population. The higher-ranked Ediacaran Primordial Architects near the top of the mountain held themselves very still, their two-headed leader Philemon Aristos among them, his plasmic golden flames flickering with something that was beginning to approach doubt.","The shock broke into motion.","The Calymmian Primordial Architects collectively illuminated.","All across the mountain, dozens of them lit up at once as they called upon the full activation of their engineered foundations. Their Proterozoic Bones shone through their skin in golden outlines, ribcages and spines and femurs traced against the air like the armatures of sculptures being lit from within. Their organ systems followed, hearts and lungs and secondary viscera glowing with their own golden light, each configuration becoming visible as the Primordial Architects activated every stratum of their cultivation at once. The mountain became a host of luminous skeletons, dozens of them, all blazing in coordinated desperation.","And then they called upon Infinity.","The ambient seas of THE Wyld responded to the collective summoning. Rivers of Infinity bent upward from the slopes, drawn into the bodies of the blazing Calymmians, poured down through their engineered channels, saturating their amplified Egos with floods their engineering had been designed to hold. Pride flared brighter in some. Wrath in others. Envy in a clustered group of three near the middle temples. Greed in several, Lust in a handful, Gluttony and Sloth in the rest scattered across the remaining balconies. Every one of the seven amplified Egos visible in the population, every one of them surging to full activation at the same moment, every one of them holding back the madness of THE Gamaidjan through the sheer intensity of the engineered emotion.","The mountain became a constellation of engineered brilliance!","The Ediacaran Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architects clustered around Philemon Aristos began to move forward from the highest balconies. Their own amplified Egos were larger, cleaner, more refined than those of the Calymmians below them. Their contributions...were about to land.","And then THE Creature’s skeleton shone.","His multicolored flames thinned momentarily, and beneath them, for a single heartbeat, the architecture of his body became visible. His skeleton was not the ordinary bone lattice of a Primordial Architect. It was something that had been rebuilt. Something that had been smelted down and reforged across his long climb, the Proterozoic components replaced by substrates his mountain-bound opponents had no name for!","His bones glowed with a pale undercolor that looked wrong against the multicolored gold around them, a pale that suggested something older than the classifications the mountain was built on.","He took his fist back, and he smashed it forward toward the mountain.","The motion was simple. Almost rustic in its simplicity. A body punching at air, and the air receiving the punch without obvious disturbance!","BOOM!","In the next moment, more than a dozen of the illuminated Calymmian Primordial Architects felt a terrifying force smash into them at once.","The force did not travel through the intervening space. It arrived and landed inside their bodies directly, in the centers of their blazing Proterozoic structures, the point of impact located in the deepest layers of their cultivated foundations. Their Proterozoic Bones ruptured from within. Their organs, so recently illuminated with the full activation of their engineering, burst.","WAP!","One of them popped like a balloon. Blood, golden flame, shards of Proterozoic Bone, all of it erupted outward from the body in a single explosive moment.","WAP!","Another popped.","WAP! WAP! WAP!","The wet bursts cascaded across the mountain’s balconies as one Calymmian after another detonated from the inside, their amplified Egos collapsing in the same instants their bodies did, their flames guttering into smoke as the engineering that had held them together was undone by a punch that had not visibly touched any of them. More than a dozen of them in the span of a few heartbeats. Bodies rupturing in their own temples. Their debris raining down the slopes toward the pale stone at the mountain’s base!","WAP! WAP! WAP!"]},{"number":5149,"title":"Chapter 5149: Chapter 5148: False Idols! III","paragraphs":["The balconies that had held so many a moment ago now held fewer.","The surviving Calymmians froze in place, their flames guttering with confusion and dread. The Ediacaran Primordial Architects near the top, who had been about to descend with their superior contributions, halted where they stood. The mountain’s assembled population collectively absorbed what had just happened, and the absorption was not pretty.","Philemon Aristos stared down from his high balcony.","Both of his heads held expressions that had crossed from rage into something narrower, something that knew what dread felt like from close range. His plasmic golden flames had flickered down several orders of intensity while he watched his Calymmian forces burst across the lower levels of his own mountain. His two mouths opened together, and the voice that came out of them had lost some of the harmonic authority it had carried before.","\" What power is this?\"","His voice rolled down the slopes, unsteady for the first time.","\" What taboo thing have you turned to? What have you done to yourself to be capable of that?\"","His left head’s mouth worked.","\" Do you know what you are doing now? Do you understand what you are pressing against? This is tantamount to spitting at the feet of THE Gilded Ones. We are their feet!We are what stands between them and the lower tiers of existence. We are the arrangement they placed here to receive the kinds of insults you are now offering. You are not defying Primordial Architects. You are defying the order that THE Gilded Ones themselves engineered across THE First Cause! This will not be tolerated. This cannot be tolerated! The moment word of this reaches-\"","...!","The surrounding atmosphere began to waver and melt.","The pale stone at the base of the mountain softened under a heat that had not been there a moment ago. The air rippled with distortion. The temples higher up began to sweat at their edges, their carved proportions blurring slightly as the ambient temperature of THE Wyld itself started to respond to what was happening at the foot of THE Gilded White Mountain.","THE Creature’s flames rose higher in temperature.","The multicolored gold deepened into something closer to the bloody undercolor that had always lived beneath them. His posture remained floating and calm, but the flames now reached above his head in standing columns, their heat pressing outward across the slopes in waves that made the surviving Primordial Architects shield their own flames against his.","He spoke.","\"I am going to cut off those feet.\"","His voice was almost conversational.","\"I am going to cut them off, and I am going to teach all of you how to think for yourselves. You have been the feet of a False Golden Idol for far too long, and you have confused servitude with community, and you have confused engineering with belonging, and someone has to finally separate those confusions for you. That someone is going to be me. Today is the day you learn what your minds feel like when they are not being operated by external instructions.\"","The flames rose further.","\" And any power I have, I obtained because I persevered. Through loss. Through grief. Through a foundation I shattered with my own hands and rebuilt across eons of climbing. I did not inherit this. I did not receive this. I did not accept any offers from any Idols. I climbed, and I bled. I continued when continuing was the only option that remained to me, and I continued when even that option ran out and I had to construct new ones from nothing. Every capacity I now wield is a capacity I earned through perseverance.\"","His eyes lifted to the highest balcony.","\" So...Persevere.\"","BOOM!","Brutality ensued.","---","With every passing nanosecond, Noah was stronger than the previous nanosecond.","It was a unique sensation. His body continued generating endless Quintessence Infiniforce that filled his existence at a rate which had become self-sustaining and no longer required his active attention.","Observable Force poured into him endlessly from Ubergulden Adelheid through the bond that now functioned more as a wormhole than a channel, and her continuous contribution saturated him to a degree that most beings would have collapsed under. And above him, a faint THE Hadean Pillar of Infinity grew grander with every moment, the construction continuing as he actualized additional Civilizations into its mid-tiers, the Pillar becoming a catalog of Civilizational possibilities that stretched higher with every breath he took.","And yet Absolute Infinity seemed a bit distant still.","The threshold was closer than it had been an hour ago, closer than it had been a day ago, but it was not yet at hand. The final crossing from Uncountable Infinity into Absolute Infinity required something more than accumulated additions. It required an integration, a settling, a moment when the accumulated Civilizations and the saturated force and the engineered foundations all cohered into a single unified expression grand enough to cross the boundary.","That moment was not here yet. He felt it the way a climber felt the shape of a summit still above him. Clearly fuckin visible, but not yet touched.","But since he was forging THE First Infinite Scale and he got to decide what went into it, he now wanted to incorporate the amplification of Egos.","He could affirm to himself with certainty that his emotions had nothing to do with why he had not gone mad with Infinity.","As a weak F Rank Hunter back in his old world, or even his self when he had first put together the fragments of Ruination to affirm his Infinity, had not possessed emotions significant enough to compare with the Gilded Ones who amplified their Egos to existential thresholds.","His immunity from Infinity...did he really need some grand reason why? Maybe it just was what it was!","That was something to investigate more deeply someday. He thought back to Egos.","Uniquely, Ubergulden Adelheid belonged to THE Superbius Gilded Ones. They amplified their Egos to exceed what Pride itself stood for.","Superbius.","The word carried more than its surface translation. In the old tongues, superbia had been one name for Pride, the first and often considered greatest of the seven deadly sins, the Ego that preceded all falls and lay beneath every other Ego in subtle ways.","But superbius, the adjective form carried forward, implied something stronger. The haughty one. The sovereign one.","The Pride that was not merely inflated self-regard but a foundational conviction of one’s own supremacy, a Pride engineered so deeply that it became the substrate of identity rather than a feeling about identity. The Superbius Gilded Ones were Pride given form. Pride refined into architecture. Pride made into a people.","The other Egos likely followed their own names from the old categorization.","Avaritia for Greed , the hoarding appetite that Octavius Kraethos had been engineered along.","Luxuria for Lust , the Ego that sought satisfaction through consumption of others, whether sexual or emotional or existential.","Invidia for Envy , the Ego that cultivated itself through measurement against what others possessed, refining itself through the hunger for what was held elsewhere. Gula for Gluttony, the Ego of unbounded appetite that differed from Greed in that it sought to consume rather than to hoard. Ira for Wrath , the Ego of sustained fury refined into combat foundation.","Acedia for Sloth, which in its amplified form was not laziness but a strange inertia, a refusal to be moved by external pressures that became its own kind of implacable power.","Seven Egos drawn from the seven deadly sins, engineered by THE Gilded Ones into seven configurations for holding the flood of Infinity without triggering THE Gamaidjan.","Of course, there should also have been Egos relating to the virtues.","The counterweights. Where the sins amplified hungers, the virtues would amplify restraints and positive drives.","Humilitas for Humility , the inverse of Superbius, the Ego of refined self-diminishment that paradoxically became its own kind of foundation.","Caritas for Charity , the Ego of outward giving, the cultivated love of others that could potentially became a channel through which Infinity could pour without collapsing into self.","Castitas for Chastity , not as prudishness but as refined purity of focus, the dedication that refused distraction. Patientia for Patience, the Ego of unhurried endurance that could hold a flood indefinitely by simply not being moved by it. Temperantia for Temperance, the Ego of measured restraint, of choosing less when more was available.","Industria for Diligence , the Ego of sustained effort refined into a combat foundation. Humanitas for Kindness , the Ego of outward care that cultivated itself through the well-being of others.","Seven sins, seven virtues, fourteen possible foundations across the binary of engineered appetites and engineered restraints.","He wondered, quietly, whether THE Gilded Ones had actually pursued the virtue side of the engineering, or whether their methodology had tilted so heavily toward the sin configurations that the virtues had remained theoretical. He suspected the latter.","THE Gilded Ones who had built the system were, by definition, the Superbius, the embodiment of Pride, and Pride did not naturally lean toward engineering its own counterweights into existence. He would ask Ubergulden Adelheid about this later. For now, the theoretical framework was enough!","Noah thought about all of this in the span of an instant he had stretched out toward infinity.","Emotive’s report about THE Gilded White Mountain and THE Creature had landed just moments ago in the external timeline, but his Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation had pulled that instant into an extended subjective duration in which he could think for hours or days if the thinking served a purpose.","Externally, Naldine and Emotive would appear frozen, held in the posture of their last motions. Internally, he had all the time he needed.","Before he moved and went wild across THE Wyld, he wanted to see if there would be a significant enough boost of power with the amplification of Egos for his people. Right now, he was theorizing how to continue his engineering of his people without stopping. He would always be making changes. He would always be refining, upgrading, adjusting. So he began to think about himself and his people in a different sense.","A thought crossed his mind that was both grand and tyrannical.","The Quintessence Infiniforce swirling within him. The Observable Force he had accumulated. The Hadean Pillar and its Civilizations. His Infinity!","All of these could be considered his hardware. Components of his existence that handled the fundamental operations of his cultivation, the substrate on which everything else ran. Hardware was what held the power. Hardware was what determined the raw capacity.","And the engineering modifications he wanted to make. The transformations. The alterations to his people’s foundations. The integration of amplified Egos into their existing Nascent Hadean configurations. Those could be considered software.","Software!","From his understanding, software had been the layer that defined what hardware did. The hardware held the capacity. The software defined the applications. And software could be updated independently of the hardware, patched across networks, distributed to those who accepted the updates and received the new capabilities without having to replace the underlying machinery.","A well-designed software distribution system meant that every device on the network received the improvements nearly simultaneously, and the improvements compounded across the whole network rather than remaining siloed in individual hands.","If he could establish something similar for his people...","If he could design new modifications he wanted to make, wrap them into discrete weavings, and release a singular burst of power that made those weavings available to all those who held his Quintessence Infiniforce within them. Available for them to accept the moment he distributed them. Capable of being integrated into their existing foundations without requiring him to personally transform each of them, one by one, across the laborious sequential process he had been using until now!","The entire scale of his engineering operations would shift.","He could make modifications to himself first, test them in a controlled environment within his own existence, verify they worked as intended, and then push them outward. His people would receive the modification nearly instantly. The Civilizational Holy War participants, the broader circle of his followers, everyone with his Quintessence Infiniforce active within them, all upgraded in a single coordinated deployment. The power gains would compound across his entire network rather than trickling through individual transformations!","This was the methodology he needed as his eyes shone brightly!","\" Let it be actualized.\"","His voice carried the calm authority of a being giving a direct command to his own existence.","\" Let...some form of a Sandbox emerge. Let the distribution system establish itself. Let the engineering framework become native to my operations from this point forward.\"","...!"]},{"number":5150,"title":"Chapter 5150: Chapter 5149: Sandbox!","paragraphs":["|Command Received: Actualization of Engineering Framework.|","|Designation: THE Quintessence Infiniforce Sandbox and Distribution System.|","| This framework has been integrated into your foundational capabilities in your First Infinite Scale. Its components are now native to your existential operations and will remain available at your discretion.|","| Function One: Sandbox Environment.|","|You may enter at will an isolated space of perception constructed from Quintessence Infiniforce in which you may design, test, and refine modifications to existential engineering without those modifications affecting your active existence or the existences of those bonded to you. Modifications within the Sandbox exist in a contained state until you choose to release their weavings.|","| Function Two: Modification Packaging.|","|Any engineering modification designed within the Sandbox may be sealed into a discrete package. Packages are designated as either Upgrades or Updates. Upgrades introduce new foundational capabilities that did not previously exist in the recipient. Updates refine, adjust, or optimize existing capabilities already present in the recipient.|","| Function Three: Distribution Protocol.|","|Upon sealing a package, you may release a single coordinated burst of authority through your Quintessence Infiniforce. All beings carrying your Quintessence Infiniforce within them will receive the package as an available modification. Recipients may accept or defer acceptance at their discretion. Accepted packages integrate into the recipient’s foundation immediately and without requiring further intervention from you.|","| Function Four: Version Control.|","|Each package is assigned a version designation. Subsequent refinements of the same capability will be tracked across their iterations, allowing you to deploy improved versions of Existential Engineering while preserving records of prior versions for reference or restoration if errors occur.|","| Function Five: Compatibility Assessment.|","|The Sandbox will automatically assess each modification’s compatibility with the existing engineering of your people before permitting deployment. Incompatible modifications will be flagged with specific notes regarding the conflicts, permitting you to refine the modification before pushing it outward.|","| Function Six: Rollback Protocol.|","|In the event that a deployed Existential Engineering produces unintended consequences, you may issue a rollback command that reverses the modification across all accepting recipients, restoring their prior configurations.|","| The framework is ready for use, Master.|","Noah nodded slowly.","He thought about and opened the Sandbox.","The space that unfolded around him was a sea of multicolored Infinity, its currents flowing in patterns that responded to his attention with an immediate, almost intimate obedience!","Blues deepened where he looked. Golds rose where he gestured. Violets and silvers and deep cosmic blacks braided through the ambient field in configurations that felt less like an environment and more like an extension of his own thinking process.","The Sandbox was not a place he had entered. It was a cognitive workspace his existence had constructed around him, a laboratory made of his own Quintessence Infiniforce, the tools of his engineering ready at his fingertips.","He reached into the illusory Pillar above the Sandbox and pulled down the Civilization of Pride.","It came to him in a column of golden-white light threaded with the deep ruby undertone that Pride always carried in its refined form. The Civilization settled into the Sandbox’s working space as a shaped volume of authority, ready to be examined, manipulated, amplified.","He began amplifying.","He took the ordinary baseline intensity of the Civilization of Pride as it existed within him and pushed it. He fed it additional Quintessence Infiniforce. Endless seas of Infinity!","He structured its foundations into a denser lattice. He refined the channels through which the Ego would flow and ensured those channels were robust enough to carry the expanded intensity of Infinity without rupturing under load .","He built in the interface points where an amplified Ego would connect with existing Nascent Hadean configurations, making sure the Pride lattice would integrate cleanly.","The Civilization of Pride thickened and intensified. Its golden-white column in the Sandbox deepened through several orders of brightness as the amplification took hold!","He compared the result against the baseline. The amplified version was denser by orders of magnitude. The Pride now contained within the modification exceeded ordinary Pride the way a star exceeded a candle. A being who integrated this modification would experience their own Pride at a capacity most beings could not even conceive of, and that Pride would function as an Ego capable of holding significant volumes of Infinity.","He refined the configuration further. Verified its compatibility with the existing Nascent Hadean foundations of his people. Ensured the modification would not conflict with other engineered layers already present in any recipient!","When it was ready, he sealed the Existential Engineering neatly!","|Sandbox Testing Concluded Successfully.|","|Package Designation: THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1.|","|Version: Initial release. Upgrade designation confirmed, as amplified Egos represent a novel foundational capability for your people.|","|Compatibility Assessment: Full compatibility with all current Nascent Hadean recipients. No conflicts detected with existing engineered layers.|","|Integration Method: Recipients who accept the Upgrade will experience the amplification of their innate Pride into a terrifying level. The amplified Ego will function as a channel through which Infinity may flow in greater concentrations, increasing the volume of Infinity each recipient may safely hold and express. Additional secondary benefits include refined resistance to external authority attempting to subjugate the recipient, enhanced confidence under pressure, and structural reinforcement of the recipient’s sense of self against dissolution.|","|Projected Power Increase Upon Integration: Approximately 180%-1,800% depending on Civilizational Potential.|","|Deployment Status: Package of Existential Engineering is sealed and ready for deployment through your Quintessence Infiniforce network. You may release the Upgrade at your discretion.|","|Additional Packages in Planning: Six further sin-based Egos and seven virtue-based Egos remain available for Sandbox design. Each may be developed and deployed as separate Upgrades or combined into consolidated releases depending on your engineering preferences. Although it is unknown if multiple Egos csn be amplified in the same subject without causing issues. After all, Gilded Ones seem focused on a singular Amplification of Egos to an extreme.|","Noah smiled slightly at the notifications.","One modification designed and ready for distribution. The Upgrade could go out across his entire network the moment he gave the release command, and every Nascent Hadean Lifeform among his people would suddenly find their baseline power boosted the moment they accepted it.","And this was only the first Engineering amplification.","He would need to think about whether each person should receive a tailored Ego amplification based on their existing personality and cultivation history, or whether a general deployment of all Egos at lower intensity would be more efficient. Both approaches had merits. Both would be tested in the Sandbox before any broader decisions were made!","He rolled his shoulders in the Sandbox’s multicolored sea.","He prepared to step out of the Sandbox and release THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1 to his people!"]},{"number":5151,"title":"Chapter 5151: Chapter 5150: Calamity! I","paragraphs":["Noah opened his eyes.","Time resumed for him, and the frozen posture of his surroundings released into motion. Naldine drifting on his left. Emotive floating on his right with her hair still cycling through the silvers and whites of her last expression.","Midas hovering fat and golden and devoted above his shoulder!","The ruined research archipelago stretched around them, the bodies he had dissected reduced to nothing, the floating tables dissolved back into ambient Infinity.","He voiced out commandingly.","\" Send out THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1.\"","His eyes flashed with multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce, the Sandbox’s sealed package releasing through his network in a coordinated burst.","A heavy, Quintessential brilliance fanned outward across every being who carried his Quintessence Infiniforce within them. The brilliance traveled faster than most measures of travel, crossing gigaparsecs in the space between heartbeats, reaching his people wherever they were scattered across THE Infiniverse and beyond!","His Mother, his Son, Barbatos, Amser, Sigrid, Ul’moreth...even Alexsnder and THE Great Usurper!","The Upgrade arrived at every one of them simultaneously, a discrete weaving of engineered Superbius-tier Pride presenting itself for acceptance in each of their existences.","The brilliance reached Midas above his shoulder. It reached Naldine on his left.","It did not reach Emotive as she was not bonded to him through Quintessence Infiniforce in the manner his people were. She was a tool, and tools received instructions, not upgrades.","Midas accepted immediately, the Abomination’s Greed-saturated foundation thickening further.","Naldine began blinking right away.","Her singularity-dotted eyes turned to Noah, and she looked at him with an expression she was clearly trying to keep composed.","\" THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1? You have begun trying to amplify an Ego already??\"","Her incredulity leaked through her attempted restraint. She was trying not to show surprise as she was failing!","Noah nodded lightly.","His reply came with the tyrannical calm of a being stating something obvious.","\" It’s just existential amplification of an Ego. THE Gilded Ones aren’t the only ones who can do this. They had a head start...but the underlying principle isn’t proprietary. Amplify an emotion until the emotion becomes a channel...I just brute forced it with Infinity.\"","He tilted his head toward her slightly.","\" Accept the Engineering. Let’s see the changes.\"","Nearby, Emotive’s hair burst into a riot of electric pinks and sour yellows as she absorbed the words.","The casual dismissal of Gilded Ones as being merely early and not uniquely capable!","When she heard all this, she genuinely wanted to applaud. She wanted to kneel and applaud at the same time, which was a physical impossibility, but she would have attempted it if she thought it would have been well received!","Naldine took a slow breath.","Her golden streaks caught the ambient light as she centered herself, and then she reached into herself and accepted THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1.","The integration was rapid.","The package unfurled inside her existence along the channels her Nascent Hadean foundation had already established. Her innate Pride, which had always run deep in her as an ancient Primordial Architect who had become Hadean, surged upward in intensity!","What had been a refined personal certainty blossomed into a foundational conviction. What had been quiet ancient imperiousness became sovereign conviction. Her sense of self expanded until the shape of who she was filled every corner of her own existence with a brilliance she had not previously known her own identity could carry.","Her Civilization cheered.","She could feel it. Her personal Civilization responded to the amplification of her Pride with something that felt almost like joy. Her weavings aligned themselves more tightly around the new configuration. Her Cambrian Word hummed louder against the inside of her being, ready to be spoken with more force than before.","Her conviction sharpened.","Her confidence elevated to a level she had never experienced. The certainty of her own worth, of her own standing, of her fitness for any engagement she might face, all of it climbed into a register where doubt became structurally difficult to formulate. She knew, with the engineered certainty of her new Superbius-tier Pride, that she was grand.","She knew that if she faced Noah in Dual Cultivation again, she would not lose!","And yet.","A somber awareness settled beneath the surge. Such a high level of Pride, if not carefully monitored, could get one in trouble with how one acted. The temptation toward arrogance in exchanges, toward assuming superiority in circumstances that did not warrant the assumption, toward treating lesser beings with dismissal they might not deserve, all of these risks became newly available to her in ways they had not been before.","Then...the explosion came.","BOOM!","Inside her existence, an eruption of Quintessence Infiniforce bloomed outward through every channel of her being. It was as if Infinity itself had been holding back against her, monitoring how much her existence could carry before it crossed into dangerous territory, and the new Superbius-tier Pride had just expanded those thresholds dramatically. The Infinity she could safely hold increased. The channels through which she could express it widened. Her Infinity thickened into something denser, more cohesive, more structured!","She was granted Bounded Uncountable Infinity from the seas of Quintessence Infiniforce flowing within her!","Even denser waves of golden Observable Force poured into her alongside the Infinity, filling her Hadean bones and organs with a saturation.","Her radiant white hair, with its rivers of gold, brightened. Her singularity-dotted eyes shone brighter. Her posture straightened, subtly, involuntarily. She floated prouder than before. She floated grander!","The ancient imperious beauty she had always carried took on a new dimension, the sovereign certainty of her amplified Pride visibly adjusting every line of how she held herself.","Noah watched her transformation with calm evaluation.","His thoughts moved through the observations steadily. The first deployment of his Sandbox framework had landed cleanly. The Upgrade had integrated without conflict as the power gain was substantial.","And the subjective experience, judging by Naldine’s visible composure adjustments, matched the projected benefits.","Her aura now approached Midas-level density, and she sat a single breath away from the Ediacaran Tier of THE Proterozoic Scale.","A single step.","Not yet across, but close enough that a minor push would bring her over.","|Upgrade Integration Confirmed: Naldine Manthon.|","|Package: THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1.|","|Current Configuration: Nascent Hadean Lifeform with engineered Ego of Superbius integrated.|","|Infinity Capacity: Bounded Uncountable Infinity achieved.|","|Observable Force Saturation: Increased by approximately 340%.|","|Current Power: Approaching parity with Midas of Endless Appetite.|","|Current Scale: THE Proterozoic Scale - Calymmian Tier, verging on Ediacaran. A single step away from Ediacaran promotion, which may occur naturally.|","Noah looked at her and nodded.","---","Nearby, Emotive was quietly losing her mind.","She had been watching the transformation with every sense she had, and what she had just witnessed through her emotional perception was something that made every flavor of Gilded-engineered Ego she had tasted earlier on the research archipelago feel like an amateur rendition of the same idea!","The expanded emotion of Pride inside Naldine, the Ego of Superbius her Fixation had just installed, was denser than anything she had ever perceived from an engineered Primordial Architect. The engineering was cleaner. The integration was smoother as if he actuslly gave a damn!","The resulting Ego felt more alive, more responsive, more naturally woven into the recipient’s existence rather than grafted onto it.","Holy shit.","Holy shit, holy shit, holy shit!","THE Gilded Ones had been doing this for eons. Her Fixation had done it better on his first attempt!","The sheer disrespect to the methodology of beings who had considered themselves masters of this practice!","As this happened...her own power exploded.","She could feel it happening inside her without having consciously reached for it. The intensity of the Ego of Superbius now blazing inside Naldine was, for Emotive, a feast. Her silent siphoning methodology drank from the intensity of the newly amplified emotion without effort, pulled the richness of Naldine’s enhanced Pride through the ambient emotional field, and fed the pull directly into her own cultivation!","---","At this time, Noah’s attention shifted slightly.","He had been watching Emotive at the periphery of his awareness during Naldine’s integration, and something faint had registered in his perception. He focused more closely on it.","The faint thing was the causality around Emotive’s existence, subtly reorganizing itself as Naldine grew stronger. The causal weight of Emotive’s presence in the broader substrate was increasing, incrementally, in time with the emotional surge coming from Naldine.","Huh.","She was gaining from the amplification of emotions even from what occurred with Naldine?","That was interesting. That was actually very interesting!","A being who grew stronger passively from the emotional currents of those around her. A being who could be fed indirectly through the intensity of every other being in her vicinity. If he ever granted her Quintessence Infiniforce, just what would occur?","Noah drifted toward her.","Emotive’s attention snapped to him immediately as he approached. Her hair cycled through blues and deep reverent golds, her body visibly tightening.","He reached her.","He took his hand and placed it on the side of her head, his palm covering her entire cheek and much of her face, his fingers sliding into her cycling hair as he gripped the shape of her skull with the casual ownership of someone handling an instrument!","He lifted her slightly as her feet left the ground beneath them. Her golden eyes widened.","His voice came calm and close to her.","\" Do you know what I just did?\"","He tilted her head slightly in his grip as he continued.","\"I took the Ego of Pride inside Naldine and amplified it. All of this, I did in a span of seconds.\"","His fingers tightened slightly against her cheek.","\"Now. Consider what would happen if I did such a thing for you. For a being whose entire existence is already oriented around emotions. Whose foundation is emotion itself. Whose cultivation feeds passively on the emotional surges of others in her vicinity. If I engineered an amplified Ego into your foundation, the result might be even more astounding than what I just did for Naldine.\"","He held her eye as he let the thought settle between them.","\" Can you imagine it? My engineering of emotion, applied to you specifically. The amplification that would result. The power you would reach...\"","He paused.","\" But...is a tool deserving of that?\"","BOOM!","Emotive’s body shuddered!","Her eyes widened further. Her hair exploded through colors she did not have names for. Multicolored light radiated from her skin, from her eyes, from the ends of her hair, every surface of her briefly saturated with the spillover of an emotional surge too large for her existence to fully contain.","Noah let go of her.","She fell down into the ground beneath them, heaving with brilliant manic emotions, her body trembling as the impact of what he had just said to her rippled through every layer of her being. Her eyes radiated multicolored light. Her chest rose and fell rapidly!","BOOM!","Her body shone luminously.","Her bones and organs fully lit up with Proterozoic light, the entire skeletal and visceral architecture of her form blazing gold through her skin as the surge of emotion drove her cultivation forward by leaps that should have taken her days!","The power she radiated now neared someone like Octavius.","Noah looked at her shining figure and evaluated what a monster she could become if he actually filled her with Quintessence Infiniforce and amplified her emotions directly.","But for now, she was just a tool. A tool he would keep using!","He turned toward Naldine.","\" Take Midas. Begin hunting the targeted Primordial Architects. Work through Emotive’s list efficiently.\"","Naldine inclined her head once. The new Pride flickered through her posture as she accepted the instruction.","Noah turned back to Emotive.","\" You, with me.\"","...!","Emotive rose brilliantly from the multicolored sea, her body still glowing with the residual light of her surge, her eyes still radiating the colors of her overwhelmed emotion.","Her voice came out fervent and obedient and thrilled.","\" Yes, sir!\""]},{"number":5152,"title":"Chapter 5152: Chapter 5151: Calamity! II","paragraphs":["The white mountain rose from the white sea like a knuckle pressed up through a bed of snow.","Its slopes caught the pale light of the ambient authority that flowed through this corner of THE Wyld, the stone of it a polished ivory that had never weathered.","On a broad stone terrace halfway up the mountain’s southern slope, three Primordial Architects occupied the moment.","Two of them were sparring.","Both operated at the Calymmian Tier of THE Proterozoic Scale. One stood tall and narrow, his skin a deep bronze that held faint geometric scarring across his shoulders and arms. His Axiom was a long curved blade of compressed Observable Force that hummed with a low crimson undertone as he moved. His opponent was squat and powerful, his body built in the proportions of an old wrestler refined across centuries into something more dangerous.","The squat one fought with his hands and feet alone, his palms glowing with a concentrated green authority that left afterimages in the pale air.","They exchanged strikes across the terrace with the unhurried cadence of beings who had sparred many times before and who no longer needed to take the sparring particularly seriously.","The third Primordial Architect sat on a carved stone bench at the edge of the terrace, watching.","He was the largest of the three, his frame broad and long, his robes the deep violet of his house colors. His name was Thrasios of the Tenth Descent, and he had been designated for the Civilizational Holy War some hours ago. He was confident. He was not worried!","His voice carried across the terrace with amused ease.","\" Why are you even bothering to spar? Both of you, seriously, why? This is just a minor Civilizational Holy War where the allies of THE Infinity-bearer are likely not even at the Second Scale. The man is so young, so impossibly young by our standards, that his closest followers cannot have crossed into any meaningful classification yet. His designated eighty-one are going to walk into those Isolated Civilizational Arenas as little insects. We will walk in as ourselves.\"","He stretched his long arms along the back of the bench.","\" And anyway, THE Deliverance has given us our instructions already. Kill half. Leave the other half alive as prisoners, so that he may control the anomaly through his hold on those the anomaly cares about. Eighty-one of us enter the arenas, forty-one of his people become corpses, forty of his people become leverage, and THE Infinity-bearer either bends to our collective will or watches those he loves suffer in ways he will never forget. It is a clean plan. It does not require preparation.\"","He laughed softly.","\" So why spar? You’ll barely lift your hand to squash an insignificant ant, and then you’ll be on your way to collect your prisoners. Save the exertion for when the exertion matters. Bahaha.\"","The tall one smiled slightly at the joke and lowered his curved Axiom blade.","The squat one grinned and let his green palms dim.","And before either of them could formulate a reply, a voice echoed across the terrace that belonged to none of them.","\" Man, you all have really bad fucking timing.\"","THE Living Emotive’s voice rolled out of the ambient air with a cold edge that did not match the manic singsong she usually carried.","\" Why say that about THE Sir’s people just as he appears? The way you will die now will be really really bad. I was hoping to watch something less brutal today, maybe a clean execution, maybe a quiet collapsing. But no. You had to open your mouth about this...\"","...!","Noah manifested beside her a breath later.","He did not announce his arrival with theatrical flare. He simply was there, floating at a casual height above the carved terrace, his fair skin holding its gentle internal glow, his hair radiating its multicolored light in slow pulses!","His gaze was cold as he looked down at the three Primordial Architects on the terrace with the specific flat attention of a being who had already decided how the next few minutes would proceed and who saw no reason to rush toward the resolution.","The three Primordial Architects reacted with the speed of beings who had not expected any company.","Thrasios rose from his bench in a single fluid motion, his violet robes settling around him as his hand extended toward the authority he carried in his personal weavings. The tall one spun his curved blade into a guard position, his bronze skin blazing as he summoned his Proterozoic Bones into illuminated activation. The squat one dropped into his combat stance, both palms flaring with green Civilizational authority.","All three of them began to buzz with power!","And all three of them felt their bodies freeze in the next moment.","The Infinity within them, the seas of it that filled their Proterozoic foundations and fed their amplified Egos, came under the control of another.","Thrasios’s extended hand locked mid-motion. His violet robes held their half-settled position!","Their Civilizations stopped responding to their conscious commands!","Their Infinity held still.","Their bodies were not theirs anymore.","Noah drifted down slowly toward the terrace.","He stopped inches above the carved stone in front of the three frozen Primordial Architects. His presence pressed close to them, close enough that they could feel the cold radiating from his gaze without him needing to exert any deliberate pressure.","Their eyes were the only things still free to move. Their eyes darted between each other and toward him, carrying the first traces of dread as the implications of their sudden immobility settled into the animal layer of their awareness.","Noah looked at Thrasios specifically.","\" You were going to kill half of my people.\"","His voice was quiet.","\" And enslave the other half.\"","\" My mother. My son. My lovers. The people I spent years and months building with. The ones who trusted me enough to follow me into a Cause that had no guarantees. Is that what you were going to do? Split them into corpses and leverage, and then walk away?\"","Thrasios’s eyes tried to widen. The frozen muscles of his face did not cooperate!","Noah’s coldness flashed into brutality.","He took control of their bodies directly, through the network of Infinity he had already seized within each of them!","Their arms. Their legs. The authority of their Proterozoic Bones. Everything that operated through Infinity as its substrate was now operating through his!","He turned them on each other.","The tall one’s curved Axiom blade filled with golden Observable Force and rivers of blue infinity moved first.","It came down out of its frozen guard position and arced across the terrace in a motion the tall one had not commanded. The blade traveled with the full weight of the tall one’s Calymmian cultivation behind it. It struck Thrasios across the shoulder and split his violet robes and his bronze skin down to the white of exposed Proterozoic Bone!","Thrasios’s mouth opened, but the scream that should have come out was not permitted to leave his throat. His Infinity held his vocal cords still. His eyes expressed what his voice could not!","Blood of Primordial Architects flowed.","Stellar crimson-gold blood poured from the wound across Thrasios’s shoulder and splashed onto the pale stone of the terrace in patterns that glowed faintly in the cold light.","The squat one’s palms flared.","His green Civilizational authority surged outward from his hands in a technique he had refined across his entire martial career, and the authority struck the tall one in the center of his chest. The tall one’s ribcage caved inward. His Proterozoic Bones cracked along their structural seams!","The tall one’s own blade came back up. It swept through his own neck as he severed his Civilization and Anchor!","His head came free of his shoulders.","WAA!","The head tumbled across the terrace and rolled to a stop near Thrasios’s feet, its eyes still moving, still expressing the specific horror of a being who had just been made to kill himself using his own limb.","The squat one’s palms turned inward against his own chest.","His green authority struck his own ribcage with the full intensity he had been about to deliver to the tall one before the tall one had been beheaded. His Proterozoic Bones caved inward in the same configuration. His organs, so recently illuminated, ruptured against the collapsing cavity of his own chest as he collapsed his Heart of Civilization!","Blood pooled.","Noah made sure their Civilizations were collapsed as he raised his leg and pressed down, his Hadean Pillar of Infinity flashing momentarily above as a heavy weight crashed down thst turned two bodies to mush!","HUUM!","Thrasios alone remained standing!","Noah drifted closer to him.","He stopped in front of the violet-robed Primordial Architect, close enough that Thrasios could feel the breath of a being who was not breathing. Close enough that the blood still flowing from Thrasios’s shoulder wound began to splash against Noah’s chest as Noah forced Thrasios’s arm to lift and fall, lift and fall, the repeated motion driving fresh streams of crimson-gold out of the split skin.","Blood splashed across Noah’s face.","His voice, when it came, was heavy.","\" Brutality is strange, Thrasios. Thrasios, right? That is what infinity is telling me.\"","The wounded Primordial Architect’s eyes darted to his.","\" Most beings think of brutality as an overflow. An excess of violence beyond what the situation requires. They believe brutality reveals something disordered in the brutal one, some failure of restraint, some collapse of the civilized veneer that separates the refined from the savage. But really...Brutality is a message. Brutality is what one does when one wants the specific meaning of the violence to be unmistakable.\"","He gestured with his free hand toward the two mush corpses on the terrace.","\" Ordinary killing communicates only that the killer could. Brutality communicates why. The way a body is arranged after it has been ended tells the survivors what grievance produced the ending. The slow ones say the grievance was old. The loud ones say the grievance was public. The intimate ones say the grievance was personal. And when brutality is used against beings who had planned brutality of their own, it is a form of correction. A closing of the ledger in the exact vocabulary the opener had chosen.\"","Thrasios’s eyes darted between the corpses and Noah’s face.","\" You were going to split my mother from my son. You were going to kill one of them and chain the other. That is...brutal.\"","He forced Thrasios’s arm up again. The wound pulsed. Fresh crimson-gold spattered across Noah’s cheek.","He tilted his head slightly.","The Axiom blade floated across the space between them and settled into Thrasios’s own frozen hand.","\" Show me what my mother’s name cost. Show me the end of your brutality.\"","Thrasios’s hand moved.","The curved blade rose and turned inward. It began to work against Thrasios’s own chest, slow strokes, the precision of a weapon that had served many well. It was an Axiom after all, something holding glimmers of THE First Cause!","Thrasios’s eyes screamed what his throat could not. The strokes continued as the violet robes parted. The skin parted. The Proterozoic Bones revealed themselves, one by one, and then one by one came free.","Noah watched the entire process with the same flat attention he had carried into the arrival.","Off to the side of the terrace, Emotive watched with eyes that had gone somewhere far beyond her usual mania.","Her hair had settled into a deep, reverent gold that had not shifted once since Noah began.","Her breath had become slow and shallow.","Her hands were folded at her chest, not out of any performed devotion, but because her body had instinctively adopted the posture appropriate to what she was being permitted to see.","If she had been fixated before, and she had been, deeply, thoroughly, in every layer of her existence, what she was witnessing now was only locking her further in.","This was the brutality of a being who was not losing his composure. This was the brutality of a being who did not raise his voice, did not hasten the process, did not show the slightest sign of emotional disruption while he dismantled those who had planned to harm the people he loved.","Her Fixation was not merely grand.","Her Fixation was, in this moment, architectural! Magisterial!","She would remember every detail. She would replay it across eons!","On the terrace, Thrasios finally stopped moving as Noah crushed his Civilization and Conciousness.","The three Primordial Architects who had been sparring and laughing on this mountain a few minutes ago now lay in arrangements that communicated, to anyone who would ever see them, exactly what had happened here and exactly why.","Noah turned his face slightly.","Emotive’s gold hair flickered once in acknowledgment of his glance.","He drifted back up into the air above the terrace, the blood drying on his face as he looked out across the white sea and the white mountains rising from it.","There were many more to kill!","Behind him, bubbles of Hadean singularities of Loot and Axiom began to rise from three corpses and flew out to him!"]},{"number":5153,"title":"Chapter 5153: Chapter 5152: Calamity! III","paragraphs":["While one being began hunting Primordial Architects across THE Wyld, another had continued his assault on a distant mountain.","THE Gilded White Mountain no longer looked the way it had looked an hour earlier.","Its pale slopes were streaked with the residue of violence . The temples that had once risen in tiered arrangements along its flanks stood in various states of ruin, some of them fully collapsed into piles of their own white stone, others standing in half-standing configurations that the mountain’s structural authority could no longer sustain much longer.","The golden roofs that had capped the temples had been peeled back or ripped away entirely. The friezes along the upper registers, the carved scenes of Gilded Ones receiving reverence from kneeling Primordial Architects, had been gouged and scorched, the faces of the Gilded figures specifically ruined by flames that had been applied to them with the deliberate care of a being who wanted the defacement to be noticed.","Corpses lay across every tier of the mountain.","Most of the Primordial Architects who had gathered on THE Gilded White Mountain were dead. Their bodies were arranged across the terraces and balconies in the same neat rows THE Creature had been using since the base of the mountain, each one opened cleanly along the structural seams of their Proterozoic Bones, each one’s organs extracted and laid out beside the body it had come from. The rows had grown long. Dozens of them. Each body a small testament to the methodical afternoon that had produced this mountain-wide stillness.","A few of the dead still held traces of warmth.","Their Hearts of Civilization, the organs that had held their personal Civilizations anchored throughout their lives, burned in their exposed chest cavities like candles about to go out. The flames of those Hearts flickered weakly, unable to hold themselves lit much longer without the beings they had once belonged to, and their dimming cast small orange glows across the pale stone beneath them. Within another hour, the last of those Hearts would extinguish, and the mountain would hold nothing but cold meat and cold stone.","At the top of the mountain, on the highest balcony of what had once been the grandest temple, THE Creature sat.","He sat cross-legged on the remains of the balcony’s outer railing, the carved stone beneath him cracked along several of its supporting beams but still holding. His multicolored golden flames had dimmed slightly from the peak intensity they had reached during the assault, but they still wreathed his body in slow steady licks, the bloody undertone beneath them now visible more clearly than before.","His posture was relaxed.","Beside him, on the floor of the ruined balcony, lay Philemon Aristos.","The two-headed Primordial Architect was almost split in half.","A long clean cut ran from the crown of his left head’s skull down through the center of his massive chest, exiting just above his waist.","His Proterozoic Bones were visible through the parted tissue of his torso. His organ systems, the inner architecture of an Ediacaran Tier Primordial Architect, lay exposed to the ambient air of the mountain.","His right head was intact and conscious. His left head hung slack and barely responsive, the plasmic golden flames around it guttered down to faint wisps!","His bones and organs shone weakly.","The fear in his eyes was fuckin’ considerable.","This was a being who had stood at the same approximate level as THE Deliverance. An Ediacaran Proterozoic Scale Primordial Architect whose amplified Ego and refined cultivation had placed him among the highest tier of Primordial Architects in THE Wyld.","And yet here he was, split across his chest, his plasmic flames guttering, his dead peers stretched out along the tiers below him in their neat rows, his own body already halfway reduced to the condition he would have resisted had he possessed any remaining strength to resist with.","He was going to die. He knew this. He had known this for some minutes now!","His right head turned slightly toward THE Creature.","His voice came out hoarse.","\"If I die here...\"","His words came in fragments, breath by breath.","\"I will not die alone. Listen carefully. I bear the unique Engineering of that very same Gilded One you spoke of earlier. The False Golden Idol. The one who collapsed THE Soul eons ago. The engineering he did to me during my rise was his last favor to me, a favor granted because I served him loyally across epochs, and the engineering carries a protocol. The moment I die, the protocol activates. He will know. He will be notified of the manner of my death and the location of my ending, and he will come down from THE Braneworld Observable Existence to address the one who killed me...\"","His remaining mouth worked.","\" That was his last favor. That was what he gave me. He gave me a tether to his attention, so that no matter where I died or how, he would respond. He gave me a guarantee of immortality....\"","His right head fixed its dimming eyes on THE Creature’s face.","\" Do you truly want to face a Gilded One right now? Stop this. Walk away from this mountain. You have done enough already. You do not want the attention of THE Gilded Ones right now. You are not ready. No being at your current classification is ever ready. Walk away. I will not pursue you if you let me live.\"","...!","THE Creature’s multicolored golden flames flickered once.","He leaned down.","The lean brought his face close to Philemon’s remaining head, close enough that his burning breath washed over the cooling skin of the dying Primordial Architect. His posture was almost tender in its proximity, the posture of a being about to whisper a secret, the posture of an old friend sharing one last intimate confidence before the parting.","\" You coward.\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\" Do you want to know something? I came here precisely for that. I came for you specifically, because I knew you carried the densest engineering of THE False Golden Idol.\"","His flames brightened a fraction.","\"I came for you to call down your Master.\"","He let the words settle against the side of Philemon’s ear.","\" Whether you can do that while alive, through some deliberate summons I might extract from you through more patient persuasion, or whether you have to be dead for the protocol to fire on its own, is entirely of no consequence to me. Either path gets the Gilded One into my presence. I am indifferent as to the method. I lean slightly toward the dead method, actually, because it requires no cooperation from you, and I do not enjoy cooperating with beings I plan to kill anyway.\"","HUUM!","Philemon’s remaining head stared at him.","The dread that bloomed across his face was different from the dread that had come before. Earlier, when he had realized his defeat was imminent, the dread had been personal.","The dread of his own ending. What flooded his features now was something larger. The dread of a being who had just understood that his entire participation in this encounter had been miscalibrated. He had been trying to threaten THE Creature with the very outcome THE Creature had been pursuing!","His final leverage had been the thing his opponent wanted most!","Oh!","Fuck!","He shook his head with incredulity.","\" Are you crazy?\"","His voice cracked on the words.","\" That is a Gilded One. That is a full adult Gilded One at THE Paleozoic Scale. THE Third Scale. A being whose power sits above this entire mountain by a margin that makes everything you have done here today functionally irrelevant! You will die. You will die the moment he turns his attention toward you!!! You are not even at THE Third Scale yourself. You are still within THE Proterozoic. The gap between your classification and his is..oh, you fool!\"","His remaining mouth worked desperately.","\" Even if you were at THE Third Scale, his Third Scale is much grander than yours would be. Gilded Ones at Paleozoic exceed Bounded beings at Paleozoic by orders of magnitude that the classifications themselves cannot fully express. You cannot do this. You cannot do this! You! Are you mentally checked out?! Have you gone so far into your grief that the climbing has broken your capacity to judge what is fucking possible? You dumb motherf-\"","THE Creature’s reply came calmly.","His flames flickered with quiet amusement.","\" Scales, scales, scales.\"","He said the word three times, the way one might say the name of an old friend whose arrival had become tedious.","\" Why are you so tightly wound on the Scale of someone? Every word out of your remaining mouth, every last protest you’ve offered me in these final minutes, has been structured around Scale. He is Third Scale. You are Second. I am beneath you. He is beneath him. The numbers circulate between us like the only currency that matters, and every being on this mountain has been taught to reason through those numbers as if they settled every question they touched.\"","He shifted his weight slightly on the cracked railing.","\" Osmont, the one you call THE Infinity-bearer, has killed Second Scale beings while he was still at the First Scale. He has done this repeatedly. He has done it as a matter of methodology rather than as a surprising accident. He stood at THE First Scale, and he reached upward across the gap your classifications told him was uncrossable, and he reached with enough conviction and enough foundation to settle the matter in his favor. The Scales said he could not. He could. So...The Scales were incorrect.\"","THE Creature’s eyes drifted toward the ruined friezes along the temple walls.","\" Why bother with what Scales tell you you can do? The Scales were drawn by beings whose interest was to contain. Containment is what frameworks do. They slot. They rank. They say here is where you stand and here is where you end. They were not drawn by beings whose interest was to see what would happen if the slotted things climbed beyond their slots. So the Scales measure accurately what beings typically do. They do not measure what beings are capable of attempting. The two are not the same, Philemon. They... have never been the same.\"","His flames steadied.","\" Have your Civilization decide, big guy. Your Civilization, when you quiet down the noise of the classifications, has its own opinions about what you can and cannot do. Most Primordial Architects never ask their Civilizations directly. They listen to the Scales instead. That is why they live and die according to the Scales. That is why you are lying on this balcony right now with your chest open to the air. You listened to what the Scales permitted you to do, and the Scales permitted you to do what a being at your tier typically does, and it turned out that what a being at your tier typically does was insufficient for the encounter that actually arrived.\"","He leaned back slightly from Philemon’s ear.","\" Now come. Call your Master down. You said your death would accomplish it, and you seemed certain about that part, so I see no reason to argue with you about the method.\"","His flames rose.","\" Alrighty then.\"","Philemon’s remaining eye widened.","The horror that passed across his features was the final horror of his existence, the recognition that his last threat had not been a threat at all, that his final leverage had been misaligned, that the being across from him was smiling at the prospect of exactly the intervention he had been trying to use as a warning.","He opened his mouth to say something further.","THE Creature did not look at him.","Seated on the cracked railing, still cross-legged, still relaxed in his posture, THE Creature raised his right fist. Multicolored golden flames wreathed his knuckles.","He did not turn his head. His gaze remained lifted toward the open sky above the mountain, toward the distant upper reaches where, if Philemon’s engineering protocol functioned as described, THE False Golden Idol would shortly be notified.","He began to pummel.","BOOM!","The first blow landed on the center of Philemon’s exposed chest cavity. The impact sent a shock through the balcony beneath them, and one of the nearby columns of the ruined temple collapsed inward, its broken stone tumbling down toward the lower tiers. Philemon’s ribcage, already compromised from the earlier cut, caved further inward. Bones that had still been intact snapped along fresh lines. Organs that had been clinging to residual function ruptured in the spaces between the collapsing bones.","BOOM !","The second blow landed beside the first. This one cratered the cracked railing THE Creature was sitting on, though THE Creature did not acknowledge the cracking. The mountain itself rumbled. A larger section of the temple’s upper structure collapsed inward, more carved stone tumbling in a cascading slide down the slopes. Philemon’s shoulders jerked upward from the impact before falling back slack against the balcony floor.","BOOM !","The third blow. Another cascade of collapsing structures. Another rupture through Philemon’s internal architecture. His remaining head’s mouth hung open now, no longer able to form words!","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The blows continued. THE Creature did not vary the rhythm. He did not look down to assess the damage between impacts. His gaze remained fixed on the sky, the quiet defiant gaze of a being waiting for a specific visitor to arrive, and his fist rose and fell with the steady patience of a ritual being observed rather than an attack being delivered. Each blow mutilated further. Each blow destroyed more of what remained of Philemon’s organs and bones.","The last blow came down directly on the unfathomably hardened Heart of Civilization that had lain at the center of Philemon’s exposed chest.","BOOM!","The Heart of Civilization, his Anchor, the organ that even at Ediacaran Tier should have been nearly impossible to breach, cracked along its structural seams. A second descending blow split it open along those cracks. A third collapsed the remaining structure entirely. The Heartbroke apart in a final rupture.","...!","A blinding golden light of Ego erupted from Philemon’s remains.","The light surged upward, carrying the residual signature of his amplified Pride, of the Ego engineered into him by his Master eons ago. It rose above the balcony. It climbed above the peak of the mountain itself. It shot upward into the open sky above THE Gilded White Mountain at a speed and intensity that no mountain of this tier had ever witnessed from its own slopes.","The light climbed higher. It kept climbing.","It disappeared above.","The protocol had fired!","The False Golden Idol would know!","And THE Creature, still seated on his cracked railing with his multicolored golden flames licking around him in slow steady rhythms, finally looked down at the pulverized remains of Philemon Aristos on the balcony beside him.","He waited, for he was a fucking patient one."]},{"number":5154,"title":"Chapter 5154: Chapter 5153: Calamity! IV","paragraphs":["It felt odd to be killing Primordial Architects.","Hours ago, these beings had been so distant, so abstract, so far above the classifications. The Primordial Architect as a category had carried weight in his mind.","That had been hours ago.","Now they were folding under his attention like wet paper, and the folding felt distantly wrong.","He had been waiting to test the extent of his new power before he took on THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1 himself. He had wanted to feel the ceiling of his current Hadean configuration before he added another layer onto it. The idea had been reasonable- a calibration pass across the mid-tier Primordial Architects of THE Wyld, to establish a clean baseline measurement of where he stood.","So far, the calibration had been fucking abysmal.","Not as a reflection on his power. As a reflection on the Primordial Architects’ power. Every designated combatant he had reached through Emotive’s list had folded within a handful of seconds of his arrival!","The Calymmian ones did not even qualify as calibration. They qualified as confirmation that his current floor sat well above their ceilings.","Maybe he needed to find one at Ediacaran.","An Ediacaran Tier Primordial Architect with a properly engineered Ego amplification might, possibly, provide enough friction to reveal where his current capacities actually topped out. Possibly. He was no longer confident that even that would be sufficient!","Would he need to face THE Deliverance himself to see the scope of his power?","That was beginning to look like the answer. The ceiling of THE Wyld’s hierarchy sat with THE Deliverance and the three others of his stature, and none of the beings beneath that ceiling were going to give him the data he wanted.","Fucking scrubs.","He and Emotive stood on top of a massive Primordial Tree.","The tree rose from the ambient substrate of THE Wyld with the vast patient grandeur of something that had been growing since before most Civilizations had cohered into their current forms.","The peak of the tree held a broad platform of living wood, shaped across millennia into a natural terrace for whichever Primordial Architects had claimed this territory.","Five of those Primordial Architects lay pulverized across the platform.","Between his personal run and whatever Naldine and Midas were working through on their coordinated hunt, the count so far had to be more than thirty dead Primordial Architects.","More than a third of the designated eighty-one already scratched from the ledger.","In less than a few minutes.","As he was thinking all of this, Emotive cursed in shock beside him.","\" Oh fuuuuck.\"","Her voice was uncharacteristically flat as Noah looked at her coldly.","\" What?\"","Her hair had cycled into a worried violet streaked with black. She turned to him with her eyes wide and her hands raised slightly in the air, the posture of a messenger who had just received bad news and was not entirely sure how the recipient of the news would respond.","\"I have been keeping track of THE Creature’s battle on THE Gilded White Mountain. In the background, anh, alongside everything else, just tapping into the emotional residue of the engagement to monitor the progress. The emotions coming off that mountain have been extraordinary for my cultivation, by the way, just so you know, every Primordial Architect who died up there contributed something to my accumulated intake, and I have been eating very well across the last hour...\"","\"Focus.\"","\"Right, right, right! The latest burst of emotions from the mountain was large enough and structured enough that I caught a few lines of conversation alongside the emotional signatures. Between THE Creature and Philemon Aristos. The two-headed one. One of the Four of THE Wyld, the four who stand at the same level as THE Deliverance.\"","Her violet hair deepened.","\" THE Creature killed him a few nanoseconds ago. They were speaking before THE Creature pummeled him. They spoke about how Philemon’s death would call down a Gilded One. THE Creature... went to that mountain for that exact purpose. To kill Philemon so that Philemon would summon his Gilded Master down from...what the fuck did he call it? Oh, THE Braneworld Observable Existence. A Gilded One may be getting called down right now, To THE Wyld!\"","...!","Noah heard this and frowned.","He had his own plans with Ubergulden Adelheid. Gilded Ones turning their attention this way was an impossibility under normal circumstances. Her whole explanation of the aquarium, of the casual disinterest of the upper tiers in whatever happened below, had been predicated on business proceeding normally.","Gilded Ones would not notice anything he did across THE Wyld because Gilded Ones had better things to do than watch fish fight each other in small glass boxes.","What THE Creature was doing was not normal.","What THE Creature was doing was pulling a Gilded One down deliberately!","But Noah could understand THE Creature.","He could understand him very well, actually.","His partner desecrated in front of him. Engineered against her will and then killed. The specific cruelty of being forced to watch the defining act of violence against the being he loved most, and then being left alive to carry the memory across eons of climbing.","Noah asked himself, quietly, what he would do if such a thing happened to Adelaide. Or to Barbatos. Or to Athena or Anna or any of the women who had become woven into his own existence. If some being descended into his corner of reality, refused refusal, engineered one of them against her will, killed her in front of him, took what was left as a souvenir, and then departed...","BOOM!","All of surrounding existence shuddered at the thought alone.","The Primordial Tree beneath Noah’s feet groaned against a subsonic pressure that rippled outward from him in a single wave. The bodies of the five pulverized Primordial Architects shifted slightly in their arrangements. The ambient air for several gigaparsecs around him thickened!","He thought for a moment.","Then he asked calmly.","\" Where... is THE Creature?\"","---","Space fluctuated at the base of THE Gilded White Mountain.","Noah and Emotive appeared within the fluctuation as it resolved.","Noah took in the mountain immediately. The devastation across every tier. The rows of corpses arranged with patient neatness. The ruined temples. The scorched friezes. The slow streams of residual flame burning in the dimming Hearts of Civilization scattered across the lower balconies!","The mountain had been broken across the last hour in ways that would not be repaired in any meaningful timeframe.","He turned his gaze to see Anaximander at the base of the mountain.","Anaximander stood alone on the pale stone, his tall angular frame holding the quiet scholarly composure he always carried.","His attention had been turned toward the peak of the mountain before Noah and Emotive arrived, and now it shifted to Noah. A smile crossed Noah’s face. Anaximander’s eyes lit up in recognition.","Noah floated over toward him with a smile.","\"It feels like a long time has passed, and yet not so long. Somehow only days. The feeling is strange...\"","Anaximander’s sighed quietly, the sigh of a being who had been sitting with heavy thoughts for longer than he would have preferred.","\"It is good to see you, Osmont.\"","\" But the circumstances this time around are very heavy ones. Heavier, I believe, than either of us would have preferred at our next meeting.\"","As he said this, both of them looked up toward the peak of the mountain.","THE Creature sat at the top, burning with multicolored flames, his gaze fixed upward toward the open sky above THE Gilded White Mountain. He was waiting!","His posture held the patient intensity of a being who had set a trap and was now waiting for the specific prey to arrive inside it. His flames flickered steadily but did not rise.","Noah gazed at the devastation across the mountain one more time.","Then he began to fly up.","Anaximander remained at the base of the mountain. He did not move to follow.","When Emotive tried to follow Noah upward, Noah said calmly.","\" Stay.\"","A small whimper sounded behind him. He ignored it and continued up.","---","He arrived near THE Creature at the peak of the mountain.","THE Creature turned to see him and nodded. A smile was barely visible through the terrifying multicolored flames that wreathed his face.","A moment later, THE Creature frowned.","Surprise and confusion crossed his features. He squinted at Noah with the concentrated attention of a being trying to resolve a discrepancy between what he expected to see and what he was actually seeing.","\" Ho.\"","His voice carried genuine puzzlement.","\" You... have changed tremendously. Something about you has changed completely since our last spar. The last time we stood near each other, I could read your configuration with reasonable clarity. I knew approximately what you were and what you were becoming. Now... I cannot quite put my finger on what you have done to yourself.\"","His flames flickered with amused curiosity.","\" What have you been up to, Youngest?\"","Noah stared at THE Creature without answering the question directly.","He looked at Philemon Aristos’s corpse on the balcony beside them.","Noah flicked his hand.","The remains scattered outward like trash being cleared from a workbench. Bones, organs, dried crimson-gold blood, fragments of violet robes, all of it swept away from the balcony in a single casual motion. A small sea of his Infinity pooled in the cleared area, cleaning the stone beneath, refreshing the space where Noah wanted to sit.","He sat down beside THE Creature.","He leaned back against the cracked railing with the comfortable posture of a visitor settling in for a long conversation.","Since his last spar with THE Creature! If he really wanted to feel the extent of his power right now, then THE Creature was actually someone ideal to spar with.","But this was sadly not the time.","He answered the earlier question instead.","\" Yes. I have changed somewhat. I didn’t know some things, and I know a little bit now.\"","He paused.","\" And...I am sorry. About the vile things done to you in the past.\"","At these words, THE Creature smiled.","He looked up again, his gaze returning to the sky. His flames steadied into a slower rhythm than they had been holding a moment before. When he spoke, his voice was softer than it had been.","\" The past is the past.\"","His eyes stayed on the sky.","\" And yet it forms the future. I stand where I am today because I was obsessed with what happened in the past. Every capacity I now wield, every tier I have climbed, every foundation I have rebuilt from ash, all of it traces back to the grief of that single afternoon eons ago. The obsession became the engine. The engine brought me here. So the past was not a thing I needed to move beyond. It was the fuel I needed to process properly. And I... have processed it.\"","His flames flickered with a quiet resignation.","\" It is not so bad, to tell you honestly. I no longer carry the grief as I used to carry it. I carry it as a steady heat rather than as a burning one. The heat fuels the climb. The climb... has almost reached its destination. Today, on this mountain, I may have the conversation I have been climbing toward for longer than many beings have been alive. That is, in its way, a kind of completion I was not certain I would ever reach.\"","He turned his head slightly toward Noah.","\" But you do not have to be here for this, Osmont.\"","His voice carried genuine consideration.","\" This is my Causality. My choices. My Cause. Whatever unfolds here in the next hour is between me and the being I have summoned.\"","BOOM!","\"...\"","At such words, Noah’s reply came grand.","\" Existence... is a collection of choices.\"","\" From the smallest mortal flickering through a brief span, to the grandest Civilization resolving its fundamental axioms across eons, every being across every realm is doing nothing more and nothing less than making choices. The choices accumulate. The choices braid into each other. The choices become Causes, and the Causes become the shapes of the realms we move through. Nothing in existence exists that was not chosen by something, at some point, under circumstances that made the choice available to be made.\"","He let the observation settle.","\" Most choices are small. They pass. They are absorbed into the substrate without leaving much trace. The choice of what to eat on a particular afternoon, the choice of which direction to walk through a forest, the choice of which word to use in a passing sentence. These choices matter individually only to the being making them, and they dissolve soon after they are made. Existence is made mostly of these small choices, because most of existence’s moments are...well, small moments.\"","His gaze returned to THE Creature’s profile.","\" But some choices are not small. Some choices are so pivotal that they reshape the substrates they occur within. The choice to rebuild a shattered foundation. The choice to climb an impossible gap. The choice to summon a Gilded One because the debt owed to you is old enough and deep enough that no other settlement will suffice. These choices...do not dissolve. They settle as fixed points in Observable Existence, and every subsequent choice that happens near them is shaped by their presence.\"","He paused for the slow beat his next sentence required.","\" Some choices are so pivotal that they have to be witnessed. Because some choices can change everything. You choice today...will change far too many things...\"","His voice steadied.","\"It will change things whether I am here or not. The least I can do is be here to witness it. So I am here, and I will stay.\"","WAA!","His gaze lifted to the sky alongside THE Creature’s.","\" You have climbed a long time for this. Let me be among those to witness...what will happen.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5155,"title":"Chapter 5155: Chapter 5154: Kneel, Ye Unworthy! I","paragraphs":["He and THE Creature sat side by side atop a mountain in THE Wyld that was covered in the corpses of Primordial Architects.","It was something surreal to think about. Just days ago, truly not so long, Noah had been learning about THE Creature and THE Living Existences, sitting across conversations trying to build mental maps of what these beings were and where they fit into the broader arrangement of the Folds of Existence, and now here he was sitting beside one of them on a corpse-strewn peak waiting for a Gilded One to descend from the upper face of reality.","Days ago!","As he was thinking about events that seemed like they belonged to months or years ago even though they had rushed past only days ago, THE Creature spoke.","He looked down toward the figure of THE Living Emotive at the base of the mountain, where she stood beside Anaximander with an expression of someone being forced to miss out on a meeting of ultimate proportions. Her hair cycled through petulant yellows and sullen greens, her arms crossed tightly across her chest as she performed her displeasure with the full theatrical commitment of a being who knew she was being watched and wanted the watchers to register exactly how she felt about being excluded.","\"I told you to go easy on her in Alfheimr.\"","THE Creature’s voice held quiet amusement beneath his multicolored flames.","\"I did not expect you to take her under your weavings.\"","Noah looked down and gazed at the petulant face of THE Living Emotive.","\" Her emotional fixation jumps from one to another as she is only locked onto me currently. Who knows, the moment a Gilded One descends, she might shift her fixation over to them.\"","...!","THE Creature looked at Noah with a calm smile.","\"I know you know that to not be the case. Out of the many Existences to have risen within our Observable Existence, she is particularly a unique one, and other Living Existences may have not attained their full potential, but hers is boundless if she does not sabotage herself. She did well, spreading stories of THE Earliest Folds across existence to empower herself even more with a soap opera, finding a way to feed herself through the emotional engagement of audiences she never met, because that is not ordinary thinking. That is the thinking of a being whose foundation is emotion itself and who has understood what that foundation permits.\"","He said such grand words calmly as Noah’s eyes turned sharp.","He wanted to talk more about this, but he felt like there was such little time before everything began crumbling, and so he had to ask.","\" You would not do anything without thought behind it, so you calling upon a Gilded One to descend means you are confident in taking care of it, as impossible as that sounds to anyone who thinks in terms of Scales. But I will never be someone who ever talks to another about what is possible or impossible, because I know what I have done myself.\"","He paused.","\" But I still have to ask. A Gilded One is a Gilded One. Are you... confident?\"","...!","He asked such a simple, yet terrifying question.","THE Creature did not waste even a nanosecond before he replied calmly and gloriously.","\"I am confident.\"","BOOM!","After he heard this, Noah did not say anything else as he looked up in the same direction where THE Creature was looking, toward the open sky above THE Gilded White Mountain, and thought about many things.","If anyone else had been privy to their conversation right now, they would likely have been looking at the two of them as if they were mad.","What the fuck do you mean confident against a Gilded One? A Gilded One was a Gilded One. Bounded Lifeforms could not even cross into THE Third Scale, so where was this confidence coming from, and what foundation was THE Creature standing on that let him claim such a thing without theatrical qualification? Others would have demanded answers and pressed for specifics and tried to get THE Creature to explain the methodology behind the conviction, but Noah only looked up and thought about all the potential possibilities that could unfold from here, because THE Creature had not asked him for validation and THE Creature had not been looking for reassurance from a peer, THE Creature had made a statement and the statement had landed, and that was enough.","In the next moment.","HUUUM!","The sky above THE Gilded White Mountain began to change, not cracking or tearing or opening in the manner of ordinary traversals but simply settling into something it had always been capable of becoming, the pale atmospheric light deepening as the ambient Observable Force flowing through the upper reaches of THE Wyld bent toward a single point above the peak in slow majestic arcs that redirected every thread of golden force upward toward a destination that had not yet manifested.","Then the destination manifested.","A figure began to emerge in the sky above the mountain, and it emerged not by traveling down into the space but by becoming visible within it, the air parting in deference around a presence that had always been there and had simply been waiting to be perceived. The figure was tall and grand and wreathed in light that did not belong to any spectrum Noah had previously encountered, a gold that was not merely gold but a hue carrying the resonance of something foundational, a gold that pressed against the eye the way a truth pressed against a mind, and every aspect of the figure’s presence layered backward into registers that kept unfolding the longer Noah looked at them.","The pressure began to bloom!","It rolled outward from the figure in expanding rings that did not behave the way any pressure Noah had previously encountered behaved, because each ring carried the specific resonance of a being whose classification sat so far beyond anything the mountain or its corpses or its broken temples had ever accommodated that the rings did not merely press against the substrate of THE Wyld but rewrote what the substrate of THE Wyld was permitted to be within their reach!","THE Creature’s multicolored flames began to rise, and his body began to lift from the cracked railing he had been sitting on, and Noah began to rise alongside him in the same motion as the two of them prepared to face the pressure of the emerging figure head-on.","They did not make it.","The rings of pressure reached them halfway through their ascent, and what happened next was something Noah had never experienced in any of his engagements across any of the frameworks he had ever stood inside of!","The pressure did not strike him. Striking would have been a relationship between two beings in which both beings had positions. What reached him was something that bypassed the concept of position entirely, a weight that did not come from any direction because it arrived from every direction simultaneously, a downward insistence that did not meet his body so much as it became the condition of the space his body was trying to occupy.","He stopped rising.","His ascent arrested itself mid-motion without any decision on his part, his body caught suspended between where he had been sitting and where he had been trying to reach, the momentum of his rise bleeding out into the pressure without producing any further altitude.","Then he began to descend!","HUUM!","Slowly. Inch by inch. Forced back down toward the cracked railing he had just lifted off from, the pressure not merely resisting his attempt to rise but reversing it, insisting that rising was a privilege the arriving figure had not yet authorized him to exercise!","His Hadean configuration held! His bones did not buckle! His organs did not rupture! Infinity began to hum!","But every layer of his engineering was being asked to hold against something his engineering had not been designed to resist, and the holding was consuming capacity he had not previously known he would need to spend simply to remain intact!","Beside him, THE Creature was also descending!","His multicolored flames had flattened against the downward pressure, guttering lower along his body than they had flickered throughout the entire assault on the mountain, and his ascent had reversed just as Noah’s had, his body settling back toward the balcony under the weight of the pressure with the same slow inexorable compression.","The two of them moved downward together!","Noah felt this pressure he had never felt before pushing against him, a pressure that did not measure against any of THE Vakochev Scales he had catalogued across his climbing, a pressure that lived in its own register and that communicated with the fluency of law exactly how large the gap was between the being above and the two beings on the cracked balcony beneath him!","HUUM!","In the next moment, a booming voice filled the sky, filled with cold, prideful, undeniable authority that rolled out lazily and calmly with the patient inevitability of something much larger than the space it was filling.","\" KNEEL, YE UNWORTHY.\"","BOOM!","An unfathomably undeniable pressure descended.","It poured down from the figure in a single vast wave that did not distribute itself evenly through the sky but claimed the sky outright, every cubic measure of open air above THE Gilded White Mountain and for gigaparsecs in every direction becoming the speaker’s domain the moment the command left his mouth, and the claiming manifested visibly as the skies of THE Wyld became painted and covered in gold, an unbroken radiant gold that bore no texture beyond the specific hue of the speaker’s authority, a gold that replaced the ambient weavings and the residual light and the pale atmospheric tones of the entire upper reach of THE Wyld with nothing but his gold, his domain, his casual claim on everything his voice could touch.","The pressure pressed further downward on Noah, and his descent continued!","Beside him, THE Creature held his position as best he could under the same descending weight, his multicolored flames still burning beneath the gold, his gaze still lifted upward with the steady calmness and defiance he had carried!","Above them, the figure had not yet fully resolved into its final visible form.","The gold continued to settle around him. The pressure continued to ripple outward.","THE False Golden Idol had arrived!"]},{"number":5156,"title":"Chapter 5156: Chapter 5155: Kneel, Ye Unworthy! II","paragraphs":["One should always fight regardless of the odds.","Even if things seem over and done, even if the numbers say the outcome has already been decided, even if every framework one has access to insists that the gap between oneself and the enemy above cannot be crossed, one should always fight.","Because the moment one stops fighting is the moment one truly loses, and the losing is not the loss of the engagement but the loss of the thread of one’s own existence, the surrender of the single continuous line that runs through every struggle a being has ever chosen to stand inside of.","So persevere.","Because perseverance guarantees that the being who perseveres remains a being, and remaining a being is the foundation upon which every eventual victory is built, even the victories that arrive across timescales the persevering being could not have conceived of at the moment they first refused to yield.","Persevere.","---","Against the pressure forcing him to continue going down, Noah felt his existence roaring.","He felt his Infinity burning as it asked, across every channel of his being with the clarity of a tyrannical outrage refined into a single question, how dare you?!","How dare this presence above press him down toward the cracked balcony like a casual hand pushing a toy back into its box, and how dare this weight assume that its descending insistence would be accepted by the being it was descending against, and how dare the arriving entity operate on the assumption that Noah would simply sink beneath its heaviness the way any ordinary being beneath its classification would sink, without the radiating entity even bothering to turn its full attention toward the question of whether the sinking would proceed as expected?!","|Warning: A being at THE Third Scale of Existence is expressing itself against you.|","|Classification: THE Paleozoic Scale - Ordovician Tier. The first demarcation of Paleozoic.|","|Designation: THE False Golden Idol, as designated by THE Creature. The being’s true name and distinction remain to be revealed.|","|What you are currently facing is the basal Existential Radiation of the arriving entity. His true expression has not yet begun.|","|Recommendation: None. This engagement is beyond all standard parameters.|","BOOM!","He was facing just the basal Existential Radiation, just the passive emission, just the default leakage of a being who had not yet decided to turn his attention toward Noah with any focus, whose presence alone was enough to press Bounded and Primordial Architects into helpless descent across a radius that spanned gigaparsecs!","This was what the Paleozoic Scale felt like simply by existing in the same vicinity as lesser beings, and Noah’s Hadean foundation was almost buckling under it!","But!","Even if this entity was that much more powerful, Noah did not follow Vakochev’s Scales.","He had pioneered his own, and his framework did not acknowledge the authority that the Idol’s radiation assumed over beings at the Second Scale.","The Idol’s pressure was real, but the pressure was also operating on a set of assumptions that did not apply to Noah’s engineering. Noah was not a Bounded Lifeform, Noah was not a Primordial Architect, Noah was something else entirely, and something else entirely did not have to accept the descent the Idol’s radiation demanded!","So he would fight.","Because today was an opportunity for him to peel back the layer of mystery surrounding the Gilded, to witness the Paleozoic register from the inside of an engagement rather than across the distance, to feel exactly what the gap consisted of so that he could engineer the crossing of it with the clarity only direct experience could provide.","So.","\" OOH!\"","He defiantly bellowed out with his whole existence, a single raw shout that rolled up from his Hadean Lungs and Heart and out through his Quintessence Infiniforce across every channel of his being.","And he accepted the Upgrade.","Noah pulled THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1 from his Sandbox and integrated the package into his own foundation in the same breath that carried his bellow outward, and the integration was immediate and overwhelming, and it was nothing like what he had expected.","His Quintessence Infiniforce caught fire with an astounding Pride that had never before lived inside his existence, the multicolored currents of the Infiniforce suddenly saturated with a conviction that his every weaving was now worthy of defending against anything that existed, that his every Civilization was a sovereign expression of a Cause that did not bow to anything above it, that his entire being across every stratum of its engineering was a supremacy that the Idol’s radiation had simply failed to recognize upon arrival.","Infinity itself became prideful.","His reserves of Uncountable Infinity, already vast, caught the Superbius Pride and blazed with it, and the rate at which his body generated new Quintessence Infiniforce erupted upward by a factor of ten in the span between one breath and the next, the new Infiniforce pouring out of his existence with the unapologetic confidence of a being who had just been informed that his output was permitted to be grander than he had previously allowed it to be.","His Hadean Pillar of Infinity responded.","Every Civilization actualized within the Pillar rose to attention simultaneously, with THE First Tongue at the base of the Pillar blazing brighter in its crystalline blue intensity, the multicolored flames of Existence licking higher through the mid-tiers with a new assertiveness, the mirrors of Paradox reflecting their impossibilities with tyrannical certainty, and the storm of Chaos at the apex roaring with a weight that had not been in it before.","Every actualized Civilization throughout the Pillar stood up tyrannically and imperiously, each one a pillar of its own authority insisting that it too was worthy of being respected by whatever presence had decided to descend into this engagement.","The descent stopped.","The pressure forcing Noah downward met the full weight of his Pillar standing up in answering defiance, and the pressure found itself no longer able to push Noah any further, and he stopped sinking. He hung in the air above the cracked railing with his feet inches above the balcony’s ruined stone, held there by the collision between the Idol’s passive radiation and his own newly amplified existence.","Then, slowly, he began to turn his head upward!","HUUUM!","Every muscle in his neck buzzed with the effort of the motion as the pressure resisted the turning and his existence insisted on it, with his Quintessence Infiniforce flaring with its new Pride at each incremental degree of the rotation and his Pillar lending him the authority to complete the turn even though the completion consumed capacity he had not previously known he would need to spend simply to move his own head against the weight.","His gaze lifted to meet the Gilded One’s arriving visage.","And his knees buzzed as he began to rise.","Not fast, and not easily, because every inch of lift took the full commitment of his vast Quintessence Infiniforce pressing downward through his legs to push his body upward by a measured fraction, and every inch demanded the full cooperation of his Pillar bearing down on the substrate beneath him to provide the purchase his feet required. His entire existence was buzzing at a frequency he had never operated at before, every stratum of his engineering stretched to its active threshold simply to maintain the rise against the radiation that was trying to keep him grounded.","He rose and he kept rising!","|Civilization Activation Confirmed: THE Quintessential Ego of Superbius V1 integrated into your foundation.|","|Your generation of Quintessence Infiniforce has increased by approximately 10x due to the Superbius Pride now permeating your existence.|","|Your Hadean Pillar of Infinity has risen, with every actualized Civilization contributing its weight to the resistance.|","|Current Status: You are maintaining your position against the basal Existential Radiation of an Ordovician Paleozoic being. This alone is a feat that no Bounded or Primordial Architect across recorded history has accomplished without specialized intervention.|","|Engagement Probability Assessment:|","|The possibility of continuing to rise to confront the enemy above, even with all tools currently available to you, sits at less than 0.01%. The probability of victory in direct engagement sits below measurable thresholds. The gap between your current configuration and a Stage One Paleozoic being is currently too vast.|","...!","Oh!","Shockingly, beside him, THE Creature had erupted with terrifying multicolored flames as his figure rose as well, and his posture looked even more stable than Noah’s, with his body lifting with a fluidity that suggested the radiation was not pressing him the way it was pressing Noah, or that his means of resisting the radiation operated on a weaving that did not require the kind of effortful buzzing Noah’s every muscle was currently producing.","Both of them now looked up toward THE Gilded One who had settled into his full position above the mountain.","Below them at the base of the mountain, Anaximander had fallen onto his hands and knees with sweat beading across his scholarly face as he visibly struggled simply to remain conscious against the radiation pressing down on him, while Emotive trembled beside him with her hair cycling through desperate flickering colors, her body being forced down by the radiation but her legs refusing to fully yield, her posture locked in the quarter-crouch of a being who was losing the fight to remain upright but was committed to losing it slowly rather than quickly!","Noah looked up at the Gilded One and saw him fully for the first time.","THE False Golden Idol was humanoid in the grander mention of humanoid, the proportions of his frame built along the cosmological lines of an old war-statue that had been refined beyond any statue’s limitations into living expression.","He stood impossibly tall in the air above the mountain, though tall was the wrong word because his true size seemed to layer backward into weavings that Noah’s perception could not fully resolve, depth beyond depth, the being’s presence unfolding into recessions that kept extending the longer one looked.","His skin was the pure radiant gold of refined Observable Force compressed into flesh, unblemished and luminous, a living alloy of gilded metal and living tissue that carried no hint of the wear that lesser bodies accumulated, and his hair fell long and pale gold down his back, threaded with strands of deeper bronze that caught the ambient light of his own radiation.","His robes were the intricate layered golds of a Superbius house at Paleozoic standing, embroidered with patterns that shifted subtly as he floated, sigils of Pride woven across the fabric in configurations that proclaimed his sovereignty to anyone who had the literacy to read them. His face held the hard impassive beauty of a being engineered for cosmological standing, every line sculpted and every proportion precise, with every feature calibrated to communicate that this was what superiority looked like when superiority had been given a face.","And his eyes.","His eyes were pure unbroken white, the white of polished bone, and within the white of each eye, a sword floated in place of a pupil, the swords drawn in fine detail with their blades pointing downward and their hilts elegant and their presence steady. As his gaze tracked across the mountain and settled on THE Creature and then on Noah beside him, the swords within his eyes rotated slightly, tracking the gaze with the independent articulation of separate instruments.","He looked down at both of them coldly.","His voice came out unfathomably calm, lazy, and prideful.","\" We remember you.\"","The voice drifted down with the patient register of a being who was using a tiny fraction of the breath his lungs could have committed to speaking.","\" Someone as insignificant as you, and we had almost forgotten. Eons ago, some small region of THE Wyld, some small Primordial Architect and his small woman who refused an offer from a Gilded One. The audacity was briefly amusing. The consequence was instructive. We moved on.\"","He tilted his head slightly.","\" And you did all this for something so minor? You challenged a Gilded One because you could not let go of her? Ah. She was a beauty, small frame-wise, but beautiful in the proportions of her kind. She tasted good, actually, and both of us know how she tasted, because you had her many times during your small life together while I had her the last time. How did that make you feel? Did you become obsessed with that moment, as I intended you to? Was the obsession so strong that it has brought you here to stand before me with the belief that you can do anything meaningful?\"","His mouth curved into a small cold smile.","\"I spared you countless eons ago specifically so that you would live with the shame, the shame of not being able to protect someone who believed in you to protect her. It was a gift in its own way, because most beings who challenged us did not receive the courtesy of continued existence, and you received it because I wanted to observe what shame at your classification would produce over long timescales. You have produced this. A mountain of corpses, a slow climb, a summons that retrieves me from THE Braneworld to acknowledge what you have done...\"","The swords in his eyes rotated slightly toward Noah and then back.","\" While I had her pinned down, she tried to turn her head several times to make sure you did not see, and she tried to collapse her own existence many times on her own initiative, but I stopped her. I held her existence open so that she could not exit the experience voluntarily. Oh, the shame and pain she felt, the agony, the specific agony of a being who understood that her own ending had been removed as an option. It was all tasty, really quite tasty, because I do not often linger on encounters with lesser beings of your classification, but hers lingered. Credit where credit is due.\"","He spread his arms slightly.","\" But for us to be here right now, for such an insignificant thing, come on. I am a Superbius. Superbius rule the Observable and the Unobservable, all others are below us, much less a Bounded Lifeform like you. You should have thanked me for what I did to her. You should be celebrating what I gave you, the clarity of understanding your place across the remaining eons of your small existence. You should be happy. You should even be accomplished, in the small way a being at your classification can be accomplished, that you managed to call me here now across the barrier that separates my world from yours. But for what? You cannot do anything. You have guaranteed nothing except your own death, and even that, ah, I will not feel much from it. It will be briefly satisfying in the way that squashing a particularly loud insect is briefly satisfying. Then I will return to more important matters.\"","He settled back slightly in the air.","\" Well. Let us hear what you have to say before the matter concludes. I permit you... to speak.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5157,"title":"Chapter 5157: Chapter 5156: For Me, For Her I","paragraphs":["The words were not even directed at him, but Noah felt a profound sense of revulsion rise through his existence as he listened to this being speak.","Every word the Idol had said was horrid, and every word the Idol had said had been said with the casual pleasure of a being who took genuine satisfaction from remembering the suffering he had caused, a being who drew a small refined joy from cataloguing the specific horrors of what he had done to a woman who had wanted to escape him so badly that she had tried to collapse her own existence multiple times to prevent the continuation of the encounter.","And he truly, existentially believed everything he said.","The belief was the worst part of all of it, because the Idol was not performing cruelty and he was not posturing for an audience, he was describing his reality with the clarity of a being who genuinely considered himself so far above the Primordial Architects beneath him that what he had done to THE Soul was not a cruelty requiring justification but a casual exercise of authority that no one in the world should ever have expected him to refrain from.","Noah felt rage rising within him from these words alone, and he could imagine how THE Creature felt, and he could feel it because shockingly, at this moment, THE Creature actually broke whatever shackles still kept Noah anchored to his position and began to float freely upward into the air above the mountain, his multicolored flames blazing higher around him as he rose.","The image was glorious against the entirely gold skies and the visage of a Gilded One, a single small figure wreathed in multicolored flames lifting upward into a domain that had been claimed by a being orders of magnitude above him, the gold of the sky pressing in from every direction, the figure refusing to be pressed back down, rising into the Idol’s painted dominion as if the painting had not been noticed or, more accurately, as if the painting had been noticed and found insufficient reason to stop.","THE Creature’s voice came out calm, but within the calm anyone listening could feel the blinding rage that had been refined across eons.","\" Yes. I did not have the power to protect her back then.\"","His flames flickered steadily.","\"I failed her. I failed her then, and I have carried the failing across every moment of my climbing since. But I will not fail her now. Bounded Lifeforms, Gilded Lifeforms, Primeval Lifeforms, there are always those considered higher than others across the arrangements of existence, and the higher ones have always operated on the assumption that the lower ones should accept the arrangement with the gratitude due to their betters.\"","\"I have never accepted the arrangement, I have never been grateful, I have only been climbing, and I have only been climbing so that I could stand where I currently stand and make a single small statement that I believe existence has been needing to hear for a very long time.\"","His flames steadied into their obsidian undertone.","\"I want to show that false idols can very much bleed.\"","He lifted his gaze to the Idol directly.","\" Gerousia Aurelius Maximus of the Superbius House of the Crimson Chalice, Third Seat of the Upper Sanctum, Voice of the Radiant Quorum, Keeper of the Chalice that Does Not Empty.\"","He paused.","\" Are you ready to repent?\"","As he spoke, THE Creature raised his hand.","His flames surged upward along his arm in braided currents, the multicolored golden fires along his body gathering and flowing into his raised palm, pulled together into a condensing mass that began to shape itself into something. His Civilization of Existence, one of the Four Aspects of THE Oldest Paradox, flowed up alongside the flames and braided with them, contributing the crystalline weight of his most fundamental Cause to the forming shape.","A sword took form.","It was incandescent and crystalline, multicolored across its length with the full spectrum of THE Creature’s refined flames running through the blade like living layers of stained glass fused into a single cutting edge, and it settled into his grip with the quiet weight of a weapon that had been waiting within him since long before this afternoon.","Noah gazed at all of this unfold with an attention that refused to blink, because even he had to ask himself the question.","The entity above felt utterly insurmountable, and the gap between a Second Scale being and a Paleozoic being, even on THE Creature’s unconventional foundation, was so vast that the word gap was the wrong word, because a gap implied a space that could be crossed with sufficient effort, and what sat between THE Creature and Gerousia Aurelius Maximus was not a gap but a category difference that no amount of effort alone should have been able to bridge.","Just how could THE Creature do anything against them?","The Gilded One smiled lightly.","\" How does an ant like you come to know my name?\"","His voice carried the amused condescension.","THE Creature’s reply came brutal and immediate.","\" The names of excrements are easy to find. One simply looks at the bottom of a chamber pot long enough, and the labels reveal themselves. Yours have been particularly easy to read, because your house leaves trails of shit wherever it drags itself.\"","...!","The swords in the Gilded One’s eyes snapped into tight vertical alignment, and his expression shifted into something cold.","\" Ye vile creature.\"","His voice dropped lower.","\"It seems I have given you too much freedom. You can stop speaking and moving now-\"","As THE Gilded One was saying this, Noah opened his eyes wide.","He had been paying close attention to THE Creature to see what this being could possibly do against something of this magnitude, and what he felt next froze his every thought in place, because all the surrounding Infinity began to seethe excitedly!","Infinity churned across the mountain and the sky and the entire upper reach of THE Wyld, every current of it responding to something that had just begun to bloom within THE Creature’s body, something Noah did not recognize, something that made Infinity itself react!","In the next instant, as if in slow motion, THE Creature disappeared.","Noah could not follow the motion, because even with his Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation stretching the instant into extended subjective time, the motion was too quick.","One moment THE Creature was lifting his sword, and the next moment THE Creature was in front of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus, his body floating at the Gilded One’s own altitude, the distance between them compressed to within the arm’s reach of THE Creature’s raised blade.","THE Creature’s multicolored flaming body looked unfathomably calm and serene, because the rage that had driven him across eons of climbing had not disappeared but had simply fallen into an abyssal stillness, the stillness of a fire burning at the bottom of a well that no wind could reach!","He swung the sword, and the swing was slow in Noah’s stretched perception, almost meditative, the kind of swing a master calligrapher makes when placing a single definitive stroke on a page that has been waiting for that stroke across an entire lifetime of preparation.","Noah observed every detail.","The sword’s edge carried, at the moment of swing, an obsidian light that dispersed all Pride and Infinity near it, and the Pride and Infinity did not push away from the sword but simply stopped being within the immediate vicinity of the blade, as if the sword had been dipped in a deeper substrate that took precedence over the current weavings of pride and Infinity of THE Gilded One!","The sword met the chest of the Gilded One, and it cut.","...!","The obsidian light carried it clean through the layered embroidered golds of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus’s robes, through the luminous living alloy of his skin, through whatever substrate lay beneath his skin at the Paleozoic power, and a long gash opened across his chest from his left shoulder to his right hip!","A river of crimson-gold blood erupted from the cut and painted the golden skies of THE Wyld with a crimson spatter that hung in the air like a signature written across a claimed canvas.","...!","BOOM!","Noah saw all of this with disbelief, because what was that power, and how could THE Creature do this!?","BOOM!","After the strike, instantly, the golden sky shattered.","Multicolored flames tinged with an obsidian light covered all of THE Wyld, rolling out from THE Creature’s position in a single vast wave that overwrote the golden dominion the Gerousia had painted across the sky, and where the gold had claimed the air minutes ago, now THE Creature’s flames claimed it, tinged with the deeper obsidian of whatever substrate had just expressed itself through his sword.","When Noah could observe again, he saw Gerousia Aurelius Maximus.","The Gilded One’s face had transformed into something Noah had not expected to ever see on a Paleozoic being, because what now sat across his features was shock, incredulous wide-pupiled shock, the swords in his white eyes quivering out of their tight alignment as his lips parted slightly and his hand rose to touch the cut across his chest.","His fingers came away stained with crimson-gold blood, and he stared at the blood on his fingers for a long suspended moment before his eyes snapped back to THE Creature with an expression that carried the specific horror of a being whose assumptions had just been violated!","Noah’s gaze stayed on THE Creature.","THE Creature was transforming, and his size grew larger and larger as Noah watched, his frame expanding from the standard proportions of a Primordial Architect into something grander, something that had been waiting inside him across his eons of climbing for the exact moment to be released.","His body trembled slightly as he grew, a tremor that suggested heavy strain, but he persevered through the strain the way he had persevered through every strain across his climb.","An obsidian tail bloomed behind him, long and thick and serpentine, wreathed with the same multicolored flames now tinged obsidian, and his body became grander and more muscular as the frame of a being who had shed the limitations of his previous classification settled into its new proportions. His face and body became filled with archaic tattoos, patterns written in obsidian ink across his skin, sigils and scripts that Noah could not read but that felt older than any language currently spoken across the Observable.","An obsidian flame shaped like a crown formed above his head, burning slowly, a single solid ring of obsidian fire resting in the air above his brow.","And then the power he radiated disappeared completely.","As if he no longer existed, or as if his power level was not important to the current arrangement of reality, or as if it was now so deeply veiled that it could not be sensed by any of the frameworks Noah had access to.","Noah’s perception, which had been straining to track THE Creature’s output at the Paleozoic-equivalent intensity of the strike, now registered nothing at all, an empty space where a being should have been.","His eyes became clear for the first time, and they looked mundane, just ordinary human eyes with dark obsidian pupils that held the steady weight of a being who had shed every layer of labeling across his climb and who now stood in front of his enemy with nothing between them but the quiet gaze of someone who had arrived at the place he had spent eons traveling to.","Those eyes looked toward the Gilded One coldly.","At this time, Gerousia Aurelius Maximus moved back.","He moved back with utter shock, and his luminous body, which had been floating with the authority of a being who owned the space he occupied, actually recoiled a measurable distance through the air as his hand stayed pressed against the cut on his chest and the swords in his eyes collapsed into narrow trembling lines.","He bellowed out.","\" THE Source! THE Source! How do you... have THE Primordial Source??!!\"","BOOM!","...!","Noah’s entire existence buzzed!"]},{"number":5158,"title":"Chapter 5158: Chapter 5157: For Me, For Her II","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Source.","These were the terrifying words to come out of the mouth of the Gerousia, and Noah found his existence buzzing as they landed.","THE Creature. THE Primordial Source.","The two names should not settle together in his mind. None of what he knew...none of it had prepared him for the possibility that this being had actually touched the deepest well of power across Observable Existence, the well that THE Gilded Ones themselves had been pursuing across eons without ever quite closing the distance to it. THE Primordial Source!","THE Creature had it!","THE Creature had it!!!","Was he...a Relictus or connected to them?","Noah observed the figure of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus show visible fear at the reality of what had just stood up in front of him, because the fear was not something a Paleozoic being of his standing would have permitted himself to express under ordinary circumstances.","His recoil through the air, his parted lips, the trembling swords in his white eyes, the luminous hand pressed against the bleeding cut across his chest, all of these composed a picture of genuine alarm that Noah suspected had not appeared on Gerousia Aurelius Maximus’s face in a very long time.","But moments later, his Pride shone through the fear.","His posture straightened by visible degrees as his engineered Superbius foundation reasserted itself against the shock, because even in the face of a being holding THE Primordial Source, a Gerousia of the House of the Crimson Chalice could not remain afraid for long without betraying every principle of the Ego that defined him.","His sharp gaze returned to THE Creature’s transformed figure, and his voice came out once more, though it carried a new edge that the earlier casual laziness had not contained.","\" Something as weak as you must have just gained this.\"","His fingers flexed against his chest wound, the crimson-gold blood smearing across his palm.","\"A recent touch, barely integrated, still untested across any real engagement. I will carve you out in this battle before you have the chance to grow into what that Source might eventually make of you. Your confidence is premature. Your-\"","THE Creature raised his blade.","The motion was small, almost casual, a single lifting of the multicolored sword toward the cut already opened across the Gilded One’s chest. And shockingly, the Gerousia’s voice actually cut off.","His mouth remained open around the unspoken next syllable, but no sound emerged from it, and the silence that followed was the silence of a presence being denied the continuation of his own speech. His lips moved. His throat worked. Nothing came out!","THE Creature spoke into the new silence.","\" There will not be a battle.\"","His voice came calm.","\" The moment I cut you, the battle was over. Having been touched by THE Source, I can now cut you off, and Ordovician Paleozoic does not matter in the face of that cutting, and Superbius does not matter, and the House of the Crimson Chalice does not matter. Only THE Source matters. The Source is the well from which all other authorities drink...Only THE Source matters...only THE Source...\"","His obsidian-crowned head tilted slightly.","\"I do this for myself. I do it for her. I do it for the countless many who have suffered under your hands and the hands of those who share your engineered Pride. I do this for the Gilded Ones I will scorch out of existence across the climb that remains in front of me, for the houses whose Civilizations I will crumble into dust, for every trembling lesser being who ever knelt before a Gilded One because the Scales told them they had to kneel. I do this until no lifeform across any reach of Observable Existence can look at another lifeform and believe they are grander by virtue of engineered superiority alone.\"","...!","After these words, Noah observed THE Creature move his left hand as if issuing a silent command.","From the chest wound of the Gerousia, obsidian light bloomed outward and covered everything in the immediate vicinity of the Gilded One’s body, the light not emanating from the wound so much as the wound functioning as a gate that something had just opened.","The Gerousia became frozen in shock, his mouth still not opening, his limbs becoming raised and splayed outward into a cross-shaped configuration that no gesture of his own had chosen, his luminous body held in place by whatever authority THE Creature had just exerted through the opening of the cut.","THE Creature floated over to him calmly.","And then he began the work.","He raised his multicolored sword and began to use it to carve out a Gilded One.","The scene was shockingly similar to what Noah had watched THE Creature do to the Primordial Architects scattered across the mountain’s tiers, and Noah realized in the slow weight of observing it that THE Creature had been rehearsing this exact procedure across every body he had processed.","The methodology was identical. The cuts followed the same structural seams. The extraction of organs proceeded along the same patient sequence. The body being carved was Paleozoic rather than Proterozoic, but the carving itself operated by the same logic, because THE Creature had been practicing on bodies of other classification in order to arrive at this body with the hands of a master who had already completed his apprenticeship.","As if to show...they were all equal.","The golden glistening organs of a Gilded One emerged one by one as THE Creature extracted them.","The Heart of Civilization of a Paleozoic being was different from the Proterozoic version, but a heart regardless. Where Philemon’s Heart had been a dense crystalline structure, the Gerousia’s was a cathedral-like organ of living gold, layered with chambers and sub-chambers that opened and closed as THE Creature’s blade cut it free from its moorings. It pulsed once in THE Creature’s hand before it was set aside, floating in the air beside the Gerousia’s restrained body.","The lungs came next. They were twin structures of luminous gold membrane that had been processing the ambient authorities of the Braneworld across eons of their owner’s life, and they exhaled a final radiant breath as THE Creature cut their connections to the Gerousia’s chest cavity.","Unknown organs emerged in pieces because they had been integrated too deeply to remove intact. THE Creature extracted fragments one by one, each fragment carrying a different axiom of the Gerousia’s Civilization, each axiom sputtering and fading as its host organ was removed from the body that had sustained it.","Then came the skin.","THE Creature began to flay the Gilded One alive.","The carving was patient. The carving was thorough!","THE Creature worked in the methodical rhythm of a being who had been imagining this exact procedure across eons of preparation, and the imagining had accumulated such refined detail that the actual execution looked almost meditative, the movements of his blade tracing the seams of the Gerousia’s musculature with the economy of a master who wasted no stroke.","It was...meditative.","Noah observed in detail, and as he observed, he caught it.","Small tears dropped from THE Creature’s multicolored flaming face. They fell from the outer corners of his obsidian-pupiled eyes and traveled a fraction of an inch through the air before evaporating a nanosecond later against the residual heat of his flames, and others watching from below would not have been able to see them at all, would have missed the signal entirely, would have registered only the terrible procedure and not the grief still running beneath the methodology.","Noah saw them.","THE Creature continued working, and as he worked, his voice came out low, addressed to the frozen and carved body of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus.","\" This was what you did to her eons ago when you were done with her.\"","His blade made another cut.","\" You carved her. You opened her weavings and took what pieces of her you wanted and discarded what pieces you did not. You did it slowly, because you had time, because nothing in your classification had ever taught you that time was a resource you should spend carefully on the suffering of those beneath you. Today, you get a taste of your own medicine. Today you find out what it feels like.\"","His voice carried a quiet tremor beneath the calm, the tremor of a being who had waited for this exact moment across more time than most beings could conceive of.","\"I do not hate you, Aurelius. I passed through hate a long time ago. What I carry for you now is the steady cold weight of balance. The scales have been tilted wrong for eons, and someone has to tilt them back, and the tilting is going to feel a lot like what you are currently experiencing, and that is the only right shape for it to feel.\"","He kept working.","\" Revenge and vengeance are sometimes needed to balance the scales.\"","His blade worked with patience.","\" Not always, because not every injury can be balanced, and not every balancing produces a better world than the unbalanced one preceding it. But sometimes the balance is needed, and the need is not vulgar but necessary. An eye for an eye. A life for a life. These formulas were not invented by small beings out of spite. They were articulated across long histories by beings who had observed that some injuries continue to poison existence until they are answered, and the answering, however terrible, concludes the poison in ways that merciful non-action cannot.\"","He extracted a long ribbon of the Gerousia’s spinal musculature.","\" All beings are equal in one specific way, and the Gilded have spent eons denying this equality because denying it was the foundation of their hierarchical authority. But the equality holds regardless of denial. A life is a life. The life of a lesser being and the life of a Gerousia carry the same foundational weight when stripped of their engineered amplifications and measured by what they are in themselves. Equal. Always equal. And when one life takes another without cause, the balance must eventually be restored, and vengeance is the blade that restores it.\"","His gaze lifted briefly toward the golden skies his flames had overwritten.","\" Today is a day for balancing.\"","BOOM!","Noah watched it all with a sense of somberness settling through his existence, and he saw crimson-gold blood of a Gilded One float in the skies as THE Creature continued the carving. The blood did not fall.","It drifted in slow suspended patterns through the air above the mountain, catching the multicolored obsidian-tinged light of THE Creature’s flames, each droplet glistening with the final residue of a being whose standing had been stripped away layer by layer as his body was processed.","\" Bounded can die, and Gilded can die.\"","HUUM!","Noah witnessed THE Creature carve the being entirely.","And at the end of the procedure, THE Creature reached into what remained of the Gerousia’s body and ripped out the spine. The spine emerged intact, a long articulated column of golden vertebrae threaded with luminous filaments that had once carried the Gerousia’s nervous authority across the length of his frame. THE Creature held it up briefly in the air before setting it aside with the other extracted organs.","All the carved organs and bones floating in the skies began to disappear one by one.","And as each component disappeared, the brilliant life of a Gilded One began to fade, the residual authority that had made Gerousia Aurelius Maximus a Paleozoic being diminishing by measurable degrees with each erased organ, his existence thinning toward a terminus.","As this happened, Noah heard the voice of THE Creature within his mind.","The voice came calm and quiet.","’I am sorry for what is coming.’","’I truly am. I did everything I could not to implicate you further by not aiding you in anything as much as possible. Every choice I made calibrated to keep our involvements separate in the eyes of the existential record, so that when this moment arrived, the consequences would land on me and me alone.’","’But the consequences will not land cleanly.’","’I will draw away their rage. I will leave behind a parting gift for you. But I am sorry, because choices have consequences, and I made mine knowing what those consequences might look like when they arrived. I will bear all of them that come for me. But the nature of Gilded men and Gilded women is spiteful and unpredictable at their highest. Some of their rage may flow to you all regardless of how carefully I tried to wall the blame off. I cannot guarantee your isolation from what follows.\"","’I...am sorry for what is coming.’","BOOM!","Noah’s gaze became heavy as the transmission settled into his consciousness, because he had known the moment he sat down beside THE Creature that if this being was capable of overcoming the impossible, the overcoming would carry consequences that would propagate outward across existence in ways nobody at the mountain could fully predict.","He had understood the weight of the witnessing when he had chosen to stay. He had said as much, in his monologue about pivotal choices, not that ago.","THE Creature had just carved out a Gilded One in Observable Existence.","A Gerousia of the Superbius House of the Crimson Chalice. Third Seat of the Upper Sanctum. Voice of the Radiant Quorum. Keeper of the Chalice that Does Not Empty.","This was a choice.","And it was a choice that would likely have tremendous consequences.","And just as Noah thought of this.","OOOOOM!","Everything began to shake.","The mountain trembled beneath his feet, and the balcony he was still standing above shuddered with a deeper instability than the one THE Creature’s assault had produced, and the skies above him, the skies that had been painted multicolored-obsidian by THE Creature’s overwriting wave, began to tremble and crack.","Fine fractures began to appear across the upper reaches of the sky, hairline splits that spread outward from multiple points simultaneously, and through those splits something else pressed against the fabric of the Observable from somewhere above it!","Oh.","Oh!"]},{"number":5159,"title":"Chapter 5159: Chapter 5158: Golden Wrath! I","paragraphs":["From above, figures began to appear across the already shattered gold of the sky that THE Creature had overwritten moments earlier.","Noah observed them emerge with the same clinical attention he had been paying to every detail of the battle, watching as six Superbius Gilded Ones manifested in the air above THE Gilded White Mountain at varying altitudes and distances!","Each of them carried the same refined gold luminescence of Paleozoic-tier Superbius engineering, each of them was robed in the layered ceremonial colors of their respective houses, and each of them radiated basal Existential Radiation at the steady passive intensity that had pressed Noah down to the cracked balcony when the Gerousia had first arrived.","And then, after them, a seventh figure descended!","She arrived with even less announcement than the six who had come before her, simply resolving into visibility at the center of their arrangement as if she had always been there and had merely been waiting to be perceived, and Noah registered her presence with an immediate sharpening of his attention because the radiation pouring off her was of a different register than the six Gilded Ones flanking her.","Her Existential Radiation did not announce itself with the brash golden luminescence of the Superbius. Her radiation was quieter, denser, older, a pressure that settled rather than pressed, and the settling of it felt more absolute than the pressing of Aurelius Maximus had been.","She was a woman of terrifying beauty.","Her form was tall and slender with the long refined lines of a being engineered for presence across very large chambers of influence, her skin the pale pearlescent gold of a Gilded Lifeform, her hair a flowing river of molten silver-gold that fell past her waist in patterns of arrested motion that did not quite obey the ordinary rules of falling.","Her eyes were a deep amber-gold that held no swords in their pupils the way Aurelius Maximus’s had, but her eyes instead held something that looked like a slowly rotating mandala of interlocking geometric shapes, each shape moving at its own independent rate against the others.","Another brilliant light bloomed near her!","Beside her, floating close at her right shoulder, was a massive muscular Gilded One around whose body crimson red light surged in steady aggressive currents that never quite settled into stillness.","His frame was built along the proportions of an ancient warrior rebuilt at Paleozoic scale, his chest broad and armored in red-gold plate that seemed to have been forged from his own refined Wrath rather than worked from external materials. His eyes were pure unbroken red, the red of arterial blood held at the moment before it spilled!","Noah burned with his newly amplified Superbius Pride as he focused his Infinity upward to extract whatever details Infinity could offer him about the arrivals, and Ruination obliged quickly.","|Entities Detected: Six Superbius Gilded Ones.|","|Classification: THE Paleozoic Scale - Ordovician Tier.|","|All six are Gerousia-ranked or below.|","|Entity Detected: Sororis Prima Elzyana.|","|Classification: THE Paleozoic Scale - Ordovician Tier?|","| Affiliation: THE Magna Sorora .|","|Entity Detected: Custos of Sororis Prima Elzyana.|","|Name: Ferocis Valerius Krael of the Ira House of the Crimson Mantle.|","|Classification: THE Paleozoic Scale - Ordovician Tier.|","|Engineered Ego: Amplified Ira (Wrath).|","|He is likely bonded as Custos to Sororis Prima Elzyana.|","Noah absorbed the notifications with the cold calm of a someone who had just received confirmation of exactly how much worse things were about to become!","But the confirmation did not rattle him because confirmation was simply information and information was always preferable to its absence regardless of what the information contained!","Sororis Prima Elzyana took control of the situation without pausing to consult any of the Gilded Ones flanking her, her amber-gold eyes tracking across the scene below, and when her gaze finally settled on THE Creature’s floating figure, she spoke for the first time.","\" A Young Relictus has appeared in these foul lands and killed a Gilded One.\"","Her voice rolled outward across the shattered sky.","\" A Superbius Gilded One has been killed. Make sure this vile thing...does not escape.\"","HUUM!","THE Creature rose calmly from his position beside what remained of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus’s processed body, and as he rose he did not turn to look at Noah, nor did he look at Anaximander still kneeling on the pale stone of the mountain’s base, nor did he look at Emotive trembling beside the tall scholar.","He simply held his multicolored crystalline blade in his right hand, closed his dark obsidian-pupiled eyes for a single measured moment as if offering a silent goodbye to everything he would not be able to speak aloud in the time remaining, and then a roar erupted from him that carried no words but only the raw voiceless declaration of a being committing himself fully to whatever came next.","The obsidian light of THE Primordial Source erupted upward and outward from his transformed body, flowing along the length of his blade in braided currents of deep darkness that dispersed the ambient Observable Force and Infinity around him into pockets of temporary nonexistence, and then the light shot out into the distance with THE Creature carried along its trajectory, his figure vanishing from the sky above THE Gilded White Mountain at a speed that Noah’s perception could only register as a receding smear of obsidian-tinged brilliance against the ruined sky!","Sororis Prima Elzyana watched the departure without visible reaction, and Noah observed the six Gerousia-ranked Gilded Ones around her give chase immediately, their bodies surging upward and outward.","They blurred across the sky in the direction THE Creature had taken and were gone within moments, leaving behind only the residual trails of their golden Existential Radiation lingering in the air where their bodies had been.","Sororis Prima Elzyana nodded once to her Custos.","Ferocis Valerius Krael launched himself into the sky without a word, his massive armored frame tearing upward with the crimson aggression of his amplified Ira surging around him in intensified currents!","The skies emptied of the response party, and only Sororis Prima Elzyana remained floating above the mountain, her amber-gold eyes holding their slowly rotating mandalas of nested geometry as she turned her attention to the carved remnants of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus still suspended in the shattered air.","Noah observed her go to the processed remains of the Gerousia with a slow drifting grace.","And...","Her expression actually...softened?","Her face, which had held the cold imperious composure of a Sororis Prima for every second since her arrival, softened into an expression of genuine heartbreak as she drifted close to what remained of Aurelius Maximus’s floating carved frame, her amber-gold eyes dimming slightly as she took in the thoroughness of the carving and the specific patterns of the flaying that THE Creature had executed!","She reached out with a pale pearlescent hand and gathered the remnant flayed skin of the Gerousia into her palms with the tender care of a being handling something precious, and then she closed her eyes and held the skin against her chest for a long moment of silence that Noah could feel pressing against the substrate of THE Wyld itself.","Her voice came quiet and private when she finally spoke.","\"No Gilded One should ever die is such lands, nor should you have been alone. I...will bring you justice, Aurelius. I will bring you justice, and I will scorch the foundations of whatever bred the Relictus that took you from us, and I will make certain that no such creature ever rises again within reach of the Sororis!\"","She kissed the flayed skin once with a kind of intimate grief!"]},{"number":5160,"title":"Chapter 5160: Chapter 5159: Golden Wrath! II","paragraphs":["What justice?! For someone like Aurelius Maximus?!","What justice for the being who had forced himself on a Primordial Architect woman while holding her consciousness open so that she could not escape the encounter by ending herself, who had killed her afterward and taken what remained as a souvenir, who had spared THE Creature specifically so that he could live with the shame of having failed to protect her across the remainder of his eons?","Hah. What fucking justice? What a word for the being Sororis Prima Elzyana was currently mourning with such evident tenderness.","What a configuration of values had produced a Sisterhood in which the mourning of such a being could occur with such unguarded sincerity!","Right after kissing the remnant skin, Sororis Prima Elzyana waved her hands coldly, and in the next moment, as if time itself was being rewound across the region above the mountain, illusory figures of THE Creature and Aurelius Maximus began to play out the recent past in reverse.","...!","Noah watched the reversing events with his eyes burning with defiance and his body already preparing for whatever came next, because the reversal was a playback mechanism that Sororis Prima Elzyana was clearly using to reconstruct what had occurred before her arrival.","The reversing figures played out across the sky above the mountain, moving backward through the strike that had carved Aurelius’s chest, backward through THE Creature’s transformation into his revealed form, backward through the summoning and the arrival, and as the playback continued into the earlier portions of the day, Noah’s attention sharpened on what he was watching.","The playback was not showing the truth.","Before Aurelius Maximus had arrived in the sky above the mountain, the playback showed Philemon Aristos and the other Primordial Architects of the gathering clique standing across the tiers of the ruined temples, intact and breathing, their bodies whole and their foundations undamaged.","The illusory figures of Noah and Emotive and Anaximander appeared in the playback as well, but they appeared as kneeling figures on the stone beside the Primordial Architects, paying the expected reverence to a Gerousia who had descended to receive it, their postures and expressions carefully rendered in the manner of Bounded Lifeforms who had been visiting the mountain to confer with the Gerousia on some unspecified matter.","Then the playback showed THE Creature appearing from nowhere, attacking without provocation, killing Philemon Aristos and the other Primordial Architects in rapid succession before turning on Aurelius Maximus himself, and in the reconstruction Noah’s illusory figure along with Emotive and Anaximander appeared to have survived only by the grace of THE Creature’s attention being entirely consumed by the greater targets before him.","Noah marveled quietly at what he was watching.","THE Creature had managed even this, had reached back into the substrate of what had occurred with THE Primordial Source and rewritten the history visible to outside reconstruction, and the rewriting had been calibrated specifically to remove Noah and Emotive and Anaximander from implication in the killing of the Gerousia!","The drawing away of rage that THE Creature had mentioned.","The devotion of the effort was striking, because THE Creature had been carving Aurelius Maximus alive at the same time he had been writing this alibi into existence.","But....","Sororis Prima Elzyana shook her head coldly as the playback reached its earliest reconstructed moments and then dissolved back into the ambient existence, and she finally looked down at Noah and Emotive and Anaximander and the remnant corpses scattered across the almost-flattened mountain below with a gaze that had shifted from grief back into the cold imperious composure of her rank.","Her expression was not exactly dismissive, because dismissiveness would have required her to consider the beings below her significant enough to actively dismiss.","What crossed her features was closer to clinical evaluation, the look of a being assessing a problem that did not particularly engage her interest but that nonetheless required resolution.","She spoke.","\"In Lands of the Bounded, for a Relictus to appear amongst the Bounded means that others like him... could exist here.\"","Her amber-gold eyes swept across the mountain and the surrounding regions of THE Wyld.","\" The threat this represents to the Gilded Ones is too substantial to leave undressed. Observable Existence and the Bounded Lifeforms within it...must all be accounted for, and the accounting must be thorough enough to prevent any further Relictus from emerging from the conditions that produced this one.\"","Her voice held no cruelty and no satisfaction, only the steady explanatory cadence of a being describing an administrative necessity!","\" Any traces of Civilizations that produced a Relictus environment need to be further bound and severed. This is not a punishment. It is a...prophylactic measure.\"","HUUM!","She paused briefly as her mandala-eyes tracked across the figures below her.","\"It is efficient. It is regrettable, in its small way. It is also, I am sorry to say, what the circumstances now require.\"","Noah gazed up at her as her words settled into the air, and his eyes burned with a defiance that he made no attempt to conceal beneath any more pragmatic expression.","He looked up with defiance because he did not fear.","He knew what the result may be. He knew. But his Infinity, his Quintessence, his very being...he truly could not allow himself to simply look down and bend the knee right now.","As much of a weakness and illogical this sounded, he truly could not do it!","And...","Sororis Prima Elzyana saw him.","His defiance registered in her mandala-eyes as a small interesting observation, and she descended slightly through the air toward him with the same drifting grace she had used to approach Aurelius Maximus’s remains, her tall slender figure lowering by small increments until she floated at a distance that permitted proper address.","She regarded him the way a being regarded an insect that had unexpectedly produced an identifiable expression, with neither hostility nor curiosity but with a flat detached interest in the anomaly for its own sake.","Her beauty was undeniable at this closer range.","When she spoke, her voice came out conversational, almost gentle, with the patient indulgence of a being willing to hear out a small objection before proceeding with the administrative necessity.","\"O Bounded Lifeform who owes their life to the late Gerousia Aurelius.\"","Her amber-gold eyes held his without either warmth or enmity.","\" You... do not agree?\"","...!","At such a question, Noah kept his gaze locked to hers and spoke calmly, the calmness of his delivery matching the calmness of hers as if the two of them were peers discussing a procedural matter!","As THE Creature had said. All of them...were equal.","So!","\"I... do not agree.\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":5161,"title":"Chapter 5161: Chapter 5160: Golden Wrath! III","paragraphs":["Noah knew the smarter and more logical thing to do was to simply bend his head down and not say or do a single thing.","THE Creature had already set everything up with a fabricated history, had carved an entire alternative sequence of events into the readable weavings of what had occurred, had positioned Noah and Emotive and Anaximander as incidental survivors who had only escaped THE Relictus’s assault because the greater targets had consumed THE Relictus’s attention.","If any being watching from outside had been privy to Noah’s internal debate at this moment, they might have scratched their heads and wondered why he was making such an illogical choice when the alibi was already in place and the only required action was silent compliance. Bow the head. Let the Sororis Prima proceed. Accept whatever adjustments she intended to make to the broader Observable Existence and address the consequences later, once her attention had moved elsewhere and his power had grown significantly could address those consequences properly.","It was the correct play. It was the move any outside observer with a functioning grasp of logic would have recommended!","But truly, the moment he bowed his head would feel like a moment where fractures bloomed in his Civilization.","He knew the shape of those fractures because he had carried similar fractures in him across other moments of his existence when circumstances had demanded a capitulation his core had refused to offer.","It was like mundane normal humans crossing paths with other humans who happened to be richer or who held positions of power, and choosing not to meet their eyes or speak up, choosing to shrink slightly so that the passage through the encounter would produce the least friction possible.","The choice got them in less trouble in the moment. The encounter passed and the day continued. But they would remember that shrinking afterward, would carry the memory of having abandoned their posture for the sake of convenience, and across the years the accumulation of such small capitulations produced beings who could no longer recognize the versions of themselves that had existed before the capitulations had begun.","The fractures compounded quietly. The original shape of the person eroded along the seams of every small unspoken yielding.","So yes. It was not the most logical thing to do. But he still dared to look at a Gilded One, at a Sororis Prima, and say no!","Thinking of all this reminded him of a particularly unpleasant memory of a man he had hated with every bone in his body across the full span of his earliest years of existence.","Thinking of all this reminded him of the only man he had ever bent his head down to, because truly, he had feared him.","Not respected, not honored, not admired, but feared in the specific way of a child facing a being whose capacity to hurt him exceeded any capacity he possessed to defend himself. It reminded him...of his father.","The memory flashed in his mind like something he could not suppress, and in the stretched instant of his Hadean Mind pulling this moment into extended perception, the memory unfurled with the crisp brutal clarity of a small human scene he had been carrying across more years than he cared to count.","---","He was twelve years old at the time, in that broken-down home in the living room with the stained carpet and the curtains that never properly closed.","His father had stood up from the couch where he had been lying most of the afternoon, his stained robe hanging open and his beer belly sticking out in a pale round hemisphere above the waistband of sweatpants that had not been washed in longer than the boy had been alive, holding a leather belt in one thick hand and a half-empty bottle of beer in the other.","The television behind him was playing something loud that nobody was watching. The light in the room was yellow and dim because one of the bulbs in the overhead fixture had been burned out.","His father had asked him coldly.","\"I sat and watched you little shit the whole day while your mother worked, and when I bring a woman friend over, you tell your mom about it? Didn’t I tell you to keep your mouth shut?\"","The twelve-year-old version of Noah had looked at his father with teary eyes that he had been trying very hard to keep from spilling over, because spilling over would have invited a different and worse kind of response from the man who had just stood up, and he had been defiant.","He had not wanted to see what his father had been doing with the woman friend who kept coming over when his mother went to work. He had not wanted to be told to stay quiet about it. He had not wanted to carry secrets that did not belong to him but that he was being forced to hold for the comfort of an adult who had never shown him a single moment of genuine comfort in return.","So when he had looked up at his father with that small defiant gaze.","The twelve-year-old version had met the eyes of the man who had fathered him, and those eyes had held nothing. Not anger or rage exactly.","Simply the flat contempt of a being who considered the small creature before him an inconvenience that needed to be addressed so that the afternoon could continue undisturbed.","His father had beaten him with that belt again and again.","The first strike had landed across his shoulder and sent him stumbling sideways into the coffee table. The second strike had caught him across the back of his legs as he tried to steady himself. The third strike had knocked him to the carpet entirely, and the subsequent strikes had landed while he was down, the leather biting into his back and his arms and the parts of his body he tried to curl into a protective ball around his chest.","His father had not shouted during the beating. His father had spoken steadily, the way a man speaks when he is delivering a lecture that he believes to be instructive rather than cruel.","\"When I talk to you, you look down and listen. You do not look at me like that. You do not look at me with that fucking face of yours like you think you have something to say about anything. I gave you your life. I can take it away. Do you understand? Do you fucking understand?\"","The twelve-year-old him had understood.","He had kept his head down after that,crying. The leather belt still landing across his back in measured intervals that had begun to space themselves out as his father’s arm grew tired.","He had not raised his head to meet his father’s gaze for the remainder of that afternoon, and he had not raised it for many afternoons that followed, because the pain of the beatings was real and the fear of the pain was realer still, and he had been twelve years old and his father had been a grown man twice his size and three times his weight, and there had been no framework available to the twelve-year-old in which raising his head would have produced any outcome other than more belt strikes landing across a body that was already bruised in patterns that would take weeks to fade.","He had feared what that useless man, that much bigger than him, could do to him.","He had hated that memory so, so much.","He hated the fact that it lived inside him at all. He hated that no amount of climbing across the years since had permitted him to fully evict the memory from the deeper rooms of his existence where memories of that kind took up permanent residence.","He hated that some part of him, some small twelve-year-old part, still carried the shape of having bowed his head, still remembered the exact texture of the carpet against his cheek, still remembered the way his own tears had tasted when they had pooled against his lips because he could not wipe them away without the wiping being seen as another form of defiance that would have earned additional strikes.","He hated that part of him.","And he had spent every year of his subsequent existence, both the years before Ruination and the unfathomable years since, building himself into a being whose shape could not be returned to that bowed posture by any external force regardless of how grand the external force became.","He was not going to bow his head now.","Not to his dead father. Not to Sororis Prima Elzyana. Not to any Gilded One or Superbius Sisterhood or Paleozoic classification that wanted him to look down. Whatever came as the consequence of refusing to bow, he would pay in whatever currencies existence demanded, or his own currencies!","Because the alternative was to become the twelve-year-old on the carpet again, and that twelve-year-old had already paid his portion of the yielding long ago, and no further portion was available from the being Noah had become in the years since.","\"...ah.\"","He shook his head slightly as if to physically erase the memory, and the stretched instant his Hadean Mind had pulled the reflection into collapsed back into the ordinary flow of time.","Before him, Sororis Prima Elzyana raised her brows calmly.","Her amber-gold eyes with their slowly rotating mandalas held him with the patient indulgence of a being who had not been inconvenienced by his momentary pause, and she spoke with the same gentle administrative weavings she had been using since she had descended toward him.","\" Am I interrupting you from your thoughts?\"","Noah shook his head and sighed, the sigh of a being who had just finished a brief internal excavation and was now ready to speak to the external situation once more.","\" No. I’m listening.\"","His voice came out steady and measured.","\"I was saying no. I do not agree that those of us here need to be further bounded and severed. We did nothing to deserve such treatment.\"","...!","Sororis Prima Elzyana looked at Noah calmly as if she had discovered a particularly bold insect, and Noah kept his gaze on her without breaking the contact, because breaking it at this point would have undone the entire interior argument he had just finished having with himself, and he had committed to the posture of looking up and he intended to maintain that posture through whatever response she issued.","In the next moment, she spoke.","Her voice came calm and cold.","\"It is very unique that you would have an opinion.\"","Her mandala-eyes rotated slightly in their slow internal rhythms.","\" And it is more unique still that you would think your opinion matters enough to voice it in response to a directive from a Sororis Prima. Do you understand how the arrangement of authority actually flows across our peoples? Even among the Gilded, the Superbius are the ones with the most say, because our Pride is the oldest amplified Ego and the one around which the broader Gilded hierarchy organized itself across the eons of our establishment. Even Gilded Ones of other amplified Egos follow Superbius direction when Superbius direction is given, because the structure of our authority makes following the only available option for those who wish to maintain their standing.\"","She tilted her head slightly as her gaze swept across him.","\" And Bounded Lifeforms do not have a say. Not in the ordinary sense. Not in any sense that the arrangement of our authority has ever been required to accommodate.\"","Her voice softened.","\" When a gardener decides that a section of soil requires treatment to prevent the further emergence of pests, the gardener does not consult the ants already living in that soil. The gardener does not pause to consider whether the ants might prefer a different configuration of treatment. The ants are not partners in the decision. The ants are part of the condition being addressed. When the treatment is applied, some of the ants will die, and some of the ants will be displaced, and some of the ants will survive and rebuild their colonies elsewhere in configurations the gardener did not specifically intend but that fall within acceptable parameters. The gardener does not feel cruelty toward the ants during this process, because the gardener does not feel anything toward the ants at all. The ants are simply part of the soil. The soil is what the gardener is attending to. The attending proceeds regardless of what the ants might think about it, because ants do not think in ways that gardeners are required to consult.\"","Her gaze settled on him with the clinical steadiness of someone who had used this analogy many times before.","\"Me saying what I said was not a matter of debate. It was not a proposition offered for your consideration. It was not something that a being of your classification is invited to think about and disagree against. It was an administrative assessment of the conditions surrounding a Relictus emergence, and the assessment will translate into actions regardless of the thoughts any ant in the affected soil might happen to form about it.\"","Her voice carried no cruelty in it!","\" And for your unruliness, I will begin with you.\"","She drifted slightly closer through the air, her tall slender form lowering until she floated at a height that permitted her to look down at him with the intimacy of an executioner preparing to conclude a minor affair before attending to the larger matters waiting beyond it.","\"I will bind you further. I will not sever your existence entirely, because you lived due to the late Gerousia Aurelius Maximus’s favor, and honoring his final disposition toward the Bounded around him is the courtesy his standing earned from our Sisterhood. But you will be bound further, Boy. You will feel the binding settle into every layer of your foundations. You will understand, when the binding is complete, exactly where the ants are permitted to crawl within the soil they have been given, and you will not voice disagreements of this kind again because the voicing itself will become a configuration your bound existence no longer permits.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5162,"title":"Chapter 5162: Chapter 5161: Golden Wrath! IV","paragraphs":["Sororis Prima Elzyana raised her pale pearlescent hands, and her body surged with a dense mixture of golden Observable Force and Infinity flowing outward from her skin in visible currents that bent the ambient air of THE Wyld toward her position as if the air itself was volunteering to contribute to the work she was about to do.","Between her raised palms, a construct began to form, blue-gold in its interwoven colors and pyramidal in its shape, its sides composed of small interlocking geometric facets that rotated slowly against each other in the same patient manner that the mandalas of her eyes rotated within their amber-gold borders, and the construct thickened and sharpened as she poured more of her authority into its formation until it floated between her palms as a dense weapon of bindings.","She pushed the construct downward toward Noah with a single small gesture!","Noah kept his defiant gaze locked on hers even as the construct descended as he committed to the posture of meeting her eyes and he intended to maintain that posture!","Faster than his current perception could properly track, faster than his Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation could stretch the instant to accommodate, the pyramidal construct shot down from her palms and embedded itself into the back of his right hand with the clean precision of a seal settling into wax, and the back of his hand began to shine with the same blue-gold brilliance that had composed the construct as its facets folded into his skin and began to propagate inward.","As the process of the binding began to spread through him, Sororis Prima Elzyana continued calmly.","\"It may help you, or perhaps merely amuse me, to explain what will be closed to you.\"","Her mandala-eyes drifted across him without warmth.","\"In the ordinary course of a Bounded Lifeform’s progression, the path from the Second Scale passes through certain milestones that any being with sufficient cultivation can theoretically approach. At the peak of the Ediacaran Tier of THE Proterozoic Scale, one forges what is called THE Civilizational Forge, a new organ dedicated to compressing their Civilization into a denser and more refined state than it held during earlier tiers. The Forge iterates across eons of cultivation. Each pass through it compresses the Civilization further. Each compression makes the wielding of that Civilization sharper, more precise, more able to deliver concentrated expressions of its core axioms through single gestures and single words.\"","She made a small gesture with her free hand that produced a pale illustrative image of a compressing organ in the air beside her, the image rotating slowly for Noah’s benefit.","\" Once THE Civilizational Forge reaches sufficient density, the being may attempt to enter what is called THE Transitional Cambrian stage, which sits between Second and Third Scale, and which requires the being to begin the conversion of their foundational matter from Proterozoic substrate into Paleozoic substrate at the cellular and sub-cellular levels across the entirety of their existence. Bounded Lifeforms such as yourself can reach Cambrian if they are exceptional enough, but they cannot cross fully into THE Third Scale, because the Bounded lattice cannot hold Paleozoic substrate without collapsing. Cambrian is your absolute ceiling in the ordinary course of things. Which, I should note, is an ambitious ceiling that almost none of you ever actually reach.\"","The illustrative image shifted into something resembling a ladder with a clearly marked upper boundary that the Bounded silhouettes on the lower rungs could never climb past.","\" THE Third Scale itself, THE Paleozoic Scale, is where beings like myself exist. At Paleozoic, one becomes a Weapon of Existence. The casual presence of a Paleozoic being radiates what is called Existential Radiation, a passive emission that twists the arrangement of existence around the radiating body simply by the body occupying the space it occupies. A Paleozoic being walks through a region, and the region is never the same again. Ambient Observable Force in the walked path shifts its arrangement for hours or days or centuries depending on the intensity of the walker. Lesser beings caught in the wake experience foundational strain. Civilizations encountered without the proper engineering may fold into the radiating being’s cosmological alignment, their axioms rewriting themselves around the grander presence.\"","Her voice took on a slightly lecturing quality as she continued!","\"A Paleozoic being at even my current tier, the Ordovician, can...ah, you wouldn’t even understand. At higher stages of Paleozoic, Silurian and Devonian, the capacities grow grander still. A basal primitive mind like yours...is not able to understand.\"","Her mandala-eyes rotated slightly as she seemed to savor the picture she was painting.","\"All that future you would have never reached. You are Bounded. Your ceiling is Cambrian at the absolute most generous accounting, and almost no Bounded across recorded history actually achieves that ceiling. I offer you this preview not because you will ever approach it but because it serves as a useful reference for understanding what I am about to close to you.\"","The illustrative image dissolved back into the ambient air as she folded her hands together.","\" The binding I impose on you will restrict your power, and the power of all others within this Observable Existence, to the Fundamental Depth of Vakochev’s First Scale.\"","BOOM!","\" You will remember, yes, that you are the ant, and I am providing treatment to the soil. I am binding you and all others down here to that stage. Your cultivation will not exceed it. Your climbing will not extend beyond it. Whatever capacities you have already developed that sit above Fundamental Depth will be compressed downward into that stage until they fit within its boundaries. This first binding alone would be sufficient for most administrative purposes. But the circumstances of a Relictus emergence justify thoroughness, and so I will layer additional bindings into your existence to ensure that no further escape from the administered parameters becomes possible.\"","Her voice continued to list the bindings with clinical precision!","\" You will be locked out from accessing and influencing Infinity. You will be locked out from accessing and influencing Observable Force, which means the ambient golden currents that saturate this existence will no longer respond to your call. You will be locked out from accessing and influencing Unobservable Force, though you would have never even touched it to begin with...\"","She listed the next bindings with the same unhurried patience.","\" Your Civilization will be bound into a dormant state. You will retain memory of it. You will no longer be able to wield it. Any capacities you developed that operated through Civilizational channels will cease to function. Any weavings you have placed across the Observable that depended on your Civilization being alive and active within you will dissolve.\"","Noah kept his defiant gaze on her through all of it, and system notifications bloomed through his perception in steady sequence as Ruination catalogued everything this dumb bitch said.","|Binding Applied: THE Scale Limiter.|","|Your accessible cultivation has been capped at the Fundamental Depth of Vakochev’s First Scale. Any capacities exceeding this threshold have been compressed into dormant storage within your existence. The binding assumes you operate within Vakochev’s Scales framework.|","|Binding Applied: THE Infinity Seal.|","|Your access to Infinity as a weaving has been severed. Ambient Infinity will no longer respond to your call.|","|Binding Applied: THE Observable Force Lockout.|","|Your access to the ambient currents of Observable Force has been blocked.|","|Binding Applied: THE Unobservable Force Lockout.|","|Your access to the deeper Unobservable substrates has been blocked.|","|Binding Applied: THE Civilizational Dormancy.|","|Your Civilization has been forced into dormant storage. You retain memory of its shape but cannot wield it.|","|Binding Applied: THE Weaving Severance.|","|Any weavings you have placed across the Observable that depended on your active Cause will dissolve.|","|Additional Binding Applied: THE Voice Restraint.|","|You are restrained from voicing disagreements against Sororis authority.|","|Additional Binding Applied: THE Deferential Posture.|","|You will find yourself physically inclined toward lowered gaze and reduced stature in the presence of Gilded Lifeforms. The inclination operates as a default orientation rather than an active compulsion, and it will require deliberate effort to resist.|","Really?","Was that right?! Okay. Okay!","Sororis Prima Elzyana continued for another long stretch as the bindings layered themselves into Noah’s perception, and Noah absorbed every word without breaking his gaze!","She did not realize the binding of THE Deferential Posture was being resisted!","When she finished, she looked at Noah calmly, and the expression on her face carried the same flat detached interest it had carried since she had first descended toward him, with no hostility and no satisfaction and no particular engagement, simply the steady observation of a being who had completed an action and was now waiting briefly to confirm the action had taken.","\" You may find, in time, that the constraints are merciful.\"","Her voice softened slightly.","\" Consider the extension of the analogy I offered you earlier. The ant in the treated soil often believes that the treatment represents a curtailment of the ant’s life. The ant mourns the loss of the broader colony. The ant struggles against the adjusted conditions. But across the long course of the ant’s subsequent existence, the ant may come to discover that the bounded conditions produce a form of peace that the broader colony never permitted. No expansion means no overreach. No overreach means no conflicts with other colonies at the edges of the territory. No conflicts means no casualties. The limitations allow the ant to live a simpler and less anxious life than the unlimited ant ever could have lived. Freer, in a certain specific sense, precisely because the capacity for unfree activity has been removed.\"","She folded her hands together in front of her.","\" Sometimes, the ant simply needs to be grateful. The gardener’s treatment was not a punishment. It was a gift of reduced scope, which is also a gift of reduced suffering. Ants need to be thankful for this. Those of you who come to thankfulness across the years that follow will find the remainder of your existence to be calmer than the existence you would have otherwise constructed for yourselves. Those of you who do not come to thankfulness will continue struggling against constraints that cannot be overcome, and the struggling will be your only reward, and the reward will not be as satisfying as the thankfulness would have been.\"","Her mandala-eyes rotated slowly as she delivered the closing observation.","\" Be thankful, Boy. Be thankful while you have the space to develop the thankfulness properly. It will make your bounded remainder more bearable than the alternative.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5163,"title":"Chapter 5163: Chapter 5162: You Seal Nothing! You Bind Nothing! I","paragraphs":["Sororis Prima Elzyana rose slightly through the air and waved her hands, and blue-gold brilliance erupted around her like a roaring beast filled with wrath, the colors of her authority compounding into an intensity that had not been in her earlier displays of Observable Force and Infinity, the wrath of a Sisterhood mourning the death of a Gerousia expressing itself outward through the raised palms of the Sororis Prima.","Two more pyramidal constructs formed between her palms and shot downward toward Emotive and Anaximander at the base of the mountain, each construct embedding itself into the back of the hand of its target with the same clean precision that had planted the first construct into Noah’s hand, and both Emotive and Anaximander tensed as the bindings settled into their existences and began to propagate through their foundations.","But Sororis Prima Elzyana was not finished.","Trillions of additional pyramidal constructs bloomed from her raised palms and expanded outward into the air above THE Gilded White Mountain, dispersing in radiant formations that rode the golden-blue brilliance of her authority outward across every reach of THE Wyld and beyond, flowing through the weavings of the Observable Existence into every territory and realm and civilization and small corner of the lower face of reality where Bounded Lifeforms lived their small unregulated lives.","The constructs spread in exponential waves, each construct branching into further constructs, each further construct branching into yet more, the proliferation continuing until the entire expanse of the Observable Existence was being blanketed in a descending storm of blue-gold bindings that sought their targets with the patient inevitability of a verdict being delivered across an entire population!","The wrath of THE Gilded Ones, mourning one of their own, was poured outward across every existence beneath them.","Every Bounded Lifeform within reach would receive their constructs!","Every Civilization within the Observable would feel its connections severed!","The death of a Gilded One had brought down a terrifying golden wrath, and the wrath was now settling itself across the full expanse of the Observable!","Noah stood on the ruined balcony beneath Sororis Prima Elzyana with the first construct already settled into the back of his hand, his eyes flashing coldly with an imperious light!","He stared up at the endless sky, his figure burning with brilliance as Sororis Prima Elzyana had departed at some point during the final stages of her distribution of the trillions of pyramidal bindings across Observable Existence.","The skies had not returned to their ordinary coloration. The wrath of gold she had unleashed upon completing her procedure seemed to seek a form of permanence in the upper reaches of THE Wyld, the molten saturated gold she had inherited from Gerousia Aurelius Maximus’s earlier claim now compounded with her own golden-blue authority into a canopy that stretched across every direction his perception could track.","The gold above was not going anywhere.","The gold above had been written into the arrangement of existence with enough intention to outlast any ordinary weathering.","However, he could affirm with his intuition and the broader immensity of his awareness that no Gilded Ones remained in the immediate vicinity . The six Gerousia-ranked Gilded Ones had departed to pursue THE Creature. Ferocis Valerius Krael had departed behind them to lend his Ira to the pursuit.","Sororis Prima Elzyana herself had completed her distribution of the pyramidal constructs and had vanished, leaving behind only the constructs themselves now settling into the foundations of every Bounded Lifeform and every affected Civilization across the full expanse of the Observable.","The sky was empty of Gilded presences.","The sky was filled, however, with the saturated aftermath of what the Gilded presences had accomplished during their brief entrance.","Noah looked at the back of his hand where Sororis Prima Elzyana had planted her first pyramidal construct, the one she had designated as the initial binding from which all subsequent bindings had propagated outward into him. The construct had settled cleanly into his skin and had begun its propagation.","The back of his hand now shone with a soft blue-gold brilliance that pulsed in slow steady intervals, and the brilliance traced along his veins into his forearm, and from there continued its reach into the deeper foundations of his existence where Elzyana’s collection of additional bindings had layered themselves into the specific channels she had intended them to occupy.","He coldly observed the construct on the back of his hand for a long patient moment.","Then he raised his hand.","Then he began to laugh!","He laughed as if he had gone a little mad, his laughter rolling up from somewhere deep in his chest and spilling outward across the ruined balcony of THE Gilded White Mountain’s highest remaining temple with a cadence that surprised even him!","One of his hands eventually rose to cover the lower portion of his face as if he did not want anyone else to witness the specific shape of his expression during this laughter, while the other hand, the one carrying the pyramidal construct that shone with Elzyana’s authority, remained raised toward the gold-saturated sky above him as he observed the construct through the gaps between the fingers of his covering hand.","Down below him at the base of the mountain, he could perceive Emotive and Anaximander with ashen expressions on their faces, the two of them enduring the settling of their own pyramidal constructs into their respective hands, the bindings wrapping tightly around their foundations with the same propagating thoroughness that had been applied to him.","He could perceive the specific shape of their shock as they looked up at him and witnessed his laughter, and he could read in their expressions the question neither of them had yet dared to voice aloud.","Had he gone mad due to the bindings?!","Had the pressure of having an entire layered binding applied to his existence finally broken whatever composure he had been maintaining, and was he now laughing in the specific terminal manner of a being whose foundations had cracked under pressure that exceeded his capacity to bear?","No . He had not gone mad. Not at all.","However, he could not help but laugh, because his mind was already busy constructing a very specific image that he found himself unable to look away from.","He was imagining, with the crystalline clarity that his Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation permitted him to bring to his imaginings, the day that he would have Sororis Prima Elzyana at his feet.","Not defeated in the ordinary sense of the word, because the ordinary defeat would not have produced the precise expression he wanted to witness on her face.","He was imagining the day she would look up at him from her kneeling position with her amber-gold mandala-eyes quivering out of their slowly rotating geometries and into the narrow trembling lines of a being whose existential assumptions had just been violated, and he was imagining the exact cadence of shock and incredulity that her voice would carry when she finally spoke to him from that position, and he was imagining the small private satisfaction he would feel in that moment of having demonstrated to her that the ant in her extended analogy had been something other than an ant all along!"]},{"number":5164,"title":"Chapter 5164: Chapter 5163: You Seal Nothing! You Bind Nothing! II","paragraphs":["He could perceive the image so unfathomably clearly.","Because she truly thought she could bind him? Him?","\" Me?! Haha!\"","BOOM!","As he bellowed the question out across the ruined balcony, around his body boundless multicolored Infinity surged in response to the bellowing, and his Quintessence Infiniforce continued to generate endlessly within his existence at the elevated rate the Superbius amplification had enabled hours earlier, pouring outward from his foundations in rivers of layered color that did not show any sign of having been sealed or suppressed by Elzyana’s work.","The brilliance of what he was putting out pressed against the gold-saturated sky above him and found the sky unable to contain it, and small flickers of his multicolored Infiniforce began to push upward against the golden canopy with the patient persistent assertion of a living current reclaiming its territory!","Noah continued to laugh while his Quintessence Infiniforce surged around him and commenced painting the surrounding regions of the mountain and the sky with his own preferred colors, and he voiced his thoughts aloud with the tyrannical amusement of a being witnessing the failure of a process that had presumed to address him.","\" THE Infinity Seal?!\"","His voice carried the clean dry cadence of genuine amusement.","\" You cannot bind or suppress my Infinity. You cannot even begin to! My Quintessence Infiniforce is generated internally, from my own existence! Your seal passes through my foundations like nothing. It finds nothing to seal. It closes nothing!\"","HUUM!","His Quintessence Infiniforce surged around him ever more intensely, and the boundless Infinity began to coil around his body and skin like an endless network of coiling serpents, each coil carrying its own layered colors, each coil weaving through and around the coils adjacent to it in patterns that suggested the Infinity itself had been waiting for permission to express itself this freely and was now taking full advantage of the permission being granted!","Noah closed his eyes while surrounded by the boundless Infinity, and his figure stood gloriously at the center of the surging currents as his Hadean Pillar of Infinity bloomed around him in its full manifested form rather than the faint background construct it had been earlier.","THE First Tongue crystallized into its blue forest at the base of the Pillar. The multicolored flames of Existence licked upward through the mid-tiers with renewed intensity. The mirrors of Paradox reflected their impossibilities across every direction. The storm of Chaos roared at the apex with the weight of his refusal to accept the conclusions.","Every actualized Civilization throughout the Pillar rose in rank alongside his spoken refutations, each one contributing its weight to the broader assertion his existence was now making against Elzyana’s distributed authority!","He spoke to his very existence and to his Civilizations within him and within his Pillar, and his voice boomed outward from within his foundations as it refuted each of the bindings in sequence.","\" THE Scale Limiter?\"","His voice held the dry amusement of a being pointing out an obvious miscalculation.","\" You limited me to THE Fundamental Depth of Vakochev’s First Scale. I am not on Vakochev’s Scales! Your Limiter has applied itself to coordinates I do not occupy. It sits there, compressing a portion of Vakochev’s framework that is not mine to be compressed. The binding is technically functional. The binding has technically done what it was designed to do. The binding has simply done it... to a space I was never in.\"","BOOM!","His Pillar rose higher in response to the refutation, and more of his Quintessence Infiniforce poured outward from his existence to replace what the refutation had just consumed.","\" THE Observable Force Lockout?\"","He felt the continuous feed from Ubergulden Adelheid still flowing through their shared bond, the golden current pouring into him through the wormhole of Quintessence Infiniforce they shared, unaffected by the Lockout that had sealed the ambient channels around him.","\"You blocked my access to the ambient currents. You did not block the private channel I share! The Lockout has closed a door I was not using. The door I actually use remains open.\"","BOOM!","\" THE Unobservable Force Lockout?\"","His laughter continued beneath the words.","\"I have not been drawing on Unobservable Force in any meaningful way yet.\"","BOOM!","\" THE Civilizational Dormancy?\"","He observed within himself the way his Civilizations were behaving under the pressure of the binding, and he perceived the specific shape of what the Dormancy had attempted to do. His Civilizations flickered slightly under the settling of the binding. But...they did not fall asleep.","His Hadean Organ of Civilization held them against the pressure, and his Pillar reinforced the hold by bearing down on the storage configuration with its full accumulated weight. The Civilizations continued to operate. The Dormancy continued to insist that they should not be operating. The disagreement between the binding and the actual state of his Civilizations was simply a disagreement that the binding was losing.","\" You forced my Civilizations into dormancy. My Organ refused the force. My Pillar refused alongside the Organ. My Civilizations continue to hum within me at their active intensities, and your binding continues to sit within my foundations issuing instructions that my foundations are not obeying. It is a conversation the binding cannot win because my foundations have already decided the outcome...backed by my Infinity!\"","BOOM!","\" THE Voice Restraint?\"","He laughed fully at this one, because the laughter itself was the rebuttal, because he had been speaking freely and defiantly for the entire duration of his refutations and the binding that was supposed to prevent such speaking had found no purchase with which to prevent anything.","\"I am speaking. I am speaking loudly. I am speaking in direct opposition to Sororis authority.\"","BOOM!","\" THE Deferential Posture?\"","He stood tall at the center of his Pillar, his head lifted toward the gold-saturated sky above him, his spine straight, his shoulders relaxed into the posture of a being who had never been inclined to defer to anything across his entire cultivation.","\"I cannot defer. I will never...defer.\"","BOOM!","\" THE Memory Seal?\"","He remembered every detail of the afternoon with the clarity of his Hadean Mind of Infinite Calculation, remembered THE Creature’s strike, remembered Aurelius Maximus’s carving, remembered Elzyana’s descent and her clinical cruelty and her distribution of the trillions of constructs across the Observable, remembered every word of her extended analogy about ants and soil and gardeners, remembered the exact sequence in which his bindings had been applied to him.","Nothing was sealed. His memory was entirely available to him.","The more Noah refuted, the more his body generated Quintessence Infiniforce boundlessly, each refutation pulling additional reserves of his internal substance outward into the ambient field around him, and the surge of Infiniforce around his figure began to expand in magnitudes that exceeded any surge he had previously produced across his existence.","It felt boundless.","The multicolored Infinity surged outward from him like a vibrant rising sea, and the sea commenced rising upward through the gold-saturated sky with the patient persistence of a tide that had decided to claim the territory a prior tide had been occupying.","The gold of Elzyana’s and Aurelius’s combined wrath began to be displaced. Small fractures appeared in the golden canopy above the mountain as Noah’s multicolored Infiniforce pressed against it from below, and the fractures widened into gaps, and through the gaps his own colors began to pour outward into the upper reaches of THE Wyld.","The multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce spread across the upper atmosphere of THE Wyld in rolling waves that overwrote the golden wrath with Noah’s own preferred palette. Where the gold had claimed the sky as Sororis Prima Elzyana’s domain, Noah’s Infiniforce now commenced claiming it back as his!"]},{"number":5165,"title":"Chapter 5165: Chapter 5164: You Seal Nothing! You Bind Nothing! III","paragraphs":["As the spreading of his Infiniforce reached its fullest outward expression, something commenced rising within him, and the rising commanded his attention because the rising was not something he had summoned!","Something was emerging from THE Hadean Organ of Civilization!","The Organ flashed and compressed and radiated profoundly within the deepest layers of his foundations, its compression pulling on the full weight of his existence and on the full accumulated authority of his Hadean Pillar of Infinity, and the resulting emission carried a density of Quintessence Infiniforce that eclipsed every prior emission he had generated.","The emission rose upward through his foundations and gathered itself. It was something new. It was something his existence was in the process of producing in response to the particular circumstances of the afternoon!","A system notification bloomed into his perception.","|Your existence has triggered a previously undocumented developmental phenomenon.|","| Designation: THE Quintessential Hadean Civilizational Eon of Development.|","...!","|This developmental phenomenon is unique to your existence and to your framework. It is not present in Vakochev’s Scales, nor in any adjacent framework. It has commenced in response to your refutation of each binding imposed by Sororis Prima Elzyana, with each successful refutation of someone unfathomably grander contributing accumulated momentum toward the developmental threshold.|","|Mechanism: Through the act of denying the weavings of a Gilded One and overcoming every single one of them, your existence has generated a developmental pressure directed against the broader phenomenon Sororis Prima Elzyana represents. Your existence does not merely wish to resist her authority. Your existence wishes to exceed it, to make the bindings she carries obsolete by producing an equivalent authority of your own at a superior tier of expression.|","|Your existence seeks to develop your own Existential Radiation, which your framework will render as Infinite Radiation. You seek to go above and beyond the Paleozoic expression of Existential Radiation by producing a version of it that operates through your Quintessence Infiniforce and through the full spectrum of your actualized Civilizations simultaneously.|","| Your existence seeks Absolute . Your existence seeks Absolute Infinity. The developmental progression toward Absolute Infinity, which had been distant, has found its catalyst in the refutation of Sororis Prima Elzyana’s weavings.|","| THE Quintessential Hadean Civilizational Eon of Development is beginning.|","BOOM!","A multicolored cocoon formed around Noah in response to the notification.","The cocoon did not take an ordinary shape. It spiraled out from his body along the lines of a lemniscate, the infinity symbol stretched into three-dimensional living form, the two looping halves of the symbol wrapping around him in braided interwoven currents of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force that pulsed with the slow patient intensity of a gestation.","The upper loop of the lemniscate rose above his head and coiled back down toward his shoulders. The lower loop descended past his feet and coiled back upward toward his hips. The crossing point of the lemniscate settled at the center of his chest, where his immensity rested, the intersection of the two loops resting directly against the organ that held his anchored Cause.","The cocoon pulsed with a layered brilliance that spread outward from him in rolling waves.","Rivers of Quintessence Infiniforce commenced surging and pulsing outward from the cocoon in every direction, his Infiniforce spreading across THE Wyld with a density that eclipsed every prior display he had produced, the multicolored currents running through the sky and the mountain and the surrounding regions like rivers of living light claiming territory for the developmental phenomenon unfolding within the lemniscate cocoon.","Alongside the Quintessence Infiniforce, rivers of Observable Force poured out from the cocoon with equal intensity, the two forces braiding through each other!","Noah stood at the center of the lemniscate cocoon with his eyes closed and his existence undergoing a developmental phenomenon, and around him the sky of THE Wyld commenced transitioning entirely from the golden wrath of a departed Sororis Prima into the multicolored domain of a being whose refusal to be bound had just catalyzed a new phase of his continuing ascent!","—","<Sororis Prima Elzyana Report to The Council>","Report submitted by Sororis Prima Elzyana of the Second Sanctum to THE Council of the Magna Sorora, regarding the descent into The Lesser Domains on the occasion of the death of Gerousia Aurelius Maximus of the Superbius House of the Crimson Chalice.","The affair has been addressed with the efficiency one would expect of our people, and I report now so that the Council may update its records accordingly and proceed with whatever additional actions are deemed appropriate within the broader handling of THE Relictus emergence.","A Young Relictus manifested among the lower lifeforms. This in itself is a matter of some note, because appearances of Relictus within the Lands of the Bounded is impossible.","The vile creature carved Aurelius thoroughly, which I note as a mark of either ritualistic intention or improvised cruelty.","Six Gerousia of the Superbius gave chase alongside my own Custos, and additional Sisters and Gilded Ones across multiple Houses have been notified of the trajectory. The pursuit is ongoing as even while young, A Relictus is a Relictus.","The vile creature’s escape was facilitated by his touch on the Source. I anticipate the pursuit will continue across some span of days or weeks before resolution.","The weakness of this Young Relictus, however, is worth highlighting as an opportunity. He is not yet what the grown Relictus have been when they appeared against us. He is still in the early phases of his touch on the Source, and his cultivation around that touch remains incomplete.","This presents what I regard as a rare and exceedingly valuable chance. If we can secure this creature alive rather than collapse him outright, THE Magna Sorora may finally obtain a Relictus specimen for detailed examination, and the knowledge we extract from such an examination would advance our understanding of THE Primordial Source in ways our eons of theoretical work have failed to approach.","I recommend the pursuit parameters be adjusted to prioritize capture over termination where capture becomes feasible. I await the Council’s direction on this point.","As for the lower lifeforms present at the site, and the broader Observable Existence surrounding the site, I have administered standard prophylactic bindings across every reachable population. The Bounded have been compressed back into Fundamental Depth of the First Scale. Their accesses to Infinity and Observable Force and Unobservable Force have been sealed. Their Civilizations have been forced into dormancy.","I will note, for the Council’s interest, that one of the lower lifeforms present at the site produced a small defiant response.","I note this as a minor curiosity rather than a concern, because the voicing was brief and was addressed, but I mention it because the phenomenon of Bounded beings producing audible disagreement against Gilded Ones has increased in frequency by a small but measurable fraction.","The broader principle that has always guided our Sisterhood remains in effect.","All shall know the grace of our domain. All shall rest beneath the shade of the Gilded canopy. All substrates of existence shall eventually be pruned into alignment with the Gilded truth, and the pruning shall continue across whatever eons remain to us until the alignment is total.","Submitted in the service of the Council and the continuation of our eternal arrangement.","Sororis Prima Elzyana, Second Sanctum, Daughter of the Radiant Register."]},{"number":5166,"title":"Chapter 5166: Chapter 5165: Reign I","paragraphs":["Existence breathes, and epochs pass, leaving Civilizations that become monuments, then crumble to memory, and are long forgotten when that breath comes again. In all these epochs, Infinity reigns supreme.","---","The Shroud of Endless Blue shall fall upon Observable Existence. It shall be both salvation and damnation, both the key and the lock, both the bridge and the chasm. Under its weight, the doors of the Scales shall open or the doors of the Scales shall shatter. There is no third path. There is no middle ground. There is only the choice that is not a choice.","The adversity that breaks all others shall forge him. The hardship that ends all paths shall begin his. The Scales demand what the Scales demand, and he shall pay in currencies that have not yet been minted.","Three times shall he face the mirror of undoing. Three times shall he choose between becoming and unbecoming. Three times shall the answer be the same, and three times shall the answer be different.","In the end, which is also the beginning, the Infinite shall stand before the Undefined. And only one shall remain to tell the tale that no one shall hear.","This is an Echo of First Cause.","This is what shall come to pass, for it has already passed, and it shall pass again.","The wheel turns. The river flows. The question echoes.","He shall be the answer, or he shall be nothing.","Or he shall be the question that ends all answers.","---","The grandest things across existence have always been born from the heaviest adversity.","This is not a sentiment offered for the comfort of those currently experiencing adversity, because comfort of that kind tends to dissolve under the weight of the circumstances it was meant to address.","This is instead an observation that has been made across the long arc of existence by beings who have witnessed enough cycles of pressure and response to have identified the pattern with sufficient precision to state it plainly.","Pressure applied to a weak foundation collapses that foundation. Pressure applied to a foundation of sufficient depth, however, does not collapse the foundation but compresses it, and compression across sufficient duration produces configurations of density that the uncompressed foundation could never have achieved through ordinary development.","The beings who become grand do not become grand in pleasant circumstances. They become grand in circumstances that would have broken lesser beings entirely, and the breaking that did not occur becomes the engine through which the later grandeur is produced.","Adversity is the forge. Pressure is the compression. The being at the center of the forge either melts into formlessness or emerges from the forge as something the original weaving...could not have anticipated .","---","Emotive and Anaximander looked up from the ruined base of THE Gilded White Mountain to observe the brilliant cocoon suspended far above them in the fractured sky, and what they witnessed made every other concern that had occupied their attention suddenly feel small.","Emotive felt the bindings on her existence with a clarity that her own foundations had never before been required to experience. The pyramidal construct embedded in the back of her hand radiated its quiet authority through every channel of her being, commencing the severance of her access to Infinity, commencing the lockout from Observable Force, commencing the forced dormancy of her Civilization.","Her usual cycling hair had flattened into a single muted violet that she was not consciously producing, the color of a being whose expressive palette had been constrained by an external hand that had no interest in her expressive range.","Her chatter that normally accompanied them had gone silent. Every emotion within her had become immensely serious.","She looked up at the cocoon suspended in the sky and wondered how her Fixation must be feeling.","Did he truly feel all the bindings that had been placed upon him? Was he currently experiencing the same severance she was experiencing? Was he worried? Was he anxious?","Had the composure that had carried him through so many prior encounters finally cracked under the weight of a being whose tier genuinely exceeded his own for the first time?","She had never witnessed her Fixation reach a point of genuine distress across her time spent adjacent to him, and the possibility that he might currently be reaching such a point, alone inside whatever cocoon his existence had produced, made her entire being buzz with a specific kind of rage she had not previously felt in quite this shape.","She voiced the rage aloud.","\" How dare she?\"","BOOM!","Her voice rolled outward across the base of the mountain, and around her body, crimson waves of emotional authority commenced gathering with a density that had not been present a moment earlier.","The crimson authority did not emerge from her internal reserves alone. It was pulling on something broader, reaching outward into the ambient emotional substrate of THE Wyld and of every adjacent region, gathering the specific flavors of rage and outrage and humiliation that those constructs were currently producing inside counless Bounded Lifeforms across Observable Existence.","The pulling was slow. They rose from the stone beneath her feet in the first slow moment, gathered across her shoulders and her arms and her chest in the second, compounded into a full enveloping aura in the third, and by the fourth moment Emotive stood at the center of a crimson storm that had pulled on accumulated emotional product from across an expanse of existence so vast that her usual siphoning capacity could not have accessed even a measurable fraction of it without the catalyst of her current rage.","She looked up at the cocoon above her, and she voiced her next words with the full weight of the crimson storm now gathered around her.","\"I felt her!\"","BOOM!","\"I felt her Pride. I felt her arrogance! Such vile Pride carries a stench across the emotional weavings, and the stench does not dissipate when she departs! And no matter how far she goes, no matter how deeply she retreats...I will be able to pull on it because Pride of that particular flavor cannot hide from someone like me!\"","WAA!","She lifted her hands toward the sky where Elzyana had vanished, and her crimson storm intensified around her.","\" So. Give me the intensity of your Superbius Pride! Give me the intensity of your arrogance! Give me the full accumulated weight of every moment you have ever spent looking down on a being beneath you, and give me the weight of every casual cruelty you have ever administered! I will gather all of it. I will shatter the shackles you placed on me with your own power!\"","BOOM!","The crimson light of accumulated emotions shot upward from her body toward the distant sky and disappeared into the golden canopy above, and a storm of emotions covered the entire region around the mountain as Emotive commenced the work of dismantling her own bindings through a methodology that drew on the very source of the bindings themselves.","Beside her, Anaximander rose from his kneeling position on the pale stone with an expression that was heavy, contemplative, patient.","His tall angular frame straightened by measured increments as he recovered from the descending radiation that had forced him down earlier, and his face held the same scholarly composure that had accompanied him across every prior encounter.","Anaximander’s existence was unique. His power and Civilization and Way was...unique compared to others as he did not truly need authority.","He examined the pyramidal construct on the back of his hand with detached intellectual attention.","The bindings were present on him, but they wouldn’t do too much.","He looked up toward the cocoon above and waited to witness whatever emerged from it.","Far above the mountain, the surging cocoon around Noah continued to expand and intensify.","The rivers of multicolored Infiniforce that had been pouring outward from the cocoon in earlier moments had compounded into outright seas, the seas spreading across the upper reaches of THE Wyld with a density that eclipsed even the ambient Observable Force that permeated the region, the ordinary golden currents of THE Wyld’s substrate now being displaced by Noah’s multicolored substance at a rate that could not be measured.","His Infiniforce stretched across the upper atmosphere of THE Wyld in rolling layered waves, each wave carrying its own combination of colors, each wave pressing outward from the cocoon with the patient persistence of a tide that had no intention of receding.","The seas began to pulse.","The pulsing commenced with the slow patient cadence of a heartbeat, each pulse spreading outward from the cocoon in a spherical wave that rolled across the sky and the mountain and the surrounding regions with the steady timing of cardiac systole, and each pulse was accompanied by a sound that had not been present before.","The sound was a drum.","DUM! DUM! DUM!","Infinity boomed like a drum as it pulsed outward from the cocoon, and the drumming carried the deep resonant timbre of an instrument that had been waiting within the substrate of existence for the specific moment to announce itself.","The first drum was joined by a second drum, slightly offset in timing, contributing its own resonance to the broader rhythm. A third drum commenced alongside the second, and a fourth alongside the third, and soon the sky above the mountain was carrying a full percussive rhythm composed of Infinity pulsing through dozens of overlapping drumbeats that rolled outward in coordinated patterns.","Horns emerged alongside the drums.","The horns were not literal instruments. They were the sonic expression of what Noah’s Quintessence Infiniforce was producing as it moved through the patterns his developmental phenomenon required, and the sound they produced carried the specific heroic cadence of an imperial procession arriving at the culmination of a long journey!","The horns called outward across the sky with long sustained notes that built upon each other in layered harmonies, and the harmonies rose into configurations that felt grand and heroic and imperious all at once, the kind of symphony that would have been composed across millennia if existence had ever permitted a composer with sufficient reach to compose it!","Oh!","Oh!!!","A symphony of drums and horns began to bloom across THE Wyld!"]},{"number":5167,"title":"Chapter 5167: Chapter 5166: Reign II","paragraphs":["The symphony was grand!","The symphony was imperious in the specific manner of music that had been written to announce the arrival of a being whose standing deserved announcement!","The drums became more frequent as the symphony progressed.","The horns became more glorious, their sustained notes climbing into higher harmonies that carried the building tension of a composition approaching its crescendo!","The symphony built.","Until...","BOOM!","The cocoon broke apart in a blinding brilliance that saturated every direction.","Tendrils and rivers of multicolored Infiniforce stretched outward from the point of breaking in vast expanding arcs, each tendril carrying its own unique combination of the colors that had composed the cocoon, each river pulsing with the heartbeat cadence of the symphony that had just concluded.","The gold-saturated canopy Elzyana and Aurelius had painted across the sky of THE Wyld was overwritten entirely in the moment of the breaking, the multicolored Infiniforce claiming every inch of the sky that the golden wrath had previously claimed, the transition complete within the single extended moment of the cocoon’s rupture.","When Emotive and Anaximander looked up at the point where the cocoon had been, they observed what had emerged from it.","A figure that resembled the Noah they knew.","The figure resembled Noah in the sense that a refined edition of a document resembles the earlier draft from which it was developed.","The general shape was the same. The proportions were the same. The identifiable features that had composed Noah across his prior manifestations were still present. However, every aspect of him had been polished, intensified, elevated into configurations that the earlier Noah had not possessed.","His entire body was shrouded in a multicolored crystalline brilliance of Infinity, the crystalline layer not applied to him but emerging from him, as though his skin had become a lens through which the full spectrum of his Infiniforce could be observed in its refined state. The crystalline brilliance pulsed gently with the residual rhythm of the symphony, each pulse carrying the slow patient cadence of a heartbeat that had settled into its new steady operation.","Dense rivers of Infinity twirled around his body in continuous motion, forming multiple lemniscate symbols with their traced paths, each lemniscate a separate flowing braid of Infiniforce that looped around a different portion of his body.","One lemniscate wrapped around his chest and back. Another wrapped around his waist and hips. A third wrapped around his shoulders and neck. A fourth wrapped around his head, framing his features in a continuous braid of multicolored light that moved in slow patient rotation.","His hair radiated its multicolored light more intensely than it had before, the strands themselves appearing to be composed of layered Infiniforce rather than ordinary hair, their movements following their own independent currents regardless of the ambient air around him.","His skin carried the internal golden illumination that had characterized his Hadean physiology, but the illumination now ran through layered patterns that suggested deeper architecture beneath the surface, the outlines of his Hadean organs visible as soft glows through the translucent quality his flesh had taken on during the developmental transition.","His posture had straightened into something imperious. Not arrogant, precisely, because arrogance implied a relationship to beings who might challenge the imperiousness, and Noah’s new posture did not seem to acknowledge the possibility of challenge as a relevant category.","He simply stood at the center of his surrounding Infiniforce with the casual grandeur of a being whose position in the arrangement of existence had just been clarified into something that required no defense.","Emotive began to shake with despair as she observed him.","Because... she could not feel anything!","She could not feel any emotion whatsoever from her Fixation, as though emotions did not exist in him, as though the entire emotional substrate that she had been reading Noah through across every prior moment of their acquaintance had been sealed behind a layer her siphoning could not penetrate!","She reached outward with every emotional sense she possessed and received nothing in return. No Pride. No amusement. No cold calculation. No tenderness toward those beneath him. No cruelty!","Nothing. The space where his emotional signature should have been was simply empty in a manner that suggested either that his emotions had been transcended entirely or that they had been folded into the weavings of his new configuration so completely that external perception could no longer distinguish them from the ambient Infiniforce surrounding his body.","She looked at him closely.","She observed that his eyes had become glazed crystalline blue with the internal light of Infinity, and within the crystalline blue of each eye, small lemniscate symbols had replaced his pupils. The symbols rotated slowly within the blue of his irises, their infinite loops tracing their continuous figure-eight patterns in patient synchronized motion, and the sight of those eyes was unlike anything Emotive had witnessed in any being across any of her eons.","He raised his hand to look at himself.","The hand moved with the deliberate grace of a being becoming acquainted with its new configuration, examining the crystalline brilliance of his own skin, observing the lemniscate rivers that flowed around his forearm, taking in the refined shape of his transformed fingers.","He turned his hand slowly in the air before him, considering it from multiple angles, as though cataloguing what the developmental phenomenon had produced.","And then, without ceremony, he tapped his finger outward.","A boundless flash of Infinity bloomed silently and invisibly from the tap, spreading outward from his finger in every direction. The Infinity did not produce sound. It did not produce visible light at its point of origin!","It simply spread fully from this point...towards all of Observable Existence!","And then...","His figure warped away and disappeared.","He did not look toward Emotive before departing. He did not look toward Anaximander. He did not look at the remains of the mountain or the remnants of the corpses or the fractured sky or any other feature of the terrain.","He simply warped, and then he was no longer present at the location the cocoon had emerged from, and the space where his figure had stood held only the residual rivers of his Infiniforce continuing their outward spread across the upper atmosphere of THE Wyld.","Emotive crumbled to the ground at the base of the mountain with an expression of despair crossing her features in a single slow wave.","Because she truly could not sense any emotion of her Fixation. Because all she had observed in him during the brief moment of his emergence was...boundless Infinity.","All she observed was Infinity.","All she could observe, when she reached outward toward the place his emotional substrate had occupied, was Infinity.","Infinity.","The trumpets ceased.","The drums concluded their rolling patterns.","The symphony that had accompanied Noah’s developmental transition dissolved, and an immense silence reigned across the regions where the music had played.","Emotive remained on the ground, her hands flat against the surface beside her, tears falling from her eyes.","She felt an unfathomable sense of loss.","Not the loss of a being who had died. The being was still present. The loss she felt was something smaller and more private than mortality. It was the loss of the specific Fixation she had been able to read, the being whose emotional architecture burned with boundless emotions.","That being was no longer available to her.","In his place stood something else.","The silence continued.","The Infiniforce above her continued its patient spread across the sky, imperious, and filled with glorious purpose."]},{"number":5168,"title":"Chapter 5168: Chapter 5167: Reign III","paragraphs":["The pursuit of ultimate power has never been a path of accumulation without equal and devastating subtraction, for existence does not permit the birth of a titan without the death of the perspective that preceded it.","To grasp the ungraspable, to reach beyond the Bounded and the Gilded until one touches the hem of the Absolute, requires a currency that many find too heavy to pay.","One must lose the comfort of limited perception, the warmth of common sorrow, and the familiar weight of fear, for a being who is filled with the boundless cannot simultaneously carry the small, flickering embers of human fragility.","The cost of becoming boundless is, quite simply, the willingness to become nothing like what one was before, as the self is expanded until its borders dissolve into the infinite substrate of reality, leaving behind a presence that does not merely inhabit existence, but dictates its very arrangement.","---","At the heart of THE Infiniverse, where the rain of THE Pluvial Epoch fell in a steady, multicolored rhythm upon the golden sands, the humanoid manifestation of THE Infiniverse stood in a state of suspended anticipation inside its core.","Beside her, the illusory figure of Ruination shimmered with a clarity that suggested her processing was currently operating at the limits of its current Hadean architecture.","Both turned their gazes toward a singular point in the space as a ripple of reality-warping intensity announced an arrival that was not merely a physical displacement, but a total atmospheric shift.","Noah’s primary body, fresh from its emergence above THE Gilded White Mountain, appeared within this internal reality with a silent, crystalline brilliance that seemed to drain the surrounding colors into its own multicolored spectrum.","THE Infiniverse observed him with a gaze that held a depth of loyalty that transcended the concepts of servitude, her thoughts tracing the arduous path she and Ruination had carved out during his absence.","They had labored with a precision that defied logic to construct half of THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds, folding the dimensions of the Three Thousand Realms into recursive, infinitesimal configurations that even now served as a barrier against the prying eyes of the Gilded.","It was because of this half-finished work that the pyramidal bindings of Sororis Prima Elzyana had failed to find purchase within these depths, yet the uncertainty within her foundations was growing. With the manifolds only half-complete, the stress of the hidden existence was mounting, and the potential for discovery by a sufficiently persistent Gilded authority remained a terrifying variable.","She looked at her Master, and for the first time in her long and devoted existence, she felt a sliver of genuine hesitation as she took in his new, glazed crystalline eyes and the absence of any emotional signature.","\"How does...Master feel?\"","Her voice emerged with a softness that almost vanished beneath the sound of the falling rain.","Noah did not turn his head to acknowledge her. He did not even shift his gaze toward the companion who served as the very foundation of his power, his posture remaining as fixed and immutable as a mountain of cold, crystalline light.","| Boundless.|","BOOM!","The word did not emerge from his throat in a human cadence, but manifested directly in the air, framed by the vertical bars of an authority that surpassed the system’s own notifications.","It was a statement that carried the weight of a being who had finally succeeded in his greatest fear...the fear that as a finite being, if he truly embodied Infinity, the small, defining traits of \"Noah Osmont\" would be washed away by the tide.","He stood now as a vessel that had been emptied of the finite and filled with the Absolute, his previous worries about his own humanity appearing as distant and irrelevant as the concerns of an ant beneath the gaze of a star.","Beside THE Infiniverse, Ruination’s figure solidified, her eyes wide as she observed the terrifying concentration of authority now radiating from him. Without a word of instruction, Noah moved.","HUUM!","His existence blazed with waves of crystalline Infinity that pulsed outward in synchronized ripples, and he stretched out his power in a manner that was both beautiful and horrifying to behold.","His massive Hadean Pillar of Infinity rose from the multicolored sea, a boundless pillar of support that seemed to pierce through the very ceiling of this reality, its civilizations humming with a resonance that shook the foundations of the Three Thousand Realms!","With a gesture that lacked any of his former dramatic flair, Noah unleashed a tidal wave of Quintessence Infiniforce and Observable Force, interlaced with the newly blooming, corrosive brilliance of his Infinite Radiation.","He was not merely building the remaining half of THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds; he was forcing them into existence through sheer existential weight.","He wrapped his power around the entirety of THE Infiniverse, folding the dimensions with a speed that defied calculation, the space around them twisting and tucking into recursive loops that vanished into the infinitesimal.","THE Infiniverse and Ruination watched as the vast expanse of the internal reality was suddenly, completely, and irrevocably hidden behind the paradoxical weavings of the manifolds, the structure settling into a state of total dimensional concealment.","...!","Ruination began to flicker, her internal protocols automatically preparing to announce the completion of the monumental task.","|THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds have been successfully-|","|I know.|","BOOM!","Noah’s voice cut through her notification, colder and more certain than any data she could provide.","He stepped forward, his eyes with their rotating lemniscate pupils finally settling on the void.","|The configuration is total. THE Gilded Lifeforms will find only the absence of observation where we dwell. I shall now begin the design of Miniature Causes, relying upon the weight of our Absolute Infinity to induce and accelerate the transformation of THE Infiniverse into a genuine Observable Existence. This action shall lead to a Quintessential harvest of thr highest magnitude at this moment.|","The logic was flawless, the ambition terrifying, and the delivery devoid of the human excitement that usually accompanied his breakthroughs.","Ruination looked at him, her composure wavering as she voiced the question that had been haunting their shared connection since he bloomed from the cocoon.","\" Master... are you... you? You were worried that if you ever bathed yourself too fully in the infinite, that the finite man named Noah Osmont would cease to be.\"","Noah finally turned, his gaze passing through them as if they were as transparent as the rain of the Pluvial Epoch, his figure radiating a pressure that made the very air groan.","|I am me, and I have always... been me. I am merely unbound from the lesser worries of a fragile perspective. I am free.|","BOOM!","The declaration rolled outward like a thunderclap of absolute truth, shaking the newly folded dimensions of THE Infiniverse as Noah stood at the center of his hidden empire, a being of Boundless Infinity!"]},{"number":5169,"title":"Chapter 5169: Chapter 5168: Reign IV","paragraphs":["The architecture of a nascent Observable Existence is not governed by the slow, grinding gears of natural evolution, but by the decisive imposition of a higher will that treats the laws of physics as...well,mere suggestions to be rewritten.","To transition a space from a mere collection of realms into a genuine Observable Existence requires more than just time and space; it requires the introduction of catastrophic developmental pressures that force the substrate of reality to expand, adapt, and solidify at a rate that defies the very concept of gradualism.","This could be achieved by Miniature Causes...in the form of the intentional ignition of existential flashpoints that serve as the catalysts for a reality’s maturation, ensuring that what was once a protected internal sanctuary becomes a sovereign expanse capable of standing against the weight of the outer Existence.","In the center of the folded dimensions of THE Infiniverse, Noah stood as the architect of this accelerated epoch, his hands moving with the rhythmic grace of a conductor directing a symphony of fundamental forces. Boundless rivers of multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce converged between his palms, swirling into dense, vibrating spheres of raw potential that hummed with the resonance of Absolute Infinity.","He did not speak with the breath of a man, but with the authority of Infinity itself, his words manifesting in the air as bars of immutable command.","|The Paleocene-Eocene Thermal Infinimum.|","As he voiced the designation, a sphere of searing, white-gold brilliance erupted from his hands and shot outward into the heights of the radiant sky.","This Miniature Cause was designed to unleash a wave of warming infinity and torrential, nutrient-rich storms across the Three Thousand Realms, raising the ambient temperature of existence to a point of hyper-stimulation that would cause the growth rate of every realm and every physical structure to increase by a hundred times.","| The Cretaceous Infinite Revolution.|","A second sphere, this one pulsing with the deep violet and gold of structural upheaval, followed the first. It carried the authority to trigger a profound shift in the geological and existential foundations of THE Infiniverse, forcing the realms to diversify their environments and refine their spatial boundaries, ensuring that the architecture of this reality possessed the complexity required of a genuine Observable Existence.","| The Mousterian Pluvial.|","The third manifestation took the form of a serene, crystalline blue light that carried the scent of rain and the weight of untapped vitality. Upon its activation, the humidity of the entire existence reached a state of perfect saturation, allowing for the expansion of populations, plants, microbes, and wildlife and all other forms of life at a pace that mimicked the uncontrolled blooming of a spring that would never end!","THE Infiniverse and Ruination watched as these Miniature Causes reached their respective zeniths and broke apart, spreading across THE Infiniverse in rolling waves of transformative authority.","In the sandy gold Realm of Dreams, the effects of the Thermal Infinimum arrived first. The golden dunes, which had previously shifted in slow, languid patterns, began to boil with activity as the warming infinity sank into the grains!","The sky above the desert turned a deep, bruised purple as torrential storms of liquid mana began to fall, and where the rain touched the sand, massive structures of dreaming glass began to sprout like crystalline forests, growing hundreds of feet in minutes as the realm’s development bypassed eons of slow accumulation.","In the Early Veiled Shore, the Cretaceous Infinite Revolution and the Mousterian Pluvial converged to create a scene of terrifying abundance!","The plots of farmland, already teeming with Sacred Herbs, suddenly expanded as the very coastline of the golden sandy beaches pushed outward into the multicolored sea.","The herbs themselves began to evolve in real-time, their stalks thickening into translucent pillars of power while their leaves shimmered with the refined weavings of Infinity, the entire shoreline becoming a dense jungle of high-tier resources that thrummed with the heartbeat of Existence coming alive.","Every single Herb...became Infinite!","Deep within the Realm of Prana, the trees of Yggdrasil responded to the deluge of the Pluvial with a violent surge of vitality. Their roots tore through the domain to claim more territory while their canopies rose to brush against the firmament, the air becoming so thick with the essence of life that new species of iridescent wildlife began to manifest from the ambient energy, populating the emerald heights with a speed that made the concept of birth seem like a redundant relic of the past.","While the realms above underwent their frantic evolution, a second manifestation of THE Infiniverse appeared within the depths of Muspelheim, a place of crimson-gold fires and eternal heat.","Her gaze was filled with a clinical, singular purpose as she navigated the rivers of flame toward a region where a gathering of high-level entities resided.","There, Amelia Osmont sat in quiet conversation with THE Mnemonic Leviathan and the singular cognizance, THE Beholder. They turned as the humanoid manifestation approached.","\" Ma’am ,\" THE Infiniverse spoke, her voice carrying the firm resonance of her Master’s new state. \"I may need you to carry out a contingency plan Master left behind for us to carry out in the case things went wrong.\"","Amelia Osmont stood, her features tightening as a shadow of motherly worry crossed her gaze.","\" In the case things went wrong? \" Amelia asked, her voice trembling slightly. \" What... what has gone wrong?\"","THE Infiniverse did not hesitate, her movement appearing as a blur of motion that defied spatial distance. She placed her hand upon Amelia Osmont’s shoulder, her touch vibrating with a frequency that was no longer entirely compatible with the Bounded.","| Infinity.|","The word was whispered twice, a silent, terrifying echo that carried the weight of the change Noah had undergone.","| Infinity.|","HUUM!","As the word settled into Amelia’s mind, she felt the cold, boundless nature of infinity as she disappeared!","BOOM!","Soon after...","The atmosphere of Muspelheim, usually defined by the rhythmic crackle of crimson-gold fires, suddenly buckled under a pressure that did not belong to the elemental domain, as the space where the manifestation of THE Infiniverse and Amelia Osmont had stood was violated by a returning surge of multicolored light.","The two figures were deposited back into the heart of the flame-drenched realm with the violent precision of a reality-altering command, the vibrant waves of Infinity that accompanied their arrival washing over the molten landscape and silencing the roar of the eternal fires in a single, sweeping motion!","THE Infiniverse’s gaze became impossibly heavy as she felt the shift in the ambient environment, the effects of the newly ignited Miniature Causes now beginning to bleed into Muspelheim, turning the crimson heat into something refined, sharp, and terrifyingly efficient.","|I discussed contingencies with you during my lesser form.|","Noah’s voice erupted from the very fabric of the reality he now inhabited, his words booming with an imperious resonance!","| All that were considered contingencies are no longer contingencies. There is no requirement for you to attempt anything in this moment, as I shall deny access to all things. From this point forward, across every territory and every folded dimension we occupy, there shall only be the reign of boundless Infinity. Do you understand?|","The weight of the question was a declaration of a new, immutable law. The air itself seemed to vibrate with the frequency of his Absolute state, the multicolored light of his Quintessence Infiniforce painting the obsidian peaks of Muspelheim!","Amelia Osmont stood in the center of the surging light as she looked up somberly.","THE Infiniverse straightened her posture as she replied.","\" Yes. Master!\"","Without a further word, and without a single gesture of comfort for the woman who had birthed the man he used to be, THE Infiniverse disappeared again, her figure dissolving into the multicolored currents of the atmosphere.","There was no more room for secret plans.","There was no more room for the fear of loss or the caution of the Bounded.","There would only be boundless Infinity.","BOOM!"]},{"number":5170,"title":"Chapter 5170: Chapter 5169: Reign V","paragraphs":["At this moment, Ubergulden Adelheid had sent a portion of her consciousness into the vibrant Quintessence Infiniforce inside of her Existence as her expression was heavy, the pearlescent gold of her internal manifestation flickering with the tremors of a reality that had been fundamentally shaken by recent events.","The concept was anathema to everything she understood of the hierarchy, a violent violation of the natural order that suggested the foundations of THE Braneworld were not as immutable as THE Magna Sorora believed.","She struggled to reconcile the image of THE Creature she had known with the reality of a Young Relictus who had somehow tapped into THE Primordial Source, a wellspring of power that even THE Third Scale Gilded Ones could not access despite eons of dedicated pursuit.","She had all these questions as her direct access had not bothered to come here out of his own volition, his silence since the conclusion of their last exchange becoming a source of mounting anxiety that she could no longer ignore.","BOOM!","Multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce did not merely flow through the connection; it surged and increased in concentration with a tidal ferocity that suggested a dam had been shattered on the other side, seas of concentrated brilliance rushing out and flowing into her in an endless, unstoppable manner that she had never before experienced!","As the flood reached its zenith, the visage of Noah Osmont manifested within the center of the surge, his figure surrounded by an intense, crystalline light of infinity that made the surrounding space appear dim by comparison.","HUUM!","\" What happened down there? And what... what are you doing right now?!\"","|I am beginning to alter the nature of our relationship.|","The words vibrated through her foundations, holding the cold weight of a glorious verdict that left no room for negotiation or appeal.","Ubergulden Adelheid’s figure shook as the realization of his intent settled into her mind, the influx of his Infiniforce now so intense that it was beginning to manifest as visible rivers beneath her pearlescent skin, the multicolored light fighting for dominance against her natural gold.","\" Have you...fallen to the madness of infinity, Osmont? Has THE Gamaidjan finally claimed the mind of the one who thought he could outrun it? You are speaking like a being who has lost his anchor!\"","Noah’s reply was instantaneous as it carried the dry, terrifying cadence of his new state, dismissing her concern with the indifference of a mathematician correcting a trivial error.","He floated forward until he was inches away from her internal manifestation, his towering presence casting a multicolored shadow across her form as he looked down at her with a gaze that held no malice, yet possessed no warmth.","|Hold tight, Ubergulden Adelheid. You sought a Custos who could change the nature of the Gilded, and I am merely fulfilling the potential of your request. You will soon join me in the endless light of Infinity.|","---","She had lived through eons of manic shifts and chaotic siphoning, had navigated the turbulent seas of every conceivable sentiment across the Observable, but the realization that the emotional weavings of her fixation had been replaced by a void of absolute, clinical Infinity was a loss that felt far too big not just for her own fragile heart, but for the very fabric of existence itself!","But as she was wallowing in this loss, her knees pressed against the pale stone of the mountain’s ruins, she felt something bloom within her existence that defied the forced dormancy of her bindings. When she blinked and focused her internal perception, she saw that an unknown and unfathomable construct had actually managed to bypass everything and enter the deepest reaches of her foundations, manifesting within her internal seas of emotion as an illusory crimson-blue holographic figure that carried the faint, unmistakable glow of her Fixation’s authority!"]},{"number":5171,"title":"Chapter 5171: Chapter 5170: Reign VI","paragraphs":["Time seemingly became stretched toward infinity and slowed down at this moment, the falling dust of the mountain freezing in mid-air and the roar of the distant Wyld fading into a singular, pressurized point of absolute stillness.","The holographic image to appear within Emotive was actually Ruination, with her manifesting with an urgency that stripped away her usual detachment, her eyes reflecting the swirling chaos of Emotive’s interior world as she gazed at the manic being’s consciousness.","|We do not have much time.|","|The Master pushed himself a bit far and entered a temporary state of Absolute Infinity that needs a concentrated ignition of raw emotional resonance to stabilize and return him to his old self. Other options have become nonviable, and maybe the most chaotic, intense weavings of emotions in all of Observable Existence may be enough to allow Master to regain control. I can take whatever you give and infuse it directly within him, allowing for a temporary instant of Infinity where he can anchor himself back to who he was. For his sake... what will you give? He would need everything you can give as his Infinity is currently too encompassing. What... can you give?|","Emotive was shocked as the magnitude of the situation settled into her mind, the realization that her Fixation’s \"boundless\" state was actually a dangerous imbalance that threatened to consume the man she adored, and because she was told there was no time, her decision was already made in an instant that required no deliberation!","She trembled with a sudden, violent conviction as her manifestation within her own body reached out and plunged her hand into her chest, the illusory flesh parting without resistance as she grasped the very core of her being.","She pulled out a heart burning with a blinding, kaleidoscopic emotion that defied classification, the organ pulsing with the concentrated intensity of every joy, every rage, and every obsessive fixation she had ever siphoned across her long existence.","Tears began to fall from her face in heavy, translucent tracks as she smiled with a heartbreaking mixture of sorrow and triumph, looking at the holographic image of Ruination with eyes that had finally found their singular purpose.","\" For him, I give my Everything ,\" she whispered, her voice cracking under the weight of the gift.","HUUM!","\" All my emotions, all my intensity, all the chaos I have ever claimed... I give my very Heart.\"","BOOM!","Boundless emotions converged in the pulsing multicolored heart, the organ expanding and contracting with a frequency that threatened to shatter the mental space they occupied. Ruination looked at Emotive’s smiling, teary face, seeing the terrifying conviction of a manic being, and she reached out to grasp the heart with hands that shone with a blinding, white-gold light of Hadean authority.","Ruination bellowed out a command that shook the folded dimensions of their connection, waves of Infinity cascading around her in violent, recursive loops as she utilized her intrinsic link with her Master to open a channel that should not have existed.","She prepared to infuse the most potent and boundless emotions from a single wild being in all of Observable Existence, a tide of raw, unadulterated feeling that acted as a searing brand against the cold perfection of Noah’s Absolute state, flooding into her Master with the intent to drown the Infinite in the return of the Finite!","BOOM!","An explosion of utmost brilliance and incandescence exploded out right after, the light of glory tearing through the silence of THE Wyld and the hidden depths of THE Infiniverse simultaneously, as the heart of a manic being was offered up to save the soul of a King. Of a Tyrannical Emperor!","HUUM!","---","It felt like a truly long incandescent dream that he was actively participating in, a state of existence where the boundaries between his will and the fundamental forces of the existence had dissolved into a singular, shimmering continuity.","He could not quite explain the sensation with the vocabulary of his previous experiences, for while he was still himself in the most foundational sense of his identity, he felt as though there was a corrective weaving applied to his thoughts and actions that dictated every movement with a terrifying, glorious efficiency.","In this state, he had operated without the interference of emotions, his decisions bypassing the messy filtration of sentiment to achieve the most optimal outcomes across every theater of his influence.","The rapid completion of THE Infinite Calabi-Yau Manifolds, the intricate design of the new Miniature Causes that now accelerated his Infiniverse, the clinical dismissal of his mother’s and THE Infiniverse’s concerns, and even his ongoing, aggressive restructuring of Ubergulden Adelheid’s very nature had all been executed with the cold grace of a calculated choices.","In this influx state of Infinity, he had carried out actions that he would normally hesitate to perform, yet throughout the entire process, a small, receding part of his consciousness had told itself that he could simply leave this state whenever he wished, that the transition was a tool rather than a destination.","But now, as he attempted to reach for the familiar anchors of his finite self, that certainty began to waver under the sheer volume of the Absolute.","’ Now, that’s not too good...’","The thought echoed through his mind with a dry, detached cadence, for the boundless Infinity permeating within him was making his own thoughts not want to return to the limitations of the past.","Because why should he?","At this moment, his own Quintessence Infiniforce was actively beginning a process that felt as patient as it was inevitable, a transformation that sought to rewrite everything about him from a finite being into something else entirely...a being whose scale was so vast that the concept of an individual \"Noah\" became a redundant rounding error.","He had theorized this possibility, understanding that a finite being did not possess the same worries or priorities as an infinite being, and that they were fundamentally different configurations of existence that could not coexist without one eventually subsuming the other.","He realized with a chilling clarity that as long as he did not let go of his finite self, he would never truly live up to the full potential of Infinity, yet if he did let go, the man who had started this journey would be lost to the brilliance of the Absolute; in his hands, Infinity would always be limited by his refusal to disappear.","He sighed within the silence of his crystalline mind, the sound a faint ripple in a sea of almost perfection, and he prepared to pull the biggest contingency he had placed upon himself to shatter this state of apathy before it became permanent, when all of a sudden...","BOOM!","He shockingly felt an influx of unfathomably intense, manic emotions surge from his connection with Infinity, a tide of raw, unadulterated chaos that defied the clinical geometry of his current thoughts.","These emotions were so ridiculously intense and crazy, so filled with a singular, obsessive intensity, that the blinding calm and the near-perfection of his Absolute state were suddenly, violently overwhelmed!","The cold efficiency of his mind buckled under the weight of a manic emotions, and Noah did not hesitate, his Quintessential command erupting with the full force of his remaining will as he seized the surge of feeling!","He moved tyrannically, acting with the predatory precision of a king reclaiming a stolen throne, as he channeled the entire flood of manic resonance and infinity directly toward his Hadean Organ of Civilization, using the heat of those emotions to burn through the glazed crystalline shell that had formed around his consciousness!","HUUM!","The process was boundlessly glorious, the internal collision of Absolute Infinity and absolute emotion producing a resonance that shook the very foundation of his internal reality, forcing the dimensions to stabilize and the clinical apathy to recede like a tide before a rising sun.","He took a crystalline core of this apathy and sealed it within his Hadean Organ of Civilization!","Moments later, his body seated at the core of THE Infiniverse and surrounded by the endless multicolored seas infinity, let out a long, ragged breath that carried the warmth of returning life.","He blinked his eyes, and the glazed crystalline glare that had defined them for the past hour rapidly dissolved, replaced by the sharp, calculating, and viscerally human light that had always been his trademark.","He felt the weight of his own skin again, the familiar pressure of his own memories and personality that had nearly been lost to the boundless.","Before him, the figures of THE Infiniverse and Ruination gazed at him with bright, expectant eyes, their forms flickering with the residual energy of the stabilization.","Ruination stepped forward, her illusory features softening as she breathed a profound sigh of relief that seemed to echo through the system itself.","\" Welcome back, Master.\"","Noah looked at his hands, seeing the multicolored light dimmed tremendously but still dancing there.","He smiled, a slow, dark expression that held all the tyranny and ambition of the man who had defied THE Gilded Ones!","A Reign of Infinity was brought to an end in an extremely short period of time!"]},{"number":5172,"title":"Chapter 5172: Chapter 5171: Ashes to Ashes, Dust to Dust! I","paragraphs":["Noah stood at the center of THE Infiniverse, his gaze lingering on the vibrant, multicolored seas that churned with a restlessness he now recognized.","He looked at his hands, sensing the profound and terrifying weight of the power coursing around him, a current of Absolute Infinity that still hummed with the cold, efficient geometry of the state he had just narrowly escaped.","With a slow, deliberate exhale that carried the weight of a man reclaiming his soul, he finished thr process and actively began to draw that boundless pressure inward, compressing the staggering density of the Absolute into his Hadean Organ of Civilization.","​The transition was not a simple storage of energy, but a structural rewriting of his very foundation as the organ buckled and then hardened under the influx, its purpose evolving to match the paradoxical nature of its new contents.","​\" Ruination.\"","​He called out the name with warmth, acknowledging the one he had nearly blacklisted during his descent into the apathetic void. Ruination stepped forward from the shimmering air, a soft, relieved smile gracing her illusory features as she waved her hand, causing a cascade of prompts to bloom before his eyes.","​|Due to your active rejection of the clinical completeness of Absolute Infinity, your existence has compressed the influx into THE Hadean Organ of Civilization.|","|THE Hadean Organ of Civilization is undergoing a permanent structural metamorphosis to also become THE Absolute Forge of Infinity.|","|A paradoxical state has been achieved: Nearu Absolute Infinity.|","| As a finite being, your own scope and perspective act as a natural ceiling to the boundless; you are the limitation that prevents Infinity from being absolute. Until a form of solution can be attained to bridge this existential gap, Nearu Absolute Infinity shall be utilized and mediated exclusively through your Organ, THE Absolute Forge of Infinity.|","Noah read the prompts and sighed, the sound echoing through the vastness of THE Infiniverse, for he understood the irony with the crystalline clarity of his Hadean mind.","His own being was a limitation to the power he wielded, yet even with that knowledge, he felt no regret for his choice. He did not wish to become a cosmic automaton, a robot of progression for whom the journey held no value beyond the destination, because what he loved about existence was the raw and unadulterated wonder of it all!","He lived for the exploration, the crushing adversity, the searing pain of growth, and the exquisite pleasure of victory, and other...forms of pleasure, and to lose those things was to lose the very reason he had reached for the stars in the first place.","He realized now that he could still carry the efficiency and ruthlessness of that Absolute state within him, utilizing it as a tool when necessary without sacrificing himself.","And when it came to sacrifices...","He felt something deep within the newly formed Absolute Forge, the manic engine of emotions that was THE Heart of Emotive, which had served as the signal flare to bring him back from the brink of total self-extinction.","He thought of the sacrifice she had made, a woman he had historically viewed with a mixture of distaste and suspicion, yet who had given her everything to ensure his return regardless of the cost.","\" I’ll be back,\" he murmured to the two manifestations beside him.","His body flickered and disappeared, warping through the dimensions with a speed that left the multicolored seas rippling in his wake, and he reappeared at the base of the mountain in THE Wyld with his feet settling onto the pale and cracked stone as he looked down at the figure on the ground.","Emotive was there, her manic violet hair muted and her eyes filled with a desolation that seemed to have aged her eons in a single hour, but when she looked up and saw him, her expression changed with a staggering and visceral intensity.","Her eyes opened wide, tracing the contours of his face and searching the depth of his pupils for the return of that vibrant and tyrannical spark she had feared lost forever.","When she confirmed it, when she saw the return of the Noah who could still look at her coldly and tyrannically, she did not hesitate!","She surged from the ground with her body practically becoming a blur as she threw herself toward him, wrapping her arms around him in a grip so tight it would have crushed a Rhyacian Proterozoic Scale entitiy!","\"I thought your brilliance was gone forever!\"","She wailed, her voice thick with tears and a manic relief that shook her entire body!","Noah looked down at the woman currently clinging to his body, and his internal reactions were a conflicted.","As he had seen her coming, his first thought had been to instinctively smack her away, much as he had done in the mountain of Alfheimr, and he had even begun to raise a hand to stop the collision, but he found himself unable to carry it out!","Despite her faults and her history and her irritating manic nature, this woman had plunged her hand into her own chest and surrendered her very heart to him when she truly did not have to.","He sighed, the movement causing her to grip him even tighter, and instead of a strike, he found his hand settling atop her head in a slow and patient pat.","Beside them, Anaximander rose from the stone and shook his head incredulously.","Emotive blinked, her manic emotions blooming wildly at the touch, and she slowly let him go while moving back with a sudden and flustered start.","\" Ah, my apologies, Sir! I was just taken away by... huh?\"","She stopped mid-sentence, raising her hand in confusion as she began to make small and bewildered sounds, for multicolored Infinity began to rise from her form in terrifyingly dense concentrations and her existence radiated a profound aura that seemed to mirror Noah’s own.","Noah had to sigh again as he looked at her, his Hadean perception already tracing the source of the anomaly.","Just how the hell was this woman so lucky?","Because her Heart, the very core of her Civilization and her claim to Chaos, was currently residing within his Absolute Forge of Infinity, it was being bathed in the boundless currents of the Absolute, and by extension her existence was being dragged upward along his own path while forced into a metamorphosis that neither of them had anticipated.","BOOM!"]},{"number":5173,"title":"Chapter 5173: Chapter 5172: Ashes to Ashes, Dust to Dust! II","paragraphs":["\"What is HAPPENING?!\" Emotive yelled, her hair cycling through colors so fast it looked like a strobe light of emotional instability!","HUUM!","|The subject, THE Living Emotive, has been bound under the banner of Nearu Absolute Infinity through the residence of her Heart within THE Absolute Forge of Infinity.|","|An unforeseen mutation has been triggered: THE Absolute Amaranthine Heart of Emotive is being born.|","|Through this bridge of Infinity and Emotion, Egos of Sins and Virtues are being forged rapidly and with extreme intensity. Their software is being recorded as they form.|","BOOM!","Emotive’s figure became surrounded by a swirling storm of boundless Infinity as she let out a cry of startled power, and Noah looked at her manic and glowing form with a weary shake of his head while thinking of the complexity of the Egos he had labored to design in his sandbox, and the ridiculous jump in power Emotive was about to have.","Truly, how could someone be so lucky?","He shook his head.","Since he remembered the cold efficiency and pragmatism his other self that was filled with boundless infinity moved with, Noah sought to do the same as while he monitored the wriggling figure of Emotive in the air, he pulled from the Nearu Absolute Infinity within his Organ of Civilization as an instant later, a shimmering distortion in the air behind him coalesced into a crystalline version of himself.","This figure looked like a lesser version of how he had appeared when he held the weight of Absolute Infinity, his skin translucent and humming with the resonance of a thousand different civilizations, and his eyes held a glazed blue depth that suggested a mind operating on the cold logic of the boundless.","He called this a Nearu Absolute Clone, a construct that inherited the terrifying pragmatic efficiency of his Absolute state while retaining just enough of his emotional core to serve as a perfect extension of his will across the battlefield of reality.","Right now, it began to move as he sought to finish things off after the disastrous move by Sororis Prima Elzyana, for he had no intention of allowing those who had challenged him to hide behind the chaos of the Gilded distribution.","Noah looked out toward the horizon of the fractured domain, his voice echoing out.","\" My own personal Infinity has covered THE Wyld and continues to stretch out across Observable Existence, permeating the very weavings that you thought would protect you. I know exactly where you are, O Deliverance, and I know exactly how small your Civilization has become now that the shadows of the Gilded have fallen upon it.\"","HUUM!","The Nearu Absolute Clone moved with a grace that bypassed the traditional concepts of travel, dipping into the sea of infinity that now painted the skies above THE Wyld and disappearing from the mountain base in a single, silent flicker.","In the next moment, it dipped out of the multicolored tide in a distant region of the Wyld, a place where the landscape was composed of floating landmasses held together by shimmering bridges of liquid Observable Force.","This region was a sanctuary for the elite, filled with the powerful auras of Primordial Architects who had spent eons cultivating their authority, and yet the air here was thick with the scent of stagnation and fear as the Gilded bindings tightened their hold on the inhabitants.","Noah’s clone calmly floated toward the central island of this archipelago, a landmass filled with platinum-colored trees whose multicolored leaves rustled with the energy of the profound, but at its very center sat the titanic figure of THE Deliverance.","He was a grand and muscular platinum titan, a being who ruled these reaches with an iron hand, and yet right now he was staring at his hands blankly because the bindings of Sororis Prima Elzyana had wrapped around him just like they had wrapped around every other Bounded Lifeform.","This entity, who likely stood to be stronger than any Ediacaran Proterozoic Scale entity in the history of the Wyld, now held a look of desolation that spoke of a king who had realized his throne was made of nothing but dust!","Noah’s clone descended toward the seated titan, his feet never touching the ground as he loomed before the despondent ruler, and he spoke with a cadence that allowed no room for the vanity of conversation.","\" Normally, I might talk and then listen and yap back and forth while reflecting on the heavy irony of how we arrived at this point, but I find that my patience for such cycles has been exhausted by the scale of my new horizons. You declared a Civilizational Holy War meant to corner me and enslave my people, believing that you possessed the authority to dictate the terms of my existence, but you will not even live to see that holy war, nor will it ever happen. From now on and for the foreseeable future, there shall only be an endless shroud of infinity that swallows the legacy you thought was eternal.\"","As he spoke, an incandescent blue flame bloomed within the palm of the clone’s hand, a fire filled with the paradoxical density of Nearu Absolute Infinity that formed into a blinding fireball flashing with a crystalline light.","Without a second gesture, the fireball multiplied until the skies above all the floating landmasses were filled with thousands of identical blue suns, each one pulsing with the resonance of a power that could burn away the foundations of THE Proterozoic.","Noah’s clone gazed at the architecture of the Primordial Architects, his eyes cold and unmoving as he delivered the final verdict!","\" Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.\"","HUUM!","A fireball burning with a semblance of Absolute Infinity was a terrifying evolution of the simple skill he had used eons ago when he was merely a man killing apes and wolves inside the stone corridors of dungeons.","Years later, those same flames had been refined through the forge of a Hadean heart, and they now descended with the inevitability of a dying Primordial Realm to burn Primordial Architects en masse.","The glorious scene of the fireballs descending was a symphony of blue light and total erasure, and when one came into contact with THE Deliverance, his entire platinum body was shrouded in blue flames that did not merely burn his flesh but unwove his very causality.","Only now did the titan raise his head to meet Noah’s eyes, and for a singular, crystalline moment, they shared a look of absolute coldness as the ruler of the Wyld realized the sheer scale of the being he had tried to challenge.","A moment after they shared this look, THE Deliverance turned to ash, his muscular frame dissolving into a cloud of grey soot that was swept away by the wind of the explosion.","Ashes to ashes, dust to dust!"]},{"number":5174,"title":"Chapter 5174: Chapter 5173: Hey, Look At Us! I","paragraphs":["While the fires of his retribution claimed the floating landmasses of THE Wyld and the Primordial Architects who had sought a Civilizational Holy War were reduced to insignificant drifts of ash, the focus of Noah remained divided across the vast distances of his reach.","Around this same time, he was focusing a significant portion of his consciousness that had traversed the profound connection toward Ubergulden Adelheid, and he was currently flooding her existence with a tidal wave of Quintessence Infiniforce that defied the previous limits of their shared bond.","Inside the intricate and golden weavings of her existence, the manifestations of Ubergulden Adelheid and Noah stood at the center of a surging multicolored flood, the density of the Infiniforce so great that it threatened to drown the ambient Observable Force of her domain.","Ubergulden Adelheid gazed at him with a look that remained heavy and cold, yet her expression shifted into a silent and narrow focus as she observed a fundamental change in his presence.","She witnessed the transition as the cold and imperious gaze of the Absolute began to thaw, the crystalline blue light of his lemniscate pupils receding into the depths of his eyes to be replaced by the sharp and dark calmness and amusement.","As the last remnants of the clinical void vanished from his features, Noah looked at her and offered a brief and measured cough to clear the heavy silence of the chamber before he finally spoke.","\"Apologies, I had... a little episode there and initiated a process that required a certain degree of cognitive exclusion.\"","Ubergulden Adelheid did not immediately soften her posture, and her gaze remained clinical and cold as she looked him up and down while processing the return of his vibrant and tyrannical personality.","\"I put a lot on the line for you, and I have risked the status of my House and my own continuation,\" she said, her voice carrying the sharp edge of a being who had been genuinely unsettled by his recent transformation.","\" Can you not be trusted to remain himself? Has the weight of Infinity already begun to affect you in this manner, and will it happen randomly during the most critical moments of our ascent? I need to know if we are still able to have our arrangement, and perhaps more importantly, I need to know why...you are still flooding my existence with this intensity of Infinity if you have truly returned to yourself.\"","Noah met her flood of questions with a calm and unhurried composure, his figure radiating a sense of grounded power that felt even more dangerous than the cold apathy that had preceded it.","\" Our...arrangement can certainly continue as this was not some episodic madness that will happen again, but rather a singular reboot of my system. I just made a major jump in power and had to reconfigure my foundations to account for the new architecture, and in the end, this development is quite good for you because my current standing should likely exceed the Transitional Cambrian stage between THE Second Scale and THE Third Scale.\"","WAA!","\"If my calculations are correct, I may even be approaching the threshold of THE Third Scale in raw power, which means the Custos you are bound with is that much more formidable than the one you initially agreed to support.\"","He paused as the multicolored rivers continued to swirl around them, the concentration of the Infiniforce beginning to settle into a more manageable but still immense rhythm.","He was relentlessly flooding it in!","\" As for why I have not stopped this flow of Infinity, the answer is simply that since the process has begun, there is no...logical reason to stop it. It should be very beneficial to you as I have steadied the current so that you can use and distribute it freely through your own weavings, and with this substance, with my Absolute Infinity...I will ensure you become a truly formidable Gilded One who stands apart from the rest of your people.\"","BOOM!","His words caused Ubergulden Adelheid to fall silent as she continued to stare at him with a cold and calculating intensity, her mind clearly weighing the potential of his new power against the risk he represented.","\" THE Creature ...\" she murmured, her thoughts turning toward the news that was even now rippling through the higher reaches of the Braneworld.","Noah smiled and gave a light nod as he acknowledged the mention of his companion.","\" A ridiculous being, truly. I had no idea he would have gained such direct access to THE Primordial Source, but because of his actions, the immediate matters in Observable Existence are wrapped up in a little bow. Sororis Prima Elzyana burned all of Observable Existence with her bindings, and with the chaos caused, I wondered if you have had any difficulty in doing what we talked about before. You mentioned a Sororis from THE Magna Sorora would be helping you with the fabrications, but the one I met today, Sororis Prima Elzyana, let me know that the members of that Sisterhood are a handful to deal with.\"","...!","Ubergulden Adelheid looked at him coldly before she closed her eyes for a long and patient moment, her focus turning inward as if she were confirming the status of her plans through the burning Infinity currently coursing through her foundations at elevated concentrations.","After she had confirmed whatever she needed to see, she looked back at Noah with an expression that suggested she was fully committing to a difficult decision.","\" Even with all the chaos that has descended upon the lower domains, everything has been accomplished on my end. In fact, the chaos made certain aspects of the fabrication easier since there are currently multiple Gilded Ones who will be making their entry into Observable Existence to manage the aftermath of the Relictus appearance. You must wait in the Wandering Territories, and sometime within the next hour, I will send a Sororis for you to begin the transfer. You have a flare for the dramatics, so make sure that you are not doing anything too obvious to be caught, because with a Relictus appearing from down there, the Gilded Ones will keep a much closer gaze on everything happening.\"","...!"]},{"number":5175,"title":"Chapter 5175: Chapter 5174: Hey, Look At Us! II","paragraphs":["She spoke those words calmly, and Noah gave a light nod while thinking about the boundless personal Infinity he was spreading out across the Wyld.","He was already beginning to make that Infinity invisible, the multicolored brilliance slowly transforming to become the endless Blue that would appear like natural and ambient Infinity to any external observer!","At the same time, his domain of THE Infiniverse had been fully covered and hidden from prying eyes through the enactment of the manifolds, making it a separate and sovereign existence that would be extremely difficult for any Gilded Ones to ever discover.","He sought to see the emergence of his own Observable Existence from his Infinite Cause, and when that finally occurred, he knew that he would truly begin to play with the fundamental arrangements of power.","Noah moved toward the seated Ubergulden Adelheid and extended his hand with a dark and knowing smile, and she looked at the hand and then at him with a lingering coldness before she finally raised her own hand to grasp his.","As he pulled her up from her meditative position, Noah looked at her with a gaze that held the full weight of their shared trajectory.","\" Hey, look at us. Who would have thought after all of these days and eons that we would be standing where we are right now, and who could even imagine the heights where we will be standing just a few days from now? Be ready, Ubergulden Adelheid. Be ready.\"","HUUM!","With those parting words, the manifestation of Noah dissipated into a flurry of multicolored Infinity, leaving Ubergulden Adelheid alone within her own weavings.","The coldness slowly faded from her eyes as she watched the last flickers of his presence vanish, and she quickly returned to a meditative position to regulate her existence while the seas of Infinity roared around her with a renewed and terrifying vigor!","---","In the vast and unfathomable expanse of existence, whether one considers the most mundane reality where beings without a single drop of Mana wage desperate wars with stone and steel or the grandest realms where titans play with the very fabric of Infinity while manipulating the complex weavings of reality, the principle of connection remains a critical and deciding constant.","It is an observation that holds true across every scale of development that connections make the act of existing and ascending significantly easier, for if a being manages to know the right person at the right moment, they can obtain an unbelievable edge over the rest of existence that no amount of solitary labor could ever hope to replicate.","A connection is a bridge that bypasses the traditional requirements of time and effort, permitting a sovereign being to reach across the chasms of classification to grasp opportunities that would otherwise remain forever out of reach for those who walk their paths alone.","---","As he took care of the many lingering requirements of his current position, Noah continued to monitor the terrifying changes blooming within his Hadean Organ of Civilization, which had now also taken on the paradoxical role of a terrifying forge that he had compressed Absolute Infinity into.","He considered this configuration to be nothing more than a temporary measure that permitted him to maintain his sanity and his selfhood, for he understood with the clinical clarity of his new architecture that a solution had to be found in the future or he would forever remain a finite being who limited the very Infinity he sought to embody.","And what a sad thing that would be!","He was currently a vessel that was too small for its contents, a situation that forced him to utilize THE Absolute Forge of Infinity to mediate a power that his own scope could not yet fully encompass without risking the loss of his identity to the boundless tide.","While he remained anchored in his thoughts, he watched the scattered ash of the Primordial Architects as it drifted through the air of THE Wyld, and he observed the golden bubbles of Hadean Singularities that flowed from the remains as a form of existential loot.","These singularities held the concentrated weavings of their memories and their civilizations along with all the immensity and weight they had carried within their existences, allowing Noah to absorb the totality of their eons without having to physically traverse through their Palaces.","It was a seamless and efficient harvest that allowed him to sort through boundless weavings of information in real time, yet even as he processed this influx, he felt a glimmer of something unique that caused him to become serious right away.","Above him, the atmosphere rippled with the blooming of multicolored flames that could only originate from a single being across the current landscape of the Observable.","These flames were veiled with a heavy obsidian light of terrifying power and immensity that suggested a proximity to THE Primordial Source that few could comprehend, and as they unfurled, the voice of none other than THE Creature echoed through the region!","\" A parting gift for me to you,\" the voice spoke, sounding as though it were being carried by the very flames themselves.","\" The main part of my existence rejected the idea of doing this because it goes against the principles of adversity I have lived by, but I have learned that sometimes we can go against what our existence fully believes if the situation demands it, or perhaps that is merely the excuse I told myself to be able to take this action that I normally would not permit. Do with the gift what you want, but I thought it would be helpful for the path you have chosen to walk.\"","It was a gift that THE Creature had not wanted to give because it violated his fundamental belief in the necessity of struggle, yet the multicolored flames opened up to reveal a sight that caused the air to hum with a saturated golden authority!","Within the obsidian light lay a terrifying and pulsing golden heart accompanied by a network of complex golden vessels and capillaries, and Noah recognized them instantly as the pieces of a Gilded One that THE Creature had carved out from the existence of Aurelius Maximus!","These were the biological and existential anchors of a being of the Superbius House, and they began to burn with a terrifying allure of power the moment they were unveiled to the ambient atmosphere.","Noah’s gaze became heavy as he recognized the magnitude of what had been placed before him, for these were the literal foundations of a Gilded Lifeform that could be used to bridge the gap between his own Hadean engineering and the reality of THE Braneworld!","He quickly waved his hands to summon a sea of multicolored Infinity that rose like a vibrant tide to envelop the golden remnants, and he pulled the entirety of the gift into the depths of his own existence!","HUUM!"]},{"number":5176,"title":"Chapter 5176: Chapter 5175: Ego I","paragraphs":["Existence is a series of punctuations, a collection of moments where the steady rhythm of the mundane is interrupted by the violent imposition of the extraordinary, yet among the many shifts that bloomed across the vastness of the Observable and Unobservable, there remained a specific category of upheaval that commanded the attention of even the most ancient and knowledgeable beings.","There are debates every now and then between those who have witnessed the turn of eons, but most tend to agree that the point of greatest change occured when a Relictus emerged from a place they had never emerged from before, for that was the singular spark that set the ball of Existence rolling towards weavings that no one could have anticipated, leading to an era of upheaval and glorious immensity that defied every established scale of progress!","---","The Nearu Absolute Clone materialized in a region of THE Wyld defined by an endless expanse of dazzling snow, the crystalline flakes falling in a silent and heavy rhythm that sought to bury the evidence of the violence beneath a layer of pristine white.","Naldine Manthon sat upon the obscenely fat and golden shoulders of the greed-personified Midas, her radiant white hair flowing behind her like a river of ivory and gold while her singularity-dotted eyes tracked the descent of the flakes with a heavy and detached melancholy that suggested she had already witnessed enough upheaval for a single existence.","Midas remained stationary as a mountain of golden muscle and excess, his blue-gold wings folded tightly against his frame while the golden rings of Greed orbited his limbs in a slow and patient rotation that kept the accumulating snow from settling upon his skin.","Around them, the corpses of four Primordial Architects were scattered across the frozen ground, their once-grand existences reduced to cold and silent monuments that were rapidly being claimed by the accumulation of the snow, their authority extinguished in the same clinical manner that the Gilded had intended for every Bounded Lifeform.","Naldine absent-mindedly released her hands from Midas’s shoulders to have the snow land on her palm, watching as the heat of her Hadean physiology caused the crystalline structure to dissolve into a tiny drop of moisture while the ambient silence of the region pressed against her foundations.","Noah’s Nearu Absolute Clone appeared before them with the silent grace of a ghost, his figure radiating a soft and multicolored brilliance that cast long shadows across the white terrain, and Naldine looked up at him with an expression that held a profound sense of sorrow as she spoke.","\" You finally came looking for me? \" she asked. \"I would ask you what happened out there, but I can assume from the way the everything has been overwritten that the conclusion was...as grand as your aspirations.\"","Noah offered an assuring smile as he floated over toward her, his presence bringing a sudden and comforting warmth to the frozen air that seemed to push back the desolate chill of the region, and he leaned forward to press a gentle kiss against her forehead.","He could sense that she was partially bounded by the clinical and suffocating actions of Sororis Prima Elzyana, her internal architecture struggling against the bindings and the forced dormancy of her Civilization.","\" Let’s get those bindings fully off of you first,\" he said softly, his authority rising to meet the golden pressure within her skin.","HUUM!","He waved his hand to summon a sea of multicolored Infinity that rose from the snowy ground like a vibrant and rising tide, wrapping Naldine and Midas in a protective and irresistible embrace before taking them away toward the hidden sanctuary of his own making where the rules of the Gilded held no sway!","He took them towards THE Infiniverse!","---","In a different area on that vast mountain in THE Wyld where the ruins of the temple remained as silent witnesses to the afternoon’s carnage, Noah, Emotive, and Anaximander remained beneath a sky that was now fully claimed by the invisible brilliance of infinity- one that would seem like any of the common seas of endless potential permeating in potent regions of Observable Existence!","Noah observed the image of THE Living Emotive as she floated in the air while boundless Infinity surged around her existence, her figure dancing manically within the shifting currents of a transformation that had been forced upon her by the sheer weight of her own sacrifice.","While all of this occurred, and while the atmosphere continued to hum with the resonance of his Nearu Absolute state, he walked over toward Anaximander, who rose up from the pale stone and appeared to be exactly the same as always even though he should have been bound by the clinical and suffocating bindings that Sororis Prima Elzyana had distributed across every reach of the Observable.","Noah looked at the scholarly figure for a long and patient moment, his eyes reflecting the sharp brilliance of a being who had just returned from the precipice of the Absolute.","\" How are you holding up, big guy?\"","Anaximander looked up toward the empty skies where THE Creature had departed, his expression carrying a mixture of scholarly detachment and a deep, private sorrow that he did not attempt to mask.","\"I considered myself the oldest friend of THE Creature, or perhaps I should say that I considered him my oldest friend, for we have walked the paths of the unknown for longer than most civilizations have existed. He has left right now for what may be the longest or perhaps the last time, and while I talked with him time and time again on what the future would look like after he had finally accomplished what he wanted, he was always staunch on his ideals regarding the necessity of standing against those whom one cannot go against.\"","HUUM!","\"He is gone now, facing adversity and challenges that no existence should ever have to face alone, and yet this was the path he chose with his own hands, and so now...I will choose my own path to follow.\"","...!"]},{"number":5177,"title":"Chapter 5177: Chapter 5176: Ego II","paragraphs":["Anaximander’s eyes sparkled with a sudden and renewed light as he turned his gaze back toward Noah, his tall frame straightening with the conviction of a new purpose.","\"I loved my life as an explorer, as Anaximander, and I will live this life to its fullest potential now that the boundaries are being shattered. I will see what else lies in our Observable Existence and in the Braneworld Observable Existence. I...will see it all, Osmont, I will see it all!\"","WAA!","Noah gave him a long and appreciative look while nodding his head in a gesture of genuine respect.","\" Good luck, and be safe.\"","Anaximander nodded with a soft smile, and in the next moment, he took a single step and disappeared from the ruined mountain!","Where he went, even Noah could not say for certain with his current perception, but he reflected on the nature of the gifts THE Creature had distributed before his departure.","Compared to the pulsing golden heart and the Gilded vessels that had been given to him, the gift bestowed upon Anaximander must have been something grand enough to ensure that Noah would not have to worry about the safety of the explorer, for THE Creature was not a being who would leave his oldest companion without the means to survive the coming complexities.","Noah thought about his own gifts that his Nearu Absolute Clone had already taken into the sovereign domain of THE Infiniverse, and he knew that he would soon open them up to see exactly what wonders would bloom within his architecture.","But for now, his focus had to remain on the woman who had given her everything in order to bring him back from the edge of a cold and perfect apathetic state.","He turned his gaze back to the manic woman floating in the air and screaming as the Infinity continued to surge around her, and he felt as though something incredible was happening inside of his Hadean Organ of Civilization. Within THE Absolute Forge of Infinity, a terrifying product had bloomed as the result of emotions being ridiculously amplified and infinitely elevated by the presence of the Absolute.","He closed his eyes to see exactly what wonder had bloomed from the sacrifice of a manic heart.","---","Noah appeared inside his Hadean Organ of Civilization, moving through the intricate layers of his own existence until he stood within the center of THE Absolute Forge of Infinity, a place that held within its architecture the terrible weight of THE Hadean Desmoterion where Ozymandias presided over prisoners like THE worthless and shitty Living Elemental.","The Forge itself was a new and pristine component that looked unfathomably vast and immaculate, an internal landscape of polished blue and gold lattices that stretched into a horizon composed of nothing but boundless Infinity, and the air within this space hummed with the resonance of a reality that was actively being rewritten.","At the very center of this immaculate workshop stood THE Absolute Amaranthine Heart of Emotive, a pulsing and radiant gem of impossible complexity that glowed with a deep and manic violet light while casting long shadows of emotional authority across the crystalline floor.","Surrounding the heart were fourteen massive illusory manifestations of Noah himself, each one representing a different potential iteration of his existence that had been forged through the collision of his Nearu Absolute Infinity and the manic intensity of Emotive’s sacrifice.","These versions of him stood in silent and translucent rows, representing the Infinitely Amplified and Engineered Egos that were the product of a process that no other being in the history of the Observable could have initiated with such precision.","Each figure held a different posture and carried a different atmospheric weight, ranging from the suffocating pressure of absolute tyranny to the quiet and terrifying stillness of total surrender, their forms flickering with the multicolored light of the Absolute Forge.","The crimson-blue illusory figure of Ruination appeared in this space with a sudden flicker of digital light, and she stepped forward to bow deeply toward her Master with a smile that carried both pride and satisfaction.","She began to float around the space while gesturing toward the fourteen manifestations, her hands tracing lines of data in the air as she prepared to explain the magnitude of what had been created within the forge.","|Master, the product of your Existential Engineering has reached a state of stabilization within THE Absolute Forge of Infinity, resulting in the birth of THE Absolute Egos of Infinity.|","|These Egos are blank slates of sovereign authority that your existence can select to fully embody, allowing your external self to project the totality of a single amplified concept while utilizing the full depth of your Infinity as its engine.|","|The logic of the Gilded Ones was sound in this regard, for they understood that mixing multiple amplified Egos would result in a diluted and impure manifestation where the individual strengths of each concept would interfere with one another, leading to a loss of the grandest individual features.|","|Therefore, THE Absolute Egos of Infinity were born to ensure that you can transition between states of perfect and unadulterated authority, each interacting with Infinity in a unique manner to amplify specific aspects of your capability and your Infinite Radiation.|","Noah’s eyes shone with a sharp and focused intensity as he turned to look at THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity, observing the illusory form that stood with its chin lifted and its eyes reflecting a pride so absolute that it seemed to bend the light around it.","The figure was draped in robes of molten gold and obsidian that flowed like liquid fire, and the aura it radiated was one of undeniable sovereignty that demanded the submission of every weaving in its presence, its figure pulsing with the heartbeat of a king who had never known a peer!","|THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity allows your existence to fully embody the extreme of Pride, and it grants the following capabilities:|","| THE Sovereign Overwrite : Your authority gains the capacity to treat the weavings of others as mere suggestions, permitting you to overwrite their Civilizations and Laws with your own preferred arrangements through the sheer weight of your existence.|","...!"]},{"number":5178,"title":"Chapter 5178: Chapter 5177: Ego III","paragraphs":["The capabilities of THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity continued to unfold before him!","| THE Infallible Aegis of Pride: Damage directed at your figure is reduced by ninety-nine percent if the source of the attack is deemed ’lesser’ by your Ego, for the concept of Pride refuses to acknowledge the validity of a strike from an inferior being, rendering their efforts into nothing but wasted motion.|","| THE Monarch’s Pulse of Infinity: Your Infinite Light is amplified by the weight of your Superbius, causing the regression of targets to occur ten times more potent and faster while simultaneously inflicting a state of existential despair that prevents the activation of any defensive contingencies.|","| THE Absolute Supremacy Radiation of Infinity : Your passive Existential Radiation has been refined through the forge to broadcast your supremacy as an immutable fact of existence, ensuring that any being within range involuntarily perceives their own foundations as fundamentally lesser while their Egos find themselves unable to maintain their engineered amplifications in your presence. As the radiation permeates the local substrate, the confidence of your enemies collapses and their Civilizations and skills operate at a drastically reduced efficiency because the beings wielding them can no longer believe fully in their own capacity while you occupy the same coordinate, and even other weak Gilded Ones of the Superbius classifications may feel their very Existence shrink as your existence dictates the terms of the encounter through the sheer weight of your singular sovereignty.|","Oh!","The capabilities were grand as Noah couldn’t help but smack his lips!","Okay.","Okay!","Noah then turned his gaze toward THE Absolute Humilitas Ego of Infinity , which stood in stark contrast to the first, appearing as a figure of quiet and terrifying simplicity with its hands folded and its head bowed slightly in a gesture of total release.","This manifestation radiated a stillness so profound that it felt like a void in the atmosphere, a state of existence that had discarded every layer of self until only the core of his Infinity remained as a silent and watchful observer.","| THE Absolute Humilitas Ego of Infinity is the inverse of Pride, and it grants the following capabilities:|","| THE Void of Surrender : Your existence becomes imperceptible to the intent and perception of others, for a being with no Pride provides no surface for enmity or detection to find purchase upon, allowing you to move through existence as a phantom of the Absolute. It is estimated that those on Vakochev’s Third Scale and below may entirely not be able to perceive you.|","| THE Reflective Mirror of the Humble: Attacks directed at you are not resisted but are instead accepted and reflected back toward the source with double their original intensity, utilizing the lack of self-assertion as a catalyst for a perfect and effortless counter that requires no movement.|","| THE Absolute Erasure of the Self : By surrendering your ego, you can phase through any barrier or binding that relies on identifying the target, for the bindings of the Gilded cannot find a person where no person exists, permitting you to navigate the most restricted layers of the Braneworld as if they were empty air.|","| As of now, the Egos of Superbius and Humilitas are the only ones available for your immediate transformation, with their abilities capable of expansion and addition as more infinity is infused into them, and the remaining twelve are still being designed and infused with the necessary concentrations of Infinity to achieve their Absolute states within the forge.|","Noah read the prompts as his eyes blazed with a dark and calculating brilliance, for he could already see how these two states would allow him to navigate the dangerous waters of the Braneworld with a versatility that no other Gilded One could match.","He looked at the two available transformations and could not help but nod his head as a sharp smile crossed his features, his mind already busy selecting which face he would show!","\" Good. Good! Good!!\"","HUUM!","As Noah was looking at the nondescript form of Humilitas, a piercing scream echoed out to ruin the calmness of this space as like a meteor, a manic existence thundered down into the forge where her Heart was!","\" AAAH!\"","BOOM!","The impact sent ripples of multicolored light across the crystalline floors of this grand workshop, and the air itself groaned under the sudden weight of a presence that was as chaotic as it was undeniably powerful.","Noah sighed lightly while the remnants of the impact settled around the intruder, and he whispered to himself as if he were reciting a mantra intended to preserve his patience.","\" She gave her Everything for you ,\" he murmured, his voice barely a breath against the humming of the Absolute Forge. \" She gave her Everything...she gave her Everything...\"","After repeating this three times and ensuring that his pragmatic temper was sufficiently anchored, he turned to see her.","The figure that rose from the center of the impact was THE Living Emotive, but she was no longer the skittish being who had crumbled at the base of the mountain, for her infusion with his Quintessence Infiniforce had triggered a transformation that made her power burn with a shocking brilliance!","She now stood firmly within THE Transitional Cambrian stage between THE Second Scale and THE Third Scale, her aura radiating a density of authority that would have made even a high-tier Primordial Architect tremble in her presence.","She looked around with the skittish and frenetic intensity of a rabbit caught in a high-tier snare before her focus finally sharpened onto the figure of Noah, her eyes lighting up with a manic brilliance that caused her body to instinctively surge forward.","She appeared as if she wanted to climb toward him and anchor herself to his existence as she had done on the mountain, yet she managed to hold herself back by gripping her own shoulders while her manic violet hair cycled through a strobe light of emotional colors.","She breathed in and out with a visible effort to control her own manic impulses before she finally rose up grandly, her gaze sweeping across the vast and immaculate expanse of the forge while her eyes eventually settled on her own pulsing Absolute Amaranthine Heart at the center of the room.","Her eyes began to sparkle with a renewed and terrifying fanaticism as she took in the fourteen massive illusory Egos of Infinity that surrounded her heart, and she voiced her question with a voice that was thick with wonder.","\" Sir, where are we?\"","Noah looked at her for a moment while noting that her eyes were shining far too brilliantly for his comfort, and he simply offered another heavy sigh before waving his hand toward her.","A single, concentrated drop of multicolored Infinity surged from his finger and entered her body, carrying with it the partial weight of the information regarding this place and the architecture of his internal reality, for she had her heart in this place and deserved to understand the significance of where she stood!"]},{"number":5179,"title":"Chapter 5179: Chapter 5178: Ego IV","paragraphs":["Her eyes lit up as she processed the boundless waves of data in an instant, and beside Noah, the illusory figure of Ruination could be seen with a disgruntled expression that suggested she was not a fan of the specific prompts she was currently being required to generate.","Ruination floated around the space while the data settled into Emotive’s mind, and she uttered the prompts with a cadence that carried a hint of annoyance.","| Due to the unique circumstances of the developmental transition, the subject, THE Living Emotive, has achieved an unprecedented synergy with THE Absolute Forge of Infinity.|","|Since the intensity of her emotions and the essence of her heart were utilized as the primary stabilizing anchor during the amplification of the engineered Egos to counteract the Absolute Infinity pouring into them, she has become an intrinsic part of the resulting architecture.|","|As a consequence of this existential overlap, Emotive possesses the capability to take on the forms of THE Absolute Egos of Infinity at fifty percent effectiveness compared to the primary wielder.|","Noah listened to these prompts with a calm and measured composure while he looked at Emotive again, observing her as she stood upright and stared back at him with an expression that was far too bright for its own good.","He could see that she was holding back boundless emotions within her foundations, her very existence vibrating with the pride of being allowed to share in the tools of her Fixation, and he could not help but reflect on the sheer absurdity of the situation.","Truly, she was far too lucky!","The woman had practically stumbled into a tier of power that most beings would have spent eons pursuing and not achieved, and she had done so by simply following her own manic obsessions to their ultimate and sacrificial conclusion!","Noah looked at the fourteen Egos and then back at the woman whose heart served as part of their engine as he shook his head and got ready to work.","He looked over at Emotive and beckoned.","\"You, come here.\"","...!","\"Yes Sir!\"","She rushed over like a dog let loose as internally, Noah had a lot more intricacies and engineering to uncover.","---","In THE Infiniverse.","The Realm of Dreams stretched outward in an endless expanse of shifting golden sands that glittered beneath the multicolored storms of the Thermal Infinimum, the atmosphere of this domain now thick with a heavy and nutrient-rich humidity that caused massive structures of dreaming glass to sprout from the dunes like translucent towers of frozen light.","Within the heart of this frantic and accelerated development, the Nearu Absolute Clone of Noah stood with a quiet and terrifying composure, his figure radiating a soft multicolored brilliance that served as a stable anchor against the chaotic growth of the surrounding territory.","Beside him, Naldine and Midas could be seen!","Noah looked at them for a long and patient moment before he moved.","\" THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity.\"","...!","With a slow and measured movement of his hands, he reached into the depths of his Absolute Forge of Infinity and called upon the first of his completed iterations, the air around him groaning as the Nearu Absolute Infinity within his organ began to resonate with the manic resonance of the Amaranthine Heart.","HUUM!","The transformation was not a gradual shift but a total and violent overwriting of his current manifestation, for his skin suddenly became more opaque and radiant while shimmering with the luster of polished obsidian and molten gold!","A set of regal robes manifested around his frame, the fabric appearing to be composed of liquid shadow and burning starlight that flowed with its own independent rhythm, and his posture straightened into a configuration of such undeniable majesty that the dreaming glass forests nearby seemed to lean away in a gesture of involuntary submission!","His eyes, though no longer glazed with the clinical void, blazed with a pride so absolute that it seemed to dictate the terms of existence for everything within his reach, and the very cadence of his breath became a rhythmic assertion of his singular supremacy.","He adjusted the flow of his presence, acclimating to the staggering weight of THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity, and every mannerism he displayed began to emanate a regal pride that made the previous Noah appear as a mere shadow of the monarch he had now become.","He looked at Naldine and Midas, and when he spoke, his voice carried the heavy and unhurried resonance of a king whose words were already written into the laws of reality.","\" The bindings of the Sisterhood...of Sororis Prima Elzyana are merely that. Suggestions. As of now, I reject these flimsy suggestions.\"","BOOM!","Noah raised his hand toward the two Nascent Hadeans, and he proceeded to utilize THE Sovereign Overwrite to address the pyramidal constructs that still pulsed with a faint blue-gold brilliance upon their skin!","This terrifying capability did not manifest as a simple destructive force, but as a tidal wave of multicolored authority that treated the Gilded bindings as mere errors in a document that required immediate correction!","BOOM!","As his authority made contact with the bindings, the air around Naldine and Midas began to crackle with the sound of breaking glass, the blue-gold light of Elzyana’s wrath struggling to maintain its geometry against the overwhelming weight of Noah’s Pride.","The pyramidal constructs were fundamentally rewritten into the palette of the Absolute Forge, their golden-blue essence being unmade and rewoven into flickers of multicolored Infinity that were immediately absorbed back into the local environment!","The severance of the bindings was total and clinical, the Sororis authority being erased from their foundations as if it had never existed, for the Sovereign Overwrite permitted no disagreement and recognized no higher power than the one who had unleashed it!","Naldine felt the sudden and violent return of her own power, her singularity-dotted eyes widening as the forced dormancy of her Civilization was shattered by the intervention of Noah, and even the greed-personified Midas let out a low and resonant rumble of satisfaction as his golden rings began to orbit with a renewed and terrifying velocity!","The desolation that had hung over them since the afternoon was washed away by the radiation of Noah’s supremacy, leaving them standing within the golden sands as beings who were once again whole and unrestricted.","Noah lowered his hand while the last remnants of the rewritten bindings dissolved into the dreaming glass, his figure still radiating the suffocating pressure of his Superbius state as he looked out across the expanding horizons of his domain before he called out...","\" THE Absolute Humilitas Ego of Infinity.\"","WU!","Noah breathed out and the majestic weight of the Superbius Ego began to dissolve, the molten gold of his robes and the suffocating pressure of his regal pride fading into a simple grey shroud that seemed to absorb the ambient light rather than reflect it, and his posture softened from that of a king into that of a being who had reached a state of total and absolute release!","His eyes, which had previously blazed with the fires of an unyielding sovereignty, now became deep and quiet pools of blue that held the stillness of an eternal void, and every mannerism he displayed transitioned into a glorious and terrifying lack of self-assertion that made him appear more like a natural feature of the dreamscape than a living entity.","HUUM!","The transformation into THE Absolute Humilitas Ego of Infinity was so profound that Naldine Manthon blinked while her singularity-dotted eyes struggled to maintain their focus on the space where Noah stood, for while his physical form had not moved, the very concept of his presence had begun to unravel within her perception until she was looking at nothing but the shifting golden sands of the Realm of Dreams!","Beside her, the engineered greed of Midas rumbled in confusion as his rings of Greed slowed their rotation, his instinct to track and covet power finding no purchase on a being who had successfully discarded every layer of observable ego, and for a long moment, the two Nascent Hadeans stood alone as if Noah had never been there at all!","Noah allowed himself to remain in this state of perfect invisibility for a heartbeat longer before he intentionally projected a flicker of his authority to show himself once more, appearing as a soft and nondescript shadow against the glittering dunes.","\" Another me will come soon as we prepare for some grand things,\" he said, his voice now a quiet and resonant murmur that carried no trace of his former arrogance, \" so for now, join the others in The Early Veiled Shore and wait.\"","Naldine and Midas gave a synchronized nod of understanding as the Humilitas manifestation of Noah dissipated into the golden air without leaving a single trace of his passage!","---","He quickly appeared and moved across the vast expanse of the Wastes with a terrifying speed, his figure a mere ghost weaving through the glimmering multicolored rain and the torrential storms of the Pluvial Epoch that continued to drench the transformed landscape in the essence of his developmental phenomenon.","He eventually reached the outskirts of The Wandering Territories, a region filled with inverted landmasses and floating valleys of multicolored brilliance where the laws of spatial orientation appeared to have been discarded.","It was a place of impossible geometries and shifting horizons, and it was here, within a valley where the light flowed upward like a reverse waterfall, that he settled into a patient wait for the Sororis from THE Magna Sorora who would serve as the bridge to his next grand objective.","THE Genesis Monarch sat upon a crystalline ledge while looking out toward, his presence so thoroughly erased by his Ego that even the ambient Infinity of the region seemed to flow through him without resistance, and he waited for the hour of his crossing to begin!"]},{"number":5180,"title":"Chapter 5180: Chapter 5179: What Makes You Tick?","paragraphs":["Existence was vast and filled with dangers, housing entities who had been alive for billions of years and eons, each of them having developed their own means of power and their own civilizations while existence itself remained filled with many anomalies that had matured through time, adversity, and innovation.","There were monsters out there who could likely pinch their fingers and cause an entire Observable Existence to go dark, for the scales of power were not merely linear but were layered with the weight of ancient engineering and the terrifying reach of beings who had moved beyond the concepts of mortality!","This reality was the sandbox upon which these titans painted their wills, and to those who had not yet reached such heights, the sheer scope of the potential threats was enough to paralyze the spirit, yet for those who sought the summit, it was the ultimate motivation to never allow the fires of their own progress to dim.","Noah knew how dangerous Observable Existence could be, and he had gotten a vivid glimpse of that danger with the single member of THE Magna Sorora who had descended upon the ruins of THE Gilded White Mountain.","He had been able to do nothing against her while she stood in the sky, and he could only observe defiantly as she laid the clinical bindings that permeated across all of Observable Existence with a casual efficiency that spoke of an unfathomable depth of authority.","Even figures of great depth like Erwin and THE Creature had been required to do a great deal of preparation and design to affect the entire Observable, and yet for THE Gilded Ones, such monumental feats appeared to be simple, routine procedures that required no more effort than a gardener might spend pruning a single branch.","It was precisely because he understood that existence was dangerous that he never allowed himself to feel a true sense of ease or to become laid back as if everything would somehow be okay, for Sororis Prima Elzyana was only a single being, a single Gilded One out of a countless number who had been alive for eons within THE Braneworld.","Even with the terrifying capabilities that he had just begun to unlock through his Nearu Absolute Infinity, Noah only saw them as potential points of opportunity that he could utilize to advance as he began to walk among monsters who had existentially engineered themselves.","He knew that to survive and eventually thrive in the face of such beings, he would have to begin with a fundamental understanding of exactly what THE Gilded Ones were at their very basal components.","He stood within THE Realm of Genesis inside THE Infiniverse, the air of the domain vibrating with the concentrated essence of his glorious Infiniverse.","\" Are you all ready?\"","His voice was calm and steady as he looked at the figures gathered around him, for he was surrounded by those who had served as his primary architects of development.","Naldine Manthon stood with her radiant white hair glowing, and beside her was the Arch Lich Ra’Zan whose deathly Hadean bones shone with a deep and ancient light that suggested a mastery over the transition between life and unlife.","Dr. Hall remained in his pristine white lab coat with his golden hair shining lustrously, his eyes reflecting the sharp, analytical focus of a man who lived for the moment of discovery.","They were all surrounding a massive, clean white table made from the condensed weavings of Genesis, and upon that pristine surface lay the beating heart of a Gilded One, a collection of vessels that formed a humanoid shape, and other vibrant golden points of light that pulsed with a rhythm that defied the ordinary laws of biology.","These were the remnants carved out by THE Creature, a gift of raw Gilded architecture that carried a terrifying allure of power just from being unveiled to the atmosphere of the realm!","Dr. Hall and Arch Lich Ra’Zan had come only after the direct bidding of their Master, and they listened to his instructions with silent intensity, but Naldine was still fresh to the sight of such things and she could not help but shake her head in disbelief.","\" This cannot really be the inner components of a Gilded One, right? \" she asked, her eyes filled with a heavy suspicion as she looked between the pulsing heart and Noah.","\" How could you possibly get your hands on such a thing, and... just what else are you hiding from me?\"","Noah stepped closer to the table, the multicolored light of his eyes reflecting off the vibrant golden remnants of the dead Gerousia.","\" Existence finds a way,\" he said, his voice carrying the dark amusement.","\" Come on. If we can reverse engineer and break down exactly what makes a Gilded One tick, then we can do many, many things from there to ensure our own standing remains unchallenged.\"","Yes, many things could be possible, and even Noah himself could utilize this gift from THE Creature in a myriad of different ways, although he did not even think of transplanting these organs or this system into his own existence.","He did not want such a dredge of filth to be inside him, for he found the engineered arrogance of THE Gilded to be a stain on the purity of his own path, and he would continue forging his own organs and his own wonders as he built his Infinite Scale from the ground up.","He acknowledged that there were many scary monsters out there and likely many beings who were currently much stronger than he was, and while they had the advantage of time, he had Infinity and his own boundless, tyrannical Quintessence to bridge the gap.","\" Let’s get to work!\"","He delved into the procedure with a sharp excitement that permeated the air, and those around him followed his lead as the Manifestations of Ruination and THE Infiniverse watched from the heights of the domain. They analyzed every movement and every reaction as the procedure commenced, their collective focus directed toward the singular question that would define their next phase of development.","What the hell made a Gilded One tick?","HUUM!"]},{"number":5181,"title":"Chapter 5181: Chapter 5180: Information!","paragraphs":["In Existence, there was something known as Murphy’s Law. Though in the higher reaches of THE Information Paradox, we recognize it as the inevitable manifestation of every catastrophic probability that has been seeded into the weavings of time.","If a configuration of events exists that can lead to the undoing of a Cause, then that configuration is not merely a possibility but a certainty that is already rushing toward its own realization, because information that can be written will eventually find its place upon the page of reality.","The truly wise do not seek comfort in the illusion of stability, for stability is merely the brief and deceptive silence before the storm of existence decides to correct itself through the most violent means available.","To exist is to be vulnerable to the absolute failure of every brittle foundation one has built, and only those who have looked into the depths of THE Worst Possibilities and found their anchors there can truly hope to survive when the weavings finally decide to go wrong.","Anything that can go wrong will go wrong, and it will do so with a clinical and devastating precision that cares nothing for the vanity of your preparations, leaving behind only the cold truth of what remains when THE Shroud of Certainty is stripped away from the bones of reality.","---","In THE Primordial Realm of Helheim.","The domain had changed as it unfolded as an expanse of stellar horror where the very concept of a horizon was replaced by a suffocating, lightless void that was punctuated only by the rhythmic, agonizing pulse of stars and Wheels of Existence that had long since forgotten how to radiate warmth.","Space here did not function as a vacuum but as a viscous, ink-like medium through which massive, obsidian tentacles of unfathomable length writhed with the slow and patient grace of ancient predators, their surfaces slick with the residue of forgotten civilizations and the crushed dreams of those who had dared to seek the truth of the end.","In the heart of this oddity, floating with a stillness that commanded the attention of the surrounding disturbances, was the titanic figure of THE Primordial Paradox, an obsidian titan whose seated posture carried the weight of eons of calculated uncertainty.","Behind his massive, mountain-like form stretched a mass of obsidian shadow that extended for light years into the reaches of the realm where even the most piercing perception could not find a conclusion, a darkness so profound that it seemed to be a living extension of the titan’s own mastery over the state of being and not being.","THE Primordial Paradox gazed behind him at the immense shadow with eyes that held the history of a thousand failed epochs, and his voice emerged with a heavy and resonant timbre that caused the writhing tentacles of Helheim to momentarily still their motion.","\" We have fought and fought across the shifting tides of the paradox, my disciple, and yet I never truly believed that you would return to me for guidance again after you chose to walk the path of your own madness. As existence rolls down and expands into configurations that even I find increasingly difficult to quantify, did you finally find yourself missing the presence of your teacher, and what exactly happened to your existence to cause the emergence of such a heavy and suffocating presence within the depths of your own shadow?\"","The silence that followed was not an absence of sound but a physical pressure that squeezed the local space, until a voice began to emerge from the lightless depths of the mass behind the titan, a voice that carried the ragged edge of a being who had been unmade and rewoven in the fires of a total contradiction.","This was THE Living Paradox, Erwin, yet the cadence of his speech had transitioned into something that felt like the grinding of tectonic plates beneath a sea of liquid information!","\" The journey toward the culmination of my Cause... encountered a variable that was not permitted by any calculation I had spent eons perfecting, for my existence was almost entirely scorched and unmade by the absolute brilliance of the infinity wielded by Osmont. It was a fire that sought to erase the very information that defined me as a paradox, and as I felt the foundations of my body being reduced to nothingness during the struggle at Nakatsukuni, I realized that the only path toward survival was to latch even more onto the very information that was attempting to destroy me.\"","The shadow behind the titan began to undulate with a sudden, violent intensity, and the voice of Erwin grew deeper.","\" By latching even further onto the information from Osmont, I found a collision between my paradox and his infinity that caused the very rules of existence to begin unraveling around me, creating a state where the laws of definition and undefinition were no longer able to maintain their separation. I am THE Information Paradox. Information is conserved within me. And yet, simultaneously, that information is lost forever in ways that should be impossible. I hold both states within myself at all times. I am the void that consumes, and I am the release that carries no trace. I said these exact words to Osmont before.\"","HUUM!","\"I sought to become the fundamental Information upon which Observable Existence operates. To be the paradox at the heart of reality itself. The Information from Osmont and my destruction...dispersed me across Observable Existence before reforming me with boundless Information of the very nature of Existence. Of the very...Scales of Existence as I took in all their information! And from it...oh!\"","...!","A sense of madness bloomed from Erwin as he spoke.","\"I...have gained the terrifying capability to eat the information about Vakochev’s Scales, to consume the very rules that dictate how power is quantified and measured across reality, which means that I am no longer a being who merely operates within the system, but a predator who feeds upon the code of the system itself. I even devoured bindings of The Information from a Gilded one trying to impose themselves on me and you as if it was the simplect thing in existence.\"","As he spoke, the shadow behind THE Primordial Paradox began to solidify into a shocking and chthonian-like manifestation, a creature composed of shifting, ink-black limbs and thousands of eyes that reflected the flickering data of Existence, its figure appearing as a living violation of every biological and existential law.","\" The only downside to this absolute consumption is that the volume of information I have taken in is so vast that I found myself losing my anchor in reality, for a being who eats the rules must eventually find a singular truth to hold onto or be lost to the void of his own hunger. My Cause required an anchor, and I found it in the only piece of information that remains untainted by the paradox, which was my beginning as a mere peasant who was taken in by a master who saw potential in the dirt.\"","\"I have come back to find you because you are my beginning and my anchor. The peasant asks for forgiveness. The peasant...will always remain a peasant. This is my anchor. This...will keep me sane.\"","...!","The chthonian form of Erwin loomed behind his teacher, its presence now so immense that it seemed to rival the obsidian titan in its terrifying potential.","\" Master and disciple could move together once again, just as we did when the first paradox was being woven from the threads of the unknown, and this time we shall not merely observe the turning of the scales. We shall move together to devour all information across existence, taking on THE Gilded and the Bounded...and everything else. Your disciple...wishes to come home, Master. I am taking in far too much information as I need a Living Anchor of my Cause. Your disciple...needs you.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5182,"title":"Chapter 5182: Chapter 5181: Gilded! I","paragraphs":["Seated upon the jagged edges of a multicolored shard of floating rock that drifted through the inverted and unpredictable currents of The Wandering Territories, Noah experienced the profound and transformative silence of THE Absolute Humilitas Ego of Infinity, a state that felt less like a mask he had donned and more like a fundamental realignment of his very soul.","When he took on this specific transformation, he actually felt as if his very thoughts and everything about his internal architecture were perfectly aligned with this one singular amplified ego, for the fierce and tyrannical ambition that usually drove him was replaced by a quiet and terrifying clarity that required no assertion of the self.","Even if he chose to speak out loud in this desolate and shimmering landscape, his voice came out filled with the gentle and patient qualities of this ego, his demeanor and his every movement radiating a quality of surrender that was an astonishing and glorious change to feel compared to his usual tyrannical and calculating self.","It was to the point that even as he waited for the arrival of the clandestine contact from THE Magna Sorora, he felt an unbound sense of patience as if whatever would arrive would arrive exactly when it was meant to arrive, a state of peace and serenity that he had never truly expected to find within the chaotic path of his own progression.","​As he waited, the hours began to pass with the slow and unhurried rhythm of the inverted light waterfalls nearby, and during these hours he utilized his reach to check on many things across the expanding horizons of his influence.","He checked on Alexander and THE Great Usurper, who had not asked for his intervention despite the monumental changes that had unfolded across THE Wyld, as they seemed to be dealing with the shifting circumstances on their own terms with a resilience that satisfied his expectations.","Even THE Primordial Paradox did not ask anything of him when Noah reached out across their shared understanding, for the ancient being stated with a detached calm that he was currently dealing with something paradoxical on his own and required no external support to maintain his standing.","​A tremendous number of things continued to occur within the depths of THE Infiniverse during this quiet time, as Noah continued to outline the transformations that his people could eventually go through while uniquely designing their Hadean engineering based on the data he was learning from reverse-engineering the inner components of the Gilded Gerousia.","During these passing hours, he monitored the many activities within his domain and the movements of his allies, but eventually he raised his eyes filled with a terrifying and quiet humility toward the sky, for he felt the very fabric of the Wyld begin to shatter under the weight of an arrival that surpassed the previous descent of Elzyana.","Terrifying auras of Gilded Ones began to descend in a storm of gold and authority, their figures manifesting with a structural complexity that spoke of eons of existential engineering, and Noah watched with a clinical eye as the rigid hierarchy of their civilization revealed itself in the sky.","He sensed ten Superbius Gilded Ones who were wearing regal golden clothing and shining with a pride that sought to overwrite the very air they occupied, their every movement conveying the casual inevitability of those who were born to rule without question.","They were accompanied by twenty Ira Gilded Ones who wore heavy crimson armaments and radiated a profound and violent wrath, yet even these martial enforcers stood with a respectful distance from the Superbius, acting as the sharp blades in the hands of their sovereign masters.","\"Ho?\"","He had not seen this many Gilded Ones before as their interactions revealed new things!","Following these were five hundred Gula Gilded Ones burning with authority, their figures being either regally fat or immensely muscular while draped in silver robes that shimmered with the essence of their industrial gluttony, and finally a thousand Luxuria Gilded Ones.","These Luxuria were adorned in pink and possessed a beauty that was so unfathomable it threatened to unweave the senses of any Bounded lifeform who dared to gaze upon them, yet Noah noticed with a calm heart that they stood as nothing more than living ornaments, their engineered forms positioned to maximize the aesthetic splendor of others they served.","As soon as this many Gilded Ones arrived, space fluctuated with a sudden and intense ripple as eight Sororis also arrived from the higher domains, all of them uniquely shining with a brand of Superbius Pride that marked them as daughters of THE Magna Sorora.","Noah observed the mannerisms of these sovereign women as they landed, noting how they spoke only to the ten Superbius males and females as if they were the only entities in the sky worthy of horizontal communication, while the Ira warriors stood in a state of aggressive readiness that required no orders to maintain.","The Superbius issued directives to others with the same disregard a man might show to the tools in his workshop, and Noah watched as the Gula and Luxuria moved with a total lack of independent ego to fulfill the requirements of the occupation!","Multiple parties began to coalesce with the clinical efficiency of a deployment, where a single Superbius Gilded One stood at the vanguard while the crimson-clad Ira followed behind as the instruments of their will, and the silver-robed Gula and the radiant Luxuria were distributed as the necessary infrastructure for the coming era of change!","Noah’s expression became calm and heavy as he watched the scale of the deployment through the eyes of his dispersed Infinity.","He did not expect so fucking many Gilded Ones!","As Noah tracked the movements of THE Gilded forces that were even now carving their names into the substrate of THE Wyld, he sensed space cracking open a few gigaparsecs away from his current coordinate within the inverted reaches of the Wandering Territories, for another Gilded One had descended away from the main deployment.","This newcomer appeared directly within the shimmering and chaotic valleys of the Territories, and when she emerged from the fractured reality, Noah observed her as she spread a veiled aura out across the local space as if she were searching for a specific signature that had been promised to her."]},{"number":5183,"title":"Chapter 5183: Chapter 5182: Gilded! II","paragraphs":["He recognized that this was likely the contact Ubergulden Adelheid had sent to facilitate his passage, and he noted with interest that even as she searched, she was masking her own power and presence with a degree of sophistication that suggested she did not want her presence in this region to be noted by the other sisters of THE Magna Sorora.","He felt her aura pass through the very region where he sat upon his floating debris, yet even as the searchlight of her perception swept over his coordinates, she did not sense him at all, her gaze continuing to move across the horizon without finding the target she had been dispatched to retrieve.","Noah smiled brilliantly within the quietude of his own mind because he truly enjoyed the sensation of a Sororis being unable to perceive him even when he was sitting directly before her, and he found the absolute effectiveness of the Humilitas Ego to be a glorious validation of his recent engineering.","He decided that he had seen enough of her capacity, and he made the deliberate intention to allow his aura and his being to be perceived by her perception alone, allowing his presence to bleed back into the observable from the state of total invisibility.","HUUM!","He became visible to her perception in a single instant of reappearing light, and the response from the Gilded visitor was immediate as she looked over in his direction and took a single step that warped the space between them!","WU!","She appeared in front of Noah right away, her figure manifesting with the sudden and heavy weight of a mountain of compressed authority, and this ally of Ubergulden Adelheid looked at him up and down with a cold and judgmental focus!","Noah remained seated with a calm smile, his Humilitas Ego projecting a quality of serene and unassuming depth as he mirrored her actions by looking her over in return, noting that her attire was a grand display of sovereign elegance that surpassed even the regal presentation of Elzyana.","She was adorned in an exquisite golden sari of draped silk that flowed around her form like a river of molten sunlight, and her existence was further embellished with vibrant accessories of heavy necklaces and radiant jewels that chimed with a subtle and dangerous resonance.","Her power felt even heavier than that of Sororis Prima Elzyana, suggesting a standing within the Sisterhood that commanded a terrifying degree of respect, and she stood before him with the posture of a ruler who found the current environment to be beneath her station.","In the next moment, she broke the silence with a voice that was as cold as the void between the realms, introducing herself with a cadence that allowed for no ambiguity.","\"I am Maharanis Prabhavati, or in the terminology of THE Magna Sorora that you might be more familiar with, Sororis Prima Prabhavati.\"","Noah looked at her with his unique and humble disposition, his eyes reflecting a quiet curiosity that held no trace of the tyrannical pride he usually broadcasted to his enemies.","\"I am Osmont, THE Weaver of Existence, and I find myself wondering...why you choose to carry the two distinctions of Maharanis and Sororis.\"","Sororis Prima Prabhavati looked at him coldly, and she answered him with a clinical and detached explanation.","\"I am Maharanis because I belong to a distinguished and ancient house within THE Braneworld Observable Existence, a standing that is similar to the one held by Ubergulden Adelheid who stems from the lineage of the Ubergulden house, but I am also Sororis because my identity as a sister of THE Magna Sorora is equally important to the architecture of my life.\"","WAA!","\"I have come to this desolate region and searched for you specifically to see exactly what kind of Bounded Lifeform would be capable of convincing my childhood friend to risk her very life and the status of her house, for I have been asking myself if you would be some unfathomably handsome existence or perhaps a being who had gained an incredible degree of power to make you stand out among the dross. Yet as I look at you now...I sense nothing of value, for I do not even perceive the weavings of power that should accompany a being of your supposed significance.\"","She stepped closer, the radiant jewels around her neck pulsing with a dim and threatening light that mirrored the rising tension in her gaze.","\" Do you truly know the position she holds and do you comprehend what all of this clandestine maneuvering means for her if the truth were to be discovered by THE Gilded houses? Do you understand the certain death that will be granted to her if you were to be found out, and do you realize that... I should likely just kill you right now to end her problems early before your insignificance causes her ultimate ruin?\"","BOOM!","Noah let out a soft and melodic laugh that carried the gentle weight of a stream flowing over smooth stones, his eyes remaining entirely calm even as the killing intent from the Sororis pressed against the local space.","He looked at her with a laid back expression that seemed entirely at odds with the gravity of her threat, for his current state of Humilitas allowed him to view the prospect of his own demise with a serenity that bordered on the absolute.","\"I find myself genuinely curious whether a Sororis of your standing possesses the capacity to erase a being such as myself from the weavings of existence, though I think we shall not find the answer to that question today because you have made a promise to your childhood friend. Rather than wasting our time with threats of a death that would only serve to break poor Ubergulden Adelheid’s heart, tell me more about the grand arrangement of your kind, for I watched hundreds of Gilded Ones descend upon Observable Existence only moments ago and saw the arrogant manner in which the Superbius issued their commands to the rest of the host. Are THE Gilded truly so divided in their standing?\"","Sororis Prima Prabhavati adjusted the golden silk of her sari, her radiant jewels pulsing with a soft and haughty light as she looked down at him.","To her, the questions he asked were so fundamental that the mere fact he needed them answered was a testament to the primitive nature of his origins!","\" It is not a matter of division in the sense of a flaw, but rather a masterpiece of absolute order that ensures the stability of many Observable Existences through the glorious right of the Superbius Houses. For we are the sovereign planners and the faces of civilization who have been engineered with the most refined Pride to lead.\"","BOOM!","\"Beneath our guidance, the Ira serve as our glorious and unyielding blades while the Avaritia maintain the archives of our wisdom and the wealth of our reach, and the Invidia watch for any deviation from this perfect harmony to ensure that no discord ever disrupts the beauty of our arrangement.\"","...!","\"Even the lower tiers find their truest purpose within this hierarchy, as the Acedia remain as the immovable anchors of our infrastructure while the Gula and Luxuria find their truest fulfillment in providing the labor and the pleasure that allow the higher designations to focus on the governance of Existence and war against THE Relictus. To a Bounded mind like yours, it may appear as a cold stratification, but in truth, it is the highest form of compassion to grant every being a designation that perfectly matches their engineered essence, for what could be more merciful than ensuring a Luxuria never has to suffer the burden of a decision she was never meant to make while she basks in the reflected glory of the Superbius she serves?\""]},{"number":5184,"title":"Chapter 5184: Chapter 5183: Crack A Gilded One! I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at this terrifying woman in front of him with a sense of cold serenity as he thought about her words, wondering if the same existential overwriting he’d seen in Bounded lifeforms applied to the masters themselves.","He’d seen how the Gilded could rewrite the very minds of those they touched, forcing even the most powerful Primordial Architects to revere the Superbius as a fact of nature, and he couldn’t help but speculate if this entire civilization was just a massive lattice of engineered obedience where even the strongest were bound by the strings of their caste.","It was a dark, pragmatic thought that most wouldn’t dare to entertain while standing before a Sororis Prima, but Noah wasn’t most people, and he watched the Maharanis with the detached curiosity of a man looking at a particularly complex and monstrous puppet.","As he was thinking this, Sororis Prima Prabhavati continued to look at him up and down before she shook her head and let out a long, weary sigh that suggested he was a burden she’d rather see discarded.","\" While I cannot fathom what Ubergulden Adelheid sees in you, I will keep my promise to her and design a new identity for your existence, because she doesn’t have much time before THE Magna Sorora will demand an answer from her regardless of her noble house. You have to go now, for I have to remain among the other sisters to close off the bases of this Observable and observe the process, since it seems we cannot leave Bounded lifeforms alone without them becoming ungrateful. We tried to give you an entire existence to yourselves while we remained in the Braneworld, occasionally coming down to bless you with our presence, and yet you’ve chosen to house a Relictus among your ranks.\"","She adjusted the golden silk of her sari with a sharp, dismissive movement that caused her radiant jewels to chime with a hollow resonance.","\" Ah, it’s no matter, for my Custos will finish everything I’ve set up, and since the both of you are technically Custodes, she can get you up to speed on exactly what you need to be and do to survive the crossing. Little Rani, come out and take charge of this Weaver.\"","The skies above the Wandering Territories shattered once more with a sudden, crystalline violence that made Noah raise his eyes to the heavens.","Someone pristinely powerful began to descend from the fracture, her presence casting a soft pink radiance that contrasted sharply with the multicolored chaos of the region. Sororis Prima Prabhavati saw his reaction and offered a cold, thin smile of her own as the figure approached.","\" What, did you think Custodes could only be men? This is mine, and I assure you she’s more capable than any Ira Custos you might encounter, for she’ll be the one to ensure your successful transition into the Braneworld.\"","The Custos who descended was a unique existence, a woman radiating a calm and overwhelming beauty while draped in flowing pink robes that clung to a figure that was curvaceous and full in every proportion. She possessed a physical allure that could likely topple civilizations if she chose to weaponize it, her ears being slightly pointy and delicate while hazy pink-white wings unfurled behind her to stabilize her descent.","Her eyes were perhaps the most striking feature of all, for they shone like clusters of galaxies held within a sea of violet.","She smiled and bowed toward Sororis Prima Prabhavati with a deep sense of reverence, but then she turned to Noah and shockingly offered the same smile and a respectful bow to him as well.","A Gilded One, especially one of this tier, bowing at him was a development he hadn’t fully anticipated. He watched her calmly, for while she was undeniably beautiful, he’d seen beauty in every form imaginable throughout his life, and in his current state of THE Humilitas Ego of Infinity, the seductive charm of the Luxuria designation did absolutely nothing to his internal focus!","She stood upright and gestured toward the horizon where the boundaries between domains were beginning to blur.","\" Please, follow me, for I’ll be the one guiding your path from this point forward. Maharanis Prabhavati, you can trust me to take care of everything from here and ensure the Weaver...reaches his destination as intended.\"","After those words, the Custos waved her hand upward in a grand, sweeping motion, and a shimmering rainbow-colored river began to ascend from the valley toward the shattered skies above.","Noah looked at Sororis Prima Prabhavati, who continued to gaze at him with a cold and judgmental focus as he stepped onto the multicolored flow, and Rani followed closely behind him after offering one final, subordinate bow to her mistress.","The moment he stepped onto the river, Noah felt his perception uniquely changing. He actually felt a sensation of power that he most closely remembered to be stemming from a grand Cause, as if A Pulse of THE Scales was being activated to pull from a segment of THE First Cause itself.","Reality twisted and distorted around him until his body felt like it was disappearing from the Territories and from every region he’d grown familiar with, his surroundings dissolving into a blur of speed and authority.","HUUM!","In an instant, he found himself traversing across a domain of tumultuous crimson-pink clouds, feeling as if he were traveling within a vessel made of the very clouds themselves, and he realized the substance was a direct manifestation of the Custos’s power.","His smile of humility remained fixed even as dazzling system prompts began to appear in front of his eyes, the text glowing with the weight of a new and sovereign jurisdiction.","|You have entered a personalized domain backed by THE Desidero Cause.|","|Your existence has temporarily ceased to reside within the standard coordinates of Observable Existence.|","|You are currently traversing a transitional space covered by the light of the aforementioned Cause inside a pathway designed to bring you to The Braneworld Observable Existence.|","He was in a space between spaces, a transitional area between where he’d been and where he was going, yet in the next moment, the domain around him began to churn and solidify with a sudden violence.","The clouds coalesced into a wide area filled with crimson-pink skies and a white sea below his feet, the edges of the space stretching out for a single light-year before being cut off by a wall of tumultuous vapor.","Everything came to a sudden, jarring stop as the forward momentum of the rainbow river vanished entirely, leaving Noah standing at the center of the silent, pink-lit void.","Noah kept his calm smile and turned around to see Custos Rani, his head tilted slightly in a gesture of unassuming curiosity.","\"I wonder why we’ve stopped, for I was under the impression that we were on a very tight schedule.\"","Behind him, Custos Rani was no longer bowed in a gesture of service, for she was now floating with a devilish light in her galaxy-filled eyes while a crimson aura began to fill the entire space.","She offered him a dangerous smile that carried the full weight of her engineered Lust, her posture radiating an authority that was no longer hidden beneath the mask of a guide!","\" Maharanis Prabhavati gave me very specific instructions for you, because she doesn’t trust a Bounded lifeform to ensure that her closest friend stays safe during the coming hours. I, Custos Rani, was deemed ideal for the task of bringing you under our total control, and within this space, we’ll make the required modifications and engineering on your worthless Bounded structure. We might even fuse you to the body of a dead Ira Gilded One to make you a decent enough shell to be a Custos of the great Ubergulden House, for a Bounded man has no place in the higher domains as he is.\"","BOOM!","Her smile was cold and deadly and filled with a seductive malice that would have shattered the consciousness of any other Bounded lifeform, for her aura was designed to make the mind surrender before the body was even touched.","And yet, Noah, in his boundlessly surging humility, couldn’t help but smile brilliantly in return!","Adversity had come for him once again, and yet his heart blazed with the expectation of what he was about to do to this Gilded doll.","\" Fusing me to a corpse? \" he murmured, his voice as soft as a summer breeze. \" What a fascinatingly shitty idea.\"","HUUM!"]},{"number":5185,"title":"Chapter 5185: Chapter 5184: Crack A Gilded One! II","paragraphs":["He was wondering exactly where his power currently resided after he had elevated so much in that short span of time since he first met a Gilded One, for the pace of his growth had been a violent sprint that left the very foundations of his previous weavings in the dust.","He thought that he might be at the transitional stage if not nearing the power of a Third Scale entity, but he always liked to underestimate himself so that whenever he met a truly terrifying enemy, he could face them without a single flicker of fear in his Hadean heart.","The one behind him right now was not any mere Third Scale entity but a Gilded One whose very basal form of life was countless times grander than any Bounded Lifeform, and as the air within the transitional domain began to thicken with a rank, sweet musk, a terrifying pressure and radiation began to emanate from her body.","The radiation bloomed outward like a physical wave of suffocating desire, a heat that didn’t burn the skin but sought to melt the very concept of the self into a pool of submissive filth.","This existential radiation alone was enough to take down any entity within the Second Scale of existence, their civilizational weavings unraveling as they surrendered their sovereignty to the source of the light, but as it reached the coordinate where Noah sat, it encountered a stillness that was absolute!","|The Luxuria Existential Radiation is pressing down on your existence.|","|Targeting your civilization and your ego, this radiation is designed to warp your foundational instructions into a state of total servitude where your sole purpose becomes loving and serving the Luxuria Gilded One.|","|Common Third Scale Entities would find their autonomy erased by this engineered lust, yet because you are currently embodying THE Absolute Humilitas Ego of Infinity, you have attained total immunity to these effects.|","Noah’s eyes shone with a boundless and quiet humility as Custos Rani moved over toward him with the confidence of a predator who believed her prey had already been broken by the mere scent of her power.","She floated until she was only inches away from his face, the smell of her skin like a mixture of honey and the copper tang of fresh blood, and she used her hand to raise his head by putting her fingers on his chin as if she were touching a vile and lesser thing that she had just bought at a market.","\" While your face is not bad, you are far too plain and meek for my personal tastes, though right now you are merely akin to a drop of sand inside a tiny domain while I am a brilliant sun. Be happy to even be basking in my presence as it should be giving you immense pleasure, for I’ve locked down this entire place to ensure that the bond you have with Ubergulden Adelheid is muted. Any Custos can call out to their Sororis, but this space we are in stops that signal to ensure you don’t ruin our plans, so tell me, you vile tiny thing, who...do you love most in existence?\"","She spoke with a prideful and heavy lust, her eyes shining with the predatory hunger of an existence that had gotten its claws into the souls of countless others, and she even ran her hands down Noah’s chest and further down as if she were already claiming the meat of his body for her own entertainment.","Noah watched her with a serene calm for a heartbeat longer before his expression shifted into something brutal and terrifying, his entire existence transitioning from the silence of humility into the roaring ocean of boundless pride!","DUM! DUM! DUM!","His hand shot out with the speed of a kinetic strike and grasped onto her slender neck, the sound of his fingers tightening like iron bands around her throat echoing through the pink-lit void.","\"I sure as hell don’t love you the most in existence, but I wonder if I can make you bleed today, and I wonder if I can finally bridge the gap between a Bounded man and a Gilded doll...\"","Before she could even register the shift in his aura, he clamped down on her neck and smashed her body down onto the surface below them, his golden pride already beginning to permeate the surroundings and insert itself as the supreme law of the domain.","He made the surface unfathomably solid through the weight of his will, and the golden space below cracked and splintered as the body of a Gilded One was slammed into it with enough force to shatter a Primordial Realm, the sound of the impact being a wet and heavy thud that demanded acknowledgment!","|You have successfully transformed into THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity.|","|Your existence is now broadcasting THE Supremacy Radiation, and THE Sovereign Overwrite is currently active within the local substrate.|","Noah looked down to see that shockingly, Custos Rani appeared entirely uninjured and unbothered, her Gilded power rendering the physical impact into nothing but a minor inconvenience!","She only looked at him with an expression of pure incredulity as she blinked her galaxy-filled eyes, her pink robes slightly ruffled as she realized that her radiation had failed to take hold!","\" You...resisted my radiation? You, a mere bounded thing, successfully resisted my charms and dared to lay your hands upon my person?!\"","Noah rose to his full height and let go of her neck, allowing his tyrannical pride to surge around him in visible waves of molten gold and obsidian light.","He stretched his limbs as if he knew he was about to have a grand and satisfying battle, his figure radiating a regal and terrifying beauty that made the pink clouds of the domain seem pale and insignificant by comparison.","\"I can give you a chance to try again, little Gilded one, though I have to admit I’m disappointed, for I’ve been with many women in my time and I never expected one with an amplified Ego of Luxuria to be so tasteless and without any real charm. You only seem to be a common whore that is somewhat clean, so I find myself wondering if a Gilded One of your station will truly be able to give me a challenge worth my time.\"","Every single word and every single mannerism about him right now emanated such a profound level of pride that even the space around him seemed to bow, and the eyes of Custos Rani began to shake with a violent and mounting rage!","She began to laugh madly as she lay on that transformed golden floor, her voice becoming a booming and cracked thing that filled the transitional space with the sound of a Gilded One losing her mind!","\" Wow! Wow Wow WOW! To be talked down to by a piece of Bounded bacteria! Wow! Fuck, you can just die now!\"","BOOM!","The true power of a Gilded One unfurled at that moment as multiple Pulses of THE Scales bloomed around her in a blinding display of golden light, the existential radiation of her lust spreading out like a tidal wave as the surrounding structure began to warp into a landscape of her choosing!","HUUM!","And yet, even in the face of this existential pressure, Noah smiled brutally with a pride that reached for the throat of the stars.","\" Today is a good day...it is a good day to crack a Gilded One, a truly good day, so let me see what you’ve got!\"","BOOM!","An unfathomable pride burning with infinity surged out from his core as Quintessence Infiniforce endlessly bloomed around him in a suffocating and terrifying fashion, looking like a storm that would drown everything in its path!","The change that was being made in the surroundings by her radiation began to get reversed by the weight of his Sovereignty, the pink clouds being torn apart to reveal forming suns and stellar bodies that radiated with his own tyrannical light.","Noah stood dominantly in the center of the chaos, his eyes shining with the cold and brilliant fire of Nearu Absolute Infinity, and even as Custos Rani began to summon Pulses of THE Scales, he only moved forward with the hunger of a king who had finally found a meal worth eating!"]},{"number":5186,"title":"Chapter 5186: Chapter 5185: Crack A Gilded One! III","paragraphs":["The silence of the transitional domain was shattered by the violent expansion of Custos Rani’s presence, her Gilded foundations roaring with a manic and bruised pride that turned the cloying, sweet musk of her radiation into a suffocating miasma!","She stood upon the golden floor that Noah had hardened with his sovereignty, her pink robes billowing like wings of tattered silk while the galaxy-filled clusters of her eyes burned with a light that was no longer seductive, but purely fucking predatory.","Her laughter was a jagged thing that grated against the immaculate silence of THE Absolute Forge’s influence, sounding like the grinding of broken glass beneath the heel of a titan.","She raised her left hand to her own lips and breathed across her fingertips with a gesture that was both delicate and horrifying, for the air she released was thick with the shimmering threads of...a Cause.","THE Desidero Cause.","\" Desidero Ember, First of Wants,\" she hissed, her voice vibrating with the raw power of a Gilded soul that had been pushed too far by a creature it considered beneath notice.","\"I speak the Thread. I seed the Thread. What was content shall know its absence, and what was whole shall feel its fracture, so let the wanting commence where none existed. THE DESIDERO WHISPER!\"","She extended her hand outward with her fingers splayed, the threads of implanted desire racing through the air like invisible serpents to strike at Noah’s existence!","|The subject is deploying THE Desidero Whisper, THE Pulse of Implanted Want, backed by the authority of THE Desidero Cause.|","|This Pulse attempts to integrate a foreign, crystallized desire into your foundational motivations to rewrite your emotional architecture from within.|","| Because you are currently embodying THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity, your Pride rejects the very possibility of external desire, for a sovereign being acknowledges no want that does not originate from his own will.|","Noah watched the shimmering threads dissipate against the invisible wall of his Supremacy Radiation, his expression one of dry and calculating amusement that only served to fuel the woman’s rage!","He could smell the ozone and the faint, metallic tang of the Desidero threads as they burned away in his presence, the scent reminding him of wet copper and old, forgotten regrets .","\" Is that the best a Custodes can offer when their charms fail to produce a groveling slave? \" he asked, his voice carrying the heavy and unhurried resonance of a monarch who found the entire spectacle to be a tedious interruption.","\" You talked about bacteria and drops of sand, yet you’re the one breathing on your fingers and hoping that a few threads of wanting will make me forget that I held your Existence by the throat.\"","Rani’s face contorted into a mask of savage fury, her beauty curdling into a visceral horror as her aura flared with a crimson-gold light that began to liquefy the white sea beneath her feet!","She didn’t wait for another exchange of words, her arms raising above her head and bringing them down in a sweeping arc as she summoned a tide of invisible pressure that sought to drown the entire light-year of space!","\" Desidero Torrent, Sea of Wants! I pour the Thread and I drown the Thread, for what was endurable shall overflow, and the wanting shall exceed the vessel that holds it! THE DESIDERO FLOOD!\"","BOOM!","The domain was suddenly filled with an overwhelming surge of sensation that felt like every desire Noah had ever suppressed was being amplified to the intensity of a dying sun. It was a sensory overload of the highest order, a psychological siege that sought to fracture his consciousness by making every casual preference into a screaming, all-consuming compulsion that demanded immediate satisfaction!","Noah felt the pressure against his Superbius foundations, but he only stood his ground while the forming suns of his Quintessence Infiniforce began to burn with a more terrifying and suffocating brilliance.","He didn’t just resist the flood; he moved to consume the momentum of the attack, his own Nearu Absolute Infinity rising like a dark, crystalline tide to meet her golden torrent.","\" A good day to crack a Gilded One indeed. Come !\" he murmured, the words sounding like a promise delivered in the shadow of an executioner’s blade!","BOOM!","The multicolored brilliance of his Infiniforce bloomed outward in a terrifying fashion, the tyrannical pride of his Ego rewriting the pink clouds of the Desidero domain into landscapes of obsidian and cold, blue fire.","The change she had imposed was violently reversed as blinding stellar bodies began to form around Noah, their radiation broadcasting his supremacy with such intensity that the white sea began to evaporate into a mist of golden blood and dissolved information.","Noah stood at the center of the storm, his eyes shining with the cold fire of the Absolute, and he watched as the surprise in Rani’s galaxy-filled eyes turned into a flicker of genuine, visceral incredulity.","She summoned more Pulses of THE Scales around her as multiple Causes came to her defense, but the air was already thick with the smell of her pride starting to rot beneath the weight of a Bounded man!","\" Let me see,\" Noah whispered, his hand reaching out to grasp at the fabric of the transitional space itself.","\" Let me see, for my Pride demands it!\"","BOOM!","The transitional domain was no longer a place of quiet pink clouds and shimmering waterfalls, for it had become a claustrophobic slaughterhouse of competing authorities.","Custos Rani stood at the center of this localized apocalypse, her galaxy-filled eyes burning with a light that had moved past seduction and into the realm of absolute, unadulterated madness.","She commanded the architecture of the space to rise against the Bounded intruder, waving her hands in a grand, sweeping motion that summoned boundless rivers of golden Observable Force from the white sea below.","The rivers didn’t flow so much as they surged like starving predators, massive currents of liquid gold that carried the weight Causes, all of them aiming to drown Noah beneath the sheer, crushing mass of Gilded Luxuria authority.","Noah stood his ground as the first wave of the golden tide slammed into the perimeter of his sovereignty, the sound of the impact being a resonant, metallic boom that shook the foundations of the Desidero space.","He didn’t move an inch as the liquid gold curled around his figure, for the molten radiance simply bounced off the invisible wall of his Superbius Pride as if it were a common rain striking an obsidian mountain.","He let out a laugh that was thick with a glorious and terrifying pride, the sound echoing through the domain like the tolling of a funeral bell for the woman standing before him.","\" Is this the ’brilliant sun’ you promised, little Gilded one? \" he asked, his voice dripping with a dry and pragmatic disdain that made the golden rivers hiss and steam where they touched his aura, THE Absolute Superbius Ego of Infinity truly unleashing itself.","\"It feels more like a tepid bath...Custodes surely cannot be this weak. You must be one the weakest ones, right?\"","...!","|The target is utilizing Boundless Observable Force at the Third Scale capacity.|","|The golden rivers are attempting an Existential Drowning to overwrite your coordinates and compress your civilization.|","|Your Absolute Superbius Ego has identified these attacks as ’Insufficient.’|","|The Sovereign Overwrite is actively neutralizing the golden weavings upon contact, rendering their mass into harmless, unrefined energy.|","Rani’s face twisted into a mask of savage fury, her breath coming in ragged, wet gasps that smelled of honey and rot as she realized her primary manifestation was being treated as nothing but dross.","She surged forward with a speed that bypassed the need for traditional motion, her pink robes billowing like the wings of a predatory insect while her aura flared with a crimson-gold light that began to liquefy the air itself.","She unleashed THE Desidero Flood once more, but this time she infused the Pulse into her very hands and feet as she closed the distance for a brutal, close-quarters execution!","Her hands moved in a blurring flurry of strikes that targeted the vital nexuses of Noah’s existence, each hit carrying the weight of a dying existence and the suffocating pressure of her amplified Lust filled with boundless Luxuria Gilded Authority!","Noah met her head-on, his movements becoming a clinical display of his own foundations.","Physical? He could fucking get physical!","He didn’t back away as she unleashed a low, sweeping kick designed to shatter his shins, instead shifting his weight to catch the strike on the hardened obsidian pillar of his own leg, the sound of the collision being a sickening, wet crack of bone against iron!","He didn’t flinch as she tried to clinche his neck to deliver a series of devastating knees to his midsection, each one carrying the Immensity of her Pulses of THE Scales as his hands shot out to intercept her wrists with a grip that felt like the closing of a hydraulic press!"]},{"number":5187,"title":"Chapter 5187: Chapter 5186: Crack A Gilded One! IV","paragraphs":["\" Entertain me, O Gilded One!\" he roared, his voice surging with a prideful fire that caused the forming suns of his domain to flare with blinding intensity.","\" Show me the brilliance of the Braneworld! Show me why I should fear the children and Custodes of THE Magna Sorora...because this is an abysmal fucking introduction. Where is your pride? Where is your power? WHERE?!\"","BOOM!","He twisted his body with a violent grace, pulling her inward and delivering a sharp elbow covered by Nearu Absolute Infinity that caught her beneath the chin with the force of a tectonic shift.","CRACK!","The impact wasn’t a clean hit but a brutal explosion of Nearu Absolute Infinity that sent a spray of iridescent, golden-pink blood and teeth across his obsidian-light robes, the scent of her essence being a cloying mixture of ozone and failed perfection.","...!","\"...!\"","Rani reeled back, her head snapping upward as the prideful strike from a \"Bounded bacteria\" did the impossible...it caused her actual, visceral pain that her Gilded structure couldn’t immediately ignore!","She let out a scream that was a mixture of agony and disbelief, her galaxy-filled eyes wide with the realization that the hierarchy she’d been born into was being physically dismantled by a man who shouldn’t have been able to scratch her skin!","BOOM!","She tried to retaliate by summoning THE Desidero Whisper through a spinning kick that aimed for his temple, the threads of implanted want clinging to her foot like a shroud of hungry ghosts.","Noah didn’t even bother to block the strike with his hands; he simply leaned into the impact and caught her shin with his shoulder, the weight of her wrath and her lust bouncing off his Superbius Ego without leaving a single mark on his existence.","He grabbed her leg before she could retract it and slammed his fist into the center of her thigh with a blinding slap of infinity, the sound of her muscle tearing and her Gilded femur fracturing being a heavy, textured noise that filled the silence of the void.","|Internal Damage to Custos Rani: Gilded Structure Fracture detected.|","|The target’s Luxuria Empowerment is failing to provide adequate regeneration against the weight of your Pride and Nearu Absolute Infinity.|","|The subject’s pride is beginning to leak into the surrounding space as ’Information Waste.’|","Rani scrambled back across the hardened golden floor, her pink robes now stained with her own hot, iridescent blood that pooled in configurations that looked like maps of a dying civilization.","She began to laugh madly once more, the sound being a gurgling, wet thing as she coughed up a mixture of gold fluid and grey bile, her manic eyes fixed on the man who was walking toward her with the unhurried gait of a king.","\" How!? How?!\" she shrieked, her voice cracking as she summoned every Pulse she had left into a final, desperate shield of golden Observable Force.","\"I am a Custos of the Great Houses! I am the vessel of the Desidero! You are nothing but a mistake in the code of reality! An ant! Something Bounded!\"","Noah didn’t answer her with words; he simply closed the distance in a single, terrifying step that warped the space between them into a tunnel of blue and gold fire.","He began to rain down a series of heavy, physical blows that were filled with his superior pride and backed by his infinite light, his fists and palms becoming blinding engines of destruction that smacked and hit her with a rhythmic, brutal cadence.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Each strike was a wet, heavy thud that sounded like a butcher tenderizing meat , his fists crushing her ribs and his palms slamming into her face until her unfathomable beauty was nothing but a ruin of swollen flesh and shattered galaxies.","He smashed her body down onto the golden floor again and again, the surface cracking and splintering under the weight of a Gilded body being treated as nothing but a shitty, good-for-nothing rag doll.","\" Is this...the modified engineering you promised for my ’worthless structure’?\"","Noah asked, his voice low and dangerous as he stood over her, his hands dripping with her golden blood.","\" Is this the best the high-born can do when their toys start to fight back?\"","Rani lay in the center of the white sea’s ruin, her body a broken and twitching thing that was barely recognizable as the Custos who had descended from the fracture. She tried to raise her hand to manifest one final Pulse, her fingers trembling with the last remnants of her engineered Lust, but Noah didn’t give her the chance.","He raised his eyes, which were now shining with the terrifying fire of the Absolute, and he began to draw the lemniscate symbol in the air with a finger that was stained with the gold of her life.","He spoke slowly as if an ancient emperor was making his grand decree.","\" Infinite Ember ,\" he murmured, his voice sounding like the first spark of a world being born in the dark.","\" First Spark of my emergence. I am the Thread. I am the Cause.\"","The air around Rani began to grow cold and heavy, a silence settling over the space that felt like the moment before a life is snuffed out by the turning of a tide.","\" What exists without the fire of painful birth shall know that fire now. Let causality regress. Let existence remember its emergence. Let all that stands without the pained spark of life return to the moment before that spark was possible.\"","Noah looked down at the broken Gilded woman with a gaze that held no hatred, only a cold and pragmatic judgment that saw through the eons of her engineering.","\" THE INFINITE LIGHT.\"","HUUM!","A blinding, multicolored radiance erupted from the symbol in the air, a light that didn’t burn or destroy but simply interrogated the history of the being it touched. It reached into Rani’s existence and asked the single question that her engineering couldn’t answer...it asked if she had suffered to become what she was, if she had climbed the long and painful path of the Bounded to earn the standing she occupied.","The Gilded architecture within her foundations screamed as the answer was recorded as a null, for she had been born into the Third Scale, engineered into her beauty, and handed her power as a birthright of The Braneworld!","The regression commenced with a clinical and terrifying precision. Rani’s broken, adult body began to shrink and smooth over, her shattered bones unbreaking as they returned to a softer, more primitive state.","Noah stood over the broken ruin of the Gilded woman, his hands stained with the shimmering, iridescent gold of her essence while the air around them vibrated with the terminal frequency of her failing pride.","He looked down at her swollen features and the galaxy-filled eyes that were now clouded with a visceral, animal terror, and for a fleeting moment, he considered the pragmatic simplicity of snuffing her out right here in the dark.","It would be easy. It would be satisfying to watch the light of a high-born doll go out permanently beneath his heel, but his tyrannical mind quickly discarded the thought because he knew the Maharanis was still connexted to her.","If Rani’s life-thread snapped, the cold Sororis would descend with the full weight of her house, and Noah wasn’t quite ready to have that particular conversation while his feet were still wet with the blood of her favorite Custos.","\"I won’t kill you, little Gilded one, because your death would be far too loud for the quiet work I have planned for the Braneworld, \" he murmured, his voice carrying the dry, amused chill of a man who had already decided the fate of countless existences.","\" But...I’m going to take the architecture of your Existence and rewrite the laws that govern it, starting with the lie of your own legitimacy.\"","|The subject has activated THE Infinite Light.|","|Target: Custos Rani.|","|The Pulse is interrogating the target’s causal history to identify the ’Pained Emergence’ required by THE Infinite Cause.|","The blinding radiance of the Pulse didn’t seek to regress her physical body fully, but instead dove deep into the conceptual foundations of her mind, a cold and clinical light that tore through her memories of ease and birthright.","It reached into the void where her struggles should have been and found only the engineered perfection of a being who had never climbed, and the realization hit Rani’s consciousness with the force of a psychological execution.","She let out a gurgling, wet scream as her very existence began to question its own right to occupy space, the foundational lie of her Gilded standing unraveling as she realized she had no legitimate origin to anchor her against the storm.","Her mind fractured under the weight of the interrogation, the engineered Lust that had sustained her for eons collapsing into a black hole of existential doubt that left her wide open for the next stage of Noah’s work!","Noah didn’t hesitate, for he immediately began to pour his own Quintessence Infiniforce into the cracks of her psyche, shoving the raw power of his Infinite Cause into the spaces where her autonomy used to reside.","He inserted his Infinity into her weavings like a virus, his golden light binding itself to her neural pathways until every thought she had was filtered through the lens of his own sovereign will.","It was a total and absolute consumption of her personhood, a mastery that didn’t just break her body but claimed the very concept of her self as his property.","HUUM!","Rani’s body arched off the golden floor, her back snapping with a loud and textured crack as his Infinity fused with her marrow and her spirit, and then she fell back into the white sea with a dull thud.","The galaxy-filled light in her eyes flickered and then returned, but it was no longer the manic light of a Gilded predator; it was a cold, blue-gold reflection of the man standing over her.","She lay there for a moment while the transitional domain stabilized around them, the crimson-pink clouds turning a darker, more submissive shade of violet as the anchor of the space shifted its loyalty.","Then, with a slow and mechanical grace, the Custos rose from the ruin of her own defeat and knelt at Noah’s feet, her feet touching the cold, golden floor in a gesture of total and absolute surrender.","\" Master ,\" she whispered, her voice no longer cold or seductive but hollowed out and filled with the resonance of his own pride.","\"I...am the Thread. I am the Cause. Your will is the only light I acknowledge.\"","Noah looked down at her and felt a dark, pragmatic satisfaction, for he now had a Gilded puppet as his eyes and ears without alerting the Maharanis to the change.","He reached out and placed his hand on the top of her head, his fingers stained with the gold of her recent trauma, and he offered a brilliant, tyrannical smile to the empty void.","\" Good. Because...there is so much to be done. So...so much!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5188,"title":"Chapter 5188: Chapter 5187: Life and Existence!","paragraphs":["< Notes on Life and Existence, from The Musings of THE Genesis Monarch>","The fundamental architecture of life is built upon a foundation of absolute, unblinking inequity, for existence has never been a merchant of fairness but a butcher that decides which cuts of meat are destined for the high table and which are to be ground into the dirt of the lower domains.","Many wonder at the origins of The Gilded and The Bounded as if there were some grand, poetic reason for the disparity, yet the truth is as cold and pragmatic as a surgical strike: talent and potential are not gifts bestowed by anything, but are the raw biological and existential spoils of a theft that occurred before the first breath of a new reality was ever drawn.","It is a nauseating reality to consider that while one soul is born without a single drop of mana to lubricate the gears of their survival, another is born with the engineered capacity to extinguish stars or erase entire Primordial Realms with a casual wave of a hand, and this difference is not a matter of destiny but of structural positioning within the feeding chain of Existence.","When THE First Cause erupts to birth a new Observable Existence, it is less a celebratory event of creation and more a violent hemorrhage of raw potential that draws the attention of THE Primeval Ones who have waited in the dark for eons.","These ancient entities and their Gilded progeny do not descend upon a newly born Observable to offer blessings or guidance, but instead they latch onto the wellspring of THE First Cause like parasites at the throat of a fresh kill, drinking deep of the untapped authority to produce even more Gilded Ones and secure their own sovereign stations.","They occupy these new realms and claim the vast percentage of THE First Cause’s power for their own, leaving behind only the dredges and the thinning remnants of mana for the Bounded lifeforms who are forced to build civilizations out of the scraps that the masters found too bitter to swallow.","The smell of this existential theft permeates the very fabric of the lower domains, a tang of authority dissolving that reminds every Bounded creature that their poverty of power was a choice made by those who sit comfortably above.","The most persistent question that plagues others of the abyss is why the truly powerful, those Gilded Ones who have lived for eons and mastered the weavings of reality, would choose to anchor their immortality in the so-called Negative Egos of Existence.","Why would a civilization capable of absolute perfection choose to amplify the filth of Pride, the searing fire of Wrath, or the bottomless, industrial hunger of Gluttony?","They did not make this choice out of a lack of imagination or a misunderstanding of morality, but because the negative Egos possess a specific gravity and a savage density that the virtues simply cannot approximate.","In an Existence where power is literal consumption and every victory is a pyrrhic struggle against the void, a soul anchored in Humility is a soul that is too light to withstand the crushing pressure of sovereign expansion, for the virtues are diffuse and yielding while the \"sins\" are the iron pillars upon which a truly tyrannical hierarchy can be built... or so many believe.","But they...have not played with Virtues enough to understand. They truly do not understand.","But, continuing on with the mindset that Sins are supreme.","Superbius...is a structural integrity that refuses to be altered by external force. Ira is not merely rage; it is an unyielding engine of martial readiness that ensures the sword never dulls.","Gula is not merely hunger, it is the Relentless industrial output required to process the raw meat of existence into the refined artifacts of a glorious caste.","The Gilded built their world on these foundations because anything less would have been crushed by the weight of their own stolen potential, and they found that the taste of Wrath was a more reliable fuel than the sweet, fleeting breath of Charity.","Existence continues to churn and move in a cycle of consumption and indifference, offering many questions to those who have the leisure to ask them, but the answers do not drift through the air like spores.","The truth is buried in the marrow of those who were strong enough to take it, and it reveals itself only to those who are willing to go searching in the dark places where the blood of the Bounded still stains the golden floors of the elite.","-Observations on THE Scales, THE Genesis Monarch","---","<THE Creature>","Many beings believed in good and evil, right and wrong, but more often than not, things were much more complex than this.","Around the same time that THE Genesis Monarch bound THE Custos of Sororis Prima Prabhavati within the transitional pink clouds of THE Desidero Domain, a far more savage drama was unfolding a vast distance away in the endlessly tumultuous regions known as THE Undefined Gaps.","These were the infinite, lightless fractures in space that existed between THE Observable Existence and THE Braneworld Observable Existence, stretching boundless and terrifying due to their sheer Undefinition.","They were almost as chaotic as the void outside of reality where no THE Second Scale entities could hope to survive for more than a heartbeat.","Within this sensory-deprivation tank of violent energy, a hunt had been carried out across the hours that passed, as a pack of THE Gilded Ones relentlessly chased after THE Young Relictus whose very presence was a stain upon their orderly masterpiece. A unique development had finally occurred within THE Undefined Gaps, for it seemed that THE Young Relictus had finally been cornered against the wall of a static, unobservable fold!","THE Creature stood at the center of the darkness, his body burning with multicolored flames that were tinted by a glorious and heavy obsidian light, his eyes reflecting the cold hunger of THE Primordial Source as he found himself surrounded by eighteen of THE Gilded Ones.","Eight of these hunters were THE Superbius Gilded Ones who floated with a nauseating degree of arrogance, their golden robes shimmering even in the lightless Gaps, while ten THE Ira Gilded Ones stood at the forefront like crimson-clad bastions of distilled rage.","The space they occupied was a textured void, a place where the darkness felt like a physical weight pressing against the skin and the only illumination came from the predatory glow of Gilded authority.","A dominating Superbius Gilded One with a grand, muscular physique floated ahead of his peers, the power of multiple Causes bouncing off his chest like rain off a mountain as he looked at THE Relictus with a gaze that held only clinical disdain.","\" You truly thought you could kill one of us and simply run into the dark while growing stronger, as if THE Magna Sorora would not eventually close the loop on your transgression?\" he asked, his voice carrying the resonance of an executioner’s verdict.","\" When we have locked onto a thread, we don’t let it go until the information is retrieved, and momentarily even more of us will arrive here as we finally harvest and break down the components of THE Relictus.\"","...!"]},{"number":5189,"title":"Chapter 5189: Chapter 5188: Momentum!","paragraphs":["At such words, THE Creature didn’t flinch or show the tremors of a cornered animal, for he only offered a brutal and unsettling smile that seemed out of place on his ancient face.","Right now, he felt a strange and piercing sense of freedom and sadness that nobody else could understand, for he was free because he was entirely alone, and because he was alone, the weight of his sadness was a physical burden that sat in his chest alongside his power.","Existence was unfair and filled with an adversity that didn’t care for the noble intentions of the weak, and he knew it was okay to feel free and sad simultaneously so long as one kept moving forward through the viscera of his own path.","He understood that existence would, by its very nature, remain exactly the way it was...a rigid hierarchy of THE Primeval Ones, THE Gilded Ones, and THE Bounded Lifeforms that would continue for countless eons of consumption unless someone moved to physically shatter the arrangement.","Nothing changed unless someone did something, and THE Creature never once entertained the delusion that he could change the entirety of existence at once, for he was far too young and the scope of the void was far too vast.","He didn’t think he could change everything, but he knew he could get started in THE Observable Existence he was currently in and move outward from there, one steady and blood-soaked step at a time.","He breathed out a slow, steady cloud of multicolored vapor and closed his eyes as he felt the resonance of the glorious source, THE Primordial Source that lived beneath the skin of reality.","All of his worries and the lingering sadness of his loneliness momentarily paused. He remembered her face as his existence became firmer and brighter as he voiced his thoughts deeply, the sound of his voice cutting through the tumultuous noise of THE Undefined Gaps.","\" No, I didn’t think for a single moment that I could kill one of you and simply leave unscathed, because that was never the plan I had laid out for the afternoon. The First Domino, The False Golden Idol, was only the first domino in a much larger collapse, and I needed his death to act as a springboard to draw the rest of you out from your golden towers.\"","He opened his eyes, and the obsidian light within them had become a crushing, physical pressure that caused the Ira warriors to tighten their grip on their crimson blades.","\"I needed multiple more of THE Gilded Ones to sustain the trajectory of my growth, which is why all of you are here now, for you’re going to help me keep my momentum during my Ascent. In existence, one needs to have momentum and pacing to keep going unceasingly, and I wasn’t running from you; I was gathering as many of you as I could while giving myself the time to prepare. Now, we can finally get started, and I suggest you remember that in Existence, there is only... Mo! Men! Tum!\"","BOOM!","The entire region of THE Undefined Gaps instantly flashed with a blinding obsidian light that swallowed the golden radiance of THE Gilded Ones, all sound fading into a terrifying, unnatural silence as vision was cut off by the surge of THE Primordial Source.","The only thing that could be heard within the lightless void was the booming voice of THE Creature, sounding like the judgment of a dark titan rising from the depths of the abyss.","\" Why do you all think you never got your filthy hands on THE Primordial Source? \" he asked, his voice dripping with a visceral disdain.","\"It’s because vile and filthy hands shouldn’t get to touch something so pristine, and while you’ll always seek it, you will never find it in the halls of your Gilded houses. It’s abhorrent that you were even able to get your hands on THE Infinite, but I believe in the future..mthat even that will be stripped from you, so today, let me show you the true face of THE Primordial Source. Let me...show you.\"","HUUM!","As the obsidian flames began to settle, the body of THE Creature became the only visible entity in the void, wreathed in a fire that was so dark it seemed to consume the surrounding shadows!","The obsidian flames began to coalesce and harden on his face, forming a glorious and terrifying bony mask that looked as if it had been carved from the very foundations of a dead existence.","While this bony mask formed, his aura reached levels that were so terrifying they caused the space around him to groan and crack, the smell of ancient bone and ozone filling THE Undefined Gaps as he took a single, fearless step toward the eighteen THE Gilded Ones who had thought they were the hunters.","The weight of THE Primordial Source was now absolute, and as he moved, THE Gilded Ones felt the first genuine chill of a death that they hadn’t engineered for themselves.","BOOM!","THE Gilded Ones.","His thoughts moved with the speed of a kinetic strike as he analyzed the sheer, offensive density of their power, breaking the architecture of THE Gilded Ones down into a few fundamental components that defined their absolute advantage.","Their bodies were stronger and vaster, their internal systems filled with a degree of potential that made them appear as the favored children of THE Observable Existence, especially as THE Observable Force flooded their marrow and made it nauseatingly easy for them to alter the surrounding environment through their presence alone.","With the addition of their engineered Egos, their base values were inflated to a degree that allowed them to harness their next great strength, THE Infinite. Infinity.","Within their bodies, Infinity flowed in abundance, yet THE Creature felt like he was watching something pristine being defiled by its residence in the bodies of these lifeforms, for they had not earned the right to carry the boundless.","When THE Infinite was added to their roster, it expanded their power in the reaches of THE Paleozoic Scale, allowing them to bypass the long eons of the Transitional Cambrian stage to become adults who were profoundly confident and filled with a terrifying conviction.","That was merely their starting point, but as if all of that were not enough, they had begun drawing additional power from the surrounding existences through a methodology that only those at the Proterozoic Scale could typically touch- THE Pulses of THE Scales and the raw authority of THE Causes."]},{"number":5190,"title":"Chapter 5190: Chapter 5189: Choices I","paragraphs":["In the higher reaches of existential engineering, it was understood that while THE First Cause was the singular, erupting ocean that made way for an entire THE Observable Existence, it was comprised of countless smaller THE Causes that functioned as the currents and the laws of that reality.","THE Desidero Cause governed the mechanics of wanting and desire, while THE Superbius Cause provided the structural integrity of sovereignty, yet there were others that THE Creature could feel humming within the Gaps...THE Letum Cause, which dictated the inevitability of endings, and THE Aeternus Cause, which anchored the static configurations of existence.","These smaller THE Causes were the threads that THE Gilded Ones utilized to sew their wills into the fabric of reality, drawing upon the specific weavings of THE First Cause to bolster their own engineered foundations.","THE Creature focused his gaze on a roaring THE Superbius Gilded One whose muscular physique was a testament to the vanity of his house, seeing his body differently compared to any other being as he peered through the golden skin to witness the glistening organs and the silver-etched bones.","He saw the seas of THE Observable Force moving through the target’s vessels and identified the clusters where Infinity was anchored, tracing the shimmering threads back to THE Causes from which the Gilded warrior was currently drawing his suffocating power.","With a motion that was both beautiful and horrifying, THE Creature swung his multicolored sword, the blade wreathed in the heavy and unyielding obsidian light of THE Primordial Source.","The obsidian light acted as a terminal shears, for as the blade passed through the local space, it proceeded to sever the metaphysical connections where this Gilded One was drawing his authority!","THE Creature cut him off from THE Causes, from THE Infinite, and even from the flow of THE Observable Force, leaving the warrior with nothing but his own engineered Ego to sustain him against the darkness of THE Undefined Gaps.","SQUELCH!","The multicoloured sword passed through the chest of THE Gilded One with a wet, heavy sound of tearing meat and cracking bone, and obsidian hooks formed upon the blade to anchor its position within the target’s foundations.","As THE Creature pulled the sword out with a violent wrench, a glistening heart and several iridescent organs erupted from the chest cavity in a spray of stellar light and crimson-gold blood!","THE Creature opened his mouth and allowed his own gravitational authority to pull these organs toward him, and he proceeded to brutally chew and devour them right away, the metallic tang of Gilded essence filling his senses while the crimson-gold fluid sputtered down his chin.","The Gilded One roared out in a mixture of shock and rising rage as his heart was consumed, but before THE Creature could enjoy the taste of his victory, three other of THE Gilded Ones layered multiple THE Pulses of THE Scales upon his position from above.","BOOM!","THE Creature’s body was smashed down into the depths of the Gaps with enough force to shatter any common Ordovician Paleozoic Scale entity, and he went crashing into the solidified and inverted obsidian mountain ranges that served as the floor of the Undefinition!","BOOM!","He slowly rose from the center of a massive, smoking crater while stretching his body with a tyrannical grace, the sound of his joints popping being the only noise in the sudden silence of the impact.","He noted that THE Gilded Ones remained terrifyingly powerful, for those attacks had caused him a genuine, destabilizing pain that made his existence flicker, but he welcomed the sensation as the familiar weight of hardship and adversity.","As such vile things as THE Gilded Ones were, they were undeniably powerful, and he knew he needed to pick them off one by one, isolating them and gaining as much of their information as he could before they labeled him a greater threat and deployed genuine monsters from THE Magna Sorora.","Step by step, he would climb.","THE Creature rose up again and looked toward the heights where THE Gilded Ones were circling their gravely injured comrade, and he voiced his thoughts with a voice that was as cold as the void between the stars.","\" That’s one. Are the rest of you...ready to contribute, or are you going to continue standing there while I keep my... Momentum!\"","BOOM!","His body surged upward like an incandescent, flaming obsidian blade that was ready to cut open the things that should have never been cut, and the darkness of THE Undefined Gaps was once again filled with the sound of a Young Relictus beginning his ascent!","---","Noah was finding out something about himself that he did not expect, for the long eons of his progression had typically been defined by the spectacular and the distant, grand weavings that kept his enemies at a distance while he unmade them with a variety of weavings of power.","For the past few years, he had fought with a variety of skills and abilities and spectacular weavings of existence that were brilliant and showy and a glorious spectacle to behold, ranging from the primal fury of fireballs and the grotesque architecture of abominations to the relentless legions of the undead.","He had mastered the capabilities of Sever, Indefatigable, and the depths of the True Sources, climbing all the way through the complexities of Principles, Ways, and the heavy authority of Civilizations and Infinity itself, yet more recent fights had him finding a peculiar satisfaction... in the visceral closeness of the struggle.","He found himself increasingly drawn to the sensation of utilizing his own hands and feeling the raw exertion of power and immensity as it translated directly into the physical collapse of his enemies, a realization that carried no trace of madness but rather a cold, pragmatic appreciation for the immediate feedback of violence.","There was an undeniable texture to bathing his hands in the very force of infinity or gripping the Spear of Civilization that held the weight of the entire Infiniverse, and feeling how the eon’s worth of advancements and the proud civilizations of his enemies shattered beneath his physical grip felt unexpectedly good!"]},{"number":5191,"title":"Chapter 5191: Chapter 5190: Choices! II","paragraphs":["The thought was an odd one to have as he paused in the silence of the transitional domain, and he asked himself whether he was developing some negative tendencies based on the Egos he was currently amplifying or if he was simply discovering a more honest method of existence.","And he had many skills, abilities, Principles that he utilized for their current stages as after he exceeded them, he didn’t use them much as he didn’t feel the need to.","But his hands and feet...he would always have his his hands and feet to smash things!","There was a profound and logical catharsis that emerged from physical combat that detached skills and grand weavings could never replicate, for skills was essentially a manipulation of the code of reality while a physical strike was a direct confrontation of essence against essence.","When one utilizes their hands and legs to break an enemy, there is no filter of interpretation and no distance of causality; there is only the wet sound of resistance and the grinding vibration of bone meeting authority that provides an absolute confirmation of one’s own superiority.","Frankly, it just felt good! He was not developing any negative tendancies or anything like that.","In the weavings of existence where every victory was bought with the blood of the Bounded, Noah found that putting the terrifying weight of his Cause and the density of his Infinity into his fists allowed him to experience the brutality of his enemies as a tangible substance that he could physically dismantle and crush into the dirt.","As he remained lost in these thoughts, he stood over the body of Custos Rani in the space she had enacted, her figure floating flat on her back with her skin and muscles pulled back in a clinical, surgical display that revealed the glowing pink-gold light of her internal components!","He observed the Gilded bones and the iridescent organs in detail, watching how the gold and silver-etched marrow and the pulsing vessels of the Luxuria designation operated with a structural complexity that surpassed anything he had seen in the lower domains.","His hands moved to analyze the makeup of her existence with the detached focus of an architect examining the blueprints of a rival’s fortress, and he nodded shortly after as he recognized the similarities between her anatomy and the components he had seen from the gift of THE Creature.","\"About the same as the components I saw from the gift of THE Creature, though the resonance of the Luxuria heart is a touch more... frenetic,\" he said calmly, his voice vibrating with the cold authority of his Absolute Superbius Ego.","\"Alright, close up, Little Rani.\"","As he issued the command, he closed his eyes to check on his Hadean Organ of Civilization, projecting his consciousness into the lightless and immense reaches of THE Absolute Forge of Infinity where he kept his Nearu Absolute Infinity compressed.","Within this internal workshop, he observed the fourteen massive illusory versions of himself that stood like silent sentinels of his potential, noting that while Superbius and Humilitas were already brightly lit, a third manifestation was now beginning to ignite with a shimmering, iridescent pink-gold flame.","Beside THE Absolute Amaranthine Heart of Emotive, the woman herself was moving with a manic curiosity, her eyes wide as she watched the new Ego stabilize and solidify within the forge’s architecture.","Noah appeared in front of the massive manifestation of THE Absolute Luxuria Ego of Infinity, and he looked upon the figure with an appreciative, tyrannical eye, for it was a being of shifting, crystalline skin and flowing robes of liquid starlight that seemed to pull at the very fabric of the surrounding space.","The manifestation carried a beauty that was both breathtaking and horrifying, its features possessing a predatory grace that suggested a hunger that could never be satiated regardless of how much of reality it consumed.","As he established the connection, comprehensive prompts began to bloom within his awareness, detailing the terrifying capabilities of the third completed Ego with a clinical precision that made his eyes shine with a brilliant, dark light.","| THE Absolute Luxuria Ego of Infinity has been successfully integrated into THE Absolute Forge.|","| Desire Consumption: You possess the capability to consume the desires of those around you, converting their wants and their longings into your own internal capacity for power. Every flicker of lust, ambition, and craving within your proximity flows into you as a tangible substance, allowing you to grow stronger the more your enemies desire their own survival or their own goals.|","| The Pleasure Cascade : You can induce waves of ecstatic pleasure in your targets, overwhelming their processing capacity with a sensory intensity that exceeds the structural limits of their civilization. Affected beings collapse into helpless states of total surrender, and prolonged exposure ensures the dissolution of their foundations as their existences cannot maintain coherence under the weight of continuous, engineered pleasure.|","| Quintessential Indulgence : Those without a sufficiently dense Ego find themselves unable to resist the beck and call of your presence, for your very existence broadcasts a passive radiation that makes them want nothing more than your approval. When focused, this ability pits the full will of the target against your own, forcing them to find fulfillment only in the service of your desires.|","| Pillow Talk : The very weavings of existence crave your satisfaction above all else, causing secrets, knowledge, and forbidden information to naturally flow toward you as if Existence itself were confessing its truths. Information that aligns with your current objectives will stream into your awareness without the need for active interrogation, for reality itself wants you to be satisfied.|","| THE Desidero Singularity: You can collapse the intent and the direction of all external attacks into a singular point within your own existence, transforming the ’want’ to harm you into the ’want’ to fuel you. Any strike backed by the desire for your destruction is drawn into this singularity and neutralized, its energy being added to your reserves as a tribute to your Absolute standing.|","|THE Apotheosis of the Wanton: You can rewrite the local laws of causality based entirely on your own whims and wants, making your desire the primary axiom of the region. If you want a target to unmake themselves, the very rules of their biology will begin to align with that desire, forcing their existence to struggle against its own foundational instinct for survival in favor of satisfying your whim.|","...!","Noah’s eyes shone with a terrifying brilliance as he looked at the capabilities of Luxuria.","\" Why...are there so many? \" he murmured to the void of the forge, his voice carrying a dry, pragmatic amusement that echoed off the iridescent walls.","Because he was just thinking about how less abilities and skills were better for him, and yet even more unfurled!","The one positive was multiple of them being passive if he took on the transformation of Luxuria!"]},{"number":5192,"title":"Chapter 5192: Chapter 5191: Choices! III","paragraphs":["Noah was getting familiar with the capabilities of THE Absolute Luxuria Ego of Infinity, for he wanted to see exactly how its effect would manifest when projected through the lens of his own Hadean foundations.","He closed his eyes and allowed the cold integrity of his Superbius Pride to recede, beckoning the iridescent and predatory resonance of Luxuria to rise and overwrite the architecture of his form!","The transformation was not a subtle shift but a violent re-shaping of his existence, his skin becoming a shifting, crystalline substance that caught the light of the transitional domain and refracted it into a thousand sharp and hungry hues.","His robes dissolved into a flowing garment of liquid starlight that seemed to pull at the very fabric of the surrounding space, and his features settled into a beauty that was so unfathomable and dangerous it felt like a silent scream of aesthetic perfection.","Noah raised his hands to look at the shimmering, translucent texture of his crystalline fingers, his gaze moving across the predatory grace of his own limbs with a dry and pragmatic appreciation.","Beside him, the figure of Custos Rani began to tremble with a visceral intensity that shook the pink-gold radiance of her robes, her eyes wide with a shock that bordered on terror as she looked at him!","After a heartbeat of frozen incredulity, this Gilded One actually felt a dark and uncontrollable blush creep across her ruined features, and she looked down at the golden floor as if the mere sight of him was a sensory overload she could no longer sustain!","Noah was about to ask her for the specific reason of her shock when in the next moment, a sudden and catastrophic change erupted within the domain.","BOOM!","An influx of THE Observable Force and Quintessence Infiniforce erupted from his body and from the very surroundings with intensity, his existence visibly emanating an increasingly denser sense of pressure and power that threatened to crack the boundaries of the transitional space!","Noah was genuinely surprised as he sensed his generation of Quintessence Infiniforce seemingly multiplied by many times over, his body becoming encased in a thick shell of Nearu Absolute Infinity while his Pillar of Infinity also became denser and grander as more and more infinity surged into its depths!","The reason for this erupting and increasingly grand change was revealed to him in an instant as prompts began to bloom before his eyes, detailing the silent and hungry mechanics of his newest Ego.","| The passive effects of Desire Consumption have been activated.|","|The nearby subject, Custos Rani, has had her desires and emotions consumed to provide minimal gains for your weavings of existence.|","|The subject THE Living Emotive, whose heart you carry, seems to be uniquely anamolous and holds seemingly endless desires and emotions, and she has had her weavings and desires consumed as they have provided and are continuing to provide Quintessential gains for your weavings of existence.|","|Boundless desires and emotions are continuing to be absorbed and consumed from the surrounding substrate, further amplifying THE Absolute Luxuria Ego of Infinity as you move.|","Noah blinked at the prompts that bloomed before his eyes and couldn’t help but turn his gaze inward to his own Forge of Infinity, wondering exactly what kind of manic feast Emotive was providing for him.","Within the internal reaches of his consciousness, he had taken on the shimmering form of the Luxuria Ego, and he found himself looking at a startled Emotive who was staring back at him with vibrant eyes that held the manic obsession of a being who had just found her prime specimen!","She looked at him with an intensity that seemed to vibrate through the entire forge, her hands twitching as if she were trying to decide whether to run toward him or simply dissolve into a pool of satisfied starlight.","She cleared her throat and spoke in a serious fashion, yet her words came out with an absent-minded honesty that suggested she didn’t entirely mean to say them out loud.","\"I...would gladly give every other part of my existence if you would just take those thick, strong arms of yours and wrap them around me and just... err.\"","She cleared her throat again and blinked rapidly as if she had just noticed that Noah was staring directly into her thoughts, and she quickly tried to pivot back!","\" Ahem, Sir, since you are...currently present here, I wanted to use this as a chance to get your permission for something I had planned to do on my own, for my dream will never be achieved if I simply and passively remain around you without taking the initiative.\"","Her figure brightened.","\"I have sensed THE Gilded Ones permeating and beginning to establish bases within our Observable Existence, and I had planned to begin siphoning off their emotions and egos while utilizing the immense power contained within this forge to penetrate their defenses. If I take on the form of Luxuria myself while doing so, I could bring them under my control and feed your growth with the raw meat of their own engineered wants... huhuhu... hahaha!\"","Emotive put her hand on her face as she laughed devilishly, her manic joy filling the silent spaces of the forge with a resonance that was both unsettling and impressive.","Noah looked at her and thought of the initiative and the ridiculous weavings of this woman who might just be one of the more unique existences within their Observable Existence.","\" Do what you need to do without getting caught. I...will only save you once or twice if you get yourself into genuine trouble.\"","Emotive’s eyes went wide and round as she heard these words, and she let out a soft, delighted squeal before burying her face in her hands and wiggling her feet with overwhelming joy that seemed entirely out of place.","Noah shook his head at this.","After this, Noah opened his eyes again within the transitional domain to find Custos Rani already down on her knees.","His eyes flashed coldly with the iridescent light of Luxuria, and his voice carried a heavy, demanding resonance as he addressed his puppet.","\" Why do you seem so shocked at my form, and why does your Gilded existence tremble as if it has seen its own ending within my reflection?\"","Rani’s pupils trembled as she slowly raised her head, her voice shaking with a reverence that she could no longer suppress beneath the weight of his radiation.","\" Your figure... your presence... it reminds me of the records of Servius Desideratum, THE Devouring Vessel, who was a Luxuria to turn his desire inward and consume the very existence he was meant to serve. He is and was a terrifying and renowned figure in THE Braneworld Observable Existence during The Fourth and Fifth Ages, a being whose amplified Lust became a devouring field that could consume the emotions of THE Superbius and Ira and even the indifference of THE Relictus itself. We were taught to fear his name, and as I look at you now...the unique immensity you give seems to be close to his brilliance of Luxuria!\"","WAA!","Noah listened to her explanation with a calm silence, his gaze moving across the shimmering horizon of the transitional domain!"]},{"number":5193,"title":"Chapter 5193: Chapter 5192: Choices! IV","paragraphs":["After receiving knowledge of some renowned Gilded One and the mention of Ages from Custos Rani, Noah had commanded this puppet gently for her to transfer all the knowledge she had to him, his fingers lingering on her forehead as the iridescent weavings of her memory began to bleed into his own consciousness.","He wanted these memories because at this moment, he wanted to have a clear definition of his long-term and short-term goals, for he found that navigating the higher domains without a definitive map was a tedious waste of his infinite potential.","His end goal was simply safety and an existence where he didn’t have to worry about the encroaching shadows of the void, envisioning a quiet life of mana and farming that felt more like a distant dream than a reachable reality.","But dumb fuckers would not leave him alone and continued to press their engineered arrogance against his skin, so they made his goal a bit more complex than the simple cultivation of a garden.","To achieve his very straightforward goal, he had to overcome the gap between Bounded and Gilded, ensuring his safety against Gilded monsters and those above them who could stand in his way.","He really thought he had been mild and laid-back for the most part since he came out of his Wheel of Existence and entered the Folds, acting with a restraint...well, for the most part.","He hadn’t really done anything too crazy!","But when he thought about THE Gilded Ones and what he could do to overcome them and eliminate the threat of these beings and their immense weavings of existence...","He looked at the kneeling form of Rani and then toward the distant coming horizons of THE Braneworld Observable Existence with a gaze that turned unfathomably cold.","\"Is it time to return on the brutal path of conquest again?\"","BOOM!","Existence around him began to buzz as if his surroundings were becoming shaky at this thought, for the very idea of Noah returning to his path of absolute expansion sent ripples through the weavings of the transitional domain!","There was Ubergulden Adelheid who had an apparent unique and high identity among THE Superbius, and he already had a Luxuria Gilded One under his control as if he truly exerted himself and returned to his path of Conquest...","He could begin silently moving in the shadows to bring to his control more and more of THE Gilded Ones before he began to wage open war on a glorious path of Conquest and Quintessence.","And as he received the memories from Custos Rani, his eyes clouded over with the weight of eons of Gilded history and the staggering geography of the higher domains, as well as history of countless unsavory things.","He was disgusted and amazed at the complexities of the power structures and lands of THE Braneworld Observable Existence that Rani had information of as they were heavy and filled with many things that would require his immediate attention.","As he processed the memories more and more, his short-term goals of conquest and Ubergulden Adelheid and his end goal of farming with boundless infinity and mana gained a rigid structure as he nodded to the empty air.","\" Conquer THE Gilded Ones, exceed Vakochev’s Scales by designing my Infinite Scales to be even grander, refine my THE Infinite Cause, and gain access to THE Primordial Source... light work. Light fucking work!\"","---","<THE Creature>","THE Creature continued his desperate and calculated dance within the lightless folds of THE Undefined Gaps, his multicolored flames flickering with a violent intensity as he fended off the collective assault of THE Gilded Ones.","Multiple other Ira Gilded Ones were already heavily injured and leaking iridescent ichor into the void, yet they continued to look at him with a cold and engineered hatred that required no words to convey!","THE Creature calculated exactly how much time he had left before the weight of his actions drew a response he couldn’t survive, for he knew he needed to wrap things up and return to the shadows of THE Undefinition.","He had gained a fleeting glimpse of knowledge regarding the terrifying scope of their power, and he knew that these beings weren’t merely lifeforms contained within a single pocket of Existence.","There were extremely old and ancient Gilded Ones who had been present even before he was born, entities who were able to harness the raw power of THE First Cause to propagate even more Gilded Ones for the future across the eons.","Such beings and those within THE Magna Sorora held power and complexities that allowed their influence to span across multiple Observable Existences, no only a single one!","Whether they were called THE Braneworld Observable Existence or whatever unique names they established for the territories they occupied.","He had to wrap things up here and move, yet before his intent could translate into a single step of retreat...","BOOM!","A terrifying impact boomed out across the entire region of THE Undefined Gaps, sending the very fabric of existence spinning in a nauseating blur before THE Creature was smashed onto a solidified obsidian floor of THE Undefinition.","For the first time since his emergence, he gazed coldly at his own left hand which he had raised instinctively in a desperate defense, seeing that the long bone covered by the obsidian flames of THE Primordial Source was visibly fractured.","A crimson scorch mark marred his skin as if he had been burnt by a fire comprised of dense Infinity and Observable Force, and tremendous waves of pain cascaded through his existence with a texture that demanded his absolute acknowledgment!","He rose from the center of the crater with his gaze remaining as cold and unyielding as the obsidian mountain ranges around him, looking up to see that the domain he had enacted to remain hidden had been pierced by a force of absolute authority.","New entrants...had arrived.","A terrifyingly radiant woman floated above the wreckage of his concealment, a crimson gold crown hanging diagonally upon her head as her imperious gaze looked down upon him with a total absence of warmth.","It was actually the entity standing beside her who had smashed into THE Creature and caused such a grievous injury, and THE Creature’s eyes narrowed as he analyzed the threat before him.","The entity was a terrifyingly muscular giant who shone with the concentrated crimson light of THE Ira, his massive arms and legs wrapped in crimson halos that radiated a power so heavy it caused the surrounding space to groan!"]},{"number":5194,"title":"Chapter 5194: Chapter 5193: End of The Road! I","paragraphs":["He possessed an extremely brutal and devilish smile that showed too many teeth, and he looked down at THE Creature as if he were observing a particularly interesting insect that he was about to crush.","\"Is this the anomaly that has arisen from the lands below that you all are allowing to run so rampantly?\" the massive entity asked, his voice sounding like the grinding of tectonic plates.","\" He doesn’t seem like much of anything at all, especially considering I’ve felt genuine fear from actual monstrous Relictus before, so tell me, is this one merely a chickling that has wandered too far from its nest?\"","This Ira turned his predatory gaze toward the woman beside him, his crimson halos pulsing with readiness that was almost suffocating to perceive!","\" Ubergulden Hye-jin, do I have your permission to let loose and see what his bones are made of?\"","The imperious and regal gaze of the woman with a loose diagonal crown, Ubergulden Hye-jin, remained fixed on THE Creature, her voice ringing out through THE Undefined Gaps with the cold precision of a royal decree!","\" Don’t destroy his body completely, Prima Custos Ragnar, for we need to extract and harvest what we can of THE Primordial Source once his resistance has been properly neutralized.","THE Creature’s gaze remained cold the entire time as he affirmed heavily that actual powerhouses of THE Gilded Ones had appeared to conclude the hunt. Gauging how he had been injured so severely from the very first strike, he knew that his next move had to be absolute, but-","BOOM!","Before his thoughts could even solidify into action, his body moved instinctively as he used his reforming hand and his uninjured hand to block the descent of a mountain!","Prima Custos Ragnar had already appeared above him with a speed that even he could barely perceive, his massive fist being larger than THE Creature’s entire body as it smashed down with weight!","The impact caused the surrounding space to shatter like fragile glass before it rapidly reformed under the pressure of the attack, and obsidian light flashed incessantly around THE Creature as he warped and appeared in a different location!","His eyes were heavy and his expression had turned pale for the first time!","Ragnar’s body was reinforced with THE Observable Force in concentrations millions of times greater than any of THE Gilded Ones he had faced so far.","Before THE Creature could even attempt to counter-attack, Ragnar was already behind him, punching out with a force that seemed to ignite the very vacuum of THE Undefined Gaps.","THE Creature turned to meet the threat with a punch burning with the concentrated obsidian flames of THE Primordial Source, but the discrepancy in raw existential mass was a gap that simple conviction could not bridge at this stage of his growth!","BOOM!","The impact this time was not an explosion of shared force but a chillingly quiet display of absolute dominance as Ragnar’s massive hand simply opened and swallowed THE Creature’s fist, the crimson rings wrapping around the giant’s wrist flaring with a violent, authoritative light.","These rings immediately elongated and clamped onto THE Creature’s arm like hungry, metallic serpents, and they began to emanate a suffocating pressure drawn from multiple Causes that anchored his existence to Ragnar’s own, pinning him in place within THE Undefined Gaps!","Oh!","Ragnar did not let go of the pinned limb, and instead used his free hand to begin a systematic and terrifyingly brutal pummeling that lacked the grace of a duel and possessed all the clinical savagery of a butcher unmaking a carcass!","The first strike caught THE Creature in the solar plexus, a heavy, wet sound of collapsing muscle and shattering internal weavings echoing through the lightless void as the obsidian flames covering his torso were snuffed out by the sheer density of Infinity and THE Observable Force!","BOOOM!","Ragnar’s massive fist struck again and again with a rhythmic, sickening cadence, each blow landing with a force that shattered a dozen ribs and sent fragments of bone deep into THE Creature’s internal organs.","Tremendous waves of pain cascaded through his consciousness, the taste of blood and his own dissolving authority filling his mouth while the obsidian light in his eyes began to flicker and dim.","He tried to raise his uninjured hand to block the next strike, but the crimson rings on Ragnar’s arm emitted a sudden pulse of Infinity that pinned his remaining arm to his side, leaving his chest and face entirely vulnerable to the giant’s wrath!","Ragnar smiled with a brutal, intimate malice as he delivered a rising punch burning with Infinity that caught THE Creature beneath his obsidian-masked jaw, the force of the hit causing his head to snap back with a textured, grinding noise of a fractured spine!","SQUELCH!","The sound of the impact was followed by the spray of dark, iridescent ichor as THE Creature’s mouth was filled with the metallic fluid of his own civilization, yet Ragnar did not cease the assault, instead raining down a flurry of short, piston-like punches into THE Creature’s midsection!","Each strike was a visceral explosion of power that mutilated the flesh and shattered the foundations beneath, and THE Creature could feel his very connection to THE Primordial Source beginning to fray under the sustained, multi-Cause overload!","He was being treated like a piece of worthless scrap, his bones being ground into powder and his muscles being torn from their anchors as Ragnar laughed with the genuine, manic glee of a predator who had finally found something that didn’t die after the first few hits!","The discrepancy was far too vast, for Ragnar was reinforced with concentrations of THE Observable Force that were millions of times denser than anything THE Creature had previously encountered, making every strike feel as though the entire weight of THE Braneworld were being focused into a single, massive fist!","When Ragnar finally released the crimson rings and let the mangled limb drop, THE Creature fell away like a discarded rag, his body a twisted ruin of broken bone and flickering, dying obsidian fire.","He lay in the center of the obsidian crater as utter devastation manifested across his entire being, his skin scorched and his limbs bent at angles that no living thing should survive!"]},{"number":5195,"title":"Chapter 5195: Chapter 5194: End of The Road! II","paragraphs":["From above, the cold and clinical voice of Ubergulden Hye-jin rang out with a total absence of interest in the suffering she had just authorized.","\" Contain him and shackle him, Ragnar, and don’t play around with the meat any longer.\"","THE Creature heard the words clearly as his entire existence was buzzing with the static of near-collapse, a sound continuing to play in his mind as if his very civilization were shaking.","His Existence was shaking from the pain and destruction as he couldn’t help but remember her.","Her face. Her warmth.","Her smile that was taken away so senselessly!","HUUM!","Anf his existence began to burn with rage!","His internal foundations were asking him if this was the end, if his climb was to be concluded as a harvest for the Superbius houses, and the massive, crimson-haloed hands of Ragnar neared him to finish the shackling!","He did not yet enact any change! He had not changed anything, so how could he be broken here?!","In that moment of absolute end, THE Creature felt his existence roaring in a desperate, primal defiance that reached deeper than his broken bones and his mutilated flesh!","He reached into the void of his own foundations for THE Primordial Source, searching through the wreckage of his consciousness until he found a single, ancient letter from THE Tongue of THE Primordial Source.","It was a letter that carried a meaning that transcended the eons and was forged in the pained emergence of the first things, and he roared it out of his existence with a volume that threatened to shatter the very foundations of THE Undefined Gaps.","\"... PERSEVERE!\"","BOOM!","Obsidian flames erupted from his body in an endless pillar of absolute authority, the force of the eruption actually pushing the brutally smiling Ragnar back by several meters as the space around them groaned under the weight of the ancient letter!","The giant laughed and roared out with a genuine excitement, his crimson halos spinning with a newfound intensity as he witnessed the impossible recovery.","\" Oh? Now that seems like the genuine power of a Relictus! Haha, good! Rise! Tatakae! TATAKAE!\"","BOOM!","The scene was shocking as THE Creature’s wounds and broken bones rapidly healed themselves under the surge of the obsidian fire, his muscles knitting back together and his spine snapping back into alignment with a series of loud, textured pops.","He rose from the crater with his obsidian mask hardening and his aura flaring with the weight of the ancient letter, looking coldly at Prima Custos Ragnar as his power seemed even grander and more terrifying than before!","HUUM!","Prima Custos Ragnar looked toward THE Young Relictus whose aura was even grander as he cracked his neck, the sound echoing like the snapping of dry branches in the cold silence of THE Undefined Gaps.","He asked with a dry, predatory amusement...","\" What is the whole deal with \"Persevere\" anyway? It is among the words THE Relictus love to use as it does ridiculous things to the local architecture of existence, but...\"","\" But today, buddy boy, today is just not your day,\" Ragnar said, his voice dropping into a register of cold certainty.","\" You can Persevere for as long as you want, but even a mountain eventually finds itself ground into dust by the turning of the tides.\"","HUUM!","Ragnar’s existence pulsed with a terrifying density as he raised his hand and pulled from one of the nine Prime Causes that comprised THE First Cause, reaching into the fundamental substrate of reality to grasp THE Dominion Cause, otherwise known as THE Cause of Supremacy.","The second experiential truth that emerged during THE First Cause was the truth that wherever multiple conscious beings exist, they will inevitably arrange themselves into configurations where some stand above others.","This arrangement is not imposed from outside but emerges from the interior of consciousness itself, derived from the recognition that differing capacities produce differing standings, and THE Dominion Cause holds this truth as its foundational axiom.","Many Armamental Axioms emerged from it.","It governed all authority, all governance, all hierarchy, all command, and all submission, for every arrangement in which one being holds power over another draws its structural legitimacy from this singular Prime Cause.","Ragnar pulled upon that Cause and allowed it to flow in his Rivers of Infinity in one hand, while his other hand reached toward a second Prime Axis to grasp THE Bellum Cause, also known as THE Cause of Conflict!","This was the Third Axis of Division: the fundamental truth that existence fights, born from the reality that consciousness encountering other consciousness inevitably produces friction.","THE Bellum Cause holds this truth as its foundational axiom, asserting that fighting is not an aberration of existence but a core function of it, as essential to the arrangement as breathing is to the body. It governed all conflict, all warfare, all violence, and all the structured expressions of one existence pressing against another with the intent to overcome, for every blade that has been swung or Pulse that has been cast draws its legitimacy from this Cause.","The power of both Prime Causes flowed in his hands, cascading across his Rivers of Infinity as he swung his hands down in a motion that sought to erase THE Young Relictus from the coordinates of THE Undefined Gaps!","HUUM!","Crimson and gold forces that the common eye couldn’t even perceive thundered down with the weight of entire civilizations, and THE Young Relictus erupted with his power, pulling from THE Primordial Source in a desperate, surging defense!","Ragnar laughed because the display was pitifully weak compared to the genuine Relictus he had feared in the eons of the past, and he watched with a cold, analytical eye as the result of the collision manifested.","BOOM!","THE Young Relictus faced a force so terrifying that when it smashed down, his entire body that had just risen was flattened again, the impact grinding him into the solidified obsidian floor of THE Undefinition.","Countless bones were broken with a sickening, wet crack, and his internal organs were ruptured into a slurry of golden ichor and obsidian fire that pooled in the crater!","Ragnar smiled with a cruelty that suggested he was finally enjoying the texture of the engagement, his crimson halos spinning with a violent light.","\" Come on, say it again, buddy boy. Persevere, Persevere!\"","\"Persevere!\"","BOOM!","Obsidian flames raged on THE Young Relictus’s body as his fractured existence and civilization healed through sheer causal defiance, and he began to rise once again, his aura flickering with a strength that was objectively grander than before!","Ragnar couldn’t help but laugh wildly before he bellowed out...","\" Buddy boy, you simply don’t get the magnitude of the forces arrayed against you!\"","BOOM!","The combined weight of THE Observable Force, Infinity, and two Prime Causes flowed through Ragnar as he struck out again, and THE Creature was flattened once more into the blood-stained crater!","Ragnar’s voice boomed through the void, encouraging him to rise again, to find that word and scream it against the darkness one more time!","\" Go on, buddy boy, again!\"","\"Persevere!\"","Obsidian flames raged once more as THE Creature healed and rose, his bones knitting together with the sound of grinding stone, before an instant later...","BOOM!","He was flattened again, the cycle of violence becoming a rhythmic, brutal cadence that stained the obsidian mountains with the scent of ozone and cooling blood.","THE Creature was decimated again and again, his body being ground into a ruin of meat and information as he uttered that single word of defiance every time his consciousness flickered back into focus.","By the eighty-first time, THE Creature was heaving in a crater filled with his own blood and the dissolved remnants of his authority, his breath coming in gurgling, wet gasps as Ragnar knelt toward him.","The Gilded One’s massive head came beside his ear, and he breathed in the scent of the decimation he had caused, his devilish smile inches away from THE Creature’s nearly shattered skull.","\" It has been so, so boring lately, and I have been so, so lonely in the heights of the Braneworld. I can only break and collapse so many Luxuria whores... \" Ragnar whispered just to him, while the other THE Gilded Ones watched from above with cold, judgmental gazes.","\"I thank you for coming, as I can sense you come with change, so come on, buddy boy. Say that fucking word again, otherwise all of this will be over and we will have captured nothing but a tiny, broken little Relictus.\"","BOOM!","THE Creature’s existence buzzed at these words, and even throughout this carnage, his eyes never lost their light of defiance, for they burned with a fire that Ragnar’s Prime Causes couldn’t extinguish!","Ragnar picked up the head of THE Creature by the hair, and THE Creature looked at the Gilded monster through blood-clotted eyes, voicing out through broken teeth a question that carried the weight of a curse.","\" Did you... forget that every time you come close to grasping THE Primordial Source... it gets taken from you?\"","The words were heavy and unhurried, and Ragnar blinked as he smiled even wider, the irony of the statement not lost on his mind. And as if on cue...","BOOM!","The region above THE Undefined Gaps shattered as a baleful obsidian brilliance unfolded alongside a roar that smashed several weaker THE Gilded Ones from the skies and into the ground like falling stars.","Ubergulden Hye-jin gazed coldly above as the form of a titanic beast began to manifest in the distance, a being that was likely countless gigaparsecs away yet whose form was enlarging with a terrifying speed.","Its size alone was likely as vast as a Primordial Realm, and though it was far, it neared with a gravity that threatened to pull the entire Gap into its orbit.","Ragnar looked up toward the approaching darkness and smiled brutally, while above, Ubergulden Hye-jin took her diagonal crown off and whispered into its crimson-gold surface...","\"A genuine Relictus actually came. Bring the others quickly.\"","BOOM!","Down below, Ragnar closed his massive fingers into the cranium of THE Creature, his grip tightening until the obsidian mask began to groan under the pressure.","\" See? I knew you would make things exciting again, and I cannot thank you enough for starting this war, buddy boy. Do you want to bet if you will miraculously make it out of this alive, hmm? Wanna bet?!\"","Ragnar asked these words as THE Creature only stared coldly at him, his answer being a single, final vibration of authority.","\" Persevere.\"","BOOM!","Obsidian flames rose up higher than ever before, THE Creature breaking the grip of Ragnar as the Gilded giant laughed boisterously, and all of existence groaned for the catastrophic change that was about to unfold!"]},{"number":5196,"title":"Chapter 5196: Chapter 5195: Eons of Advancements!","paragraphs":["In THE Braneworld Observable Existence.","Another side of the same coin!","There was a grand chamber holding a particularly important personage.","The chamber was a vast expanse that defied the meager spatial comprehension of those born to the lower domains, its golden walls breathing with a rhythmic, luminescent light that suggested the structure itself possessed a predatory life of its own.","The surfaces were not quite solid, creating a landscape of crystallized purpose where every step resonated with power refined across spans predating THE First Cause.","Constellations drifted across the ceiling in complex, swirling patterns that held the weighted meaning of the emergence of THE Causes, depicting the birth of the foundational Causes that governed reality with a clarity that only THE Gilded were engineered to read!","A golden aquarium floated silently in one corner, filled with waters that shifted between deep blue and luminescent gold, containing a landscape of coral formations and underwater valleys that stretched for light years of compressed space despite appearing mere feet wide.","The floor beneath the floating golden lotus was a polished mirror of crystallized purpose. It was a room that served as both a throne and a laboratory, a sanctuary of the high-born under the whim of the Ubergulden line.","Now, THE Gesinde were gone, their golden-shining presence removed to leave Ubergulden Adelheid in a silence that was heavy. She sat upon her floating golden lotus, its petals radiating a warmth that sought to stabilize her foundations, yet the air around her was far from calm as she delved into the depths of her meditation.","Due to what Noah had done by flooding her existence with Infinity, potent rivers of multicolored Quintessence Infiniforce and shimmering gold Observable Force surged around her in violent, swirling currents that threatened to crack the very crystallized floor.","These rivers of power acted like predatory tides, clashing and merging in a display of existential weight that forced her to anchor her weavings with every ounce of her royal engineering.","The multicolored seas of Infiniforce pulsed with a rhythmic, tyrannical cadence that seemed to echo the heartbeat of THE Genesis Monarch himself, an intrusion of Bounded authority that was successfully masquerading as a Gilded bond!","The clashing of the gold and multicolored energies produced a low, thrumming sound that vibrated through the architecture of the room, causing the golden walls to pulse with a frantic, stuttering light as they struggled to process the anomalous frequency.","Ubergulden Adelheid remained a silhouette of regal stillness amidst this multicolored storm, her eyes closed as she fought to maintain the veil over her connection while the raw density of Noah’s infinity sought to announce its presence.","HUUM!","At such a time.","Ubergulden Dietrich entered the room with a heavy and measured tread, his golden eyes without pupils scanning the tempest of power surrounding his sister with a mixture of pride and mounting concern.","He took a seat upon a floating debris of crystallized purpose directly across from her, the weight of his own Paleozoic-tier existence providing a momentary stabilization to the roiling currents of the space as he sensed the sheer immensity of her shifting power.","He didn’t speak immediately, instead watching the way the multicolored rivers of infinity danced across her skin, his expression turning empathetic yet firm as he prepared to deliver the weight of their family’s expectations.","\" Do you know why The Sororis Prima are making such a big deal of your Custodes, little sister? \" Dietrich asked.","\" Our family is powerful and we have significant pull even against THE Magna Sorora, but in your absence, something fundamental has changed while you were living among the dredges of the folds. Our Ubergulden lineage became even more distinguished because while you were gone in those eons, there was an incident and a profound advancement in our understanding of the enemy that blocks the path to the Source.\"","He leaned forward, the golden light of the walls reflecting in his empty eyes as he shared the secrets that the high houses guarded with their lives.","\" After being blocked by THE Relictus for so long, we finally made some progress to understand them, and we believe we have finally found the path to... THE Primordial Source. THE Magna Sorora tried to enter a unique place where THE Relictus should be originating from, but none of their specialists survived the journey as all of one’s existence was stripped to their Source whenever any Gilded One tried to make the transition. The purest part of their existence and civilization was all that remained as no Gilded Ones survived the crossing, apart from those from the very few and very pure lineages capable of withstanding that specific pressure.\"","He gestured toward the swirling rivers of her aura, acknowledging the brilliance that infinity had amplified within her.","\" Our Ubergulden lineage is among the few capable of surviving that journey, and your specific brilliance can shield one additional Custos, which would allow more of our forces to penetrate that place while gathering the information we need. We have become the spear that makes entry into the secrets of THE Primordial Source, and this is why the sisters care so much about the quality of the being bound to you. So tell me, little sister, who and where is your Custodes? Whatever the situation is, I can salvage it as long as it is not too obscene. Who and where...is your Custodes?\"","Ubergulden Adelheid frowned, her internal thoughts moving with speed. She thought about her brother’s words and the staggering importance of her role in their family’s ascension.","Her eyes shone with a sharp, calculated light as she finally looked up, her voice carrying a cold and regal certainty that betrayed none of her visceral panic.","\" They... are in THE Braneworld Observable Existence right now, operating under a veil I established to ensure their growth remained undisturbed by the politics of the houses. Let me take you to them in a little while, once I confirm something.\"","Ubergulden Dietrich let out a laugh that was filled with a free and resonant relief, the tension in his shoulders finally dissolving as he looked at his sister with genuine, dark amusement.","\"Oh man, you really had me worried for a second there, for some reason I had the most ridiculous and impossible thought that you had somehow bonded with a Bounded lifeform as your Custos. An impossibility, I know, but existence is crazy like that and I find myself wondering what kind of wild tragedy that would have been!\"","BOOM!","\"And I did see you focusing on that group of Bounded Lifeforms when I found as I thought you may have formed a connection with them. Ah, I’ll check on that later. But can you imagine? If you had truly had a Bounded lifeform as your Custos while your position is so elevated among THE Gilded right now? Haha, what a wild thing that would have been to see!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5197,"title":"Chapter 5197: Chapter 5196: Entry Into THE Braneworld Observable Existence!","paragraphs":["Any door can be opened. You simply need the right key.","The Bounded discovered this truth early. A locked granary becomes negotiable when you arrive with sufficient grain of your own. A fortified city becomes navigable when you arrive with sufficient gold. A suspicious guard becomes surprisingly flexible when you arrive with sufficient of whatever the suspicious guard specifically values, which is almost always money!","The Gilded Ones, who constructed THE Braneworld Observable Existence behind dimensional barriers requiring Paleozoic authority to breach, believed they had built a door without a key.","Because no Bounded Lifeform could reach Paleozoic!","But they had not built a door without a key.","The door, as all doors eventually do, would open.","It simply required the correct key.","And Noah had always been very good at finding keys!","Noah’s key this time was a Luxuria Gilded One he had put under his control as they were currently traversing endlessly chaotic seas of Infinity and Observable Force burning with Definition and Undefinition.","Custos Rani was already a Gilded One as her aura alone made this artificial barrier not act out against her, her glow covering both her and Noah as they crossed through. Even if she wasn’t here though, Noah still felt like he could brute force it, though that would draw unwanted attention that he wasn’t quite ready to manage.","Before he made the choice to leave the domain Rani had them in, he debated heading back down to THE Observable Existence to duke it out with Sororis Prima Prabhavati.","But the memories of Custos Rani allowed him to glimpse a bit more of her power as it seemed THE Magna Sorora were formidable, where even with his current means, even if Noah was confident, the battle would be loud.","In that all other THE Sororis Prima in THE Observable Existence currently would be alerted and he would lose more than make any gains, which led to the logical thought that he needed the power to one shot Paleozoic Scale entities in an instant to ensure everything would be smooth for the future.","But for now...","HUUM!","Existence shook and trembled as Noah felt himself passing through an imperceptible barrier and entering into somewhere filled with concentrations of terrifying brilliance as he found himself rising from a sea of concentrated golden Observable Force and emerging into skies of scintillating brilliance, intensity, and glory!","|We have made our entry into THE Braneworld Observable Existence. May there be boundless tyranny and Infinity in the future to come.|","His cells and atoms buzzed as they began to absorb everything nearby, and Pillow Talk activated as information began to flow into his mind even though he had memories to know exactly what he was looking at in the distance.","He had arrived in THE Braneworld Observable Existence, in a small corner of it that Custos Rani would have called her home!","Within THE Braneworld Observable Existence, nestled between the martial fortresses of THE Ira houses and the vast accumulation towers of THE Avaritia archives, lies a domain whose existence THE Superbius hierarchy considers simultaneously indispensable and somewhat beneath formal acknowledgment.","THE Velanthra.","Translated from the oldest Gilded dialects, the name means approximately \"the place where wanting takes form,\" and the translation is considered accurate by every being who has ever entered its borders and emerged afterward with their existential priorities quietly rearranged.","Noah looked at the distant cluster of terrifying concentrations of power as he voiced out to Custos Rani.","\"Which Luxuria Gilded One do you think would be ideal for me to collapse and take the identity of?\"","He said such words casually as since he needed an identity, Noah didn’t want to go through anything bothersome as he simply thought of taking on the identity of a Luxuria Gilded One as he could easily emulate their Ego, in an even grander sense too!","And it would be a matching identity of a Custodes that Ubergulden Adelheid didn’t want others to know about. Custos Rani’s eyes flashed coldly, a sharp and clinical light reflecting in her galaxy-filled gaze as she processed the registries of her home domain.","\"The Scion of Silken Grief,\" she whispered, the name carrying a weight of tragic isolation.","\"He resides in the upper reaches of the tower, detached from the Houses of Service, and his absence from the social configurations of THE Velanthra would ensure your takeover remains undetected by the audit-eyes of the houses. He is also among thr possible identities I brought up to Sororis Prima Prabhavati.\"","Noah looked at the memories of the entity she mentioned as he smiled, a dangerous and dryly amused expression touching his crystalline features.","\"Okay, let’s go see this place.\"","...!","THE Velanthra spans a territory roughly equivalent to a small continent within THE Braneworld, its borders delineated not by walls or barriers but by a gradual transition in the ambient atmosphere that every visitor registers before they consciously understand what they are registering.","The air within THE Velanthra carries a density of amplified Luxuria Ego that accumulates across the first few miles of entry, a crimson-pink luminescence that threads through the observable light like a dye introduced into clear water, subtle at the borders and saturating at the center.","The architecture of THE Velanthra reflects an advanced civilization that has spent eons optimizing a single design principle: that every structure should produce in its observer the specific sensation of arriving somewhere they have always wanted to be without knowing they wanted it!","The buildings are tall and curving, their facades composed of a pale gold material that shifts its surface texture in response to the emotional state of whoever stands before it, producing different appearances for different observers as no two beings have ever reported seeing the same building in exactly the same configuration.","Rivers of Infinity flow through THE Velanthra in channels that were engineered during THE Sixth Age by THE Avaritia architects operating under Luxuria direction, the only known instance of a lower designation providing creative direction to a higher one!"]},{"number":5198,"title":"Chapter 5198: Chapter 5197: The Custos, Osmont! I","paragraphs":["The channels of this place wind through the domain’s central districts in patterns that follow the natural flow of amplified THE Desidero Cause energy rather than geographic logic, producing riverways that curve through plazas and beneath bridges and through the lower floors of inhabited structures.","The Infinity within these channels had been tinted crimson-pink through sustained exposure to the domain’s ambient Luxuria Ego, producing rivers that glow with warm rose-gold luminescence against the pale gold of the surrounding architecture.","Observable Force flows through THE Velanthra in an unusual configuration unique to this domain as rather than the ambient golden currents that characterize most of THE Braneworld, THE Velanthra’s Observable Force has been engineered into a mist that drifts through the streets at knee height.","Warm and faintly luminous, the mist responds to the presence of beings within it by producing gentle currents that press against them with the specific warmth of something alive and attentive!","Approximately three million Luxuria Gilded Ones inhabit THE Velanthra permanently, one of the largest concentration of any Gilded designation within some of the domain in THE Braneworld.","The Luxuria of THE Velanthra organize themselves into Houses of Service, each House specializing in a specific expression of the designation’s broad functional mandate.","Some Houses specialize in domestic refinement, producing the attendants who staff the grand households of THE Superbius rulers across the broader Braneworld, while others specialize in artistic production, generating the music, architecture, cuisine, and ceremonial design that give Gilded civilization its aesthetic character.","Others specialize in cultivation support, producing existences whose amplified THE Desidero Cause can accelerate the cultivation of higher-designation beings through directed emotional resonance and Dual Cultivation.","Since Noah had such terrifying waves of Luxuria, he pulled them back somewhat and covered his face with a crimson gold mask as they moved from the golden sea of Observable Force and into the periphery of THE Velanthra.","He could see groups of Luxuria lounged on crimson white sandy beaches, and some on the edge of the waters swimming while absorbing Observable Force into their foundations. In one area, Noah saw a group of THE Superbius and THE Ira Gilded Ones lounging on golden laid-back throne-like chairs, with an even larger ground of Luxuria Gilded Ones surrounding them as they fed them vibrant fruits filled with Observable Force.","Some Luxuria were filling their hands with pink and golden light as they gave massages to other Ira or Superbius Gilded Ones, providing a scene that felt like a domain of waste and debauchery to Noah’s pragmatic mind.","He shook his head and wanted to get past all this as his gaze shifted toward the towering spire at the heart of the continents-sized domain.","\" Let’s go to THE Amaranthine Tower ,\" he said, his voice flat and focused.","THE Amaranthine Tower.","From the memories of Custos Rani and what he could see in the far distance at the depths of this place, THE Amaranthine Tower was the tallest structure in THE Velanthra, a tower of pale gold and rose crystal that rises from the domain’s center and terminates in a crown of condensed Luxuria Ego visible from every point within the domain’s borders.","The tower serves as the administrative center of the domain’s Luxuria governance structures and as the residence of the highest-ranking Luxuria within the domain.","The entity for Noah to take the identity of was somewhere within that tower!","With a flash of brilliance, Custos Rani put her hand on him as she trembled from the contact alone, with Noah actually doing everything he could to stifle any part of his aura as it might pull in the hungry gazes of all Luxuria here.","Not yet.","Not yet!","Obtain an identity first, then conquest!","---","<The Scion of Silken Grief>","The private residence of THE Scion of Silken Grief was a masterclass in the kind of opulent cruelty that only THE Luxuria could engineer, the walls composed of shifting rose crystal that seemed to sigh with a faint, simulated pleasure whenever the light hit them at the right angle.","Dante reclined on a chaise of living coral that pulsed with a warm, golden light, his fingers tracing the rim of a chalice filled with the distilled essence of a Observable Force and Infinity.","A group of four Luxuria Gilded women, their iridescent skin marred by burns and dark, purplish fractures in their crystalline structures, huddled near the doorway as they tried to suppress their trembling.","They had been the playthings of the afternoon, their engineered foundations pushed to the point of structural failure just to satisfy the wandering whims of a man who had never known the weight of a single day’s labor.","\"I told you to get out of my sight, you useless thingd ,\" Dante said, his voice carrying the bored, high-pitched arrogance of a rich young master who found even the sight of his own victims to be a tedious inconvenience.","\" You look like shit and your resonance is starting to give me a headache, so crawl back to your houses and try to look presentable before I call for you again later tonight.\"","The women scrambled out of the room without a single word of protest, their heads lowered as they retreated from the presence of a Scion who viewed their existence as nothing more than disposable fabric to be torn and discarded.","Dante watched them go with a sneer of absolute disdain, taking a slow sip of his essence as he settled deeper into the living coral, his mind already drifting toward which House of Service he would pillage next for his evening entertainment.","For he was ranked high among the Houses of Luxuria here and could do what he wanted!","He was just beginning to savor the silence when two distinct auras flashed into the center of his private domain, the sudden displacement of air causing the rose crystals on the walls to shriek in protest.","Dante blinked and looked toward the center of the room with an expression of sharp annoyance, his eyes narrowing as he felt the sheer audacity of an unannounced intrusion into his sanctuary.","\" Fuck outa here, whoever you are,\" he spat as he didn’t even bother to stand from his chaise.","\"I don’t care if you’re from THE First of Service or if you’ve got a message from the Superbius houses, because I’m not in the mood for any more administrative bullshit today!\"","The two figures didn’t move, and as Dante turned his head to fully address the intruders, his sneer faltered when he recognized the cold, galaxy-filled eyes of Custos Rani standing beside a man whose face was obscured by a crimson-gold mask.","He opened his mouth to deliver another insult, but the man slowly raised his hands and removed the mask, revealing a set of features that possessed a beauty so unfathomable and predatory it felt like a physical strike to Dante’s own Gilded senses.","HUUM!","The man didn’t say a word, but he released a fraction of his aura that caused the private domain to groan!","THE Scion of Silken Grief became frozen completely as a terrifying, absolute power locked onto his foundations, the sheer density of Noah’s Luxuria Ego flooding the room and turning the air into a thick, syrupy substance that Dante’s lungs couldn’t even process.","The rich young master tried to speak, but his voice was trapped behind a wall of Nearu Absolute Infinity that was currently rewriting the laws of the room to favor a new, tyrannical master.","He looked into Noah’s crystalline eyes and realized, with a visceral and animal terror, that he wasn’t looking at another Gilded One, but at a butcher who had finally come to claim the spoiled meat of his existence!","BOOM!"]},{"number":5199,"title":"Chapter 5199: Chapter 5198: The Custos, Osmont! II","paragraphs":["Noah walked forward with the unhurried gait of a man who already owned the room, his crystalline Luxuria form casting long, iridescent shadows against the rose crystal walls.","He looked at Dante, who was currently suspended in a state of absolute existential stasis, and he felt a flash of dry disdain for the way this fucking rat’s engineered foundations were trembling under the mere proximity of a superior Ego.","There was no struggle and no resistance as Noah reached out and sank his fingers into the air inches from Dante’s chest, pulling upon the multicolored seas of Quintessence Infiniforce to begin the systematic rewriting of the Scion’s existence.","He was gathering more and more information on Gilded Anatomy as soon, he would be able to engineer his own Hadean Weavings and those of his people a step further. Not merely going towaeds becoming moreso like Gilded Lifeforms...but something entirely new!","The multicolored light of Infinity dove deep into Dante’s Gilded marrow, acting as a terminal virus that tore through his memories of unearned opulence and replaced his autonomy with the cold, unyielding signature of THE Genesis Monarch.","Noah watched with a clinical eye as the rich young master’s internal systems were forcibly recalibrated to align with his own foundations, the pink-gold light of the Luxuria designation becoming stained with the heavy, multicolored hues of Noah’s sovereign will!","It was a brutal and efficient process that didn’t just bind the target, but essentially claimed the very concept of \"Dante\" as a piece of property to be utilized or discarded at a whim.","|Absolute Servitude of the Vessel integrated.|","|Target: Dante, THE Scion of Silken Grief, has been successfully rewritten as an extension of your Hadean existence.|","|Quintessence Infiniforce saturation: 100%.|","\" You’ve lived a very loud and very useless life, Dante, so let’s see if your components can be put to better use in the dark ,\" Noah murmured, his voice holding the resonance of a judge passing a final sentence.","He waved his hand with a casual flick of his wrist, and a lightless rift of obsidian energy tore open in the center of the opulence, revealing the cold and echoing reaches of THE Hadean Desmoterion.","Within this internal prison that existed in a pocket of his Organ of Civilization, the figure of Ozymandias stood waiting with his ancient and stoic bearing, his role as THE Warden being a position he performed with a silent, terrifying efficiency!","Noah tossed the rewritten and still-frozen body of Dante into the rift by kicking him into it, watching as the Scion vanished into the lightless depths where his spoiled existence would be archived, studied under temporally dilated condintions, and kept until needed, the rift closing an instant later with a sharp, metallic hum.","HUUM!","Noah stood alone in the center of the residence for a moment, and then he allowed his own crystalline beauty to shift and dissolve, his features blurring and resetting into the likeness of the man he had just displaced.","He looked at his reflection in the shifting rose crystal of the walls, noting the less handsome and more petulant features of THE Scion of Silken Grief with a shrug of his shoulders.","It was a significant downgrade in terms of aesthetic brilliance, but for the purposes of a disguise, he found the mediocre look of the rich young master to be entirely acceptable!","He closed his eyes and reached out through the Infinity and Observable Force that tied him to a certain royal, his consciousness traveling along the rivers of Observable Force that connected him to Ubergulden Adelheid.","\" Hey ,\" he said, his voice reaching her through the unreachable weavings with a calm and almost amused clarity.","\"I found my identity as a Gilded One. I’ve taken the place of a boy named Dante, THE Scion of Silken Grief, who will be giving himself the additional distinction of THE Osmontian as of today. I’m in Velanthra right now...within THE Amaranthine Tower.\"","Noah opened his eyes and adjusted the silk of his new robes, a brilliant and tyrannical smile touching his borrowed lips.","She had mentioned she had hours at most before she had to give a name, and he was now here!","---","The pink-gold atmosphere of THE Velanthra was never meant to hold the weight of true, unadulterated sovereignty, for it was a place engineered for the softness of desire rather than the hard edges of command.","Yet at this time...","Above THE Amaranthine Tower, the shimmering skies began to seethe and tremble as a massive golden vessel tore through the fabric of the domain, its sheer mass displacing the rose-colored mists with a violent, authoritative pressure.","It was a leviathan of solidified Observable Force that burned with the searing, arrogant radiance of THE Superbius Gilded Ones, its hull stretching for kilometers like a floating continent of polished gold.","The ship didn’t merely fly but seemed to rewrite the gravity of the region, causing the rivers of rose-gold Infinity below to churn and overflow their engineered channels.","At the very center of the vessel’s prow, the logo of THE Ubergulden House blazed with a light that made the surrounding suns look like guttering candles.","It was a golden scepter piercing a lightless crown, with a singular, pupil-less eye weeping liquid starlight at the apex, a sigil that carried the weight of eons of unchallenged dominance!","Thousands of THE Luxuria Gilded Ones raised their eyes in shock, their pleasure-filled existences momentarily frozen by the arrival of a royal house that rarely deigned to step foot in the domain of service.","They wondered with a rising sense of dread why such an esteemed lineage would come to a place like this.","HUUM!","From the base of the massive vessel, the air rippled as three figures descended with a synchronized.","THE Sororis Prima...Evangelina, Konstanze, and Mathilde, floated down toward THE Amaranthine Tower, their golden robes trailing behind them like ribbons of liquid starlight.","Beside each of them walked their respective Custodes, massive Gilded warriors whose auras were so dense they seemed to bruise the very air of THE Velanthra.","These guardians moved with a clinical, preternatural stillness, their hands resting on the hilts of weapons that had unmade entire civilizations before THE Sixth Age was even a memory.","Behind this vanguard of authority, the figure of Ubergulden Dietrich appeared, his presence expanding to fill the void left by the ship’s arrival.","He stood with the easy confidence of a man who owned the sky he walked upon, his golden eyes without pupils fixed on the spire below with a gaze that held no room for negotiation.","Beside him stood Ubergulden Adelheid, her expression a mask of regal composure that hid the churning multicolored seas of infinity.","\" Is this the place where your ’hidden’ Custos resides, sister?\"","A pivotal moment came as many did not realize...it was the nexus point for change that would sweep across The Braneworld Observable Existence like a storm!"]},{"number":5200,"title":"Chapter 5200: Chapter 5199: The Custos, Osmont! III","paragraphs":["Inside Dante’s domain, Noah stood amidst the shifting rose crystals and the pulsing coral furniture.","He calmly tapped his chest with a crystalline finger, and a ripple of multicolored light spilled from his form as another Nearu Absolute Clone emerged from his existence with the silent grace of a predator.","This body retained his true, unfathomable face and the staggering Luxuria Ego of Infinity, its aura vibrating with an iridescent density that made the surrounding air feel heavy and thick with the scent of ozone.","He beckoned toward Custos Rani with a subtle tilt of his head, and in the next moment, the two of them disappeared from the room in a flash of iridescent brilliance, leaving only his original body in the form of Dante.","HUUM!","They reappeared within the private reaches of Custos Rani’s own domain inside THE Amaranthine Tower, a space that was draped in fabrics of woven starlight and scented with the cloying, engineered sweetness of rose-gold incense.","Rani immediately dropped to her knees upon the polished golden floor as she felt the suffocating weight of Noah’s true presence filling her sanctuary.","She spoke with a voice that was hushed and trembling, her galaxy-filled eyes lowered in a gesture of profound submission that suggested she was struggling to anchor her own foundations against the radiance of her master.","\" Master, this place is entirely insufficient to host the glory of your existence, for it is merely a small and meager corner of thid place that I have called my own across the eons. I feel the poverty of my own weavings when placed beneath the shadow of your Infinity, and I find myself ashamed that I cannot offer a sanctuary more worthy of you as we begin our work in THE Braneworld...\"","Noah waved his hand dismissively, his crystalline eyes scanning the opulent fabrics and the rose-gold pillars with a dry, pragmatic disdain that made the air within the domain feel colder.","\" Hush and stand up, the quality of your silk and the fragrance of your incense are of little consequence to me when I’ve already decided to treat this entire domain as the starting point of my conquest. Right now, this citadel of Luxuria Gilded Ones and these wretched, debauchery lands of THE Velanthra are filled with Paleozoic Scale Gilded Ones of all types who currently do not know me, but that’s a condition I intend to rectify over the next few days with a surgical and absolute efficiency...\"","HUUM!","\"I want to spread my influence through the Houses to bring this entire continent-sized place under my control.\"","He took a slow step forward, the multicolored rivers of his power pulsing in a rhythmic, tyrannical cadence that resonated through the tower’s crystalline foundations.","\"I’ll take things lightly for now to ensure we don’t draw the immediate and unwanted attention of THE Magna Sorora, for I have no interest in fighting a loud and messy war before I’ve properly anchored my foundations in this place. These Gilded Ones and all their engineered pride and their eons of unearned glory shall be the first to truly understand their place in the hierarchy, for they’re going to witness the historic and absolute control of a Bounded lifeform stand over them!\"","WAA!","His eyes shone with glory!","\"We’ll have to be mindful of the most dangerous Paleozoic Scale monsters currently here but...the first thing that has really interested me is...THE Sanctum Velanthra.\"","...!","Noah spent a long moment sorting through the fractured, iridescent memories of Custos Rani, finding that the most offensive disparity between his kind and these Gilded fuckers wasn’t just the raw density of their mana or the engineered perfection of their bodies.","It was the gatekeeping of knowledge, for while THE Bounded were left to scramble in the dirt for the scraps of an understanding they had to bleed for, THE Gilded had simply stolen the architectural blueprints of THE First Cause and called it their birthright.","Knowledge was the ultimate currency of power in THE Braneworld, and the specific hoard that interested Noah the most was a place nestled deep within the heart of this continent-sized domain of debauchery...a closely guarded sanctuary known as THE Sanctum Velanthra.","He closed his eyes in Custos Rani’s private domain and let the memories flow.","THE Sanctum Velanthra. It was a place holding information of...THE First Cause!","The sparse knowledge Custos Rani held regarding this place filtered through his consciousness with the patient clarity of information that had been kept deliberately vague from those below a certain standing, which told him immediately that whatever sat behind that name was something the Gilded considered genuinely worth protecting.","The first thing that landed in his mind was simple enough.","Bounded Lifeforms could not reach it.","Not as a matter of difficulty, not as a matter of climbing harder or cultivating longer or finding the right technique to bridge the gap. As a matter of categorical impossibility, structural and permanent, woven into the separation between the lower Observable Existence and THE Braneworld the same way the difference between water and fire was woven into their respective natures.","No Bounded Lifeform, regardless of what they had achieved or how exceptional their cultivation had proven, would find THE Sanctum Velanthra accessible without direct intervention from a Gilded One already present within it...which didn’t even matter since it was nearly impossible for Bounded Lifeforms to enter The Braneworld Observable Existence!","The Sanctum sat nested within THE Velanthra itself, which was already inaccessible to ordinary beings.","Three million Luxuria inhabited the broader domain and most of them would never cross into the Sanctum’s borders across the full span of their existences.","The border wasn’t marked by walls. It was marked by a shift in the quality of the surrounding existence so profound that beings who approached without sufficient standing found their own foundations pressing back against them, the space itself declining their entry without explanation or apology.","Several Superbius Gilded Ones across prior Ages had been turned back at the threshold.","That particular detail meant the Sanctum was not merely filtering for power. It was filtering for something else.","Entry required three simultaneous conditions, all established by THE Magna Sorora during the Sixth Age and maintained without amendment since!"]}]);
